window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":6601,"title":"Chapter 6601: Chapter 6599: The Obstinate Jie Baobao","paragraphs":["Chapter 6599: The Obstinate Jie Baobao","“Jie Baobao, I shan’t make things hard for you. All I’m asking you to do is to distance yourself from Chu Feng by listing his crimes and scolding that little bastard. I’ll pretend that nothing has happened if so. That shouldn’t be difficult, right?” Ling Kun asked.","Many people sent voice transmissions to Jie Baobao, advising her to do as she was told. Ling Kun was already trying to de-escalate the situation as well by giving Jie Baobao an easy way out; all she had to do was criticize Chu Feng a little.","“Why should I scold him?” Jie Baobao asked.","The crowd was taken aback.","Ling Kun had given Jie Baobao a way out, but she refused to take it. Could the rumors that Jie Baobao was in cahoots with Chu Feng be true? That would change the nature of this matter.","Ling Kun’s eyebrows shot up as he scoffed, “Why? Chu Feng is a wanted criminal of our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Do you not think that his actions deserve to be criticized?”","“What did he do? Our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion already views him in enmity even when he hasn’t done anything at all,” Jie Baobao replied.","“Audacious! Isn’t he the one who wreaked havoc in our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion? Jie Baobao, are you truly colluding with Chu Feng?” Ling Kun questioned.","“Lord Ling Kun, look at Jie Baobao’s right hand. She has been holding onto something since coming out of her chamber. Could it be related to Chu Feng?” an elder standing behind Ling Kun pointed out.","That drew scrutiny to Jie Baobao’s tightly clenched right hand, especially when she visibly tightened her grip when that was pointed out.","In an instant, everyone was interested to know what she was holding.","“What is in your hand?” Ling Kun asked.","“It has nothing to do with you,” Jie Baobao replied.","“Audacious!” An elder stepped forward to search Jie Baobao.","“Stop.” But Ling Kun stopped that elder. “Jie Baobao, I have given you chances in view that you’re a talent of our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I’ll only ask you one last time. What are you holding in your hand?”","There was a cold glint in Ling Kun’s eyes as he posed that question.","“It is my property. You have no right to know,” Jie Baobao replied.","Shoosh!","Fresh blood gushed from Jie Baobao’s right arm. Her right arm had been severed.","Ling Kun had made a move.","The crowd was startled. They didn’t expect Ling Kun to make a move. That was Jie Baobao! Even with the Enforcement Token, Ling Kun would still face intense scrutiny for making a move on a talented prodigy like Jie Baobao.","Talents like Jie Baobao were naturally accorded special treatment.","But even when Jie Baobao’s right arm was severed and fell to the ground, it continued to tightly clutch onto whatever was in her hand.","She had constructed a formation on her right hand that was bound to her life. Unless she were killed, it would be impossible for anyone to open up her right hand.","“You’ll have to kill me if you want to see it,” Jie Baobao said forcefully.","“Do you think I dare not do that?” Ling Kun asked coldly.","“Hah...” Jie Baobao laughed coldly. “I’ll say it now. I am not in collusion with Chu Feng, but I don’t think he has done wrong, either. I have interacted with him, and I think that he’s a good person. He didn’t do wrong; it is our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion who has done wrong.”","Her words horrified the crowd. She was courting death by saying those words aloud!","“You’re asking for it!” The infuriated Ling Kun constructed a formation that crushed Jie Baobao into the ground. The intense pressure caused blood to spurt from her mouth.","“You should have heard Jie Baobao’s words. It is thanks to our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s nurturing that she accomplished what she has today, but she knows not of gratitude. She is siding with a sinner who has crossed us many times. Jie Boabao is a traitor! She has to be executed!” Ling Kun roared.","“Jie Baobao, you deserve to die for uttering such blasphemous words. How dare you question Lord Mansion Master?” Ling Kun’s granddaughter added.","“Fine. Go ahead and kill me. I don’t want to stay in such a Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, either,” Jie Baobao replied.","“Do you think I dare not kill you?” Ling Kun’s granddaughter pulled out a formation knife and charged at Jie Baobao.","Shoosh!","Blood splattered.","Everyone fell silent, including Ling Kun.","He was the one who gave his granddaughter that formation knife. He also staged this show to teach Jie Baobao a lesson on his granddaughter’s behalf, so that the latter could vent her anger. He didn’t expect his granddaughter to stab Jie Baobao and cripple her spirit power.","“This...”","Many people panicked. It was Jie Baobao they were talking about here. Even if she deserved to die, she should only be sentenced by the Mansion Master.","Shoosh!","Ling Kun pulled out the Enforcement Token once more and roared, “Seeing the token is as good as seeing Lord Mansion Master. Jie Baobao has doubted Lord Mansion Master and deserves to be executed on the spot. She shall be sentenced to Death by Mob. Everyone present is to inflict an injury on her. If anyone goes easy on her, I’ll have no choice but to suspect them of being a traitor as well and deal with them accordingly.”","“Elder Ling Kun, surely there is no need to go this far? You can punish Jie Baobao if you want to, but you don’t have to implicate us in this,” an elder said.","He was from the same generation as Ling Kun, and they were on close terms.","Shoosh!","Ling Kun unleashed a formation sword and decapitated that elder.","“This...”","The crowd was dumbstruck. They didn’t expect Ling Kun to be so domineering.","“I have the Enforcement Token in hand. Doubting me is as good as doubting Lord Mansion Master. Is anyone else going to doubt my judgment as well?” Ling Kun asked.","The crowd knew that this was Ling Kun’s ploy. He wanted to drag as many people down with him, in hopes that Jie Tianran would spare them given that they were a large group.","But they had no choice but to do his bidding, since he had the Enforcement Token in hand."]},{"number":6602,"title":"Chapter 6602: Chapter 6600: Chu Feng’s Vengeance","paragraphs":["Chapter 6600: Chu Feng’s Vengeance","“Jie Baobao, your ego has become overinflated from years of coddling. How dare you utter such insolent words? You deserve to die!”","Someone conjured a formation sword and stabbed Jie Baobao’s left thigh.","That paved the way for others to follow suit. Some even attacked her several times.","This was Jie Baobao, a figure whom they could only look up to under normal circumstances. This was a rare chance for them to turn the tables on a prodigy like that, and the notion excited them.","Most of them were weaker than Jie Baobao, but they were still able to hurt her due to Ling Kun’s formation.","Actually, aside from the initial blow from Ling Kun’s granddaughter, the other attacks were not fatal to Jie Baobao. But it was an attack from tens of millions of people. So many people were hurting Jie Baobao with their weapons and formations.","Even if their intention was not to kill Jie Baobao, this accumulation of damage was more than enough to obliterate her.","Jie Baobao initially scoffed in disdain, but over time, her face turned as pale as a sheet of paper. She lay on the floor, not moving in the least. She couldn’t even utter a word.","Boom!","A resounding explosion echoed from the sky.","The crowd looked over and saw that the cultivation ground’s barrier had shattered.","“This...?”","The crowd looked at the shattered fragments of the barrier in unease. They realized that something bad had happened.","“Chu Feng!”","Someone pointed to Jie Baobao and screamed.","And indeed, Chu Feng had appeared beside Jie Baobao. He dropped to a knee and carefully carried her up.","“Chu Feng?” Ling Kun’s face warped in shock.","Despite being a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, he dared not make a move on Chu Feng. On the contrary, he even retreated several steps out of fear. He had witnessed everything that had happened in the Undying Starfield and knew how terrifying Chu Feng was.","“Chu Feng, how dare you infiltrate our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion? Die!”","However, there was no lack of fearless fools among the crowd. Some of them conjured formations to attack Chu Feng.","Pah! Pah! Pah!","But a glance from Chu Feng made them explode into crimson blood fogs. Those who dared to attack him had been blown into bits.","“Gosh, that is...”","The crowd was shaken awake. It was the Chu Feng they were dealing with right now, a merciless monster who wouldn’t hesitate to massacre millions. The realization drove many of them to flee.","Boom!","Powerful oppressive might crushed down from the sky, turning the cultivation ground into a massive prison. Little Fishy had made a move.","“Xianhai Yu’er? She has reached Heavenly God level? That phenomenon was from her!” Ling Kun raised his head and saw Little Fishy towering in the sky like a deity. He shuddered in fear.","Even Chu Feng was beyond his means to deal with, let alone a stronger Little Fishy.","Ling Kun thought about what he had done earlier, and he looked at how Chu Feng was carrying Jie Baobao now. His eyes became clear as his earlier arrogance receded from his gaze. All that was left in them was fear.","He knew he was in trouble.","“Chu Feng?” Jie Baobao feebly opened her eyes and looked at Chu Feng in disbelief.","Chu Feng’s face was icy-cold. He had no idea what happened earlier. He had only come here to claim God’s Era’s power fragment, but he noticed a commotion when he approached.","The crowd was punishing an individual. Upon closer look, he realized it was his friend, Jie Baobao.","Jie Baobao’s face was intact, but her body was in complete ruin. It wouldn’t be an exaggeration to call her body a sack of meat.","“It’s fine now,” Chu Feng said as he slipped a pill into Jie Baobao’s mouth. He channeled his spirit power to heal her injuries.","But upon closer inspection, his heart skipped a beat. Jie Baobao’s spirit power had been crippled, and her life was on the brink of being extinguished after the relentless attacks from the mob. Her death was almost inevitable.","Chu Feng’s heart blazed with fury.","He grabbed the closest elders and pulled them to him.","“ GAHHH! ”","Miserable cries followed. Streams of energy flowed from their heads into Chu Feng’s palm. Chu Feng was plundering their memories to get to the bottom of what happened.","But learning about the chain of events only further fanned Chu Feng’s anger. His murderous intent flared, causing the sky to turn dark.","A talent like Jie Baobao should have been celebrated. Even if she had done something that deserved death, there should have been a chance for her to redeem herself. Yet, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion sentenced her to death just because she refused to criticize Chu Feng.","This was ridiculous.","“Grandfather, is that... really Chu Feng? Why is he here? What do we do now?”","Ling Kun’s granddaughter hid behind Ling Kun and clutched his robe. Her face was distorted in fear, and tears wouldn’t stop streaming from her eyes.","But Ling Kun felt not the slightest pity for his granddaughter. Instead, he wanted to give her a few tight slaps. While he had intended to use this impetus to establish his authority, he wasn’t planning on things going this far. If not for his granddaughter, the situation wouldn’t have turned awry.","Chu Feng constructed a formation shaped like a chair and sat Baobao down on it. It reconstructed her body and erased her pain, allowing her to regain consciousness.","“Give me a while,” Chu Feng told Jie Baobao gently.","He glared at Ling Kun and his granddaughter. “Come here.”","He raised his palm and pulled the two of them up to him. Then, he grabbed the hair of Ling Kun’s granddaughter, dragged her up to Jie Baobao, and mercilessly slammed her head against the ground. With just a few hits, her face was covered in blood, and she was disfigured.","She screamed in agony, her teeth shattered.","But Chu Feng didn’t stop. Instead, he stomped his foot on her.","Pah!","A hole was stomped into her body.","Then, Chu Feng turned his cold gaze upon Ling Kun.","Ling Kun realized that his death was inevitable. Since there was no way to survive this ordeal, he would rather die with gusto... or at least that was what he thought till he was faced with Chu Feng’s gaze.","Chu Feng’s eyes carried such overwhelming murderous intent that Ling Kun couldn’t even utter any words of bravado. Instead, his legs caved in, and he kneeled on the ground.","“Chu Feng, I didn’t know. I really didn’t know that you knew Jie Baobao. I was only planning to use her to establish my authority. I didn’t expect things to turn out like that. I swear that I would have never dared to do this if I knew you two knew each other...” Ling Kun tried to explain.","But Chu Feng stomped his arm into the dirt and trampled it into bits. He did the same for the other arm, followed by his legs.","He grabbed Jie Baobao’s severed arm up to Ling Kun and sneered, “You want to see what’s inside her hand, don’t you?”","“No no no, I don’t want to... No no no...” Ling Kun was so terrified that he couldn’t even speak coherently anymore. He had a feeling that he was about to experience something far worse.","GAH!","Blood spurted, and Ling Kun’s scream shook the sky.","Chu Feng had pierced both of his eyes, but he didn’t stop there. He continued stabbing Ling Kun’s body. Amid splattering blood, Ling Kun’s body was reduced to a state even worse than Jie Baobao’s.","But Chu Feng didn’t deal the final blow to Ling Kun, even though the latter’s death was already inevitable. He wanted Ling Kun to suffer the maximum pain before his death.","“Stop, stop!” someone in the crowd shouted.","Watching Chu Feng’s cruelty terrified the crowd. They thought that they would face the same plight as well, and that completely crushed their will.","“Please spare us, Chu Feng. We were forced to do it!”","Some started begging for mercy. More followed suit. It reached a point where practically everyone was kneeling on the ground.","It was truly an irony. It was just moments ago that they were torturing Jie Baobao for colluding with him, but now, they were begging him for mercy.","Chu Feng swung his Monster Slayer Sword.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","His blade danced among the crowd. Amid cold gleams, blood suffused the air.","By the time the Monster Slayer Sword returned to Chu Feng’s grasp, the world had fallen silent. The crowd was still alive, but they clutched their blood-filled mouths while rolling on the ground in pain."]},{"number":6603,"title":"Chapter 6603: Chapter 6601: Jie Baobao’s Treasure","paragraphs":["Chapter 6601: Jie Baobao’s Treasure","Chu Feng walked up to Jie Baobao with a grim expression. The body he had just reconstructed for her was disintegrating.","“Release your formation, or else you won’t be able to recover,” Chu Feng held Jie Baobao’s severed arm up to her as he said.","He was planning to reattach her severed arm, but he couldn’t do so while her formation was still active. To make things worse, the formation was accelerating the depletion of her life force.","But Jie Baobao hesitated.","“What’s in your hand? Is it more important than your life?” Chu Feng asked. He was curious to know what Jie Baobao cherished so much that she would rather die than show it to others.","“They want me dead whether I show it to them or not, so I’d rather not show them. I know my condition the best. I won’t be able to live even if I release the formation. But...”","Jie Baobao’s head had been lowered thus far, but as if having made up her mind, she raised her head to look at Chu Feng and smiled. “I am happy to have met you.”","“It’s my fault. I arrived late,” Chu Feng said, even though his arrival was only a coincidence. However, if he had arrived earlier, she wouldn’t have landed in such a plight.","His words only deepened Jie Baobao’s smile.","“I used to think that it would be great if our Mansion Master accepted a talent like you. You would have been able to fulfill your potential and rise to great heights. Now, I know I was wrong. It’s a good thing you weren’t born in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion isn’t worthy of you.”","Jie Baobao’s voice grew increasingly weaker as she spoke, but her smile further deepened.","“Why are you so foolish? Even if you don’t want to show them your treasure, you could have just made some casual remarks about me, and they wouldn’t have a reason to hurt you. Is it worth throwing away your life to protect me?” Chu Feng asked.","He knew that Jie Baobao was siding with him out of loyalty, but he wasn’t so inflexible as to sever a friendship just because his friend said something bad about him to survive. The last thing he wanted was for his friends to die for his sake.","But Jie Baobao replied, “It’s worth it.”","Her answer was so resolute that it put Chu Feng at a loss.","“Chu Feng, there is one thing that I dearly regret.”","“What is it?”","“My mother was afflicted with a lethal poison while having me. I was also affected by it, and I should have died. It was your mother, Lord Jie Ranqing, who ignored the advice of others and used a valuable treasure to save my life. She was the reason I was born in this world.","“That was why my parents named me ‘Jie Bao[1]’. They wanted me to remember Lord Jie Ranqing’s grace, be loyal to her, and repay the debt to her in the future. But I was young and rebellious. I thought the name sounded awful, so I changed it to Jie Baobao.","“Now that I think about it, ‘Jie Bao’ actually sounds...”","Chu Feng interjected, “It sounds awful.”","Jie Baobao burst into laughter, but her eyes quickly became moist. Tears streamed down her cheeks. “I have let Lord Jie Ranqing down. I wasn’t able to serve her, and I couldn’t protect you, either. But I’m glad that I went to the Nine Heavens’ Zenith. That is my most cherished memory. Chu Feng, I am very happy to have met you...”","With that, she depleted her final bit of strength and fell into Chu Feng’s embrace. She had stopped breathing. As her life force receded, the fingers of her severed arms finally unraveled.","Even the members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion endured the excruciating pain they were under to look over. What they saw shocked them.","It wasn’t any special treasure or indecent object. Five pebbles rolled down her palm.","Those from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were baffled. They thought that it would be an invaluable treasure, even if it had nothing to do with Chu Feng, but who could have thought that it would be five ordinary pebbles?","But Chu Feng stiffened up. He recognized the pebbles. These were the cultivation resources he had acquired together with Jie Baobao. There were a total of ten of them, and he had split them with Jie Baobao.","The energy previously harnessed in these pebbles had been absorbed, making them nothing more than accessories now.","To think that this was the treasure Jie Baobao cherished!","Chu Feng was no fool. He immediately understood what was going on.","“You people really deserve to die,” Chu Feng murmured as he cast a frigid gaze at the crowd.","In an instant, he constructed a massive formation that made the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members turn pale in fright. As world spiritists, they could tell that it was a refinement formation.","Chu Feng was planning to turn them into cultivation resources!","The crowd wanted to flee, but they were unable to struggle free from Little Fishy’s oppressive might. They couldn’t escape at all.","At Chu Feng’s will, they fell into the refinement formation as if ingredients being poured into a pot. They shrieked in agony as their bodies disintegrated and their souls vaporized.","But Chu Feng’s face remained cold.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had already made multiple attempts on his life, but he had held back because of his mother. Only now did he realize that he was wrong. While there were people like Ling Xiao and Jie Baobao, they numbered in the minority.","Most people in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion didn’t deserve to live.","“Yu’er, I have to use their origin energies to save someone, so I can’t give them to you,” Chu Feng said.","“Big brother, saving someone takes priority,” Little Fishy replied.","Chu Feng channeled the energy from the refinement formation into Jie Baobao’s body, but that was far from enough to save her. He constructed another formation to properly fuse that energy with Jie Baobao.","This was a forbidden method. Even Chu Feng struggled to channel it.","Fortunately, Jie Baobao, despite having stopped breathing a moment ago, regained her breath and life force. Next, by sacrificing tens of millions of Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members, he managed to preserve Jie Baobao’s spirit power.","But Jie Baobao remained in hibernation. She was still in a fragile state.","Chu Feng wasn’t even sure if she could be saved. All he was doing was out of desperation.","“Big brother, someone is coming. It’s a huge group of people from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Ling Xiao is among them as well. Do you want to meet them?” Little Fishy asked.","“Let them come,” Chu Feng replied.","Little Fishy released her oppressive might, allowing Ling Xiao and the others to approach.","1. ’Bao (报)’ means ‘return (favor)’ ☜"]},{"number":6604,"title":"Chapter 6604: Chapter 6602: Declaration of War","paragraphs":["Chapter 6602: Declaration of War","“Chu Feng, who harmed her?” Ling Xiao asked in horror.","Chu Feng told Ling Xiao and the others what happened.","Ling Xiao and the others didn’t doubt Chu Feng’s words. Instead, they were enraged.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is rotten to the core. You did well, Chu Feng. Those people deserve death,” Ling Xiao spat.","“Yes, they deserve to die,” Chu Feng replied as he coldly eyed the people behind Ling Xiao.","Ling Xiao hurriedly clarified, “Chu Feng, they are Lord Nianqing’s subordinates. We have left the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to follow you. We were planning to meet Jie Baobao first before finding a way to contact you. We didn’t expect this to happen.”","Chu Feng would have been delighted under normal circumstances, but he was in no mood to respond to that. In his view, Jie Baobao had landed in this plight because of him. He would feel guilt-ridden if he couldn’t save her.","Seeing Chu Feng’s reaction to Jie Baobao’s plight, Ling Xiao hesitated to tell him about Jie Nianqing’s death, especially considering the infuriating circumstances surrounding her death. He was worried Chu Feng wouldn’t be able to calm down after hearing the news.","But on second thought, there was no way he could conceal such major news.","After some hesitation, Ling Xiao still spoke up in the end. “Chu Feng, there’s something I need to tell you.”","“What is it?”","“Something happened to Lord Nianqing.”","“What did you say?”","Chu Feng was stunned. Ling Xiao’s grim expression made his heart lurch.","“Chu Feng, you have to mentally prepare yourself,” Ling Xiao said.","Before Chu Feng could answer, Little Fishy descended to the ground and landed beside him. She was worried about him.","“Go ahead,” Chu Feng said.","Ling Xiao told Chu Feng about what happened to Jie Nianqing.","Chu Feng listened patiently without interjecting. His face remained impassive, and he didn’t exude killing intent, either. He waited for Ling Xiao to finish his story before asking, “Ling Xiao, is what you said true?”","“I won’t lie about such things, Chu Feng,” Ling Xiao replied.","“Young master Chu Feng, we can vouch for Ling Xiao’s words,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather added.","Chu Feng nodded. He turned to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members behind Ling Xiao and spoke with a commanding voice, “You have left the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, right? If so, take off your Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s robes and stow away your tokens.”","The crowd looked at Ling Xiao’s grandfather.","“I’ll follow young master Chu Feng from this day onward.” Ling Xiao’s grandfather declared his stance as he switched to an ordinary robe.","“We’ll follow young master Chu Feng from this day onward!” Ling Xiao and the others declared as they stowed away their tokens and switched to ordinary robes as well.","Chu Feng nodded.","He took out a white jade token. It had runes inscribed on the sides, but its center was empty. Like the Seven Realms Edict, it could transmit information across the entire world of cultivation.","He had acquired this token from the Heavensword Sacred Palace after slaughtering them.","Chu Feng inscribed words on the tokens and formed a hand seal.","The token surged into space in a white beam before abruptly exploding, unleashing a brilliant white light above the Seven Realms Galaxy. It was comparable in scale to the phenomenon invoked by Little Fishy, just that it wasn’t magnificent.","It was just a simple line of words.","“I, Chu Feng, will kill every Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s member I encounter from this day onward.”","There was no explanation. It was a simple declaration. However, it embodied the sheer wrath Chu Feng felt.","...","The words caught the attention of everyone across the world of cultivation.","Chu Feng’s unique aura was imbued in those words, and there was no way to fabricate that. Thus, no one doubted that the words were from Chu Feng. But they were still surprised by the declaration.","The grudge between Chu Feng and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was famous, but all along, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had been the one hunting Chu Feng down.","Chu Feng might have accomplished many astounding feats, but he was still lacking compared to the number one power in the world of cultivation. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had a strong foundation, and Jie Tianran was also unfathomably powerful.","Yet, Chu Feng still waged war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Was there any chance of him winning this war?","Many powers were confused, including the Netherworld Sect.","In the Undying Starfield, the Netherworld Sect’s experts stared at the Seven Realms Galaxy.","Baili Xukong sneered, “Chu Feng must be desperate. He speaks arrogantly, but does he have the strength to back his words?”","The Netherworld Sect had witnessed Jie Tianran’s capability. Yes, Chu Feng did have many tricks up his sleeve, but he stood no chance in a direct confrontation against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Not to mention that the Netherworld Sect was backing the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion now.","...","Many bizarre entities lurked in the innermost depths of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, from a giant whose head reached the clouds to an old man who was less than a meter tall. If one had to point out a similarity among them, it would be that they were all unfathomably powerful.","But all of these powerful entities were looking at a giant dragon silhouette.","“Lord Long Xie, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is going overboard. No matter what, Chu Feng is still a disciple of our Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. Are we not going to stand up for him?” the short old man asked.","“It’s not time for us to intervene yet,” Lord Long Xie replied with closed eyes, a stark contrast to the agitated crowd.","In his view, this was just a trivial issue.","...","Sikong Changsheng stood on the walls of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, looking at the humongous words Chu Feng had written above the Seven Realms Galaxy.","Rage simmered in his eyes.","A huge army stood behind him.","They comprised Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, the Totem Dragon Clansmen, the Totem Nine Daoists, Huahua, Xia Xingchen, and many others.","All of them understood that Chu Feng had just waged war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They wanted to leave this place to aid Chu Feng, but they couldn't do so at the moment.","“Milord, please let us leave.”","“Milord, we owe young hero Chu Feng our lives. We have been waiting for a chance to repay our debt. This is our chance. We can’t let him fight alone!”","The crowd spoke up.","“I haven’t received any news from Chu Feng. Until then, my job is to ensure your safety,” Sikong Changsheng replied.","All of a sudden, his eyes lit up. A group of people was making their way toward the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city.","The leader of the group shouted, “Why are you still hiding in there? It’s about time to let the world know about the Chu Clan Alliance.”","Sensing the auras of those people, the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief and the others trembled in excitement. Some even cheered aloud and began dancing in joy.","Even Sikong Changsheng was surprised. A faint smile formed on his lips.","...","In the Nine Souls Galaxy was a hidden realm that appeared to be manifested from a treasure. On the highest mountain peak, Song Changsheng was currently meditating with closed eyes.","A ten-year-old boy ran over and shouted, “Master, look at the Seven Realms Galaxy!”","Song Changsheng opened his eyes and looked over. His usually composed eyes widened in surprise. “Chu Feng, is that the decision you have made?”","“Master, why did Chu Feng suddenly wage war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion? Did something happen?” the boy asked out of curiosity.","Song Changsheng formed a hand seal to enhance his sight, sharpening his gaze to the point where it could peer through anything. He looked toward the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Jie Nianqing has emerged from her closed-door training to confront Jie Tianran. Jie Tianran sentenced Jie Nianqing to death for betraying the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and ordered his brethren to lynch her to death. In the end, he refined Jie Nianqing and his brethren into cultivation resources.”","“Jie Tianran refined his wife into a cultivation resource? He’s a monster!” The boy was horrified. He finally understood why Chu Feng was so angry. “Master, Miaomiao is on close terms with Chu Feng. She’d rush to help him if she was still around. Since Miaomiao has entered the Ninth Galaxy, should we help him on her behalf?”","“I won’t get involved in such matters,” Song Changsheng replied.","The boy was disappointed.","But what Song Changsheng said next delighted him. “But you can help him on Miaomiao’s behalf if you want.”"]},{"number":6605,"title":"Chapter 6605: Chapter 6603: The Counterattack Begins","paragraphs":["Chapter 6603: The Counterattack Begins","“Master, is that true?” the boy asked excitedly as if he wasn’t going to fight a war but to play.","“Fei, you have been with me for some time. You know me. If I ask you to help Chu Feng, you are to do as you are told. You should know that there are consequences if you do something I don’t intend for,” Song Changsheng said.","“Rest assured, master. I’ll do my best to help Chu Feng and not embarrass you,” the boy named Fei replied cheerily.","“Good.” Song Changsheng nodded.","“When do I make a move, master?” Fei asked with gleaming eyes.","“You can go now,” Song Changsheng replied.","“Awesome!” Fei jumped in excitement.","“You seem to be in a rush to leave. Is being with me so boring?”","“Of course not, master. What are you saying? I just want to help Chu Feng.”","Song Changsheng looked at Fei as if he could see through the latter. “You should first talk to Chu Feng. If he has truly made up his mind, you can do as he tells you to.”","“All right.” Fei was thrilled. “Master, you were observing the Seven Realms Galaxy earlier. Do you already know where Chu Feng is right now?”","Song Changsheng unfurled his palm, and a location talisman floated toward Fei. “I left a tracking imprint on Chu Feng at the Immemorial Cemetery. You can find him using this location talisman. However, the talisman will disintegrate when you approach him. You won’t be able to use it more than once.”","“Master, are you giving me a one-time-use talisman paper because you’re worried that I’ll harm Chu Feng? Do you still not trust me after so long?” Fei asked with an indignant tone.","“Your credibility still waits to be seen, but I didn’t design the talisman paper that way to guard against you. I just think that it isn’t wise to continue tracking him. He may understand that I’m doing this with good intentions this time, but he might not think that way if I persistently track his whereabouts,” Song Changsheng replied.","Fei took his leave. Holding the talisman paper, he boarded a golden flying ship and made his way toward Chu Feng.","...","The Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader used the method Chu Feng had imparted to her and successfully extracted God’s Era’s power fragment.","Surprisingly, there were no Seven Realms Sacred Mansion members in the realm.","Chu Feng had picked out several realms for her and the lunatic to visit, but the guild leader chose to go for realms where the power fragments were more scattered.","The scattered power fragments made the extraction much more troublesome, but it also made it harder for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to detect them as well. This allowed her to avoid confrontation with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","At present, she stared at the words Chu Feng had written with a tight frown. Her instincts told her that something had happened.","So, after extracting the power fragments from this realm, she made her way toward one of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s territories. She first disguised herself before slaughtering her way in.","She was an unstoppable force, being a rank two Heavenly God. It didn’t take her long to subdue the rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist in charge of this territory.","“What did the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion do to Chu Feng this time?” the guild leader asked.","“Chu Feng? I-I know that our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has been after his life all this while, but I’m not involved in it!” the elder exclaimed fearfully. It didn’t seem like he knew what had happened.","The guild leader tried probing a bit more, but she didn’t receive the answer she wanted. She knew that something must have happened to trigger such a violent response from Chu Feng.","All of the world spiritists in the realm trembled in fear. They looked at the words in the sky, followed by the guild leader. It was clear that the guild leader was on close terms with Chu Feng. They felt like their lives were in danger.","But the guild leader stood up and left without dealing with them. Just as everyone thought she would leave like that, she turned around and faced the crowd.","“Chu Feng doesn’t make empty threats. If you don’t want to die, take off your robes and leave the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. If you have made up your mind to tie your fate to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion... you'd better be prepared to lose your life at any moment.","“I’ll spare you this time, but it won’t be the same next time,” the guild leader said before leaving.","...","Meanwhile, the lunatic stepped out from a teleportation passageway into a new realm.","“Who dares to barge into our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s turf?”","As soon as she stepped out of the teleportation formation, she was surrounded by a group of world spiritists. Unlike the guild leader, she didn’t fear the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, so she went for the closest realms with a power fragment instead.","This time, she even used a Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s teleportation formation.","How could the proud Seven Realms Sacred Mansion tolerate an outsider using their teleportation formation like that? The world spiritists guarding the teleportation formation wouldn’t let someone who undermined their authority get away scot-free.","Before the lunatic could answer, she was already bombarded by multiple formations, some of them harnessing devastating prowess that could easily kill a pinnacle True God level cultivator.","However, these attacks froze in mid-air before they could reach the lunatic.","“She’s a Heavenly God! Inform the elder!”","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members scattered in a panic. A Heavenly God was beyond their means to deal with.","But the lunatic didn’t pursue them. Her attention was drawn to Chu Feng’s words in the sky.","Soon, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members returned with an army of tens of thousands. They were led by three rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists among them.","“The lunatic?”","The three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists were surprised. They had heard a lot about the lunatic and her fearless deeds. However, they also breathed a sigh of relief, knowing that there was no deep grudge between the lunatic and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","One of the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists stepped forward and said, “There should be no grudge between our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and you. May I know what you are doing here?”","A cold gleam flashed across the lunatic’s eyes.","She drew two God Armaments, and before anyone could react, she had already unleashed a barrage of sword beams that gushed through the vast territory. By the time her attack receded, everything was already reduced to ruins.","There was not a single survivor, except for the lunatic.","She nonchalantly searched for the power fragment and began extracting it. While she had never been one to shy away from force, she wouldn’t kill people just for the sake of it, either.","But when she saw Chu Feng’s message in the sky, she changed her mind.","From now on, she would tear anyone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to shreds. She ended up being the first one to lead the counterattack."]},{"number":6606,"title":"Chapter 6606: Chapter 6604: Unwavering Killing Intent","paragraphs":["Chapter 6604: Unwavering Killing Intent","Chu Feng didn’t make a move right away despite having declared war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. He was busy treating Jie Baobao’s life, trying his best to stabilize her vitals.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists offered suggestions, but none of their ideas were helpful.","“Chu Feng, are you able to stabilize Jie Baobao’s condition?” Eggy asked.","“It’s harder than I thought. I don’t know how long she can last at this rate,” Chu Feng replied.","He understood why Eggy was asking that question. She was worried that he would miss out on the power fragments scattered around the Seven Realms Galaxy while treating Jie Baobao. In other words, she was urging him to get moving.","“It won’t do for you to be stuck here. Since you have preserved her life by sacrificing the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members, why don’t you continue doing that? Those people deserve to die anyway. Her condition might be stabilized if you offer all their lives to her,” Eggy proposed.","Chu Feng’s eyes lit up. “That might work.”","He quickly constructed a recovery formation to stabilize Jie Baobao’s condition as much as possible. Then, he stood up and looked at Ling Xiao and the others. “Do you intend to follow me from now on?”","“Young master Chu Feng, we’ll follow your commands.”","“Let me get this clear first. I don’t need you to deal with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion on my behalf, but I won’t tolerate you obstructing me, either. I won’t hold back against any of you,” Chu Feng said.","“Don’t worry, Chu Feng. We have already resolved ourselves,” Ling Xiao replied.","“All right.” Chu Feng nodded.","In truth, Ling Xiao was the only one he trusted in this group.","“Chu Feng, where do you intend to head next?” Ling Xiao asked.","They already knew that Chu Feng had come to the Seven Realms Galaxy to collect the scattered fragments of God’s Era’s power. Since Chu Feng had already extracted the power fragment in this realm, he should be heading off to another realm next.","“I’m heading here.” Chu Feng took out a map.","“We can travel via the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s internal teleportation formations. It should be much faster that way.”","Chu Feng boarded the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s specially-crafted warship, and the group made their way toward a Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s teleportation formation. Using special hand seals and tokens, their traveling speed was faster than that of the bamboo boat.","Along the way, Chu Feng continued inspecting Jie Baobao’s condition.","“Chu Feng, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has a recovery formation left by our ancestors. Those are built using Ancient Era’s treasures, and they are so potent that they only stop short of reviving the dead. It’s just that the price of invoking that formation is so exorbitant that we don’t do it unless desperate. It has been a long time since it was last activated,” Ling Xiao said.","“Is that formation in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s headquarters?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes. It might be hard for us to sneak in since Jie Tianran is there right now,” Ling Xiao replied.","“Will you be able to take me there if Jie Tianran leaves?” Chu Feng asked.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had formidable defensive formations. Even if Jie Tianran was not around, it still wouldn’t be easy for them to access the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s facilities.","But Ling Xiao and the others were from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They might be privy to secret routes that outsiders didn’t know about.","But Ling Xiao shook his head and replied, “Jie Tianran has reconstructed the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s defensive formations. We won’t be able to get past his formations unless we defeat him.”","“I’ll defeat him,” Chu Feng declared.","Some time later, they arrived at their destination.","Ling Xiao and the others didn’t alight from the warship as they knew that Chu Feng was going to massacre everyone. While they had decided not to stop Chu Feng, they still couldn’t bear to see their brethren being massacred.","The only ones who stepped out were Chu Feng and Little Fishy.","“Chu Feng?”","The members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion stationed in the realm were astounded. They didn’t hesitate to attack Chu Feng, deploying a lethal offensive formation right away. They weren’t about to hold back here.","These small fry couldn’t possibly have been a match for Chu Feng. He massacred them easily with a wave of his hands.","News quickly spread. The other members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion learned that Chu Feng was in this realm, and reinforcements arrived in droves. Instead of fleeing, the elites stationed in this realm rushed over to encircle him.","In a matter of moments, the earth and the sky were completely covered by Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members.","Their leader was a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist elder.","He had been at the Undying Starfield as well and was aware of Chu Feng’s feats. He had also witnessed the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s phenomenon, and he knew about the deaths of the world spiritists they had deployed to the Immortal Sea Galaxy.","“Chu Feng and Xianhai Yu’er? I didn’t expect you two to deliver yourselves to us.”","The elder glared at Chu Feng and Little Fishy murderously. He pointed his finger at the duo, and countless formation swords rained on them.","These swords harnessed tremendous power. If struck, Chu Feng would be crippled, if not dead.","The other Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members surrounding Chu Feng and Little Fishy were thrilled. Vicious glints glimmered in their eyes. If they could capture the duo here, it would be a huge merit. They would be handsomely rewarded even just for their participation.","This was a fortuitous encounter for them.","Pu!","Just then, blood suddenly gushed from the elder’s neck. Before the crowd could process what was going on. The rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist had already been decapitated.","Horrified, the crowd turned to look at Chu Feng and Little Fishy. They had already neutralized the rain of formation swords and were unharmed.","But what scared them even more was the powerful auras coming from Chu Feng and Little Fishy. They were the auras of Heavenly Gods!","Little Fishy’s aura was stronger, but Chu Feng’s aura sent shivers down their spine. They instinctively realized that Chu Feng’s previous declaration was not empty words; he really intended to go on a massacre.","“Damn it!”","That realization stripped them of their earlier arrogance, and they turned tail and fled.","Cold gleams flashed across the air as sword beams ravaged the crowd, slicing through their bodies. Blood rained from the sky as the crowd wailed in agony. They were scared out of their wits, but at the same time, they couldn’t help but wonder why Chu Feng didn’t just kill them.","Is he showing mercy to us? Or does he just want to torture us?","Weng!","A brilliant light shone.","The crowd turned pale in fright. They could tell that it was a formation. To be exact, it was a refinement formation. They finally understood why Chu Feng didn’t kill them right away. He was planning to refine them till their deaths!","“Spare me, Chu Feng! Please don’t kill me!”","“We have no grudge against you. We were just following orders. We had no choice but to do what we did!”","“Chu Feng, we have families as well. We’re all doing this to survive. Please give us a chance!”","The crowd pleaded desperately, but Chu Feng unhesitantly tossed them into the refinement formation. Their screams crescendoed, but Chu Feng’s expression remained impassive. From the start to the end, he didn’t utter a single word at all.","His mind was made up."]},{"number":6607,"title":"Chapter 6607: Chapter 6605: You Had Your Chance","paragraphs":["Chapter 6605: You Had Your Chance","Chu Feng’s massacre didn’t stop there. He was going to make every single person who was wearing the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s robes in this realm into Jie Baobao’s tribute.","By the time Ling Xiao and the others stepped out of the warship, the previously vibrant realm had already turned into a hellscape. Buildings had collapsed, and rivers of blood flowed through the earth.","There were no corpses, however. Chu Feng had refined and assimilated them into the recovery formation.","“It’s working, Eggy. Jie Baobao’s condition has stabilized a little,” Chu Feng said.","“That’s good. Those dog things from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion should have died a long time ago. The least they could do is to redeem themselves a bit by helping Jie Baobao,” Eggy said.","“They do deserve to die,” Chu Feng replied with cold eyes.","Jie Tianran had tried to kill him time and time again, but so far, Chu Feng had limited his vengeance to just Jie Tianran and hadn’t implicated anyone else from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","He did that out of consideration for his mother and grandmother. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was their home, after all.","But knowing that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had turned against and harmed not just his mother but his grandmother as well, there was no reason for him to hold back anymore. All he wanted now was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to pay its blood debt.","After stabilizing Jie Baobao’s condition, Chu Feng extracted the power fragment from this realm and prepared to head to the next destination.","Just then, he noticed several people standing not far away, looking at him intently. These were the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members who had relinquished their identity to follow him. They had been waiting for him to be done so that they could talk.","“Do you need something from me?” Chu Feng asked.","An old woman stepped forward and asked, “Young master Chu Feng, do you intend to kill all the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members you meet from now onward?”","“Do you intend to stop me?”","“I dare not. But young master Chu Feng, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion might have changed, but not all of them are bad people. Won’t you consider giving them a chance? We can ask them if they are willing to take off their robes and leave the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, just like us.”","“I have already given them a chance.”","The old woman and the others were confused by the remark. There had been many conflicts between Chu Feng and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to date, but this was the first time Chu Feng was officially waging war on them.","Noticing their confusion, Chu Feng continued, “I have made it clear that I’ll be going after all Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members, and this is not my first time making this declaration. They chose to keep their robes on and remain loyal to Jie Tianran. Since their allegiance lies with someone who has no qualms about hurting me, my family, and my friends, why should I spare them?”","“But...” the old woman tried to argue.","“No buts.”","Ling Xiao’s grandfather walked over with the others who had left the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. As much as he wanted to protect his brethren, he had to agree with Chu Feng as well.","Under Jie Tianran’s tyranny, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members had lynched even Jie Nianqing, someone who had contributed greatly to the Sacred Mansion. There was no way they would hesitate to hurt Chu Feng and his friends.","As long as those people stayed in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, they were destined to become Chu Feng’s enemies. There was no in-between.","Yes, leaving the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was not an easy decision—Ling Xiao’s grandfather and the others had hesitated a long time before making up their minds—but Chu Feng was not obliged to give them the time to think things through.","Chu Feng had already suffered a lot because of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","It would have been hypocritical of them to ask Chu Feng to think on their behalf and expect him to show leniency right now when none of them had done the same before.","“Young master Chu Feng, I’m deeply apologetic for all the suffering we have put you through. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has no right to expect mercy from you. We’ll support you no matter what you do.” Ling Xiao’s grandfather and the others bowed deeply to Chu Feng.","The old woman’s group lowered their heads in shame. They should have been here to support Chu Feng, but they were lacking in resolve and ended up standing in his way instead.","“I understand where you are coming from. You’re probably thinking we should punish the culprit and not implicate the innocent, but the world is not that simple. I might not have spoken clearly enough, so let me clear things up for you right now.","“If you truly intend to follow me and avenge my grandmother, you can be assured that I’ll be your most stalwart ally. But if you have chosen my side, you should harden your resolve. I won’t tolerate anyone betraying me, and that includes standing in my way,” Chu Feng said.","A frigid wind raged, and the atmosphere suddenly turned cold. The threat behind his words couldn’t be clearer.","The old woman fell to her knees and said, “Young master Chu Feng, I agree that Jie Tianran and the others who harmed Lord Jie Nianqing deserve death. As for the others... Haaa. I know I shouldn’t, but I have been a member of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion for thousands of years now. I can’t bear to witness the deaths of my brethren.”","Several others from the old woman’s group kneeled as well.","They had made their stances clear. They couldn’t accept Chu Feng’s doing.","“I don’t blame you. Just don’t let me catch you in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s robes,” Chu Feng said.","In other words, he wouldn’t spare them either if they returned to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Those who didn’t kneel in the old woman’s group rejoined Chu Feng’s group. This time, they had hardened their resolve."]},{"number":6608,"title":"Chapter 6608: Chapter 6606: Wen Xue’s Motive","paragraphs":["Chapter 6606: Wen Xue’s Motive","Deep in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect was a peach-blossom forest. At the center of the peach blossom forest was a lake. It was a small lake, but it was so clear that one could see its bottom. Its water reflected the vibrant beauty of the peach blossom flowers.","Two women strolled by the lake. Despite their high cultivation, they moved slowly as if mortals admiring the scenery. They were the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster and her disciple, Wen Xue.","“Are you planning to leave?” the sectmaster asked.","“That’s right. I don’t know when I’ll see you again. Master, are you really not going to enter the Ninth Galaxy together with me?” Wen Xue asked.","“I am the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster. This is where my responsibilities lie. I have to stay here. Wen Xue, something must have happened for Chu Feng to suddenly declare war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Aren’t you going to help him?” the sectmaster asked.","She wasn't intending to raise this topic as she wanted to respect Wen Xue's will, but at the same time, she was worried about Chu Feng. She was unable to help Chu Feng due to her limited strength, so after much hesitation, she still decided to broach the topic.","“Master, I know you’re worried about Junior Chu Feng, but you can put your mind at ease. My junior has many tricks up his sleeve. I would have been in hot water in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s remnant if not for him,” Wen Xue replied.","The sectmaster was disappointed.","Three prodigies stood out among the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s juniors—Chu Feng, Zi Ling, and Wen Xue. Their talent outshone even Dugu Lingtian. They were destined for great things.","She had hoped that the three of them could stand on the same front, but she also understood that such things couldn’t be forced, so she didn’t harp on it.","“When do you intend to make a move?” the sectmaster asked.","“I returned today to bid you farewell, master. I’m prepared to head there,” Wen Xue replied.","The sectmaster frowned.","“What’s wrong, master? Do you want me to help Junior Chu Feng first before entering the Ninth Galaxy?” Wen Xue asked.","But the sectmaster shook her head and replied, “I do hope that you would help Chu Feng, but the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is an enigmatic entity. I understand that you may have your reservations, and I respect your decision.","“From the first time I saw you, I could tell you’re destined for greater things. However, you are also unruly and unscrupulous. If left be, you could have become a monster who would resort to anything to get her way. I took you in as my disciple in hopes of leading you onto the right path. You have long surpassed me, but you still treat me with respect. I am heartened by that.”","There was a long pause before Wen Xue replied, “Master, I might be cultivating from scratch, but I retain my memories. I am not a child. I was indignant when you first took me in as your disciple, and I thought of many ways to get back at you. But I soon realized that you are doing this with my welfare at heart.","“You reminded me of my old master back when I was young. My old master was not powerful, but she was a good person, just like you. But she was killed by a villain, and that was what led me down the demonic path. You reminded me of those old times.","“I earnestly enjoyed my time with you, and I’ll never forget it. No matter how strong I become, you’ll always be my master. This is a token of my appreciation. Please accept it.”","Wen Xue kneeled to the sectmaster and presented a Cosmos Sack to her.","However, the sectmaster didn’t take the Cosmos Sack. Instead, she asked, “Wen Xue, do you mean what you said?”","“There is no falsehood in my words,” Wen Xue replied.","“If so, I won’t accept your token of appreciation. Instead, I want you to return Yaoyao[1],” the sectmaster said.","Wen Xue narrowed her eyes. “Master, you...”","“My strength is limited, but we are in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. You’re looking down on me if you think that you can kidnap our people without me noticing. Wen Xue, Yaoyao has been grumbling about wanting to meet Chu Feng ever since she came out of closed-door training.","“I thought that you were bringing her to meet Chu Feng, and you kept it from me because you were worried that I’d object to it. I can see now that you have other motives. If you leave Yaoyao now, I won’t pursue this matter, and we can remain master and disciple. Otherwise, don’t blame me for turning against you.”","As she spoke, the sectmaster took out her Sect Master Token.","“Master, Yaoyao is a world spirit. Junior Chu Feng already has a stronger world spirit, not to mention that Yaoyao’s father, the Asura King, and his army have already pledged allegiance to him. No matter how capable Chu Feng is, he can only gather that many resources for nurturing a world spirit. He won’t be able to prioritize Yaoyao, and that will limit her growth.","“However, things will be different if she follows me. I can bring Yaoyao into the Ninth Galaxy together with me. I’ll take the bloodlines, and she can monopolize the origin energies. She can grow at an unprecedented pace and surpass Junior Chu Feng with ease.","“By then, if Yaoyao still wants to look for Junior Chu Feng, she’ll be more than capable of helping him,” Wen Xue replied.","“What grandiose words. Are you certain that you’ll be willing to let Yaoyao go if she insists on going to Chu Feng?” the sectmaster asked.","“Of course. I’ll respect Yaoyao’s will.”","“What about now? Did Yaoyao voluntarily choose to leave with you? Let me hear it from her directly. If she says that she’s willing to leave with you, I’ll have nothing to say.”","“Master, Yaoyao is still young. She’ll know that I have her best intentions in mind when she grows up.”","The sectmaster laughed, but her voice loomed with helplessness and disappointment. “You didn’t return to the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect to visit me. You merely wanted to take Yaoyao away with you.”","1. Yaoyao is a child sealed inside a box from the Asura Graveyard. Chu Feng brought her out of the Asura Graveyard, and when her seal broke, he named her Yaoyao. ☜"]},{"number":6609,"title":"Chapter 6609: Chapter 6607: Biased","paragraphs":["Chapter 6607: Biased","The world trembled. Tremendous energy converged to form a humongous formation that sealed off their surroundings.","The Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster had channeled her token to construct a sealing formation that harnessed power comparable to a rank one Heavenly God.","But Wen Xue wasn’t flustered.","“Master, I have returned to visit you. It’s a coincidence that Yaoyao emerged from her closed-door training at the same time. I noticed her world spirit traits and thought that normal cultivation would hinder her progress. It is more beneficial for her to come with me. I can collect a huge amount of origin energies for her and unleash her true potential,” Wen Xue replied.","“Wen Xue, you still refuse to speak the truth. Do I have to force you to do so?” the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster asked. She didn’t believe Wen Xue in the least.","Wen Xue kneeled on the floor, placed the Cosmos Sack on the ground, and bowed. “Master, I am unfilial, but no matter what, I still view you as my master. Wen Xue shall be my name from now on. I will not change my name.”","With that, she kowtowed as a show of deep respect.","Then, there was a loud explosion. The sealing formation shattered, and Wen Xue vanished into thin air, leaving behind only her Cosmos Sack.","“...”","The sectmaster raised her head and looked at the shattered formation with conflicted emotions. Only now did she realize that Wen Xue had reached Heavenly God. That explained her fearless attitude. The sealing formation couldn’t have trapped Wen Xue in.","Meanwhile, Wen Xue was surging through space when she noticed that she was swiftly decelerating. It came to a point where her body felt as heavy as lead, and she plummeted from the sky.","“Wen Xue, have you forgotten that I am in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect as well?”","An old man with the face of a monstrous beast quietly appeared before Wen Xue. He had praying beads in his hand.","“Milord, I can never forget about your existence. I’d never have reached my current level of accomplishment if not for your nurturing.” Wen Xue sweated profusely at the sight of the monstrous old man.","Despite her current strength, she was still unable to peer into the bottom of the monstrous old man’s strength. She was certain that it was not just a gap in terms of ranks; this monstrous old man was most definitely at a different cultivation level.","“You remember Lord Long Xie and me, but you still dare to take Yaoyao away with you?”","“Milord, have you forgotten? I have tried to reach out to you, but you didn’t appear,” Wen Xue explained.","The monstrous old man frowned as such a thing did happen. “You wanted to meet us to talk about Yaoyao?”","“That’s right. I wanted to discuss the matters with milords because my master listens to you. I had no choice but to resort to this because you refused to meet me. I mean the words that I said to my master. I am really doing this with Yaoyao’s welfare in mind,” Wen Xue explained.","“Release Yaoyao first,” the monstrous old man said.","Wen Xue did as she was told. She formed a hand seal, and a treasure resembling a seashell appeared.","The seashell was transparent, and a girl was sleeping inside—Yaoyao.","Yaoyao had grown considerably compared to before. She looked to be around six years old, and her features had become more delicate. One could already tell that she was a beauty in the making.","Her true age was not even six yet. For some reason, she was growing beyond her age.","But that was not important, for Yaoyao was a special entity. She was an asura world spirit, though nothing about her suggested that. She could cultivate normally in this world just like any other cultivator.","“Is Yaoyao willing to leave with you?” the monstrous old man asked.","“I wouldn’t have to resort to this if she were willing,” Wen Xue replied with an awkward smile.","“You can take her away by force, but you can’t keep imprisoning her like that. Do you think this lass will listen to you?”","“I’ll slowly talk sense into her. Don’t worry, milord. I won’t use forceful methods on Yaoyao. I’ve watched her grow from a young age. I can’t bear to hurt her, either.”","The monstrous old man waved his praying beads, forcing the seashell open.","The sleeping Yaoyao floated out from the seashell. The monstrous old man gently tapped her forehead, and her eyes finally fluttered open.","Upon waking up, Yaoyao immediately ran up to the monstrous old man and hid behind him. She pointed to Wen Xue and exclaimed, “Grandpa Monster, Wen Xue bullied me!”","“Yaoyao, how did she bully you?” the monstrous old man asked.","“She said that she wants to take me to the Ninth Galaxy. I don’t want to go there! I wanted to find daddy, but she stuffed me in that seashell!” Yaoyao cried with puffed-up cheeks.","“Yaoyao, your daddy is in huge trouble right now. Do you want to help him?” the monstrous old man asked.","Yaoyao widened her eyes, and her pupils swam around in a fluster. “Grandpa Monster, what happened to my daddy? I want to help my daddy.”","“Your daddy can still handle things on this side, but he’ll need as much help as he can get when he steps into the Ninth Galaxy. With your current strength, you won’t be able to help your daddy whether you continue staying in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect or look for him now. Instead, you can grow faster if you leave with Wen Xue. Only then will you be able to help your daddy in the future,” the monstrous old man said.","“See, Yaoyao. Even milord has said that. You can’t say that I’m lying to you anymore, right?” Wen Xue added.","“Then... when can I see daddy?” Yaoyao asked.","“I can’t give you a date, but you’ll eventually cross paths with him. Do you want your daddy to protect you then, or do you want to be the one to protect your daddy?” the monstrous old man asked.","“I want to protect daddy!” Yaoyao spoke firmly.","“Then you should go with Wen Xue. She’ll help you grow fast,” the monstrous old man said.","“All right.” Yaoyao nodded. She didn’t trust Wen Xue, but she trusted the monstrous old man.","Yaoyao was extremely favored by the powerful entities in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. She often even met Long Xie, let alone the others. Without a doubt, she was the most doted member here.","“Wen Xue, I’ll be entrusting Yaoyao to you, but I’m still worried about this. So, I’ll be binding the two of you with a formation.”","The monstrous old man pulled out a formation chain that emanated an ancient aura. He placed one end of the chain into Yaoyao’s body and the other end into Wen Xue’s body.","“Shit!” Wen Xue’s face distorted from extreme pain.","Yaoyao frowned at that sight, but her expression soon loosened up when she realized she was not in pain. She placed a hand on her hip and pointed a finger at Wen Xue, saying, “Stop acting, Wen Xue. It doesn’t hurt at all.”","Confused, Wen Xue looked at the monstrous old man.","“Milord, you’re biased! If there’s a way to alleviate the pain, why didn’t you use it on me as well? I’m also a member of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect as well, just like Yaoyao,” Wen Xue cried in indignation.","“I’m not the one behind it; it’s the effect of this formation. This formation ties the two of you together, but your relationship is not equal,” the monstrous old man replied.","“What do you mean?” Wen Xue replied vigilantly.","“Your life will be bound to Yaoyao’s from now on. Your death will not affect Yaoyao in any way, but if Yaoyao dies, you’ll die along with her. Even if Yaoyao gets injured, you’ll suffer the same pain,” the monstrous old man said.","“What?” Wen Xue’s mouth opened wide. She felt indignant, shocked, uneasy, and fearful. “Milord, I was wrong. I’ll leave Yaoyao behind and leave by myself, all right?”","She anxiously waved her hand to sever the chain, but she was unable to touch it. To make things worse, the chain was turning invisible.","“There’s no way to undo the formation. Wen Xue, I’ll be entrusting Yaoyao to you. Bear this in mind—Yaoyao’s life is far more valuable than yours,” the monstrous old man said with a sly grin.","Wen Xue dropped to her bum and wailed pitifully. “This is too much! We’re both members of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, so why is there such a huge disparity in our treatment?”","But the monstrous old man was unfazed. He waved his hand and said, “You can go now.”","Both Wen Xue and Yaoyao were transported out of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect."]},{"number":6610,"title":"Chapter 6610: Chapter 6608: The Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s Means","paragraphs":["Chapter 6608: The Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s Means","The Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster lowered her head in shame, feeling self-reproach for not being able to rescue Yaoyao. She didn’t chase Wen Xue, knowing that she was nowhere strong enough to catch up with her.","“Don’t worry about Yaoyao.”","The monstrous old man suddenly appeared beside the sectmaster.","“Milord?”","The sectmaster was shocked. This was her first time seeing the monstrous old man outside of that secret realm. She quickly snapped out of her daze and bowed to the monstrous old man. While she was the sectmaster, she knew that she was not the true master of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect.","“I have met Wen Xue. You can rest easy. Yaoyao will be fine,” the monstrous old man said.","The sectmaster breathed a sigh of relief. She knew that no matter how powerful Wen Xue was, there was no way she could be a match for the monstrous old man.","“I’m sure Yaoyao will be fine if milord has made a move,” the sectmaster replied.","“Did you feel powerless?” the monstrous old man suddenly asked.","The sectmaster was startled by the question, but she quickly answered, “Yes. I feel powerless for being unable to protect my sectmember.”","The monstrous old man looked at the sectmaster with a sympathetic gaze. “You should meet Lord Long Xie.”","The sectmaster saw her surroundings distorting, and before she knew it, she had been transported into a boundless space. This was not her first time here. She had previously met Long Xie and the monstrous old man here.","But there were tens of thousands of other foreign figures here this time, though none of them was a human. They were all monsters like the monstrous old man.","Some were less than thirty centimeters tall, but their eyes harnessed the power of the stars. It felt like their gaze could obliterate realms.","Some towered at over hundreds of thousands of meters tall. Even the clouds drifted at their thighs. They could probably destroy a realm with a single stomp.","And there were many of such entities here. Any one of them could easily reign supreme in the world of cultivation. Yet, they were nothing compared to the humongous dragon silhouette in the sky.","The humongous dragon silhouette was none other than Lord Long Xie.","The sectmaster bowed deeply to Long Xie and greeted, “Junior pays respect to Lord Long Xie.”","Long Xie asked, “Lass, do you know why the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect was established?”","“It is to protect the Ancestral Martial Galaxy,” the sectmaster replied. That was the answer she had heard from the previous sectmaster.","But Long Xie shook his head and replied, “The current Ancestral Martial Galaxy, except for the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm, is no longer necessary. There’s no need to protect it anymore.”","The sectmaster was taken aback. She hadn’t expected to hear such a remark.","“The Hidden Dragon Martial Sect was established to nurture outstanding juniors. While it may seem like we have fallen into decline, we have raised juniors who have stood at the top of their respective generations, such as Ye Wuhen, Song Wuya, and Dugu Lingtian.","“But those people didn’t think about bulking up our Hidden Dragon Martial Sect after maturing. Instead, they sought ways to leave,” Long Xie said.","The sectmaster was confused, but she dared not probe.","“I know what you’re confused about. You must be thinking that Ye Wuhen and Song Wuya died while protecting the world of cultivation from that mysterious remnant back then,” Long Xie said.","“Is that not the case?” the sectmaster asked.","“Not at all. Those two noticed the extraordinary nature of that power and wanted to monopolize it. Their ‘sacrifice’ is merely a front to leave the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. I have to concede that we have raised two outstanding talents. Their act fooled not just Shangguan Fengquan but me as well.","“It only belatedly struck me later that they were still alive. They have grasped that power and snuck into the Ninth Galaxy,” Long Xie said.","“Why did they do that?” The sectmaster was confused. This was at odds with what she had believed in all this while. Ye Wuhen and Song Wuya had always been celebrated as heroes of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, and they were two mountains that couldn’t be surmounted.","But Long Xie returned the question to the sectmaster, “Why didn’t Dugu Lingtian stay in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect?”","The sectmaster fell silent.","Long Xie chuckled. “Everyone has their own pursuits, though Dugu Lingtian is different from those two. Ye Wuhen and Song Wuya are too ambitious; they wanted to completely shake off the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. It’s not a stretch to say that they are ungrateful scums.","“On the other hand, Dugu Lingtian cares about the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. It’s just that he couldn’t maintain his identity as a Hidden Dragon Martial Sectmember as he sought to acquire power through unorthodox methods.","“We have no lack of talented sectmembers who are worthy of becoming the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster, but the ones who remain behind are people like you. You stand your ground unwaveringly, no matter how strong or weak the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect is. It is because of your character that I revealed myself to you back then.","“You have known about me all this while, but you have never requested my help. I summoned you here today to relay a piece of good news. You have cleared my trial. The world thinks that our Hidden Dragon Martial Sect has fallen from grace, but little do they know that our foundation remains.","“I shall bestow a fortuitous encounter upon you today. The world has underestimated you, but you shall be the one to lead the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect to the heights it ought to stand at.”","The sky ripped open, and a gigantic coffin fell vertically out of the spatial rift into the ground.","The coffin was so huge that it resembled a towering mountain. The coffin creaked open, and immense energy leaked out from within.","The sectmaster widened her eyes in shock. The energy seeping out of the coffin was not just simple martial power; it was cultivation.","“Do you sense it as well? Old things like us are near our limits, but we still wish to contribute to the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect before our deaths. I have sealed the powers of my old friends, who have succumbed to the erosion of time, in this coffin. This energy can be refined and turned into cultivation for your use. As long as you do as I say, you can undergo a metamorphosis.","“This is our Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s means. Even with your limited talent, you can still rise to the forefront of the present era,” Long Xie said."]},{"number":6611,"title":"Chapter 6611: Chapter 6609: The Sectmaster’s Decision","paragraphs":["Chapter 6609: The Sectmaster’s Decision","“Milord, my talent is limited. Won’t Chu Feng or Zi Ling benefit more from this fortuitous encounter?” the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster asked.","“Zi Ling has her own fortuitous encounter. She’ll reach great heights in the future. As for Chu Feng, no one has had greater fortuitous encounters than that lad. However, he’s destined to walk a different path from the rest of you.","“He seeks to shatter past limits and surpass those who come before him. He has a chance to reach the top, where no one else has ever been. His path is destined to be tough, and he will suffer more than anyone else has. Normal people can’t hope to do it.","“I am well aware that Chu Feng will benefit more from the power in this coffin; he can even minimize or completely neutralize the side effects from taking in this power. However, resorting to such means to swiftly raise his strength will only cap his future. I’ll be harming him by giving it to him,” Long Xie replied.","“But...” the sectmaster argued.","“Lass, you don’t need to push it on to anyone else. I have already decided that I’ll bestow the power inside this coffin to you and no one else. Only someone of your character is worthy of inheriting this power. However, it will come at a price.","“First, this power will permanently reduce your lifespan. On top of that, you’ll have to take on greater responsibilities after inheriting this power,” Long Xie said.","“Milord, may I know what the responsibilities are?” the sectmaster asked.","“Wen Xue might have made the first move, but Chu Feng and Zi Ling will eventually have to enter the Ninth Galaxy as well. They have a lot of growing to do, and we won’t interfere in that. However, you can do so. You can be the one to give them a push on this arduous journey. That is the responsibility I am talking about.","“I’ll respect your decision. If you don’t want to shorten your lifespan or take on this responsibility, you are free to reject my offer. I will not make things difficult for you,” Long Xie said.","The sectmaster’s expression turned resolute, and she bowed deeply to Long Xie. “I am willing to take on this responsibility.”","Long Xie smiled as if he had expected as much. “Let’s begin your metamorphosis then.”","The coffin slowly opened. An immense flood of energy gushed out, and it would have destroyed the entire realm if not for Long Xie controlling it.","At the same time, Long Xie levitated the sectmaster into the air, toward the coffin.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng was busy gathering the God’s Era’s power fragments scattered across the Seven Realms Galaxy, while making quick work of all the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members whom he crossed paths with.","There was good news—Jie Baobao’s condition had finally stabilized. For the time being, he didn’t need to sacrifice more Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members to treat her.","It wouldn’t be wise to do this beyond what was necessary since this was a taboo method; it involved sacrificing the lives of others, after all. Assimilating too many human lives would harm Jie Baobao.","But that didn’t mean that Chu Feng was about to start sparing the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members. He continued to massacre them, claiming their lives, treasures, and origin energies.","Chu Feng did encounter enemies stronger than him along the way. In such cases, Little Fishy would make a move. If not for her protection, Chu Feng’s journey wouldn’t have been so smooth-sailing.","So, Chu Feng shared half of God’s Era’s power fragments and the collected origin energies with her.","“Big brother...”","Little Fishy was about to object when Chu Feng interjected, “Yu’er, I know that you don’t need their treasures, which is why I stowed all of them into my Cosmos Sack without asking you. I’m sharing the origin energies with you because I know you need them. You should accept them.”","“All right. I’ll listen to you, big brother,” Little Fishy replied.","Chu Feng divided the origin energies he had just collected from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members into two equal portions. He gave one half to Little Fishy and tossed the remaining into his World Spirit Space.","“Chu Feng, give these origin energies to the Asura World Spirit Army instead. I am at a critical phase of my cultivation of the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s secret skill, and taking in these origin energies right now will only impede me.","“Besides, didn’t you say that the formation gate that boosts the Asura World Spirit Army’s strength is at its limit and cannot raise their cultivation any further? You should feed them some origin energies, even if only out of consideration for Yaoyao. They aren’t able to cultivate on their own. No matter what, Asura King is Yaoyao’s father.”","Eggy made a reasonable point. Chu Feng felt so indebted to Eggy that he was inclined to give everything good he had to her, but that was unfair to the Asura World Spirit Army. Since Eggy had already said that she didn’t need those origin energies, he ought to give them to the Asura World Spirit Army instead.","“Eggy, do you really not need the origin energies?” Chu Feng asked.","“Why would I lie to you? Besides, you should know how much energy I need for my cultivation. Just this much origin energies won’t be enough for me to make a significant advancement. Give them to the Asura World Spirit Army instead,” Eggy said.","“Eggy, what’s the secret skill you’re practising?” Chu Feng asked once more.","He had known that Eggy had received a secret skill from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, but it surprised him to hear that she had to stop taking in origin energies to cultivate the secret skill. The strict requirements suggested that the secret skill must be truly formidable.","That made him even more curious to know what it was.","“It’s a secret,” Eggy replied with a sweet smile.","She went back into cultivation right after saying that. She had been cultivating harder than ever since she obtained this secret skill.","Chu Feng entered his World Spirit Space and looked at the diligently cultivating Eggy. He glanced at the scroll in front of her but was still unable to decipher its contents.","Next, he turned to the huge bundle of origin energies floating above, followed by the formation gate that isolated the Asura World Spirit Army."]},{"number":6612,"title":"Chapter 6612: Chapter 6610: Jie Tianran Emerges from Closed-door Training","paragraphs":["Chapter 6610: Jie Tianran Emerges from Closed-door Training","The Asura World Spirit Army’s gate was currently open, but the formation on it had changed.","The formation gate served as a trial.","It would automatically close after Chu Feng tapped into the Asura World Spirit Army’s strength for a specific number of times, sealing them off. He would have to decipher the formation gate to unseal them.","Each time the formation gate was unsealed, the Asura World Spirit Army would grow stronger.","But it was not easy to decipher the formation gate. That was why he had only summoned the Asura World Spirit Army when necessary back then. Otherwise, if the Asura World Spirit Army were to be sealed off, he would lose his backing for a while.","After reaching True God level, he was not as reliant on the Asura World Spirit Army anymore, which was why he began borrowing the Asura King’s strength more often. He wanted to seal the gate so that he could decipher the formation and further raise their strength.","But no matter how many times he borrowed the Asura World Spirit Army’s strength, the formation gate didn’t close. Instead, the formation began to change.","Both Eggy and the Asura World Spirit Army thought that the formation gate’s energy had been depleted. It could no longer strengthen the Asura World Spirit Army anymore.","But Chu Feng examined the formation gate and deduced that it hadn’t reached its limit yet; rather, it had to be channeled by another method, and that was to feed it origin energies. Only then would it close, giving him the chance to raise the Asura World Spirit Army’s strength again.","He had kept that news to himself because he wanted to prioritize Eggy over the Asura World Spirit Army. Now that Eggy no longer needed origin energies, it didn’t make sense for him not to use them on the Asura World Spirit Army.","So, he formed a hand seal and channeled the origin energies into the formation gate.","“No, milord. We can cultivate by ourselves. You don’t need to use your origin energies on us,” the Asura King said.","He was the leader of the Asura World Spirit Army. While he was unable to decipher the formation gate, he could tell that Chu Feng was trying to help them when he infused the origin energies into the formation gate.","However, he knew that they were lacking in talent compared to Eggy, so he didn’t want Chu Feng to squander the origin energies on them.","“You ought to listen to me since you call me your lord,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He proceeded to infuse all the origin energies into the formation gate, and the formation gate closed.","“Oh? The formation gate can still be closed, just that it has to be fed origin energies now? It must have undergone an evolution. Chu Feng, you knew about it all along, but you didn’t tell me. Looks like you’re keeping secrets from me now,” Eggy noticed the stir in her surroundings and remarked.","“The same goes for you, too.” Chu Feng eyed Eggy’s scroll.","He was still curious to know what the secret skill was.","“Hmph.” Eggy harrumphed before resuming her cultivation.","With Chu Feng’s current proficiency in world spiritist techniques, it took him only a glance to decipher the formation gate. When the formation gate opened once more, the Asura World Spirit Army underwent a metamorphosis.","“Not bad!” Eggy opened her eyes and exclaimed in surprise.","In just a jiffy, the Asura World Spirit Army had grown by leaps and bounds, with most of its members reaching late True God level. If Chu Feng continued to feed origin energies to the Asura World Spirit Army, it could potentially overtake him in due time.","Even the Asura King might reach Heavenly God before him!","By then, Chu Feng would have an army of tens of thousands of late True Gods behind him. It would be a completely different sight when he clashed with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","...","Meanwhile, several elders from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were standing around a peculiar cultivation ground located somewhere in the Seven Realms Galaxy.","Heavenly Dragon elders descended upon this cultivation ground now and then. They had received orders from Jie Tianran to collect the God’s Era’s power fragments and deliver them here.","Jie Tianran was planning to use the power fragments to activate the copper mirror. He had discovered that a special method was needed for that, which was why he had stopped collecting the power fragments in person and instead entrusted the task to the elders.","“Look, there’s a change in God’s Era!” an elder shouted.","The other elders used their observation methods to look at God’s Era. What they said brightened up their gloomy faces. The humongous silhouette behind God’s Era had become clearer and more tangible.","It was indeed the copper mirror, and a figure could be seen reflected in it.","The figure was blurry at the start, but it grew clearer until it was identifiable. It was Jie Tianran.","This was a good omen for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Lord Mansion Master has succeeded!”","The elders were overjoyed. Despite their advanced age, they threw their hands in the sky and cheered... though it looked as if they were venting their emotions as well.","Soon, a gate in the cultivation ground opened, and Jie Tianran walked out.","“Congratulations, Lord Mansion Master!”","The elders bowed to Jie Tianran as they offered their congratulations. Jie Tianran looked at the copper mirror in his hand with a gleeful smirk.","The first thing he did upon successfully activating the copper mirror was to look toward God’s Era. Naturally, he saw the copper mirror in God’s Era, as well as his reflection inside the mirror.","It seemed to signal that he was the only inheritor of God’s Era’s power.","There had been a prophecy that a junior would obtain God’s Era’s final power, but he had shattered the prophecy with his own strength.","“Lord Mansion Master, does this mean that our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion calls the shots inside God’s Era now?” an elder anxiously asked.","“Not yet, but it’s only a matter of time,” Jie Tianran replied confidently.","“Lord Mansion Master, something huge has happened while you were in closed-door training,” an elder said with a troubled expression.","The other elders looked troubled as well.","“What is it?” Jie Tianran asked, though he didn’t seem particularly interested in the matter. He couldn’t imagine anything larger than God’s Era right now.","“Chu Feng has declared war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” the elder replied."]},{"number":6613,"title":"Chapter 6613: Chapter 6611: The Netherworld Sect’s Attitude","paragraphs":["Chapter 6611: The Netherworld Sect’s Attitude","“Chu Feng?” Jie Tianran narrowed his eyes, but he didn’t look too bothered by it. He asked, “Does he already know what happened to Nianqing?”","“I’m not sure about the reason, but Ling Xiao’s clan has defected to Chu Feng’s side,” the Heavenly Dragon elder said.","“They must be tired of living.” Jie Tianran’s eyes gleamed coldly. He was more infuriated by the betrayal of Ling Xiao’s clan than Chu Feng’s declaration of war.","“Lord Mansion Master, Chu Feng has been wreaking havoc while you were in closed-door training. He has breached many of our bases, plundered God’s Era’s power fragments, and massacred all members who crossed his path. Our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has suffered heavy casualties,” the elder said.","He took out thousands of shattered life tokens to prove his point.","Jie Tianran’s eyes flared with killing intent.","He was not bothered by the casualties. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was a behemoth. He wouldn’t be bothered even if billions of his brethren died, let alone thousands. Something of this level wouldn’t hurt the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Instead, what angered him was Chu Feng challenging the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s authority. Unlike before, Chu Feng was doing it blatantly.","“Continue,” Jie Tianran said.","“It’s not just Chu Feng. He has rallied the Totem Dragon Clan and others under the Chu Clan Alliance’s banner. Almost all our bases in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy have been destroyed, except for the two guarded by our Saint-tier elders. But even those two have been encircled, and they have requested reinforcements,” the elder added.","“Does Chu Feng’s side have rank five Heavenly Gods as well?” Jie Tianran asked with a frown.","His earlier composure had slipped.","He had previously boosted the spirit power of all Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Saint-tier elders to rank five Heavenly Dragon at the expense of their lifespans. It was shocking that the two Saint-tier elders were requesting aid despite their strength.","This meant that Chu Feng had experts of the same level on his side. This complicated the situation. It meant that all their bases, except for their headquarters, were vulnerable.","“It’s the Dragon Breath Clan. I don’t know what kind of fortuitous encounter they had, but they suddenly have many Heavenly Gods in their ranks. Long Mucheng has even advanced to rank five Heavenly God level. They are the ones encircling the two Saint-tier elders.","“Moreover, the Chu Clan Alliance has been openly recruiting people to oppose us, and some brazen ones have joined them,” the elder added.","“Did you not request support from the Netherworld Sect?” Jie Tianran asked.","He had previously made the Netherworld Sect promise to come to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s aid when it required help. He had informed this elder about it in passing before going into closed-door training.","While he didn’t think that they would have to use this favor so quickly, the situation did call for it.","“Lord Mansion Master, our Saint-tier elders are preoccupied with their missions across the galaxies, so we don’t have enough experts at hand to deal with this situation. So, I boldly made the call to request help from the Netherworld Sect. However, I didn’t receive a reply from them,” the elder replied.","Jie Tianran’s face darkened. “Return to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion!”","...","Chu Feng and the others were currently traveling in a teleportation passageway, but they could see what was happening outside through special means. They noticed the change in God’s Era.","“What’s going on?”","Ling Xiao and the others looked uneasy. They thought that this was a sign that Jie Tianran had obtained an advantage from God’s Era.","“Chu Feng, can you tell what’s going on? Is that a real phenomenon from God’s Era, or is this just a farce from Jie Tianran?” Ling Xiao asked.","The others looked at Chu Feng as well.","It hadn’t been long since they had begun following Chu Feng, but his reputation was too resounding. They wouldn’t be surprised if Chu Feng could discern details that eluded their notice.","“It’s a real phenomenon. Jie Tianran doesn’t have the power to interfere with God’s Era yet,” Chu Feng replied.","“Then... what does this phenomenon mean? Does it mean that Jie Tianran has obtained God’s Era’s power?” Ling Xiao and the others looked incredibly worried.","Ever since returning from God’s Era, Jie Tianran had declared that God’s Era’s power was already in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s grasp. His confidence didn’t seem to be an act.","“Jie Tianran could have received God’s Era’s acknowledgment, but since the nature of the power remains unchanged, I don’t think he has truly obtained it yet. You don’t need to pay too much attention to this. It’s only normal that he has obtained an advantage from his previous trip into God’s Era,” Chu Feng replied.","Ling Xiao and the others breathed a sigh of relief. They trusted Chu Feng’s judgment.","...","Meanwhile, Baili Xukong and the other Netherworld Sect’s experts in the Undying Starfield also noticed the changes in God’s Era.","“Xukong, the people we dispatched to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion should be reaching soon, right?” an elder from the neutral faction asked.","“Yes, but I’m worried that we haven’t sent enough experts to support them. Milord, you should have seen the changes in God’s Era. That shows that the scales are tilting in Jie Tianran’s favor, not to mention we’re relying on him for our sacred item. And Chu Feng is our common enemy. Shouldn’t we send more people over?” Baili Xukong asked the elders of the neutral faction.","“What are your current thoughts?” another elder from the neutral faction spoke up.","“I believe Chu Feng deserves death for blaspheming our sacred item. His allies are a bunch of ragtags, so there’s no need to fear them. Furthermore, we do need Jie Tianran’s help to activate our sacred item. It’s important to make our stance clear during times like this.","“We should put our everything into supporting the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion in hunting Chu Feng, and we should make this known to the entire world so that Jie Tianran can see our sincerity. This will make our future cooperation go more smoothly,” Baili Xukong said.","“That won’t do,” an elder from the neutral faction voiced his objection.","It was Cang Li."]},{"number":6614,"title":"Chapter 6614: Chapter 6612: A Secret Skill That Ends With One’s Death","paragraphs":["Chapter 6612: A Secret Skill That Ends With One’s Death","“The intel we have received indicates that Chu Feng’s allies aren’t just a bunch of ragtags.","“The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Xianhai Yu’er has defeated Xiahou Jue, and to date, we still don’t know exactly how powerful she is. That makes her a huge variable.","“The Dragon Breath Clan used to be a minor clan selling beverages in the Totem Galaxy, but many Heavenly Gods suddenly appeared in their ranks, and Long Mucheng has even reached rank five Heavenly God. They have been pushing the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion out of the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","“And these are only the powers that have appeared so far. Who knows who else is backing Chu Feng?","“Since they have gone as far as to declare war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, there is little doubt that those powers will go after us if we support the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion in hunting down Chu Feng. We will suffer huge losses if so,” Cang Li voiced his worry.","“Lord Cang Li, casualties are inevitable in war. Our Netherworld Sectmembers have never feared death. This is a necessary move. We cannot spare a person who has blasphemed our sacred item,” Baili Xukong replied.","“Yes, Chu Feng deserves death, but we have to be pragmatic. He knows where our sacred item is, and he has shown that he is a person of great means. What if we corner him, and he decides to pull some trick to ruin our sacred item? Who is going to take responsibility for that?","“Baili Xukong, don’t you dare say that Chu Feng is just a mere junior. We have all suffered for having underestimated him. Who knows what other tricks he has up his sleeves?” Cang Li said.","“Lord Cang Li is right. We cannot view Chu Feng as a normal junior.”","The crowd fell into a dilemma. Despite their powerful cultivation, none of the experts here could guarantee that they could stop Chu Feng if he went after their sacred item once more.","“Lord Cang Li’s worry is not unfounded. Our priorities are clear—the sacred item comes first. For that, we can even temporarily put aside our grudge with Chu Feng. However, it’s because we need to prioritize the sacred item that we cannot remain idle here.","“We’re relying on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion right now to activate our sacred item, so our priority should be to maintain a close relationship with them right now. If we turn our back on him right now, he may back out of our deal. That’ll be a huge setback for us,” Baili Xukong said.","“All right, stop arguing. You two make sense. This matter is of grave importance, so further discussions are required before we make a vote,” another elder from the neutral faction said.","So, the elders from the neutral faction, Baili Xukong from the new faction, and Dongfang Hansong of the conservative faction proceeded to discuss the matter at length.","The conclusion was that they needed to maintain their ties with Jie Tianran to awaken their sacred item. For that, they had no choice but to wage war on Chu Feng.","After coming to a decision, they employed a means that broadcast their message across the world of cultivation. They listed Chu Feng’s sins to justify why they were going after him. In that regard, they behaved like an orthodox sect.","Naturally, their announcement caused a stir throughout the world of cultivation.","Some thought that Chu Feng was dead meat.","The strongest power, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, and the entity no one dared to cross, the Netherworld Sect, had waged war on Chu Feng. No matter how talented Chu Feng was, he wouldn’t stand a chance against those two behemoths.","But some deduced that Chu Feng had powerful backing, judging by how he had survived the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s pursuit for so long and even turned the tables by declaring war against them. Some speculated that his backing was a powerhouse from the Ancient Era.","No matter what, one thing was clear. The world of cultivation was about to be thrown into chaos.","...","Both the new faction and the conservative faction had to dispatch their experts to reinforce the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","A group of experts had just left Baili Xukong’s palace for the Seven Realms Galaxy. Among them was Wuma Hanshuang, a rank four Heavenly God who had previously been controlled by Wen Xue.","The only ones left in the palace were Baili Xukong and Xiahou Jue.","“I disapprove,” Baili Xukong replied forcefully.","Xiahou Jue had been dispatched to hunt down Chu Feng as well, but he had a request. Before hunting down Chu Feng, he wanted to raise his cultivation by practicing the Netherworld Sect’s secret skill.","However, this secret skill was extremely dangerous. The chances of success were slim, and failure spelled death. Even if he succeeded, the backlash of using the secret skill would also result in his death.","That was why Baili Xukong turned down Xiahou Jue’s request.","“Milord, I implore you to grant my request.” Xiahou Jue kneeled to Baili Xukong.","Baili Xukong sighed before speaking gently, “Xiahou Jue, I know that you’re disheartened by your defeat to that Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s lass, but times have changed.","“We were all present when Chu Feng barged into the Undying Starfield and threatened our sacred item, whether it was you, me, Dongfang Hansong, the neutral faction’s lords, or even Jie Tianran. Yet, he still slipped past our encirclement and escaped. The juniors of the present generation cannot be viewed in the same light as before.","“So be it if you were defeated. There will be hope as long as you live and breathe. Once we activate the sacred item, no one in the world of cultivation will be a match for our Netherworld Sect.”","He might be strict on his subordinates, but he also cared about them. It was not without reason that so many experts in the new faction were loyal to him.","Wuma Hanshuang was a good example. She had returned to Baili Xukong’s side to seek punishment, knowing that she had committed an unforgivable sin against the Netherworld Sect, but after hearing her side of the story, Baili Xukong trusted and vouched for her.","Similarly, he wouldn’t allow Xiahou Jue to practice a secret skill that would lead to his death.","“Milord, I’m not doing this out of recklessness. The recent events made me realize my powerlessness, and I want to practice the secret skill not to die but to be able to contribute to the Netherworld Sect when it truly counts.”"]},{"number":6615,"title":"Chapter 6615: Chapter 6613: Cultivation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6613: Cultivation","“If I had this secret skill, I could have killed Xian Yu’er and Chu Feng at the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land and ended this mess. Milord, I know that you have once consulted Lord Netherworld Master about this secret skill, and you know how to minimize the risks of practicing this secret skill. I promise that I won’t use this secret skill unless necessary,” Xiahou Jue said.","“Practicing this secret skill still poses significant risk even if you use Lord Netherworld Master’s method. Otherwise, we would have propagated it to all Netherworld Sectmembers. A secret skill to bring down one’s opponent along with oneself during a crucial moment is a powerful weapon and deterrent,” Baili Xukong replied.","“Milord, please grant my wish.” Xiahou Jue kowtowed.","Baili Xukong could tell that Xiahou Jue had already made up his mind and that he would secretly practice the secret skill despite his disapproval. Rather than let Xiahou Jue fumble by himself, he would rather guide him along to maximize his chances of survival.","“Haa, fine. Since you insist on practicing it, I want you to make a promise to me,” Baili Xukong finally relented.","“Please speak, milord,” Xiahou Jue said.","“You can only resort to the secret skill if you’re faced with a powerful enemy or a quandary beyond your ability to solve, and you’re unable to escape. If there is even a sliver of hope that you may survive, you are not to use it,” Baili Xukong said.","“Yes, milord.” Xiahou Jue nodded vehemently.","“Also, I’ll be watching you while you practice the secret skill. If anything goes awry, I’ll step in right away and stop you, even if it means destroying a portion of your cultivation.”","Xiahou Jue’s eyes lit up with delight despite the risks. “Yes, milord!”","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng was still busy plundering in the Seven Realms Galaxy. He had reunited with the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader and the lunatic, as promised.","There were some differences in the God’s Era’s power fragments that had entered the Seven Realms Galaxy. Chu Feng had previously directed the lunatic and the guild leader to the realms where the power fragments could be more easily extracted.","As for the remaining power fragments, they were not necessarily any more potent than the ones they had obtained thus far, but the difficulty in extracting them was much higher.","The guild leader and the lunatic were unable to extract them despite using the method Chu Feng had imparted to them.","They weren’t the only ones who had reunited with Chu Feng.","Jie Nianqing’s previous subordinates had also joined forces with him. They numbered in the hundred thousands, and all of them had already resolved themselves not to interfere in Chu Feng’s vengeance against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Some of the more extreme ones even aided him.","This showed how loyal they were to Jie Nianqing, or else they wouldn’t have turned against the entire Seven Realms Sacred Mansion over her.","These people had been previously augmented by Jie Tianran, so they weren’t weak.","There were at least tens of thousands of pinnacle True Dragon World Spiritists and a large handful of rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists. They had contributed significantly to the extraction of power fragments.","Of course, Chu Feng hadn’t just been busy extracting power fragments. He had also been making good his declaration by massacring anyone who appeared before him in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s robes.","The massive influx of origin energies harvested from the massacred led to the swift growth of his Asura World Spirit Army. The Asura King and some of his subordinates had already reached rank nine True God level.","The Asura King had been the first one to reach rank nine True God level, but the accumulation required to reach Heavenly God was so great that his subordinates caught up to him. That said, there was no doubt that the Asura King would be the first to make a breakthrough eventually.","And it wouldn’t be long before that day came, given the rate at which Chu Feng was feeding origin energies into the mysterious formation gate.","At present, Chu Feng and the others were making their way to another realm, but Ling Xiao and several others looked uneasy. They had seen the Netherworld Sect’s declaration of war against Chu Feng, and they knew how powerful the Netherworld Sect was.","Even so, not a single person backed down. From the moment they defected to Chu Feng’s side, they were already prepared to die.","“Chu Feng, did Jie Tianran request help from the Netherworld Sect?” the guild leader asked.","“Probably. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion should have gathered some intelligence about us in the meantime and learned about Yu’er’s strength. Since their Saint-tier elders have their hands full dealing with other matters elsewhere, the next best alternative is for them to request help from the Netherworld Sect.","“We have to tread carefully from now on. Make sure to remain within my line of sight. It’s possible that the Netherworld Sect has already prepared an ambush in one of the realms and is waiting to catch us,” Chu Feng said.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion might have harvested more of God’s Era’s power fragments than us, but we have also claimed a considerable amount. There aren't many power fragments left, and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is bound to concentrate their forces on the remaining places. Why don’t we just give up on the remaining power fragments and reunite with the others at the Ancestral Martial Galaxy?” the guild leader suggested.","Chu Feng’s group had also been gathering intelligence.","They knew that the Dragon Breath Clan and the others, who had been stationed in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, had begun launching attacks against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion upon learning about Chu Feng’s declaration of war.","“I recently noticed something. The power fragments that are more difficult to extract are more likely to contain pieces of information. I have already obtained some of them, but I’m still not sure what these pieces of information are hinting at. I’m guessing they are related to God’s Era’s two remaining powers.","“If I can gather more information pieces, I might get an advantage when it comes to acquiring the other two powers. Worst comes to worst, I’ll use my hidden card to bring us to safety,” Chu Feng said.","“I see. Then we have to proceed no matter the danger,” the guild leader said.","“We’ll heed young master Chu Feng’s will,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather and the others said.","...","Meanwhile, Xiahou Jue sat in the middle of Baili Xukong’s palace with closed eyes, while Baili Xukong watched him with nervous eyes."]},{"number":6616,"title":"Chapter 6616: Chapter 6614: The Redsoul Sect","paragraphs":["Chapter 6614: The Redsoul Sect","When Xiahou Jue finally opened his eyes once more, he turned to Baili Xukong and bowed. “Thank you, milord.”","Baili Xukong hurriedly stepped forward to support him. “Did you succeed?”","He sensed that Xiahou Jue had most likely succeeded, but he wasn’t certain about it. He needed the latter to confirm the matter. If Xiahou Jue really succeeded, this would be a huge deal.","“Milord, Lord Netherworld Master’s method works. I have succeeded. With this, I can stand against even rank six Heavenly Gods. I’m confident that I’ll be able to kill Chu Feng and Xianhai Yu’er now,” Xiahou Jue replied excitedly.","But Baili Xukong frowned. “It’s good that you have grasped the secret skill, but you aren’t to resort to it unless necessary. Using the secret skill will cost your life.”","“My death will be worthwhile if I can bring down Chu Feng and Xianhai Yu’er for the Netherworld Sect,” Xiahou Jue replied.","“We don’t need you to sacrifice yourself to eliminate them. You have already promised me not to use the secret skill unless cornered.”","“Understood.”","“Now that you have grasped the secret skill, you should head over to reinforce the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I’ll walk you out.”","Baili Xukong personally walked Xiahou Jue out of his palace. Then, he turned to the Netherworld Sect’s elder beside him and asked, “I've been sensing another power loitering outside the barrier for some time now. What’s the situation?”","A huge army was currently camping outside the Undying Starfield.","“Milord, they claim to be an Ancient Era’s power known as the Redsoul Sect, and they wish to join forces with our Netherworld Sect. Lord Cang Li has already denied their request for alliance, but the Redsoul Sect refused to retreat and requested to meet you. You were busy earlier, so I didn’t want to disturb you,” the elder said.","“Tell them to scram.”","“Understood.”","The elder was about to deal with this matter when Baili Xukong suddenly stopped him.","“Wait. Why does the Redsoul Sect sound so familiar?”","“Milord, the Redsoul Sect entered God’s Era when it opened as well. They clashed with Chu Feng inside God’s Era and suffered a setback. Since then, they have harbored a grudge against Chu Feng. Upon learning that our Netherworld Sect has declared war on Chu Feng, they came here hoping to join hands with us to deal with Chu Feng.”","“I remember it now. The Redsoul Sect’s sectmaster was extremely arrogant in God’s Era, showing no respect for other powers. He even taunted the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master.”","“Yes, you’re right.”","“Lead the way,” Baili Xukong ordered.","The elder led the way.","Several hulking warships that resembled mini cities floated neatly outside the Undying Starfield’s barrier.","Hundreds of millions of people stood on the decks of these warships, and they were dressed in red cloaks and bamboo veil hats. They were the army of the Redsoul Sect.","As a show of sincerity, the Redsoul Sect had mobilized all its elites.","This was also why the Redsoul Sect had insisted on staying put to meet Baili Xukong despite being rejected by the Netherworld Sect. They believed that they were qualified to work with the Netherworld Sect.","The Netherworld Sect might have turned them down due to a difference in their principles, but the grudge between Chu Feng and Baili Xukong’s son had become well known in the world of cultivation. The Redsoul Sect thought that Baili Xukong would be interested to work with them.","Soon, Baili Xukong and the elder emerged from the barrier.","While the two looked insignificant compared to the Redsoul Sect’s humongous army, their arrival still caught the Redsoul Sect’s attention. The Redsoul Sect’s sectmaster stepped out from the deck and bowed deeply to Baili Xukong.","“I am the Redsoul Sect’s sectmaster, Honghun Tuozai.”","He had put on airs in the God’s Era as if everyone was beneath him, but he greeted Baili Xukong with a lowered posture. Yet, Baili Xukong was unmoved.","“Get this into your head. The name of the person who is going to massacre your Redsoul Sect today is Baili Xukong.”","Those words alarmed the crowd from the Redsoul Sect. They immediately knew that the situation had gone awry.","Boom!","Before they could even ask for the reason, Baili Xukong thrust his palm forth, unleashing a powerful wave of martial power that devoured the Redsoul Sect’s army like a gigantic tsunami.","All Redsoul Sectmembers, regardless of their cultivation levels, disintegrated into dust before they could even let out a squeak. Even the Redsoul Sect’s sectmaster, despite being a rank two Heavenly God, died instantly.","The Netherworld Sect’s elder who led Baili Xukong was confused.","The Redsoul Sect had come here searching for an alliance, and their sectmaster had lowered their posture to Baili Xukong. Considering that the Netherworld Sect didn’t have a grudge against the Redsoul Sect, there should have been no reason for Baili Xukong to massacre them.","Noticing his confusion, Baili Xukong explained, “In the present world of cultivation, only Jie Tianran’s Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is worthy of being our Netherworld Sect’s ally. The Redsoul Sect has once provoked Jie Tianran, so I massacred them as a gift to him.”","The elder widened his eyes in realization.","Baili Xukong took one last look at whatever that remained of the Redsoul Sect’s army and sneered, “Who do these people think they are to copy our Netherworld Sect’s wear?”","With that, he flung his sleeves and left.","The elder stood in a daze for seconds before shaking his head.","The Redsoul Sect had wanted to throw their lot in with the Netherworld Sect after realizing that they were no longer in a position of power. Little did they expect their past deeds to come back and bite them.","But this was how the world of cultivation operated.","...","In the meantime, Chu Feng’s group extracted God’s Era’s power fragments from two more realms in the Seven Realms Galaxy. One of them contained an information piece.","Chu Feng put together the information pieces he had gathered in an attempt to decipher them.","The crowd stood quietly, waiting for his evaluation.","When Chu Feng finally reopened his eyes, he looked toward God’s Era and remarked, “Soon, there will be another change in God’s Era.”","The crowd quickly employed their observation means to scrutinize God’s Era, only to frown moments later. They couldn’t find any changes in God’s Era at all."]},{"number":6617,"title":"Chapter 6617: Chapter 6615: The Asura King Advances to Heavenly God","paragraphs":["Chapter 6615: The Asura King Advances to Heavenly God","Chu Feng was also observing God’s Era.","“It might take more time. Let’s head to the next location. We’ll head to three more realms and obtain their power fragments before leaving the Seven Realms Galaxy. If the power fragment in any of these three places has been taken, we’ll leave the Seven Realms Galaxy right away.”","Chu Feng took out a map and marked out three realms.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was also extracting God’s Era’s power fragments, so he couldn’t guarantee that the power fragments of the realms he had chosen hadn’t been extracted yet.","There were already several realms they had been to where the power fragments had already been extracted, making them wasted trips.","Furthermore, as time passed, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s experts would slowly converge at the remaining locations, which would put Chu Feng’s group in an increasingly risky position.","“Chu Feng, where should we head next?” the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader asked.","She chose to follow Chu Feng’s instructions despite being the older one here.","“We’ll head here.”","Chu Feng chose the realm closest to them, and the group headed off.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng placed all the origin energies he had just collected into the formation gate linked with the Asura World Spirit Army. The formation gate closed, and Chu Feng inspected the gate closely to decipher it.","“Is it much more difficult than before?” Eggy opened her eyes and looked at Chu Feng curiously.","The formation gate had already closed several times since Chu Feng began infusing origin energies into it, but he had always been able to decipher them right away. This time, he was taking longer than usual.","Eggy sensed that things were slightly different than before.","“Milady Queen sure is smart!” Chu Feng said.","“Bootlicker.” Eggy smiled sweetly despite her remark. “Does it mean that the Asura King will advance to Heavenly God level this time?”","“Right on the mark. Elder Kui Ting should be able to make a breakthrough this time.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Your fighting prowess should go up if Kui Ting advances to Heavenly God level and lends his cultivation to you, especially when you’re wielding the Monster Slayer Sword,” Eggy remarked.","“I think so, and Elder Kui Ting’s strength can be further enhanced through the Asura World Spirit Army’s formation. However, there is a difference between Heavenly Gods and True Gods, so we will only know for sure when the time comes,” Chu Feng replied.","Ling Xiao and the others were the ones driving the warship through the teleportation passageway, as it was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s internal teleportation formation, so Chu Feng was free to do other things in the meantime.","In truth, the formation gate wasn’t too difficult for Chu Feng. He found the solution right before reaching their destination, and the formation gate opened once more.","Tens of millions of Asura World Spirits kneeled on the other side of the formation gate to greet him. They spoke in unison, “Thank you, Lord Chu Feng! Thank you, Milady Queen!”","Chu Feng smiled.","The Asura World Spirit Army had made significant advancement in their cultivation, and Asura King Kui Ting had made a breakthrough to rank one Heavenly God level. This time, they chose to thank Eggy as well, even addressing her as Milady Queen, much to Chu Feng’s delight.","Eggy was also pleased. She stood up and walked over to Chu Feng’s side with her hands behind her back. Despite her title of ‘Milady Queen’, she still looked no different from the first time she met Chu Feng—she was still as young and beautiful as ever.","In contrast, Chu Feng had changed a lot. His hot-bloodedness had settled down into an air of unwavering composure. It was not that he felt like an old man yet, and he would still joke around at times, but he exuded an air of maturity now.","Eggy, on the other hand, still exuded an air of youthfulness, like Little Fishy.","The two of them felt like a grown man and a young lass.","“Kui Ting, you have finally made a breakthrough and joined the ranks of Heavenly Gods,” Eggy remarked with a grin.","“It’s all thanks to you, mistress.”","“What?” Eggy was taken aback by the way the Asura King had addressed her. A blush crept down from her face to her neck, tinging even her hands and bare feet red.","The Asura King quickly corrected his words, “Pardon me. I meant Milady Queen. It’s all thanks to Milady Queen providing us with origin energies.”","Eggy furiously hammered Chu Feng. “What are you laughing at?”","And indeed, Chu Feng was chuckling by the side. “I’m not laughing at you. I just found it amusing how Elder Kui Ting misspoke out of nervousness.”","“That better be the case.” Eggy glared at Chu Feng.","“Eggy, why is your face so red? Are you shy?” Chu Feng asked with a mischievous grin.","“Nonsense! Do you think I’d feel shy?” Eggy crossed her hands in front of her chest, but her blush was not receding.","“Elder Kui Ting, be careful not to speak your true thoughts in the future,” Chu Feng said.","“Understood,” the Asura King replied.","“Understood, your head!” Eggy hurled her fist angrily, though the one she hammered in the end was still Chu Feng.","Chu Feng hissed in pain as he ran away. “All right, all right. Let’s stop messing around. Shouldn’t you respond to their words of gratitude?”","“We’re all one family. There’s no need for such formalities.” Eggy graciously waved her hand.","Her words made the faces of the Asura World Spirit Army glow in delight. They had always known that Eggy was extremely talented, and they looked up to her, but unlike Chu Feng, who saw them as a family right from the start, Eggy had only been close to Chu Feng.","Her willingness to acknowledge them was huge.","“What’s wrong, Elder Kui Ting? Why are you crying? There are many eyes on you here.” Chu Feng rushed forward to support the Asura King.","“Lord Chu Feng, Lord Massacre had many powerful world spirits with him back then. We were just a bunch of nobodies contracted to him. But with you, Lord Chu Feng, we feel cherished like a family,” the Asura King said while tearing up. “Lord Chu Feng, we’re blessed to have met you.”","Several others in the Asura World Spirit Army cried as well.","“Enough, enough. It won’t do for valiant Asura World Spirits like you to cry. Also, it’s thanks to Lord Massacre’s treasure that you grew so quickly. If not for that, you wouldn’t have been able to make such a huge advancement within such a short time,” Chu Feng said.","“Lord Massacre has been kind to us, but Lord Chu Feng, that doesn’t undermine the fact that you have treated us like a family. We will have no regret fighting to our deaths for you. Don’t you agree, my brothers?” the Asura King asked the army behind him.","“Yes!” the Asura World Spirit Army replied in unison.","Chu Feng smiled once more. He was glad to have received the Asura World Spirit Army’s recognition. However, he suddenly sensed something and frowned. He hurriedly pulled his consciousness back to his main body."]},{"number":6618,"title":"Chapter 6618: Chapter 6616: I, Song Changsheng’s Disciple, Have Come to Help","paragraphs":["Chapter 6616: I, Song Changsheng’s Disciple, Have Come to Help","As soon as they emerged from the teleportation formation, a sealing formation enveloped the entire realm, trapping them in place. Even the teleportation formation they had just stepped out of had been rendered useless.","It was an ambush, and there was nowhere for them to retreat.","Everyone looked nervous, including Ling Xiao and the guild leader. The enemy had come prepared.","The only one who remained fearless was the lunatic. It felt as if she had already seen past life and death.","Little Fishy didn’t speak, but she was prepared to make a move. She was currently the strongest one in Chu Feng’s group.","“Elder,” Chu Feng called the Divine Deer.","“I know. I’ll bring you to safety if the situation looks dire,” the Divine Deer replied.","Very few people were capable of restricting the Divine Deer’s powers. No one had ever succeeded in doing so aside from the golden-haired woman in the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s ancestral land.","“You people have really betrayed the Sacred Mansion to join Chu Feng. You deserve to die a thousand times over!” a furious voice dripping with murderous intent boomed from the sky.","Three figures stepped forth.","One was a white-haired elder wearing the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s robes. His name was Jie Tongyou, a rank four Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. He had once participated in the Saint-tier Elder Selection, and while he wasn’t chosen, he still commanded great prestige.","The other two were dressed in the Netherworld Sect’s robes.","Chu Feng recognized one of them—it was Wuma Hanshuang, Wen Xue’s master in the Netherworld Sect. Chu Feng didn’t expect Wen Xue to spare Wuma Hanshuang, and he also didn’t think that the Netherworld Sect would forgive her so easily, either.","“Kikikiki. Lady Luck must be shining on me. I didn’t expect to score such a big fish. That beautiful lass must be Xianhai Yu’er, right?” the third person standing alongside Jie Tongyou and Wuma Hanshuang spoke.","He was not wearing the Netherworld Sect’s bamboo veil hat, allowing Chu Feng and the others to see his face.","It was an emaciated old man, whose body was skin and bones. His face was pale, similar to that of a terminally ill patient. He looked like an old monster who had lived for countless years. Despite his old age, his behavior resembled that of a sly rat who was constantly up to no good.","His lustful eyes were fixed on Little Fishy.","“She lives up to her reputation as the number one beauty of the current era, but she looks nothing more than a lass. I don’t feel the air of a Heavenly God from her. Lass, tell me the truth. You weren’t the one who defeated Xiahou Jue, right?” the skeleton old man said.","“You can give it a try,” Little Fishy replied with cold eyes.","“Hahaha! Sure, I’ll give it a try. Do you think I’d fear a mere lass?”","The skeleton old man’s aura flared, revealing his rank four Heavenly God level cultivation. Clearly, he was a notable figure in the Netherworld Sect, and it would be safe to assume that he could raise his cultivation by a rank like Xiahou Jue.","“Be careful, Yu’er. Those two are likely able to raise their cultivation by a rank like Xiahou Jue,” Chu Feng said.","“Don’t worry, big brother.” Little Fishy beamed a radiant smile at Chu Feng.","She didn’t seem to view this situation as a threat to her.","She turned to the trio in the sky, and her radiant smile morphed over into chilling frostiness. “Such trash is nothing in my eyes. I can easily deal with a dozen of them, let alone two.”","Chu Feng’s words were relayed via voice transmission, but Little Fishy spoke aloud.","“Arrogant lass. Let’s see how long you can keep that bravado. Wuma Hanshuang, you stay back. I shall see what the lass who triggered a galaxy-level phenomenon is capable of,” the skeleton old man sneered.","But Jie Tongyou interjected, “Chu Feng and Xianhai Yu’er have murdered many of my brethren, and they are colluding with our traitors. Please allow me to personally apprehend them.”","While speaking, he formed a hand seal and unleashed a massive formation net upon Chu Feng and the others.","Chu Feng noticed that Jie Tongyou’s spirit power was different from the one that sealed off the realm. It would appear that the sealing formation was powered by a treasure instead.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","All of a sudden, a golden sword swooped in from the horizon and shredded Jie Tongyou’s formation net apart before returning from the direction it came from.","The crowd immediately turned their gaze over.","A little hand appeared out of thin air to grab the golden sword.","The golden sword was inscribed with runes. It was a God Armament enhanced by a formation.","“Another lass?” the skeleton old man remarked upon seeing the little hand. He didn’t look nervous despite the intruder; if anything, he looked excited.","“You’re the lass! I am your ancestor!” a childlike voice echoed.","The intruder revealed himself. It was a ten-year-old boy. He didn’t have flattering facial features, but he had an air of goofiness that made him appear adorable.","“It’s him?” Chu Feng exclaimed.","He had met the boy before. Song Changsheng had appeared together with the boy at the Dragon Spring Chamber.","The boy rested his golden sword on his shoulder before turning to Chu Feng. “You don’t need to worry, Chu Feng. I have come in my master’s name to aid you. No one will be able to hurt you under my watch. I’ll deal with those three old things. You can watch the show from the side!”","After saying his piece, the boy charged at the three old men.","“Big brother, who’s that?” Little Fishy asked.","‘He seems to be Elder Song Changsheng’s disciple,” Chu Feng replied.","“Doesn’t that make him Miss Miaomiao’s junior?”","“I think he is Miaomiao’s senior.”","The boy might appear young, but he had come under Song Changsheng’s tutelage before Xian Miaomiao.","Boom!","A loud explosion echoed.","Chu Feng and Little Fishy widened their eyes in astonishment.","The boy crawled up from the ground, cloaked in dust. There was a footprint on his chest. One of the three old men must have stamped him down.","“Don’t worry. It’s been too long since I last fought that I have gotten rusty. I’ll cripple them right now!” The boy wiped off the blood from the corner of his lips before rising into the sky once more.","Moments later, he crashed back into the ground.","This time, the boy was bleeding not just from his mouth but from his eyes, nostrils, and ears as well. He must have received considerable internal injuries from the previous attack.","“Don’t worry, I’m fine. I’m just rusty because I haven’t fought in a while.”","Despite the boy’s bravado, Chu Feng heard the other party’s bones creak as he returned to his feet. That was clearly the sound of a fracture."]},{"number":6619,"title":"Chapter 6619: Chapter 6617: Soloing Three People With Ease","paragraphs":["Chapter 6617: Soloing Three People With Ease","The boy rose into the sky once more and charged at the trio.","Chu Feng raised his cultivation to rank one Heavenly God through the Monster Slayer Sword, and by activating Heaven’s Eyes as well, he could finally somewhat keep up with the battle in the sky.","The boy was also a rank four Heavenly God.","Only the skeleton old man stepped forward to fight the boy. He was also the one who stomped the boy down the previous two times. Clearly, he didn’t think that the boy was a threat and was toying with him.","The skeleton old man sneered, “An old monster acting as a boy? I suggest you weigh your own worth first.”","A few exchanges later, the skeleton old man stomped the boy down into the ground again. This time, the boy’s bones were shattered, and his skin and flesh were torn. Blood spurted profusely from his wounds.","Yet, the boy continued grinning. “No worries, no worries. I’m almost done with my warm-up.”","“Isn’t he going to die at this rate?” Little Fishy asked.","She whipped out her God Armament and charged at the trio in the sky.","The skeleton old man and Wuma Hanshuang immediately raised their cultivation to rank five Heavenly God level. In response, Little Fishy also raised her cultivation to rank five Heavenly God level.","“T-t-this lass has not only advanced to rank one Heavenly God, but she’s able to raise her cultivation by... four ranks?!” The skeleton old man was so shocked by Little Fishy that his composure eroded, and he even stuttered.","In contrast, Wuma Hanshuang was much calmer. She drew her God Armament and charged at Little Fishy.","Clang!","Boom!","Sparks flew, and shockwaves rippled. The two of them began crossing blows.","It was also at this moment that the stoic-faced Wuma Hanshuang suddenly panicked.","She had a good grasp of Xiahou Jue. The latter was a proud person, and he wouldn’t admit defeat unless he truly thought that he was no match for a person. And Xiahou Jue’s strength was roughly on par with hers.","If Xiahou Jue was no match for Little Fishy, the chances were that it was the same for her, too.","So, she prepared a hand.","Right before clashing with Little Fishy, she unleashed all her God Taboo Martial Skills, significantly raising her speed, strength, and physical resilience. She planned to catch Little Fishy off guard and subdue her in a single swoop.","But when their God Armaments clashed, she felt her arm going numb from the other party’s sheer strength. She looked at Little Fishy’s slender frame and wondered how it could wield such power.","What further stoked her panic was that Little Fishy was not only strong but fast as well.","Wuma Hanshuang struggled to keep up with her movements, to the point where it was taking her everything just to block Little Fishy’s attack. There was no chance for her to counterattack at all.","Clang clang!","Wuma Hanshuang roared, “Damned old thing, are you still watching the show?”","She felt her organs and brain rattling under the sheer weight of Little Fishy’s attacks. It was almost as if Little Fishy wasn’t wielding a sword but a hammer. She might really die here if the skeleton old man continued watching by the side.","“Relax, Wuma Hanshuang. I have seen through her attacks. I’ll come to your aid right now.”","The skeleton old man regained his composure and joined the battle. He also had to unleash multiple God Taboo Martial Skills to raise his fighting prowess, so as to bridge the gap between him and Little Fishy.","With him joining the fray, Wuma Hanshuang was able to catch a breather... though it was really just a breather.","It didn’t take long before both Wuma Hanshuang and the skeleton old man found themselves fleeing in a fluster.","“W-w-what the hell?! How is this lass so ferocious?!” the skeleton old man exclaimed in horror.","Perhaps due to his weaker physique, his injuries were even more severe than Wuma Hanshuang’s. He looked at the sky and shouted, “Oi, Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, are you going to continue watching? I-I-I am already putting my life on the line here!”","Weng!","A brilliant light suddenly shone from the sky as a huge formation manifested. Two surges of energy converged within the formation before flowing into the bodies of the skeleton old man and Wuma Hanshuang.","It was a formation to raise their fighting prowess.","Under normal circumstances, a rank four Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist couldn’t hope to interfere in a fight among rank five Heavenly Gods. But by plastering a talisman paper on his chest, Jie Tongyou raised his spirit power to rank five Heavenly Dragon.","That allowed him to greatly enhance the skeleton old man and Wuma Hanshuang’s fighting prowess.","“That talisman paper feels familiar. That’s one of your grandfather’s means, right?” Eggy asked.","“It’s likely so,” Chu Feng replied.","“Where did he get all those talisman papers from? How is he able to raise the spirit power of even a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist?” Eggy remarked.","Jie Tianran was truly an unfathomable opponent. Despite having clashed several times with him, it felt like they had yet to see the bottom of what he was capable of.","Even Eggy was worried that Chu Feng might slip up while facing Jie Tianran and suffer a huge setback.","“Ugh! T-t-this isn’t working! Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, let’s retreat! Let’s retreat now!” the skeleton old man cried.","In the meantime, Little Fishy had lopped off the skeleton old man’s right arm and Wuma Hanshuang’s left leg. Despite the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elder supporting them, they still found themselves powerless against Little Fishy.","Weng!","The sealing formation trapping Chu Feng and the others suddenly transformed into a teleportation formation. The next moment, the skeleton old man, Wuma Hanshuang, and Jie Tongyou vanished.","They had escaped.","The teleportation formation was so advanced that Little Fishy couldn’t even give chase.","So, Little Fishy returned to Chu Feng’s side.","“You’re incredible.” Chu Feng shot a thumbs-up at Little Fishy.","The latter stowed away her God Armament before beaming a smile at Chu Feng. It was as if subduing those three powerhouses was a walk in the park for her.","Ling Xiao and the others were flabbergasted.","They looked at Little Fishy in awe. They had known that she had become powerful, but they didn’t expect her to be so strong. To think that even a rank five Heavenly Dragon and two rank five Heavenly Gods were forced to flee from her!"]},{"number":6620,"title":"Chapter 6620: Chapter 6618: The Remaining Two Powers","paragraphs":["Chapter 6618: The Remaining Two Powers","Pah pah pah!","Someone applauded.","“I heard from Junior Miaomiao that the most talented person in the world of cultivation isn’t her but the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s princess, Miss Xianhai Yu’er. I see now that my junior’s words ring true. Miss Xianhai Yu’er, I only have one word for you—badass!”","Song Changsheng’s disciple limped over. His injuries were still bleeding profusely as he made his way over, alarming the crowd. It looked as if he was half dead. Yet, he was unfazed as if life and death meant nothing to him.","“Are you... all right? Let me treat you,” Chu Feng stepped forward and said.","“I’m fine, I’m fine. As I said, I haven’t fought in a while. I had just gotten warmed up and was about to teach those three a lesson when Miss Xianhai Yu’er dealt with them. It’s a pity I wasn’t able to showcase my strength, but witnessing her means opened my eyes. This makes my trip worthwhile,” the boy said with a grin.","Despite his young appearance, his demeanor wasn’t childlike. He took out a pill and popped it into his mouth, and his injuries began to close.","“Are you really fine?” Chu Feng asked.","He could tell that the boy had only eaten a superficial recovery pill. Fighting a Heavenly God should have inflicted damage on not just his body but his soul as well, but somehow, the boy acted as if he was completely fine.","“That fellow is surprisingly resilient. He isn’t a human, right?” Eggy asked.","“Elder Song Changsheng’s disciple is indeed extraordinary,” Chu Feng replied.","He shared the same opinion as Eggy. He didn’t think that the boy was boasting, just that he was unable to unleash his true strength for some reason.","Little Fishy smiled politely at the boy’s compliment, but her gaze remained on Chu Feng. “Big brother, which realm should we head to next?”","She wasn’t worried in the least even though they had just been ambushed.","“They have already extracted the power fragment here. I reckon it’s the same for the other realms. The Netherworld Sect seems to have dispatched a huge number of experts to reinforce the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, just that they have split up to ambush us at different realms.","“I don’t think that they were lying about that. We won’t stand a chance if Baili Xukong comes as well. Let’s not linger here and return to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy,” Chu Feng said.","So, the group made their way to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","Chu Feng still didn’t fully trust Ling Xiao’s group despite taking them in, so he chose not to reveal the Nine Heavens Secret Domain to them. Instead, he told them to use their means to head to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","It was nowhere as fast as traveling through the Nine Heavens Secret Domain, but it was still much faster than ordinary teleportation formations. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion did live up to its reputation as the number one world spiritist power in the world of cultivation.","Chu Feng, Little Fishy, the guild leader, the lunatic, the boy, and Ling Xiao made their way into the warship’s palace to rest and talk to the boy.","The guild leader didn’t want Ling Xiao present when they talked. She doubted Ling Xiao’s loyalty despite knowing that he was on good terms with Chu Feng, as she didn’t think that they had proved themselves yet. There was still a chance that they might be spies from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","While Chu Feng was still guarded against the other members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, he trusted Ling Xiao. That was why he pulled Ling Xiao along.","The group sat in a circle inside the palace.","Ling Xiao had figured out from their earlier conversations that the boy was Xian Miaomiao’s senior, and he knew that their master was a hidden expert. For that reason, he wasn’t surprised that the boy was a rank four Heavenly God.","“How old are you?” Ling Xiao asked the boy.","“I am definitely older than all of you. In fact, I don’t think there is anyone older than me out there,” the boy replied.","Chu Feng and the others were taken aback. They had been in the world of cultivation long enough to know better than to judge someone by their appearance, but still, they didn’t expect the boy to be this old.","“You seem to know a lot about us, but we don’t even know your name yet. How should we address you?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’m Fei. You can call me Brother Fei or just Fei. It’s up to you,” the boy replied casually.","“I’ll call you Brother Fei then since you’re older than us,” Ling Xiao said.","“Sure,” the boy smiled.","From the boy, Chu Feng and the others learned that Xian Miaomiao had left the world of cultivation to enter the Ninth Galaxy.","Chu Feng wasn’t surprised by the news, as Xian Miaomiao had received the qualification to open the Heaven Gate in the Immemorial Cemetery. A huge fortuitous encounter awaited her at the other side of the Heaven Gate, and there was a time limit to it. There was no reason for her to give up on this golden opportunity.","“Young master Chu Feng, there’s a change in God’s Era!” someone exclaimed from outside.","Chu Feng and the others rushed out of the palace to take a look.","Ling Xiao’s grandfather and the others had constructed an observation formation using treasures, and they were currently examining God’s Era. Through the observation formation, Chu Feng and the others could see the changes in God’s Era.","There were originally three light spheres in God’s Era’s right hand.","One had transformed into a meteor shower and scattered all over the Seven Realms Galaxy, becoming the power fragments that Chu Feng and the others had been collecting.","Now, the two remaining light spheres had begun glowing brilliantly. This seemed to be a sign that they were about to move.","“Young master Chu Feng, are the two remaining powers going to be scattered as well?” Ling Xiao’s grandfather asked.","“Yes, it should happen very soon,” Chu Feng replied.","“Should we stay in the Seven Realms Galaxy then?” the guild leader asked.","The power fragments they had been collecting in the Seven Realms Galaxy harnessed tremendous energy. It should be safe to assume that the two remaining powers of God’s Era were formidable as well. It would be a waste to miss them.","“I don’t think they will descend upon the Seven Realms Galaxy,” Chu Feng said.","“Oh?”","The crowd was surprised. As the first power had descended upon the Seven Realms Galaxy, they had assumed that the same would be true for the remaining two.","However, they were inclined to trust Chu Feng’s judgment.","...","Meanwhile, a huge war broke out in one of the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s realms."]},{"number":6621,"title":"Chapter 6621: Chapter 6119: Crusade Against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion","paragraphs":["Chapter 6119: Crusade Against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion","When the first batch of Ancient Era’s races emerged from their seclusion, the Ox-nosed Old Daoist had manipulated them into attacking the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, with the intention of making the legendary Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city reveal itself.","The Ox-nosed Old Daoist succeeded, though he gave up on claiming the legacy.","He could tell the legacy was more beneficial to a junior, and he firmly believed his disciple could take it. So, he entered the Ninth Galaxy shortly after.","But there was no way the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion would give up on the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s legacy, so they dispatched and stationed many experts at the Ancestral Martial Galaxy under the pretext of protecting it.","This greatly changed the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s balance of power.","All of the Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s powers were now living under the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s shadows. They couldn’t help but feel like an outsider had taken over their home, but they were powerless to do anything about it.","But the tides turned when Chu Feng waged war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","The Totem Dragon Clan, along with several other powers that had powerful experts in their ranks, stepped forward under the Chu Clan Alliance’s flag and attacked the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s bases in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","And astonishingly, the Chu Clan Alliance gave back a portion of the treasures they took from the Seven Reams Sacred Mansion back to the indigenous cultivators of those realms.","They even openly recruited members into the Chu Clan Alliance.","Not many people in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy were qualified to join the Chu Clan Alliance, but news swiftly spread. It didn’t take long for the experts from other galaxies to travel all the way to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy to join the Chu Clan Alliance.","As a result, the Ancestral Martial Galaxy became more bustling than ever.","The Ancestral Martial Galaxy was extremely behind on world news. Its populace thought that the Chu Clan Alliance was a formidable power from another galaxy, considering how it was able to defeat even the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They were shocked when they learned that Chu Feng was its leader.","The Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s indigenous population might not know much about foreign powers, but they had all heard about Chu Feng. His feats and talent had become a legend here.","Even now, people still talked about his accomplishments to make casual conversation. Many juniors viewed Chu Feng as their idol. There were even powers that worshiped Chu Feng. This was how influential his name had become in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","But despite recognizing Chu Feng’s greatness, they still didn’t expect him to grow to this extent within a few years after leaving the Ancestral Martial Galaxy. To think that these godlike experts, who could shatter realms with casual waves of their hands, were his underlings!","The Chu Clan Alliance’s kind acts were all credited to Chu Feng, thus causing his reputation to soar once more.","Wherever the Chu Clan Alliance appeared, brave souls would rush over. Some wanted to witness their greatness in person, but more hoped to benefit from their halo. They wanted to get a share of the pie after the Chu Clan Alliance took down the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","The Chu Clan Alliance was unstoppable. They had almost completely purged the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion from the Ancestral Martial Galaxy. To date, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had only one base left standing, and that was the one guarded by two Saint-tier elders.","The formation protecting the realm was humongous and radiant, resembling a brilliant moon that had fallen into the world. It evicted the darkness of the night and brought eternal daylight to the realm.","The risk takers vaguely understood that this base was unlike the others, and they chose to stay away for the time being and just examine the situation from afar.","Even from a distance away, giant flags could be seen swaying both on earth and in the sky. These were the Chu Clan Alliance’s flags. However, this group was made up of not the Totem Dragon Clan but the Dragon Breath Clan, led by Long Mucheng.","Qing Xuantian had once saved the Dragon Breath Clan. Afterward, he left them with a treasure, saying that their bloodlines would undergo a metamorphosis if they could decipher the treasure.","So, the Dragon Breath Clan searched hard for the person who could decipher the treasure. Their search brought them to Chu Feng and Long Xiaoxiao. Under their combined efforts, the treasure was unraveled, and the Dragon Breath Clan began their cultivation.","By now, the Dragon Breath Clan had undergone a complete metamorphosis. Many of their experts had reached Heavenly God level, and Long Mucheng advanced to rank five Heavenly Dragon level in one shot.","When Chu Feng declared war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, the Totem Dragon Clan, the Totem Nine Daoists, Xia Xingchen, and the others were still in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. They had wanted to join the fight alongside Chu Feng, but Sikong Changsheng stopped them.","It just so happened that Long Mucheng and the Dragon Breath Clan arrived at the moment.","Sikong Changsheng knew that Chu Feng had found reliable backing, so he let the Totem Dragon Clan and the others leave, thus commencing the Chu Clan Alliance’s campaign against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","The true backbone of the Chu Clan Alliance was the Dragon Breath Clan, and they were the reason the Chu Clan Alliance managed to purge most of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s bases.","However, the Dragon Breath Clan was having trouble with the base before them.","There were two rank five Heavenly Dragon Saint-tier elders stationed here. They had clashed with Long Mucheng, but when they realized they were no match for her, they holed themselves into a formation.","Much to Long Mucheng’s dismay, she was unable to breach the formation easily. She had to mobilize all her clansmen and construct a bloodline formation.","Grar!","A dragon’s roar echoed.","The earth quaked as a humongous golden silhouette surged across the earth, inundating it with radiant light.","“What’s that?”","Even spectators from afar were flabbergasted to witness the golden dragon’s silhouette. It was so humongous that it covered the entire realm.","This was a Dragon Breath Clan’s secret skill.","Long Mucheng was currently inside the golden dragon’s head, and her clansmen were occupying its body. She looked down at the defensive formation that she had struggled to take down all this time and smirked.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Saint-tier elders are cowards who hole themselves up when they are no match for their enemies. You despicable cowards who oppress the weak but cower before the strong, I’ll drag you all out and kill every last one of you!”","Long Mucheng formed a hand seal, and the golden dragon silhouette opened its mouth.","Boom!","A dragon breath was unleashed upon the sturdy barrier, exerting so much force that it shook intensely and distorted. Cracks soon appeared and spread all across its surface."]},{"number":6622,"title":"Chapter 6622: Chapter 6620: The Spectating Old Friends","paragraphs":["Chapter 6620: The Spectating Old Friends","The dragon breath was so potent that it could destroy this Upper Realm. The barrier was nowhere strong enough to withstand such prowess. If not for Long Mucheng holding herself back, the shockwaves could have leveled mountains and obliterated countless lives.","Even so, it was still a sight to behold. It shook the hearts of countless cultivators.","“This is too terrifying. Is this what Heavenly Gods are capable of?”","All spectators, regardless of cultivation and age, were shocked and horrified. They feared getting caught in such overwhelming power and dying.","Some regretted coming here to watch the commotion. They turned tail to flee, not wanting to die in vain.","“There’s no need to flee,” a woman with pink pupils remarked.","She spoke with a soft voice that was barely audible compared to the loud din caused by the showdown between the dragon breath and the barrier. It seemed like she was talking to herself, but her words still caught the attention of one person.","That person rode in an exquisite white carriage. It was much larger than normal carriages, and it was driven by three white jade horses that moved realistically.","In the carriage was a young woman who exuded a rare air of purity, making her feel impeccable and sacred. Just like the carriage, she felt more like a work of art.","Her name was Wang Yuxian.","She was the Lady of Dao Sea’s disciple. She was a good friend of Chu Feng, and she was known in the Nine Souls Galaxy as a prodigy.","Unlike those from the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, her eyes were sharp enough to tell that the Dragon Breath Clan was protecting them. They were actually safe, and there was no need to flee.","The woman with pink pupils must have seen through that as well, and that was why she piqued Wang Yuxian’s curiosity.","Upon closer examination, she noticed that the woman with pink pupils was exceptionally beautiful. Her gestures exuded an air of nobility. Normal powers couldn’t nurture someone with such grace.","“Hm?”","Wang Yuxian narrowed her eyes. The woman with pink pupils was looking at her, but that shouldn’t have been possible. This white jade carriage was a gift from Xian Miaomiao, and it harnessed incredible concealment prowess.","Yet, the woman with pink pupils appeared to be looking at her. She looked at Wang Yuxian, but she didn’t speak a word. A moment later, she turned her gaze back to the Dragon Breath Clan.","“Is she from other galaxies?” Wang Yuxian murmured, but she didn’t think too deeply into it and quickly turned her attention back to the Dragon Breath Clan.","Cultivators from other galaxies had begun flooding the Ancestral Martial Galaxy after hearing about the Chu Clan Alliance’s open recruitment. Wang Yuxian had also come after hearing the news. She wanted to join the Chu Clan Alliance.","What Wang Yuxian didn’t know was that the woman with pink pupils was Chu Feng’s acquaintance as well. Her name was Mo Yuhan. Her grandfather and Long Xiaoxiao’s master, Ningyu Shangren, were from the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect.","For a long time, they had concealed their identities to liaise with Long Lin to overthrow the Totem Dragon Clan.","However, Mo Yuhan’s grandfather died before the rebellion could happen.","Back then, Mo Yuhan’s father was severely injured and needed to assimilate a potent bloodline to be saved. Mo Yuhan’s grandfather noticed Chu Feng’s bloodline and wanted to use him.","But the Ox-nosed Old Daoist was right beside Chu Feng, and there was no way he would tolerate someone going after his disciple. So, he killed Mo Yuhan’s grandfather.","Ningyu Shangren was unaware of the details, but she knew that Mo Yuhan’s grandfather coveted Chu Feng’s bloodline. From that, she speculated that someone powerful was protecting Chu Feng.","On the other hand, Mo Yuhan had no idea how her grandfather died. She left after learning about her grandfather’s death, and she wandered aimlessly like a shell without its soul. But no matter which galaxy she went to, she heard news about Chu Feng.","And the news only got more and more exaggerated.","Mo Yuhan wondered if that famous Chu Feng was the same Chu Feng she knew. It was only when the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion placed Chu Feng on their wanted list and publicized his portrait that she confirmed that they were the same Chu Feng.","Her grandfather’s death had been a huge blow to her. There were times when she had even considered ending her life. However, after hearing Chu Feng’s story, she realized that what she had been through was nothing.","She had been too sheltered.","So, she pulled herself together and began training hard once more. At the same time, she would keep a lookout for Chu Feng’s news and head to where he was.","She was present when Baili Zilin challenged Chu Feng, and she witnessed his flair and metamorphosis. She thought about the time when she first met Chu Feng. They had been at the cultivation level then, but in just a few years, there was now such a huge gap between them.","In truth, it was people like Mo Yuhan and the others who felt more intimidated by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Even though each galaxy had its own overlord, Mo Yuhan knew that there was only one true overlord in the world of cultivation—the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Whenever the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion made a demand, the other overlords had no choice but to lower their heads.","From a young age, Mo Yuhan’s grandfather had instilled a thought in her—the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was undefeatable, but she mustn’t offend them no matter what.","But when she heard about the Chu Clan Alliance’s consecutive victories against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, that belief wavered. She thought that maybe the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion wasn’t as infallible as everyone thought.","Maybe Chu Feng would be the one to topple the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","And she was witnessing history in the making.","So, she came here to join the Chu Clan Alliance.","She figured that she had nothing to lose, and if she were going to die eventually, she would rather her death be for something meaningful. If she could deal a blow to the tyrannical Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, her death would be worthwhile.","Boom!","A deafening explosion shook the dragon.","The Dragon Breath Clan’s golden dragon silhouette intensified its dragon breath.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s barrier was at its limit."]},{"number":6623,"title":"Chapter 6623: Chapter 6621: The Dragon Breath Clan’s Defeat","paragraphs":["Chapter 6621: The Dragon Breath Clan’s Defeat","A behemoth dwelled inside the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s barrier.","Towering at over ten thousand meters tall and spanning over ten thousand meters in length, it resembled a lizard carrying a mountain. It hissed at the golden dragon silhouette covering the sky.","It was a formation entity.","All the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists in the realm channeled the formation with all their might. This formation was their final hand. Despite the preparations they had made beforehand, their faces were warped in despair and fear.","They knew they would be killed if the barrier was breached.","Two elders stood on the head of the behemoth.","One had black hair, while the other had white hair, though their wrinkled faces suggested that there wasn’t a huge gap in their ages. They were the two Saint-tier elders guarding this realm.","Jie Tianran had dispatched them here to handle a task. Things had initially gone smoothly, but who could have thought that things would go awry?","The black-haired elder wielded a sword in his left hand and a massive revolving golden wheel resembling a shield in his right. Both weapons were world spiritist treasures.","He had mustered his courage to fight to his death.","In contrast, the white-haired elder looked like he was suffering from a mental breakdown. He closed his eyes and murmured, “What a twist of fate. To think that I, a Saint-tier elder from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, would die in the hands of the lowly Dragon Breath Clan!”","His words were dripping with indignation.","Just then, he abruptly opened his eyes and exchanged looks with the black-haired elder, as if verifying something. Delight erupted from their faces.","Both of them quickly formed a series of hand seals.","Weng!","Sacred white lights emanated from their bodies and enveloped their clothes, skin, hair, and beard. Even the black-haired elder’s world spiritist treasures were enveloped by the white light.","“It’s true. We’re able to tap into this power!” the white-haired elder exclaimed.","“We won’t be the ones to die today!” the black-haired elder cheered. He charged out of the barrier while roaring, “How dare you invade our territory, the Dragon Breath Clan? For your disrespect, I, as a Saint-tier elder from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, shall vanquish you!”","He charged into the dragon breath instead of taking a detour, but somehow, the dragon breath failed to hurt him. If anything, he was getting closer and closer to the golden dragon silhouette.","“Something is off.” Long Mucheng frowned.","She could tell that the black-haired elder’s golden wheel was an extraordinary treasure, but she had already beat the living daylights out of the black-haired elder while he was wielding it earlier. For some reason, the golden wheel was emanating power several times greater than before.","The power didn’t seem to originate from the golden wheel itself. Rather, it seemed to be from the sacred white light shrouding the black-haired elder.","The black-haired elder could have attacked Long Mucheng more efficiently after his power-up, but he had chosen to march straight against the dragon breath. That was clearly a taunt against the Dragon Breath Clan.","However, the dragon breath was already the strongest means at Long Mucheng’s disposal.","In a way, this showed how much stronger the black-haired elder had become under the effects of the white light.","Boom!","The golden dragon silhouette suddenly wavered as a blue beam of light wrapped itself around its body. It was a formation constructed by the white-haired elder.","The blue beam of light tightly constricted the golden dragon silhouette, causing its body to distort. At this rate, it might be squeezed into shreds.","“Dragon Breath Clansmen, channel all your bloodline power into the Golden Dragon Formation!”","“Understood!”","The Dragon Breath Clansmen’s bloodline power flowed into the golden dragon silhouette like a flood of water, causing its dragon breath to intensify.","The black-haired elder was on the verge of reaching the golden dragon silhouette when the increased intensity overwhelmed him. Shock flickered across his face, and he quickly turned tail and fled.","Unfortunately, his escape placed the dragon breath directly in the barrier’s line of fire. The barrier disintegrated right away.","“They want to massacre our people!” the black-haired elder roared as he quickly returned to block the dragon breath with his golden wheel.","He was able to slow the dragon breath, but the weight of the attack pushed him down to where the behemoth formation was.","He was already blocking the brunt of the dragon breath, but the shockwaves spilling from the dragon breath shook the behemoth formation, causing cracks to appear on its surface.","Seeing that, the white-haired elder gave up on attacking the golden dragon silhouette and instead descended to the ground as well. He took out two blank talisman papers and formed a series of hand seals while infusing his spirit power into them.","Then, he threw the two talisman papers toward the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members.","Boom!","The two talisman papers exploded.","One released a flood of spirit power to aid the black-haired elder in withstanding the dragon breath.","The other unleashed teleportation energy that simultaneously transported the black-haired elder and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members into the distance.","To the two elders’ surprise, the dragon breath also halted at the same time.","Looking over, they realized that the golden dragon silhouette had shrunk to a tenth of its previous size. Not only that, it had also turned tail and was fleeing from the realm.","“Trying to escape?”","The two Saint-tier elders rose into the sky to pursue the golden dragon silhouette.","However, the golden dragon silhouette was so fast that they couldn’t catch up with it. They had to give up in the end.","The Dragon Breath Clansmen in the golden dragon silhouette breathed a sigh of relief.","“Mucheng, those two Saint-tier elders suddenly became much stronger. Is it related to the white light they emanated?” Long Moxiao asked.","“I think so,” Long Mucheng replied.","“We wouldn’t have been able to get away if we hadn’t constructed this Bloodline Golden Dragon Formation in advance,” Long Moxiao said with a sigh.","The Bloodline Golden Dragon was powerful, but it had to be channeled using their bloodline power. While it wouldn’t shake their foundation, there was a limit to how long they could sustain it.","They had depleted half their energy strengthening the dragon breath, which resulted in the golden dragon silhouette becoming a tenth of its original size. If they continued the battle, they would have to hurt their foundation and stake their lives.","And against those two Saint-tier elders, there was no guarantee of victory even if they put their lives on the line.","It was wiser to retreat."]},{"number":6624,"title":"Chapter 6624: Chapter 6622: The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Sacred Formation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6622: The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Sacred Formation","The golden dragon silhouette continued to grow fainter until it dissipated entirely. Fortunately, they had already escaped to a safe place.","Nevertheless, the Dragon Breath Clan dared not linger. They took out their warships and continued their escape.","“It’s a relief that only our Dragon Breath Clan has attacked this base.” Long Mucheng heaved a sigh of relief.","It had been easier for them to escape because all their Dragon Breath Clansmen were inside the golden dragon silhouette. If other members of the Chu Clan Alliance were present as well, things might not have gone as well.","The spectators quickly scattered after the Dragon Breath Clan retreated, fearing that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion would take out their anger on them.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion didn’t bother pursuing those people. They were too busy celebrating their survival and cheering for their two Saint-tier elders.","The white lights imbuing the two Saint-tier elders had receded, and their complexions were paler than before. Channeling the sacred white light had taken a toll on them. However, their faces were beaming with joy.","Driving away the enemies and surviving a desperate situation made them feel as if they had gotten a new lease of life.","Most members didn’t understand what had just happened; they attributed it to their two Saint-tier elders being strong. However, the older members noticed something amiss.","“Milord, could that power be legendary...” an elder anxiously asked.","“Yes, the power of the Sacred Formation within us has been awakened. It’s all thanks to Lord Mansion Master,” the white-haired Saint-tier elder said.","There was a brief silence before deafening cheers broke out. They understood what this meant for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","The Sacred Formation was a formation their ancestors had left behind before heading to the Ninth Galaxy. It was their biggest insurance. The strongest members within the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were implanted with the Sacred Formation’s power.","But not everyone could withstand the power of the Sacred Formation. In fact, being able to withstand the Sacred Formation’s power was one of the criteria for becoming a Saint-tier elder.","Other than the 36 Saint-tier elders, the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the Shadow Corps’ leaders wielded the Sacred Formation’s power as well. Once the Sacred Formation was activated, no matter where they were, they would be able to tap into the Sacred Formation’s power.","This was the reason the two Saint-tier elders had experienced a surge in their strengths.","However, it was no easy feat to activate the Sacred Formation. In fact, no one in their generation had ever witnessed the Sacred Formation’s power, thus turning it into a legend.","But the Sacred Formation was finally activated, and the one who did it had to be their Mansion Master, Jie Tianran. In other words, Jie Tianran had accomplished a feat that even the previous Mansion Masters had failed at.","And they were right.","In the depths of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, a humongous formation spanning the size of a realm was enveloped in a white light. Even behemoths would look like a speck of dust in its presence.","Elders of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were gathered in the sky, looking down on the humongous formation. Their faces were beaming with excitement and joy. Some of them even had tears streaming from their faces.","This was the Sacred Formation.","The activation of the Sacred Formation would significantly boost the prowess of their top-tier fighting prowess. The Chu Clan Alliance no longer posed a threat to them.","Just then, a figure emerged from the blinding light like a deity.","The elders quickly dropped to their knees.","It was Jie Tianran. Upon learning about the situation, he returned to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion right away to activate the Sacred Formation.","In truth, it was a risky feat for him to unlock the Sacred Formation right now. He was not confident of pulling it off.","But he knew that he couldn’t deal with the Chu Clan Alliance alone, and the Netherworld Sect was a bunch of outsiders. It would be unwise to rely too much on them. To win this war, he needed to raise the overall prowess of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","The only solution he could think of was to activate the Sacred Formation, which past Mansion Masters had also attempted to activate but to no avail.","His face beamed with confidence now that he had succeeded, though this endeavor had weakened him as well.","“The Sacred Formation has been activated. All elders who carry the Sacred Formation’s power should be able to sense and tap into it now,” Jie Tianran declared.","“Lord Mansion Master is almighty! As long as Lord Mansion Master is around, that ragtag bunch known as the Chu Clan Alliance is nothing to be feared!” the elders exclaimed.","They meant those words from the bottom of their hearts. Their admiration for Jie Tianran was earnest.","“It’s not all my credit. This is the inheritance from our ancestors.” Jie Tianran humbly waved his hand, though his smile showed that he relished the compliments.","“The Sacred Formation is strong, but it is nigh impossible to activate it. Otherwise, it wouldn’t have become a legend in our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. It’s thanks to our Lord Mansion Master’s incredible means,” the elders said.","Many of them had advanced to Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists with Jie Tianran’s help, but they hadn’t been able to do anything when Chu Feng was sweeping through the Seven Realms Galaxy.","On top of that, the Dragon Breath Clan had abruptly grown stronger and began attacking their bases in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy. When they received a help request from the two Saint-tier elders stationed in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, they panicked.","Not even the Saint-tier elders could deal with the Chu Clan Alliance.","For a moment there, they thought that their Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was doomed.","But when the Sacred Formation was activated, their confidence returned. In fact, they had never felt this confident before.","“Enough with the bootlicking. I’m only doing what I should as the Mansion Master. Is there news from the Netherworld Sect while I was activating the Sacred Formation?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Lord Mansion Master, the Netherworld Sect declared war on Chu Feng and dispatched many Heavenly Gods to the Seven Realms Galaxy to reinforce us.”","“Oh? At least they aren’t too dumb.” Jie Tianran nodded in satisfaction.","“But...” The reporting elder suddenly looked conflicted."]},{"number":6625,"title":"Chapter 6625: Chapter 6623: God’s Era’s Phenomenon","paragraphs":["Chapter 6623: God’s Era’s Phenomenon","“Get to the point,” Jie Tianran said.","“Lord Mansion Master, we have coordinated with the Netherworld Sect’s reinforcement to ambush Chu Feng at places where the power fragments have fallen. We managed to find them, but Xianhai Yu’er was far stronger than we had expected.","“Despite being a rank one Heavenly God, she can raise her cultivation by four ranks, and her fighting prowess is incredible. Two Netherworld Marshals and Lord Jie Tongyou joined forces against her, but they were still no match for her. In the end, they had to retreat,” the elder said.","“Oh? To think that a rank one Heavenly God can raise their cultivation by four ranks.”","Jie Tianran narrowed his eyes. Even he felt uneasy about Xianhai Yu’er’s overwhelming talent. If she were already this powerful as a rank one Heavenly God, she would be unstoppable once she advanced to rank two Heavenly God.","“We’ll have to quickly eliminate Chu Feng and Xianhai Yu’er. Relay my orders. All Saint-tier elders are to put down whatever they are doing and immediately return to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.” Jie Tianran passed several scrolls stamped with his name to the elder.","“Yes, Lord Mansion Master.” The elder quickly left with the scrolls to relay the orders.","“What’s wrong? Are you panicking?” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body asked.","“Elder, I have nothing to worry about with you around, but I can’t let them continue growing like that. So, I decided to deal with them first before settling your matter. Please be assured that this won’t take too long, elder,” Jie Tianran replied.","“It’s fine. I was also thinking that you should call those Saint-tier elders back to support you. I doubt that they will be able to awaken those treasures anyway, considering their strengths. The most they can do is to plant those treasures across the galaxies,” the old entity replied.","“I’ll personally awaken those treasures after dealing with Chu Feng,” Jie Tianran said.","“Those treasures have to be awakened simultaneously. How do you intend to do that alone? Don’t worry about that. My body has recovered enough for me to awaken those treasures. You can do whatever you want from now on. I’ll deal with my affair by myself,” the old entity said.","“Elder, is that true?” Jie Tianran was taken aback.","He had raised the Saint-tier elders’ spirit power to rank five Heavenly Dragon because that was the minimum level they needed to be at to carry out the old entity’s tasks.","“I don’t talk big,” the old entity replied.","“It’s not that I doubt you, elder. I would have never obtained all those talisman papers if not for you. I’m asking because I don’t want to burden you. If you have recovered enough to settle this matter by yourself, I’m more than happy for you,” Jie Tianran said.","He was so happy that the frustrations he had felt after hearing about Xianhai Yu’er’s capabilities dissipated into thin air.","In the past, the Saint-tier elders had been an inconsequential existence to him. But after he sacrificed their lifespans to raise their spirit power to rank five Heavenly Dragon, they were no longer a negligible force in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","With so many rank five Heavenly Dragons on his side, he wouldn’t fear anyone.","Not to mention that his biggest backing was the old entity. If the old entity became stronger, he, too, would be in a safer position.","With that, he regained his confidence.","“You dare to declare war on me, Chu Feng? Very well, I shall let you know who you are going up against!” Jie Tianran sneered as adrenaline raced through his veins.","“Hm?”","Jie Tianran suddenly widened his eyes.","Ever since he activated the copper mirror, and the copper mirror appeared in God’s Era’s silhouette, he had felt a faint link with God’s Era. He could feel any changes that happened in God’s Era.","He quickly took out an observation treasure to examine God’s Era. What he saw astonished not just him but also the elders present.","A phenomenon had appeared inside the copper mirror of God’s Era’s silhouette. Nine-colored lightning crackled as nine incomparably powerful lightning beasts rampaged. The phenomenon was a mere reflection, but the crowd was still stunned by its might. It harnessed the power that could easily obliterate the world of cultivation.","Another figure appeared alongside the figure, and he towered in the sky.","Chu Feng.","He was clad in nine-colored lightning, and the nine-colored lightning was linked to the nine lightning beasts. They were a single entity.","Chu Feng’s appearance completely changed things.","When Jie Tianran first appeared in God’s Era’s silhouette, he had appeared to be the copper mirror’s master. It looked as if he had received God’s Era’s recognition. Some even wondered if he had already obtained God’s Era’s power and become its new master.","But Chu Feng’s appearance in the phenomenon changed things.","The Jie Tianran in God’s Era’s silhouette suddenly appeared small and insignificant. He stood alone on the ground, whereas Chu Feng towered in the sky with nine-colored lightning crackling around him.","Chu Feng was a god in the sky, while Jie Tianran was a mere mortal.","“How is this possible? Why did Chu Feng appear in God’s Era’s silhouette? Did he obtain a copper mirror or some other treasure in God’s Era?” someone murmured in shock before Jie Tianran could even speak.","That would have been so unfair to Jie Tianran.","Chu Feng had left prematurely, whereas Jie Tianran had gone through so many tribulations before he received some benefits and powers. Jie Tianran believed that the copper mirror was his biggest gain in God’s Era.","The elders present thought the same as well, which was why they were so shocked.","But they dared not to say too much, for they could sense the subtle changes in Jie Tianran’s mood.","Immense rage was boiling within Jie Tianran. He might not have uttered a word, but his fists were tightly clenched as he glared at Chu Feng’s figure in the copper mirror."]},{"number":6626,"title":"Chapter 6626: Chapter 6624: Trap","paragraphs":["Chapter 6624: Trap","Jie Tianran’s eyes reddened, and his veins popped. He had never appeared so unseemly before. His killing intent toward Chu Feng was stronger than ever. He had had enough of being one-upped by Chu Feng whenever he accomplished something.","He couldn’t understand why this kept happening, but it maddened him.","His anger stoked the unease of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elders. They dared not breathe loudly, fearing that Jie Tianran would vent his rage on them if they caught his attention at this sensitive moment.","But Jie Tianran didn’t vent his emotions. He closed his eyes instead.","When he reopened his eyes, his breathing had stabilized. It only took moments for him to get a grip on himself.","“You’re a stubborn grime that refuses to be washed away, Chu Feng, but the final victor will still be me,” Jie Tianran murmured.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng and the others were on their way back to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","An elder had noticed the changes in God’s Era through their warship’s observation formation, and he informed Chu Feng and the others right away.","Currently, Chu Feng and the others were standing before the observation formation.","When the crowd saw the contrast between Chu Feng and Jie Tianran’s figures in the phenomenon, with one looking like a god and the other a mortal, they swiftly turned to Chu Feng with heated eyes.","They thought that Chu Feng had gotten something huge from God’s Era. Otherwise, it didn’t make sense for him to appear in God’s Era’s silhouette, and in such a stunning fashion at that.","“Aren’t you a secretive one? You’re even hiding things from us now. You didn’t clue us in after doing something huge.” The Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s leader walked up to Chu Feng and slapped his back with a beaming smile.","The others also looked at Chu Feng excitedly. They thought that he must have done something to induce this phenomenon. They waited for him to speak up, curious to know what he had done or gotten from God’s Era.","“Big brother, could it be because you received the qualification to enter God’s Era?” Little Fishy asked.","The first thing Chu Feng did upon arriving at the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was to find the peculiar energy hidden among the power fragments. Later, he realized that the peculiar energy was actually the qualification to obtain God’s Era’s power.","Little Fishy had tried to comprehend that peculiar energy as well, but she failed.","Chu Feng succeeded, but nothing happened right away.","“It could be,” Chu Feng replied.","“God’s Era’s qualification?”","The crowd looked over with curious eyes. Chu Feng told them what happened.","“As expected of Chu Feng,” Ling Xiao remarked with a smile, even though it was just the qualification.","All of them had observed God’s Era’s power when it descended upon the Seven Realms Galaxy, but not a single one had noticed what Chu Feng saw. The chances were that Jie Tianran had also overlooked the qualification.","Otherwise, the phenomenon wouldn’t have shown Chu Feng towering over Jie Tianran.","“Our young master is truly incredible.”","The others from Seven Realms Sacred Mansion also heaped compliments on Chu Feng that came from the bottom of their hearts. They might not have joined Chu Feng on that journey, but as world spiritists, they could imagine the difficulty involved.","“Hm?”","The crowd suddenly widened their eyes.","The remaining two bundles of power rose from the palm of God’s Era’s silhouette, but they didn’t fly straight toward the Seven Realms Galaxy as the first one had.","Instead, they revolved around the silhouette erratically, sometimes fast and sometimes slow, sometimes brilliant like suns and sometimes melding into space.","“Look! Something is happening with God’s Era!”","The world spiritists on the warship immediately activated their observation-enhancing means. They instinctively understood that a secret must be hidden in the revolution of the two powers, and they wanted to do their part to help Chu Feng.","But Chu Feng turned around and returned to his room. “Don’t bother studying it. It’s a feint.”","All the world spiritists stiffened up. His words were like a pail of cold water dampening their hot-bloodedness.","“Chu Feng, could the initial part be a feint, but the secret lies in what comes after?” Ling Xiao anxiously asked.","“It’s not impossible, but based on what I have seen thus far, the chances of that happening are very low. It’s already grueling to observe these transformations, so there should be some clues woven into this as well, but I’m unable to discern anything at all. This seems to be an intentional measure to exhaust us. That’s why I don’t advise you all to waste too much time and energy on this,” Chu Feng replied before entering the palace.","Little Fishy, the guild leader, the lunatic, and even Ling Xiao followed him as well.","Most world spiritists also stopped observing the phenomenon. They had come to trust Chu Feng’s judgment after all that had happened. God’s Era appeared to be toying with those who coveted its power but lacked the capability for it.","If not for Chu Feng’s advice, they would have probably observed the phenomenon from the start to the end, wasting their time and effort.","But some continued to observe the phenomenon. It was not that they didn’t trust Chu Feng’s judgment, but they were reluctant to give up on this potential fortuitous encounter, even if it was a mirage. The odds might not be in their favor, but they still dreamt of making it big.","...","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had also noticed the changes in God’s Era.","A while later, Jie Tianran stopped his observation and instead tasked some elders who specialized in observation to continue.","He could tell this was a trap and didn’t want to squander more energy on it, though he told the elders to continue observing in case there were clues woven into it.","Jie Tianran intended to leave the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Didn’t you just command those Saint-tier elders to return to deal with your grandson?” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body asked.","“There is still time. I have more important things to attend to now. I won’t make it in time if I don’t go now,” Jie Tianran said as he took out a compass."]},{"number":6627,"title":"Chapter 6627: Chapter 6625: Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s Hiding Spot","paragraphs":["Chapter 6625: Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s Hiding Spot","The compass was covered in stars. Each star represented a realm, and countless realms came together to form a majestic starfield. In this starfield, one star shone exceptionally brightly. Light pulsated from it peculiarly, as if it were the leader controlling all the changes in this starfield.","It was a humongous formation involving the entire starfield!","“Oh? The compass is reacting. The Celestial Master Sacred Sect hasn’t been wiped out yet?” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body spoke grimly.","“I thought they were all dead. I’m surprised that they had lain low for so long before making a move. I wonder what gave them the confidence to do so,” Jie Tianran scoffed.","Even in the earlier years of the present era, each galaxy was already ruled by an overlord. However, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had two overlords—the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Celestial Master Sacred Sect.","As that era was dominated by the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Celestial Master Sacred Sect had joined forces in order to reinforce their standing in the world of cultivation.","But after the experts of the Ancestral Martial Galaxy left for the Ninth Galaxy, the world of cultivation inevitably faced a reshuffling of power. In particular, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Celestial Master Sacred Sect, as fellow world spiritist powers, began fighting over world spiritist resources.","As a result, those two old allies became competitors instead.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion won in the end.","Even though the Celestial Master Sacred Sect was pushed to the brink of extinction, some of their experts still escaped. Determined to eliminate the threat from its root, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion continued to hunt down the members of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect.","While the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was successful in cornering some of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s remnants, they were unable to capture their true powerhouses. This had something to do with the ideologies of the two sects.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion believed that world spiritists should prioritize their spirit power cultivation, whereas the Celestial Master Sacred Sect believed in forging powerful world spiritist treasures to enhance one’s strength.","While the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had the upper hand in a direct clash, the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s array of world spiritist treasures made it extremely difficult to hunt them down once they went into hiding.","After the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion took over the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s old territories, they grew stronger and began to gain a stronger grasp of world spiritist treasures. With that, they were able to find some of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s hiding spots.","However, they soon realized that the Celestial Master Sacred Sect had constructed a humongous concealment and protection formation using over ten thousand treasures spread across a starfield. It wouldn’t be easy to conquer it.","So, they pretended not to know about the hiding spot while secretly constructing a formation around it. The hiding spot was marked on the compass.","This matter was kept confidential and only passed down through the generations of Mansion Masters along with the compass.","“They must be confident if they have chosen to reveal themselves. Your ancestors may have prepared a formation to curb them, but are you sure you’ll be able to deal with them?” the old entity inside Jie Tianran asked.","Jie Tianran was a world spiritist with great potential, but he was still lacking compared to the powerhouses who dominated the early years of the present era.","The Celestial Master Sacred Sect could prove to be a troublesome foe if they still had powerhouses from the earlier years, and those powerhouses had regained their strength.","“I believe that the formation left by my ancestors isn’t for show, and I have you here with me. Furthermore, the Celestial Master Sacred Sect has many treasures that are useful to Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists. They took those treasures with them when they fled. It’ll greatly benefit the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion if we can obtain those treasures,” Jie Tianran said.","“I won’t be able to help you much right now. You’ll be entrusting your fate to your ancestors’ formation if you insist on going,” the old entity said.","Jie Tianran didn’t respond, but his face beamed with confidence. He waved his hand and covered himself in a concealment formation, thus disappearing from sight.","...","Chu Feng and the others finally arrived at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city.","The Chu Clan Alliance, including the Dragon Breath Clan, was waiting for them at the entrance. They were surprised to see that Chu Feng was accompanied by members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but they quickly accepted the matter after learning that Chu Feng had taken them in.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was a behemoth, after all. It would be extreme to alienate all of their members, including those who had already defected from them.","In fact, Long Mucheng saw it as a good thing. These people knew the inner workings of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, so they could provide them with critical intelligence required to deal with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Long Mucheng told Chu Feng and the others about the two Saint-tier elders’ transformation.","“That’s a drastic change. Could it be the Sacred Formation?”","Ling Xiao’s grandfather and the others looked grim.","“What’s the Sacred Formation?” Chu Feng, Long Mucheng, and the others asked.","“I have heard about the Sacred Formation, but are you sure it is that Sacred Formation?” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","Based on what he knew, no one had been able to activate the Sacred Formation for several generations now.","“You mentioned that their bodies and hair were imbued in a white light, right? Did it look something like that?”","Ling Xiao’s grandfather waved his sleeves, and his spirit power morphed into a white light that enveloped his body. He was conjuring the appearance of the Sacred Formation based on what was stated in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s records.","“Yes, it looked exactly like that,” Long Mucheng replied.","“It really is the Sacred Formation? This is terrible.”","Nervous discussions broke out among the members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Ling Xiao’s grandfather proceeded to explain to Chu Feng, Long Mucheng, and the others about the powerful capabilities of the Sacred Formation.","All of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Saint-tier elders had reached rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists. They would make terrifying enemies if they could tap into the Sacred Formation’s power on top of that.","“It’s fine. We have nothing to fear, no matter how many rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists they have. We’re safe in here anyway. They won’t be a threat anymore once Miss Yu’er reaches rank two Heavenly God. It’ll be our time to massacre them then. Isn’t that right, Miss Yu’er?” Long Mucheng asked Little Fishy.","She had learned that Little Fishy had defeated two rank five Heavenly God Netherworld Sectmembers.","“If they are just rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, I should be able to deal with them without making a breakthrough to rank two Heavenly God,” Little Fishy said confidently.","“Really? Shall we give it a try now?” Long Mucheng’s eyes gleamed in excitement.","She was feeling frustrated at being pushed back by those two Saint-tier elders, and she was also curious to know how strong Little Fishy currently was. The notion that a rank one Heavenly God could actually deal with rank five Heavenly Dragons sounded implausible to her, and that only further stoked her curiosity."]},{"number":6628,"title":"Chapter 6628: Chapter 6626: Let Me Show You","paragraphs":["Chapter 6626: Let Me Show You","“Big brother, can I give it a try?” Little Fishy turned to Chu Feng and asked.","“Sure. I want to know what they are doing in our Ancestral Martial Galaxy as well. But let’s first split the power fragments before you go.”","Chu Feng opened his palm, and a surge of energy flowed out. This energy was a top-tier cultivation resource.","However, Little Fishy quickly realized that there was a restriction on the cultivation resource. After assimilating a portion of it, she found that she couldn’t assimilate any more, no matter how she tried.","Chu Feng gave it a try, but it was the same.","So, he decided to share the energy with the others. There was no point holding onto it anyway.","“What is that?”","Be they cultivators or world spiritists, the crowd was mesmerized and drawn to the energy.","“This is the energy from God’s Era that descended into the Seven Realms Galaxy. I have refined them to enhance their effectiveness for cultivation, but there is a limit to how much each individual can absorb it, and it is more effective on those with lower cultivation. It won’t be very useful to Heavenly Gods, though it still helps.”","Chu Feng shared the energy with the crowd, though he prioritized his older friends like Long Mucheng, the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, Xia Xingchen, the Totem Nine Daoists, and even Ling Xiao.","“There isn’t enough energy for everyone, so you can decide for yourself how you want to distribute it,” Chu Feng said.","“Young master Chu Feng, we can’t accept such invaluable energy from you. You should keep it for yourself,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather said.","Chu Feng had put his life on the line to take these power fragments from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. It was one thing for him to share the energy with those whom he had braved life and death with, but Ling Xiao’s grandfather didn’t think that they were deserving of it.","“We’re one family now that you are following me. It’s only right for you to take a portion as well. Besides, you’ll know that I’m telling the truth once you assimilate the energy. I have reached the limit of how much I can assimilate, so the rest is useless to me. Take it.”","Chu Feng forcefully handed the energy to Ling Xiao’s grandfather.","Even though he was on good terms with Ling Xiao, he could tell that Ling Xiao’s grandfather commanded greater prestige among the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members.","“Chu Feng, this energy is from God’s Era. Is it possible that it may serve other purposes as well?” Long Chengyu asked.","Those who had received the energy also didn’t assimilate it right away.","“This energy can only be used for cultivation. Please don’t hesitate to use it,” Chu Feng said.","He had also considered those possibilities. Based on what he had observed, this energy wouldn’t help him in the fight for God’s Era’s final power.","“Share it with the others,” the lunatic said as she handed a big bundle of God’s Era’s energy to Chu Feng.","“Chu Feng, you can share mine with the others as well.” The guild leader also took out the energy she had collected.","“All right.”","The additional energy wouldn’t benefit the guild leader and the lunatic anyway due to the restriction, so Chu Feng took their bundles of energy and shared them with the others as well. However, there were so many people that there still wasn’t enough to go around.","“Big brother, why don’t you share my portion with...” Little Fishy sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng had shared half of the power fragments he had extracted from the Seven Realms Galaxy with Little Fishy, so she had a huge amount of it as well.","“Yu’er, the energy might be useful to your clansmen. I think you should keep it for the time being,” Chu Feng replied.","Following that, Chu Feng went to look for Sikong Changsheng. It was thanks to the latter that the Chu Clan Alliance could seek refuge in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. Naturally, it was only right for him to share a portion of God’s Era’s energy with him as well.","Despite the restriction, he gave Sikong Changsheng a bundle containing energy that was several times over the limit to express his utmost gratitude. He figured that Sikong Changsheng could just distribute the excess energy to whoever he wanted to.","“It is good stuff.” Sikong Changsheng was mesmerized by the energy. Moments later, he sighed. “If not for the limit, you could have reached Heavenly God level and beyond with the energy you have just given out. What a pity.”","“The path of cultivation is destined not to be smooth-sailing. It’s normal for good resources to come with restrictions. It’s fortunate that God’s Era has other powers. I sense that the remaining powers are different from the one that entered the Seven Realms Galaxy. If I can obtain them, I should be able to reach Heavenly God level.”","Chu Feng looked forward to reaching Heavenly God.","“That would be for the best. Do you intend to deal with the two Saint-tier elders from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion next?” Sikong Changsheng asked.","He was aware of the conversations Chu Feng had with the others.","“Yes. I want to know what they are doing,” Chu Feng replied.","“Go ahead. I also want to know what they are doing as well. They had dispatched all their Saint-tier elders not just to the Ancestral Martial but the other galaxies as well. I tried to observe them, but they have taken precautions to avoid my probing,” Sikong Changsheng said.","“Jie Tianran is definitely up to no good.” Chu Feng nodded.","After chatting with Sikong Changsheng, he went back to find Little Fishy. He was planning to confront the two Saint-tier elders with just the two of them, but Long Mucheng insisted on joining them together with the Dragon Breath Clan.","Considering that Long Mucheng had reached rank five Heavenly God, Chu Feng agreed.","Worst comes to worst, he could just ask the Divine Deer to take all of them to safety.","Just as they were about to set off, a person walked out and said, “Chu Feng, let me show you my skills this time.”"]},{"number":6629,"title":"Chapter 6629: Chapter 6627: Fei","paragraphs":["Chapter 6627: Fei","It was Song Changsheng’s disciple, Fei.","“Who is this child?” Long Mucheng asked.","None of them had paid attention to Fei because of his childlike appearance. They assumed that he was merely a child from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Who are you calling a child?” Fei scoffed.","“This child from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion doesn’t have any manners.”","The Dragon Breath Clansmen were displeased by Fei’s disrespectful attitude toward Long Mucheng.","“You brats don’t have any manners. I am older than all of you,” Fei said as he revealed his rank four Heavenly God level cultivation.","This shocked not just the Dragon Breath Clansmen but also Long Mucheng.","“Huh? This child... Chu Feng, where did you find this monster from?”","Long Mucheng realized that the boy wasn’t with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. The latter was likely some powerful entity whom Chu Feng had befriended. Even though she had reached rank five Heavenly God level, she had obtained that strength from her bloodline metamorphosis. With her previous talent and bloodline, there was no way she could have reached this height.","For that reason, she wouldn’t underestimate a rank four Heavenly God.","“He is Elder Song Changsheng’s disciple,” Chu Feng introduced Fei to the others.","He had chatted with Fei along the way, and the latter had said that there was no need to conceal his identity. While Song Changsheng preferred to steer clear of such battles, he wasn’t worried about having his identity exposed, either.","That was why Chu Feng told the truth to Long Mucheng and the others.","After a quick conversation, Long Mucheng and the others realized that Fei came from a formidable background, and they were curious to know if Fei was merely bragging or if he could easily subdue a rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","Even though Fei had failed to subdue his opponent in the previous battle, Chu Feng did not doubt Fei’s strength. If anything, he was curious to know how strong Fei was. If the latter were as strong as Little Fishy, he would be a huge asset to them.","After a brief introduction, Chu Feng and the others began making their way over to confront the two Saint-tier elders.","The Ancestral Martial Galaxy was much smaller than other galaxies. Given the means that Chu Feng and the others wielded now, it didn’t take them long to traverse across space and arrive at the realm where the two Saint-tier elders were stationed.","Even from afar, they saw many spectators lingering in the area.","They had previously gathered here to witness the clash between the Chu Clan Alliance and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Since the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion didn’t go after them, they decided to stay behind and see if anything else would happen.","Unfortunately, Chu Feng’s old friends, Wang Yuxian and Mo Yuhan, had already left.","Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and the Dragon Breath Clansmen remained in concealment, while Fei rushed straight into the realm.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng surveyed the realm using his Heaven’s Eyes. He was able to peer through the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation, but he didn’t notice much other than the formation energy lingering in the realm.","Next, he tried using the Three Realms Divine Eyes, but he also didn’t discern anything much.","This suggested that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion didn’t have other ulterior motives in mind when they set up a base here.","“Chu Feng, did you find anything?” Long Mucheng asked.","“I didn’t find anything, but they are currently packing up. It seems like they are planning to leave,” Chu Feng replied.","Just then, Fei’s tiny silhouette arrived before the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s barrier. He arrogantly pointed a finger down at the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and snorted, “Old things from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, get out here right now! I shall obliterate you today!”","Boom!","A light beam shot out from the barrier and instantly devoured Fei whole.","“Hm?”","The two Saint-tier elders meditating in the realm opened their eyes. Initially, they weren’t bothered by Fei as they thought that he was merely a passerby who didn’t know his place. However, they had no choice but to take him seriously now.","Their defensive formation was strong enough to disintegrate even a rank one Heavenly God, but it failed to harm Fei in the least.","“Who are you?” the white-haired elder asked grimly.","“I am the one who will kill you,” Fei snorted as he revealed his rank four Heavenly God aura.","“A mere rank four Heavenly God dares to speak so arrogantly!”","The black-haired elder unleashed a gigantic palm reminiscent of a mountain at Fei.","Fei harrumphed fearlessly in the face of the palm strike, not bothering to make any evasive maneuvers.","The next moment, the palm struck him.","A blood fog scattered from where he previously stood, and he was sent flying from the realm like a comet.","“Huh? Is he unable to raise his cultivation?” Long Mucheng asked Chu Feng.","She had witnessed the earlier clash. The palm strike didn’t kill Fei, but it crushed his bones, meridians, and muscles. His face was mashed up, and he was bleeding profusely.","“Wait. Something is wrong.” Long Mucheng widened her eyes in astonishment.","The others also sensed that something was amiss, be it Little Fishy, the Dragon Breath Clansmen, or even the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. All of them raised their heads and looked at the sky.","A humongous silhouette had appeared in the sky.","It was so huge that those with weaker cultivation only saw a blood-red sun outside the realm. However, those with sharper eyes saw a pupil embedded in the sun. That was not a sun but a gigantic blood eye!","“What is that? Is that a phenomenon?”","Even those from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were flustered, let alone the spectators. They couldn’t see what was going on, and that only further stoked their panic.","But the two Saint-tier elders saw it clearly.","It was an incomparably massive monster with a white cow head and a snake tail. It towered above the realm while gazing on the beings below with its sole, blood-red eye. Shockingly, its body was even larger than this Upper Realm.","“Is this... that boy?”","The two Saint-tier elders felt an ominous feeling. This behemoth was a rank five Heavenly God.","Shoosh!","The humongous silhouette suddenly vanished.","Boom!","The world shook.","Something pierced a hole right through the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s barrier, breaching its defenses.","A ten-meter-tall monstrous beast appeared above the barrier. It stood like a human, but its appearance was identical to the behemoth that had towered above the realm earlier. On top of that, its two front hooves had transformed into sharp claws, serving as its hands.","The monstrous beast stretched its neck as if getting warmed up.","“Not bad. Saint-tier elders are quite something. It only took one strike for me to get warmed up,” the monstrous beast spoke calmly, but its powerful voice had a penetrative quality resembling a bestial roar, causing the surroundings to quake.","The voice might be different, but it spoke in the same tone as Fei."]},{"number":6630,"title":"Chapter 6630: Chapter 6628: The Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s Four Elders","paragraphs":["Chapter 6628: The Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s Four Elders","“Black hair, your earlier strike got me all pumped up. As a reward, I shall grant you the same exhilaration,” Fei said to the black-haired elder before vanishing once more.","The two Saint-tier elders felt an ominous sense of foreboding. They immediately channeled the Sacred Formation. Light enveloped their bodies, greatly boosting their fighting prowess.","When Fei reappeared, he was already standing right beside the black-haired elder. His claws shot forth to grab the latter’s head and burst it.","Despite the Sacred Formation’s buff, the black-haired elder still struggled to keep up with Fei’s movements. This made it extremely difficult for him to evade the attack, so he had no choice but to construct a barrier in front of him instead.","At the same time, the white-haired elder constructed a slaughter formation to attack Fei.","But Fei’s claws pierced right through the black-haired elder’s barrier, and he shredded it apart. The powerful barrier was as brittle as paper to him.","At the same time, he jolted his arm to exert a martial power shockwave. It neutralized the white-haired elder’s slaughter formation.","“Let’s go!”","The white-haired elder widened his eyes in fright. He immediately formed a hand seal. Teleportation energy imbued him, and he vanished into thin air.","The black-haired elder quickly did the same.","“Trying to escape? Do you think I’d let you?” Fei roared.","A green aura gushed forth from his body. It corroded everything it touched, including space. Those from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion let out screams of agony as the green aura corroded their bodies as well.","However, the two Saint-tier elders remained nowhere to be seen.","“Shit, they got away. This paints me in a bad light,” Fei murmured.","But there was nothing he could do anymore, so he looted the battlefield with a wave of his hand. The spectators stared at him in absolute horror, unable to recover from the shock.","“You can take these. I don’t need it.”","The loot included not just treasures but the world spiritists’ origin energies as well.","Chu Feng accepted the origin energies while remarking, “Brother Fei, you have concealed your ability well.”","Fei responded with an awkward smile. It wounded his pride how he had spoken grandly but still allowed those two fellows to slip away.","“They had prepared that teleportation formation a long time ago. They could have taken everyone with them, but they panicked upon witnessing your means. They immediately chose to abandon the others and focused the teleportation energy on themselves,” Chu Feng said.","As strong as Fei was, the two Saint-tier elders weren’t pushovers, either.","While the two Saint-tier elders were indeed weaker than Fei, they weren’t so weak as to immediately fall in defeat against him. They had only fled because they were intimidated by his prowess.","“Fei, does your energy swiftly deplete in that form?” Little Fishy asked out of curiosity.","Under normal circumstances, abilities that raised one’s cultivation could only be maintained for short periods, be it her bloodline power, Chu Feng’s Lightning Armor, or even the two Saint-tier elders’ Sacred Formation.","That was why they undid those abilities as soon as the battle ended to avoid unnecessary energy consumption.","But Fei continued to maintain his monstrous beast form, showing no inclination to revert to his human boy form.","Chu Feng answered on Fei’s behalf, “If I’m not mistaken, this is Brother Fei’s true body. His human form was not just a disguise but also a limiter on his cultivation.”","In his view, it didn’t look like Fei had used any means to raise his cultivation. Rather, it felt like Fei’s base cultivation was already at rank five Heavenly God.","“Amazing, Chu Feng. You saw right through me! Yes, that boy form is a seal my master imposed on me to suppress my bloodthirst. This dashing body that you see right now is my original form,” Fei replied.","The crowd was rendered speechless. Even if they were to stretch the definition of ‘dashing’, they still wouldn’t call Fei’s current appearance that.","“Can I ask about your background?” Long Mucheng asked out of curiosity.","She had a feeling that Fei’s bloodline was much stronger than theirs, especially considering the ability he had just showcased.","“Hehe, that’s a secret. You just have to know that I am very strong,” Fei said gleefully while intentionally looking at Little Fishy.","Little Fishy smiled, and that further fanned Fei’s glee.","In truth, Little Fishy’s smile didn’t have any deeper meaning. She merely found Fei funny.","Chu Feng flew into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s base and constructed a formation to examine the area. However, he still failed to find anything peculiar. In the end, he had no choice but to give up and return.","Meanwhile, the two Saint-tier elders continued to flee despite having escaped. At the same time, they used their observation means to keep track of what was happening in the Upper Realm. From that, they saw Chu Feng entering their territory together with Fei.","“That monster is in cahoots with Chu Feng?”","The two Saint-tier elders frowned.","They thought that they could make quick work of the Chu Clan Alliance now that they had activated the Sacred Formation, only to realize that they still hadn’t fully uncovered its depths. Who knew how many more secret hands the Chu Clan Alliance still had?","“With such monsters in the Chu Clan Alliance’s ranks, we’ll have to avoid clashing head-on against them. What should we do next?” the black-haired elder asked.","“We’ll follow Lord Mansion Master’s instructions and wait for reinforcements. We won’t make a move for now, but we’ll continue observing the situation and update Lord Mansion Master,” the white-haired elder replied.","Meanwhile, in the Seven Realms Galaxy, Jie Tianran followed his compass and arrived at a barren realm covered in boundless mountains.","A spatial realm was hidden here.","This spatial realm felt like it was constructed out of a single entity; be it the earth or the mountains, it felt like everything was connected. It was just not just a realm to reside in. Everything obeyed a natural cycle, and tremendous power amassed in the form of a gleaming river.","This gleaming river flowed through the mountains and converged as a golden ocean in the spatial realm’s center. Countless world spiritist treasures lay at the bottom of the golden ocean, where they were being nourished.","Not all world spiritist treasures were equal. There were golden and bronze treasures, but there were also a handful of black treasures that emanated a divine dark-red aura. These treasures absorbed the golden ocean’s fluid at a pace much faster than the other treasures.","There was a manmade island above the golden ocean, and five figures were gathered at the center of the island.","Four of them were extremely old—three men and one woman. Their backs were bent, and they relied on canes to support their bodies. They had hardly any hair left on their heads, and some of their teeth were missing as well.","But despite appearing to be on the verge of death, they were all dressed in formidable equipment. Their robes, their accessories, and even their shoes emanated divine glows, a clear sign that they were invaluable treasures.","Whether it was the effect of their treasures or their spirit power, they were all spirited despite their aged appearances.","The fifth person accompanying them was a young woman, Fu Xing.","“Fu Xing, we have to thank you for infiltrating the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and obtaining the crucial item. Otherwise, we wouldn’t have been able to recover so quickly. After so many years of lying low, it’s finally time for our Celestial Master Sacred Sect to exact vengeance on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” one of the old men said.","“Milord, I am only doing what I should.” Fu Xing bowed deeply to the old man before turning to the old woman. “Master, have you and the other three milords considered my earlier proposal to work with Chu Feng?”"]},{"number":6631,"title":"Chapter 6631: Chapter 6629: Complete Obliteration","paragraphs":["Chapter 6629: Complete Obliteration","The three old men fell silent. The old woman, Fu Xing’s master, slowly spoke up, “Xing’er, the young man you mentioned, Chu Feng, sounds like a rare talent, but we also cannot refute the fact that he is the grandson of the incumbent Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master. Who can guarantee that he isn’t just putting on an act to trap us? I don’t think we know him well enough yet to work with him.”","“Master, I can guarantee that Jie Tianran and Chu Feng are nemeses. There is no kinship whatsoever between them. Jie Tianran is a monster. He killed even Chu Feng’s grandmother. Chu Feng has declared war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, and so far, he has shown no mercy to their members. We should join hands with him since we have a common enemy,” Fu Xing said.","“Xing’er, our Celestial Master Sacred Sect has lain low for a long time for this day. We can’t afford to take any risks. Our cultivation hasn’t recovered to its peak yet, but it should be more than enough to deal with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. There is no reason for us to take on additional risk,” Fu Xing’s master said.","Fu Xing knew that there was no point trying to convince them anymore.","The four elders before her were the true disciples of the sect founder. They were the old ancestors of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect.","Fu Xing had no say in their presence. She could only obey their orders.","“Fu Xing, don’t blame your master for this decision. She has her considerations. We do not doubt that you have our sect’s best interests at heart, and we are aware of your contributions.","“The sectmaster’s seat has been empty for all these years because we are reserving it for you. It’s just that you’re still young, and you’ll need to be stronger to make the others submit to you. Once you reach Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, the sectmaster position will be yours.”","Fearing that Fu Xing would feel jarred by their decision, an old man spoke up to console her.","The others also voiced their agreement.","“Thank you, milords.” Fu Xing bowed to the four elders.","She didn’t continue harping on this matter, knowing that her master and the others had already discussed the matter. No matter who she asked, they would give her the same answer.","“All right. Now that we are almost recovered, let’s focus on the business at hand. Let’s first deplete the energy before setting off. We shall carve our name right into the minds of every Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s member,” one of the old men said as he formed a hand seal.","His eyes gleamed expectantly.","The other three also formed hand seals, and tremendous spirit power flowed into the island.","It turned out that the island was a formation core.","The formation whirred into action. The golden ocean began bubbling furiously as its water level swiftly plummeted. Its fluid was being swiftly absorbed by the world spiritist treasures stacked at the bottom of the golden ocean.","Meanwhile, the other Celestial Master Sacred Sectmembers in this bronze realm had already gathered. In total, they numbered a million. It paled in comparison to the galaxy overlords, who easily had billions in their ranks, but these sectmembers, be it those from the older generations or juniors, were strong among their peers.","They were elites.","But none of them stepped forward to help the four elders. Instead, they formed a defensive formation as if guarding against something.","The answer was soon revealed.","A loud buzzing sound resonated within the bronze realm. Cracks appeared all around as if the realm was being torn apart.","Yet, not a single person looked surprised or flustered. Instead, they looked excited.","They knew the bronze realm was collapsing because the four elders were squeezing every last bit of energy from it to nourish the world spiritist treasures.","The bronze realm had protected them from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but it had also trapped them within it. Fu Xing had to resort to a special method to leave the bronze realm, and even so, it had taken a lot out of her before she succeeded.","Many Celestial Master Sacred Sectmembers had never left the bronze realm since their birth, and they looked forward to venturing into the world of cultivation.","Soon, the bronze realm shattered into countless fragments.","A boundless mountain range appeared beneath their feet.","The sectmembers cheered, knowing that they had finally entered the real world of cultivation.","Boom!","Just then, a burst of spirit power abruptly descended from the sky and pierced the formation maintained by the million Celestial Master Sacred Sectmembers, vanquishing them from the face of the world before they could even react.","The faces of the four elders warped in horror. Everything had happened so quickly that it was too late by the time they registered what was happening.","Fu Xing’s master immediately pulled Fu Xing behind her to protect her while stuffing a teleportation talisman paper into her hand. Then, she glared at the sky together with the other three old men.","A person had been waiting for them—Jie Tianran.","A compass floated beside him.","Fu Xing’s master and the others immediately realized what was going on. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion must have known all this while that they were hiding here, and they were biding their chance to strike.","To think that they were completely oblivious to it!","Jie Tianran studied an ancient scroll before looking at Fu Xing’s master and the others.","“Yuchi Qingchuan, Zhongli Yichen, Sikong Yunzhou, Ouyang Tianxing—it really is the four of you. I’m surprised that you four old things have survived to this day. If even trash like you is still alive, I can be assured that our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elders in the Ninth Galaxy are faring well,” Jie Tianran said with a mocking laugh.","“Die!”","One of the old men formed a hand seal, and a deluge of spirit power gushed out into the surroundings. The spirit power formed several humongous spirit power hands that covered the sky.","The hands moved, and giant spirit power bows appeared in their grasp. Amid deafening sonic booms, several massive spirit power arrows were shot at Jie Tianran.","However, Jie Tianran stood fearlessly against the arrows.","“Rank six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist? Looks like you haven’t recovered to your peak. If this is all you have, I don’t even need to use the Sacred Mansion’s formation. Your Celestial Master Sacred Sect has long outlived its time. Let me put an end to this farce once and for all.”","With a wave of his sleeve, his spirit power manifested into a sword that swept across the sky, crushing every one of the spirit power arrows.","Fu Xing’s master and the others were shocked.","The four of them were rank six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, whereas Jie Tianran was a rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. This meant that Jie Tianran wielded heaven-defying battle power!"]},{"number":6632,"title":"Chapter 6632: Chapter 6630: The Remaining Seed of Hope","paragraphs":["Chapter 6630: The Remaining Seed of Hope","“Oh? Isn’t that Fu Xing? Fu Xing, Fu Xing[1]. Your goal all along is to bring the Celestial Master Sacred Sect back to its former glory. It’s even in your name. Indeed, outsiders cannot be trusted to be loyal to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I ended up taking in a spy like you.”","Jie Tianran glared at Fu Xing with vicious eyes.","Fu Xing was one of the notable talents who had joined the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion through its entrance examination, so Jie Tianran had heard about her.","However, he didn’t bother conducting a background check as he had thought that those who joined the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion would be grateful to them. It didn’t cross his mind that Fu Xing could have an ulterior motive for joining them.","Shoosh!","Before Fu Xing could reply, a powerful surge of spirit power suddenly enveloped her. It was such a thorough seal that she couldn’t even see or hear anything outside.","She could tell that the spirit power was from her master. Her master must have been trying to protect her from being caught up in the imminent battle with Jie Tianran, but its defense was so thorough that it isolated her from the world.","Even so, she could still hear loud clangs and feel the spirit power shaking.","Soon, powerful teleportation energy seeped in from the outside.","“Xing’er, activate the teleportation talisman paper and escape!” her master anxiously instructed her telepathically.","“Master, can you hear me? I won’t leave. I want to face this with you!” Fu Xing panicked.","Her master wouldn’t have asked her to flee if they were winning the fight against Jie Tianran. This could only mean that her master and the three elders had determined that their defeat was inevitable.","This didn’t bode well.","“What nonsense are you spouting? Your presence here only hinders us! Hurry up and leave!” her master shouted in a mix of anxiety and frustration.","At the same time, Fu Xing noticed that the teleportation energy flowing into the barrier was becoming impure. Another energy had seeped into the teleportation energy. Jie Tianran must be interfering with the teleportation energy to stop her from leaving.","So, Fu Xing immediately formed a hand seal and activated the teleportation talisman.","The teleportation talisman transformed into a powerful rush of teleportation energy that enveloped her. A teleportation passageway appeared in front of her, and she was immediately pulled into it.","“I’m surprised that you managed to send her out, but she’s nothing compared to my grandson, Jie Tian. Do you really think that she can make a difference?” Jie Tianran sneered.","The realm had been destroyed.","The boundless mountain range had been reduced to a boundless pit. The sky was littered with spatial fragments.","But Jie Tianran stood unharmed in the sky, gazing down with disdainful eyes.","In contrast, Fu Xing’s master and the others had pale faces, even though their armor was still overflowing with energy and emanating brilliant lights. Their profuse perspiration and labored breathing showed that they were strained.","“Ah, I know. You sent her away so that she can at least burn joss paper for you next year, right?” Jie Tianran sneered.","The four exchanged looks of conviction. They simultaneously formed hand seals, and a terrifying energy gushed forth from their bodies. Everything that came into contact with the energy was destroyed.","“You want to drag me down with you?” Jie Tianran narrowed his eyes.","He didn’t expect the four to make such a decision after a brief clash. This energy could easily kill him if he were to be devoured by it. Yet, he remained perfectly calm.","“May you have a smooth journey. I’ll be taking the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s treasures.”","His compass unleashed a powerful surge of spirit power, enveloping not just him but also the far reaches of the realm.","...","Meanwhile, Fu Xing emerged from the teleportation passageway. As soon as she stepped out, she felt an intense spatial quake. She turned around and saw a distant realm being destroyed, reduced into fragments that floated in space.","That was the realm she had just escaped from.","Fu Xing trembled so much that she struggled to maintain her balance and fell to her bottom. She had to rely on treasures to get back up.","She hurriedly took out a delicate box from her Cosmos Sack and opened it. What she saw left tears streaming down her face.","The life tokens bound to the four elders had shattered.","Fu Xing was anguished, but she wasn’t surprised. Despite being a far distance away, she could sense their auras from the energy that destroyed the realm.","The four elders had sacrificed their lives to employ this means.","Kacha!","Fu Xing widened her eyes. Her master’s life token had shattered once more, and spirit power drifted out from it to form several lines of words.","“Xing’er, if you see these words, it would mean that I have failed. I was incompetent, but perhaps this is heaven’s will. Your little body has shouldered great responsibilities from the moment you were born. You have suffered too much trying to restore glory to the Celestial Master Sacred Sect.","“From this day on, you are free.","“You are no longer a Celestial Master Sacred Sectmember; you are Fu Xing. Don’t sacrifice yourself for the Celestial Master Sacred Sect anymore, and don’t seek to exact vengeance for us. Enter the Ninth Galaxy and live the life you want.”","Fu Xing’s breathing hastened upon seeing those words. Before she knew it, she had already broken down in tears.","Everything felt like a dream. She dared not believe this to be reality.","It was such a despairing dream.","She thought that the Celestial Master Sacred Sect could finally make a comeback after so many years, only for it to end in such a plight before it could even begin its vengeance.","For many years, they had tolerated and toiled, all just for this.","She couldn’t accept this outcome.","Just then, a familiar voice echoed from the distance that deepened her anguish.","“Fu Xing, hide yourself well. Don’t let me find you. Otherwise, those four old things would have sacrificed themselves in vain.”","It was Jie Tianran.","The four elders had sacrificed their lives to unleash a devastating attack to drag Jie Tianran down to hell with them... yet Jie Tianran survived the attack?","1. Fu Xing means to restore something to its former glory ☜"]},{"number":6633,"title":"Chapter 6633: Chapter 6631: The Netherworld Sect’s Treasure","paragraphs":["Chapter 6631: The Netherworld Sect’s Treasure","“Hide well, Fu Xing. I’ll be taking the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s treasures,” Jie Tianran announced.","He was projecting his voice in all directions, so those in nearby realms could hear him as well. The earlier explosion had caused quite a commotion, and Jie Tianran’s words gave the others a clue as to what had happened.","They figured it was related to the remnants of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect, and from the sounds of it, Jie Tianran had vanquished them all.","Fu Xing’s eyes flared with killing intent, but she didn’t make a reckless move. She knew better than to make a reckless move, or else she would be letting her master down.","But what could she do?","She thought about Chu Feng. She knew there was not much she could do right now, but perhaps Chu Feng could help her. Thus, she began making her way toward the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","Jie Tianran had spoken those words aloud not just to mock Fu Xing, but also to build his prestige. He wanted the world to know that not even the Celestial Master Sacred Sect, despite many years of preparations, was a match for him.","Needless to say, the Chu Clan Alliance wouldn’t stand a chance, either.","...","Jie Tianran rushed back to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion after he was done cleaning up the Celestial Master Sacred Sect.","On the way back, he inspected the world spiritist treasures he had obtained from them. The corners of his lips slowly crept upward.","When the four elders of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect determined that they weren’t a match for Jie Tianran, they resorted to a suicidal attack attempt. The goal of the attack was not to kill Jie Tianran—though that would have been the best-case scenario. Instead, their goal was to destroy the treasures.","But Jie Tianran had a backup plan—the formation left behind by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s ancestors to deal with the Celestial Master Sacred Sect.","The formation could be used for offense and defense, making it extremely useful. Jie Tianran had used the formation to protect the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s treasures.","This formation could only be used once, and it was bound to the starfield to specifically deal with the Celestial Master Sacred Sect, so Jie Tianran didn’t feel a pinch activating it. Instead, he had profited greatly from the clash now that he had secured their world spiritist treasures.","His gaze fell on the dark treasures.","“Elder, what do you think?” Jie Tianran asked.","“It appears to be from the same origin as the Netherworld Sect’s sacred item,” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body replied.","Jie Tianran had also figured as much. An idea surfaced in his mind.","“Elder, can we refine these treasures with your cauldron?” Jie Tianran asked.","“There is nothing my cauldron cannot refine, but it’ll cost a hefty price,” the old entity replied.","“Elder, please be assured that I’ll compensate you.”","“Compensate? Jie Tianran, you already owe me a lot.”","“Elder, I remember everything you have done for me, which is why I heed all your instructions.”","The old entity smiled. “You’re hoping to use these treasures to help the Netherworld Sect awaken their sacred item?”","“That’s right,” Jie Tianran replied.","“Would you really be that kind?”","“Of course not. I’ll sneak my gus into the treasures. As soon as they channel the treasures, my gus will slip into their bodies without them noticing.”","“That won’t be easy to pull off. The Netherworld Sect isn’t that easily fooled.”","“Perhaps, but awakening the sacred item is no easy feat. They will have to channel these treasures alongside their Netherworld Embryos, and that will take a toll on them. They might be guarded at first, but once they realize that the treasures are effective, they will devote their all to it. By then, it will be a walk in the park to plant my gus into them.”","“Fine. I’ll help you,” the old entity said.","A spirit formation gate opened beside Jie Tianran. Jie Tianran quickly tossed all the black treasures into the spirit formation gate.","Right before Jie Tianran reached the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s headquarters, a thousand black bracelets flew out of the spirit formation gate. He inspected the black bracelets before nodding in satisfaction.","“The Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s habit of collecting treasures worked to my advantage this time.” He did not doubt that the Netherworld Sect could awaken their sacred item if they were to channel these black bracelets.","The Netherworld Sect would grow much stronger after the sacred item was unsealed, but he would not need to fear the Netherworld Sect anymore. They would have become puppets that unconditionally obeyed him.","By the time Jie Tianran reached the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s headquarters, all the Saint-tier elders, except for the two stationed at the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, had returned.","He distributed the world spiritist treasures he had obtained from the Celestial Master Sacred Sect to them. This would greatly boost the prowess of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Following that, he summoned the experts of the Netherworld Sect over. He told them that he was grateful for their help, but the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion didn’t need their assistance anymore. He urged them to return and channel their efforts into awakening the sacred item.","In return for their reinforcement, he presented them with the black bracelets.","“This is a token of my gratitude,” Jie Tianran said.","“This is?”","Wuma Hanshuang and the others could hardly believe their eyes when they saw the black bracelets that emanated a dark-red aura. This was clearly their Netherworld Sect’s treasure, but why had they never seen or even heard about it before?","“Mansion Master, where did you obtain these treasures?” Wuma Hanshuang asked.","“You have the remnants of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect to thank for this.”","Jie Tianran told them the truth, as well as the method to channel the black bracelets. The only thing he didn’t tell them was that he had slipped gus into the black bracelets while forging them."]},{"number":6634,"title":"Chapter 6634: Chapter 6632: Divergence in Opinion","paragraphs":["Chapter 6632: Divergence in Opinion","“Mansion Master, you truly are our Netherworld Sect’s benefactor,” Wuma Hanshuang and the others said with utmost gratitude.","“Since I have agreed to help you awaken your sacred item, it’s only right for me to give it my all. Take these.”","Jie Tianran passed the black bracelets to the Netherworld Sectmembers.","“Mansion Master, why are these bracelets missing a piece?” Wuma Hanshuang and the others asked in confusion.","“I’ll be honest with you—these bracelets are incomplete. It was a stroke of luck that I found these treasures from the Celestial Master Sacred Sect, but it was more difficult than I thought to forge these bracelets. Nevertheless, they should still aid you in awakening your sacred item. Take them back and feel them yourself.","“I am still working on another bunch of bracelets. Once I’m done forging them, I’ll have my people send them over. With that, we should be able to fully awaken your sacred item,” Jie Tianran explained.","The Netherworld Sectmembers were overjoyed to hear that.","“We’re counting on you, Mansion Master.”","Wuma Hanshuang and the others relayed their gratitude. They earnestly believed that Jie Tianran was going all out to help them awaken their sacred item.","To prevent the Netherworld Sect from learning about his ploy, Jie Tianran had to plant weaker gus into the black bracelet. These gus were not potent enough to turn the Netherworld Sect into his puppets yet; they merely paved the way for him to do so.","The true weapon lay in the next batch of black bracelets... but he needed more time to ensure that his means were properly concealed.","“Mansion Master, you have given us something so valuable. How should we compensate...”","Wuma Hanshuang and the others suddenly thought about another problem. While the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were in an alliance, their relationship was still transactional in nature.","These bracelets were not part of the original deal, so the Netherworld Sect would have to pay Jie Tianran for them.","These bracelets were invaluable to the Netherworld Sect. They could be put to other uses aside from awakening the sacred item, so they wouldn’t return the bracelets. Jie Tianran should know that as well.","“We’ll talk about compensation another day. Don’t worry. I gave the bracelets to you because I trust the Netherworld Sect. As long as there is trust, everything can be worked out,” Jie Tianran said.","He didn’t turn down the compensation because that would spark the Netherworld Sect’s suspicion.","With that, Wuma Hanshuang and the others rushed back to the sacred item. Jie Tianran even allowed them to use the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s teleportation formation and treasures to speed up their travel.","After sending the Netherworld Sectmembers off, he summoned the Saint-tier elders. He dispatched four Saint-tier elders to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy to reinforce the two Saint-tier elders stationed there.","At the same time, however, he ordered them not to attack the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, as well as to avoid engagement with the Chu Clan Alliance and await his commands, even if they were to bump into them.","The remaining Saint-tier elders would remain in the Seven Realms Galaxy for now.","Jie Tianran knew that he would be powerless to do anything about Chu Feng and the others if they chose to hole themselves up in the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. If he wanted to breach the main city, he would have to first obtain God’s Era’s power.","In other words, the important thing right now was not Chu Feng but God’s Era’s power.","...","Soon, Wuma Hanshuang and the others returned to the Netherworld Sect.","The Netherworld Sect’s upper echelons were overjoyed to see the black bracelets.","Baili Xukong and several neutral faction’s elders immediately put on the black bracelets and attempted to channel them. The result filled them with excitement. The connection was weak, but it gave them a glimmer of hope to grasp the sacred item’s power.","Finally, it felt like they were making progress.","“Hold on for a moment,” Cang Li from the neutral faction suddenly spoke up.","He stopped channeling the black bracelet and took it off.","The others knew that Cang Li must have discovered something, so they stopped channeling the black bracelet and followed him into a palace.","The only ones qualified to enter this palace were the six neutral faction’s elders, the new faction’s Baili Xukong, and the conservative faction’s Dongfang Hansong.","“Did you sense anything amiss when channeling the black bracelets? I felt corrosive energy seeping into my body and fusing with my soul,” Cang Li said.","“It’s probably the backlash. It’s linked to the sacred item, so it’s only normal for us to suffer a backlash when channeling it,” Baili Xukong replied.","None of them were fools. They had all sensed the corrosive energy, but it was so faint that it didn’t inflict any damage on them. That was why they shrugged it off.","“It’s one thing if it’s just a backlash, but what if it is Jie Tianran’s scheme against us? We shouldn’t forget that he’s the strongest world spiritist in the world of cultivation. None of us can see through his means,” Cang Li said grimly.","“Lord Cang Li, are you suggesting that Jie Tianran isn’t sincere about helping us and that he might have tampered with these bracelets?” Dongfang Hansong asked.","“Yes, that is my suspicion.” Cang Li nodded.","The other five from the neutral faction narrowed their eyes. This was a matter of grave importance.","“Lord Cang Li, aren’t you thinking too much into it?” Baili Xukong asked.","“Carefully recall the sensation you felt earlier, Baili Xukong. Are you certain it is just a backlash?” Cang Li asked.","“Yes, I concede that it is different from the backlash we feel from the sacred item, but the backlash of each treasure is bound to differ from one to the other. Our bodies should have sensed it if the corrosive energy was truly detrimental to us, but so far, everything feels fine.","“Lord Cang Li, I understand your worry. Jie Tianran is not a trustworthy individual, especially considering his reputation. However, since we have decided to engage his help, I don’t think that we should suspect him over every little thing.","“Taking a step back, if Jie Tianran wanted to sabotage us, he could have tampered with the sacred item’s formation, and we wouldn’t have been any wiser. With these bracelets, we can awaken the sacred item without relying on Jie Tianran’s formation. This gives us far greater control over the process. Isn’t this much safer?” Baili Xukong said.","“Baili is right.”","Four elders of the neutral faction nodded in agreement.","Cang Li and Baili Xukong argued for a long time about whether they should use the black bracelets or not. In the end, they put the matter to a vote.","Ultimately, more people supported Baili Xukong."]},{"number":6635,"title":"Chapter 6635: Chapter 6633: The Netherworld Master and Chu Feng","paragraphs":["Chapter 6633: The Netherworld Master and Chu Feng","The only one who supported Cang Li was Dongfang Hansong. That was nowhere near enough to change the outcome.","So, the Netherworld Sect decided to use the black bracelets.","The upper echelons like them channeled two bracelets simultaneously, whereas the other members received a black bracelet each. Only the strongest sectmembers were bestowed with one.","But Cang Li relinquished his black bracelet. He still wasn’t willing to channel it.","Dongfang Hansong, on the other hand, compromised and accepted the arrangement.","While the black bracelets were being distributed, Cang Li called Dongfang Hansong to his private residence.","“What’s wrong, Lord Cang Li?”","Much to Dongfang Hansong’s astonishment, Cang Li crumbled to the floor weakly, his aura withering as if he were on the verge of death. It was a huge contrast to how he was a moment ago.","“I’m fine.”","The weak Cang Li waved his hand, gesturing for Dongfang Hansong not to worry.","“What happened, Lord Cang Li?” Dongfang Hansong asked once more.","Cang Li was one of the key pillars supporting the Netherworld Sect. His death would be a huge loss to them.","“Don’t worry, I am truly fine. I called you here because there is something I’d like to ask you. Hansong, I presume that you supported me earlier because you think that there is something amiss with the black bracelets. Why did you still agree to channel it then?” Cang Li voiced his confusion.","“Lord Cang Li, I supported you because I concur with your judgment. But since we have collectively come to a decision, it’s only right for me to respect it. It goes against our rules otherwise. Furthermore, if I incur the other elders’ displeasure, the members of my conservative faction will suffer together with me,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“Haa!” Cang Li sighed.","He could see things from Dongfang Hansong’s point of view and feel his helplessness.","Cang Li, as a lone individual and a respected elder from the neutral faction, was almost free from consequences. No one in the present Netherworld Sect had the power and authority to punish him, and there was no one else to bear the consequences of his actions, either.","But Dongfang Hansong was different. He was shouldering the entire conservative faction.","“Baili Xukong and the others have lost their heads over the sacred item. They want to push things through no matter the risks. However, I doubt that Jie Tianran would be that kind as to support a power that could potentially suppress his Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“If my intuition is right, even if we awaken the sacred item and grow stronger, there might be restrictions placed on us that force us to lower our heads to Jie Tianran,” Cang Li said.","“Lord Cang Li, that is what I am worried about, but I have no choice. Before Lord Netherworld Master left, he ordered us to follow the majority when we have a divergence in opinion. I would be disobeying Lord Netherworld Master if we don’t follow this rule. Baili Xukong will exploit this matter to make things difficult for my conservative faction,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“Exactly. Our Netherworld Sect would have never faced this quandary if Lord Netherworld Master were still around,” Cang Li said.","“Of course. Lord Netherworld Master would have easily awakened the sacred item, and we wouldn’t have to worry about the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion at all. Do you still remember the time when Lord Netherworld Master first came to our Netherworld Sect?” Cang Li asked with a smile.","“Of course. Our Netherworld Master was still struggling to develop our Netherworld Embryos. The success rate of an implantation was extremely low, and we were having trouble incubating the Netherworld Embryos at a large scale. Thinking back, we were extremely lucky to have survived the implantation and incubation.","“But our cultivation didn’t soar after incubating the Netherworld Embryo; on the contrary, it only suppressed our cultivation. Generations of Netherworld Masters have tried to resolve that issue but to no avail.","“We thought that we had reached a dead end.","“It was then that Lord Netherworld Master appeared. Even though he wasn’t a Netherworld Sectmember, he said that he could help us. We thought that he was just messing with us. Our leader then, in a fit of anger, attacked him, but he ended up getting killed by Lord Netherworld Master in a single strike.","“There was no way we would follow an outsider just because he was strong. We swore to resist him to our dying breath. Lord Cang Li, I remember you even ignited your life force to fight him,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“Indeed. It would have been much easier for Lord Netherworld Master to kill off obstinate old fools like us, but he didn’t hold it against us. He placated us before helping us awaken our Netherworld Embryo. Then, he shared the proper way to incubate Netherworld Embryos.","“That was the moment our Netherworld Sect grew by leaps and bounds and became a powerhouse in the world of cultivation,” Cang Li said.","“Lord Netherworld Master was unfathomably powerful, but he didn’t want to draw attention. If not for that, our Netherworld Sect could have ruled the world of cultivation,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“Lord Netherworld Master had more important things to do. He only helped us on a whim. Had we not insisted that he become our Netherworld Master, he would have left after helping us. He has already done enough for us,” Cang Li said.","“Yes, I am aware of that. Lord Netherworld Master didn’t intend to become our leader, but he caved in at our insistence. Despite his reluctance, he fulfilled his responsibilities and led us into the domains of Ancient Era’s races.","“Even though our Netherworld Sect has started taking shape in the Ancient Era and was officially formed in the early years of the present era, much of our foundation was accumulated from conquering the Ancient Era’s races.","“That is why we respect Lord Netherworld Master a lot. Even though our Netherworld Sect has grown to a point where we no longer fear anyone, in my view, our golden era was still the period when we went around conquering Ancient Era’s races with Lord Netherworld Master,” Dongfang Hansong spoke with a nostalgic smile.","“Hansong, you have never seen Lord Netherworld Master’s face, right?” Cang Li asked.","Dongfang Hansong was surprised by that question.","From the first time the Netherworld Master appeared before them, his face was already concealed. Even his voice was altered. He wielded the highest authority in the Netherworld Sect, but no one knew his origin or his appearance.","“Lord Cang Li, have you seen Lord Netherworld Master’s face before?” Dongfang Hansong asked.","“I was fortunate to have seen it once,” Cang Li replied as he drew a human’s side profile with his martial power.","It was a man’s face. He looked old and fatigued, but he had sharp features.","“Lord Netherworld Master is a human?” Dongfang Hansong blurted out in astonishment.","The Netherworld Master was already incomparably powerful from the first time they met him. His aura was more feral and intense than any monstrous beast he had ever met, and he was adept at the means of monstrous beasts.","That was also why they had insisted on making him their leader then. They sensed that the Netherworld Master harnessed power even greater than their Netherworld Embryo. In their view, this was the kind of person who was worthy of leading them.","“Indeed. Lord Netherworld Master is a human like us,” Cang Li replied.","“Could Lord Netherworld Master be from the Ancient Era?” Dongfang Hansong asked.","In his view, only someone who had survived the Ancient Era could wield such immense power.","“Take a closer look, Hansong. Don’t you think that Lord Netherworld Master resembles someone?” Cang Li asked.","“Resembles someone?” Dongfang Hansong took a closer look at the portrait, but it didn’t ring a bell with him. “Lord Cang Li, who do you think Lord Netherworld Master resembles?”","“Don’t you think Lord Netherworld Master bears a striking resemblance to Chu Feng?” Cang Li asked."]},{"number":6636,"title":"Chapter 6636: Chapter 6634: Verifying the Matter","paragraphs":["Chapter 6634: Verifying the Matter","“Chu Feng?”","Dongfang Hansong’s face warped in shock. He took a closer look at the side-profile portrait of the Netherworld Master, only to lurch in shock right away.","Indeed, there was a striking resemblance between Chu Feng and the Netherworld Master’s side profile.","“What are you insinuating, Lord Cang Li?” Dongfang Hansong asked.","He had an ominous feeling about this. He was hoping for Cang Li to refute his conjecture. Otherwise, this would be completely insane!","“Think about Chu Feng’s grasp of the Netherworld Embryo and his ability to make use of our sacred item. Do you really think those are coincidences?” Cang Li asked.","Dongfang Hansong’s complexion turned awful. Sweat trickled down his face. He was hoping for Cang Li to refute him, but the latter’s response only made him more nervous. He thought more deeply about this matter, and goosebumps covered his body.","“Lord Cang Li, you can’t think that Chu Feng is Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant, do you?” Dongfang Hansong voiced his deduction.","“To be honest, that is precisely what I’m thinking. You told me that you don’t think Baili Zilin was the one who triggered the red clouds phenomenon at the Netherworld Embryo Spirituality Summoning Altar. Baili Zilin could have easily proved himself by stepping onto the altar again, but he kept finding reasons not to do so. He obviously has a guilty conscience,” Cang Li said.","Dongfang Hansong knew that Cang Li wouldn’t mention this matter for no reason.","“Lord Cang Li, do you think that Chu Feng was the one who induced the phenomenon, but Baili Zilin claimed the credit for that?” Dongfang Hansong asked.","“Yes, that is what I’m thinking. No one from our Netherworld Sect has the means to trigger the red clouds phenomenon. Baili Zilin claims that he was the one who induced it, but he refuses to prove it. Judging by circumstantial evidence, I am inclined to believe that an outsider might be behind it.","“We know that Chu Feng possesses a Netherworld Embryo, and his control over it far surpasses any of us. Also, I suspect that the sacred item, as well as the formation and the treasures to awaken it, are all left behind by Lord Netherworld Master.","“Otherwise, don’t you think that it’s too much of a coincidence for the sacred item to surface from the Undying Starfield right after the red clouds phenomenon was triggered? I don’t know about you, but I’m inclined to believe that both things are connected,” Cang Li said.","“This...”","Dongfang Hansong was so shaken up that he began sweating profusely. Even his breathing became labored. This was not just an empty guess; it was a reasonable deduction.","“Lord Cang Li, even if Chu Feng really induced the red clouds phenomenon and is Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant, we have no way to prove that. Baili Xukong and the others won’t believe us,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“Lord Netherworld Master didn’t want to leave any traces behind back then, but sometimes, things don’t go as planned. Once, I sustained severe injuries during a campaign against the Ancient Era’s races. Lord Netherworld Master placed a recovery treasure inside my body and personally channeled it to help me recover.","“Due to the recovery treasure’s unique nature, there are traces of Lord Netherworld Master’s bloodline aura lingering on it. I have refrained from extracting his bloodline aura because I dared not, and I thought that it would be disrespectful to him.","“Our Netherworld Sect may appear strong on the surface, but threats are lurking in all directions. Jie Tianran has set his eyes on us, and Baili Xukong’s ambitions are swelling. There is a chance that we might just implode on ourselves.","“It’s thanks to Lord Netherworld Master that we have come this far. It’s one thing for us to die, but we would be letting him down after everything he has done for us. So, I tried to extract his bloodline aura from the recovery treasure despite the risk of death. It could be because heaven was looking after me, but I succeeded,” Cang Li said as he took out a transparent bottle.","The bottle contained an extremely faint aura.","“Is this... Lord Netherworld Master’s bloodline aura?” Dongfang Hansong looked at the aura reverently as if it were something holy.","“Mmhm.” Cang Li nodded.","“Lord Cang Li, you incurred those injuries from extracting this whiff of bloodline aura?” Dongfang Hansong asked.","“That’s right.”","“What do you intend to do with the aura? Look for Chu Feng?”","“I, personally, harbor no enmity toward Chu Feng, but there is a deep-seated grudge between him and our Netherworld Sect now. Even if Chu Feng allows me to verify his relationship with Lord Netherworld Master, what if I am wrong? That would be a huge farce. It’s one thing for me to be embarrassed, but I’d be bringing shame to the Netherworld Sect as well.”","“Indeed.”","“I thought about visiting Chu Feng’s homeland. Going by age, Chu Feng’s father can’t be Lord Netherworld Master, but it is possible that Chu Feng’s grandfather, a man named Chu Hanxian, is.","“If I could find a portrait of Chu Feng’s grandfather when he was younger, I could compare him with Lord Netherworld Master’s side profile. Also, since that was the place where he lived, there might be traces of his bloodline aura lying around. That would be concrete proof that no one can refute.","“The problem is that I am in a terrible condition now, as you can see. I need to recuperate right away, or else my life will be in danger. However, this matter is also urgent. If Chu Feng truly is Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant, we have to verify it as soon as possible, lest we commit an unforgivable mistake.","“Hansong, I called you here because I hope that you can handle this on my behalf,” Cang Li said.","“But I have to channel this thing to awaken the sacred item right now,” Dongfang Hansong said as he glanced at the two black bracelets on his wrists.","“I’ll tell the others you are handling something on my behalf. I’ll be the one to bear the consequences. Hansong, if Chu Feng truly is Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant, you’ll be making a huge contribution to the Netherworld Sect.","“If Chu Feng is willing to inherit the position of the Netherworld Master, you and your conservative faction will become his aides. The new faction won’t be able to compete with you anymore,” Cang Li said.","“Lord Cang Li, this matter is of grave importance. Can I take Elder Yun Ao with me?” Dongfang Hansong asked.","“Yun Ao? His loyalty toward the Netherworld Sect is unquestionable, but his cultivation is lacking. Are you sure you want to bring him along?” Cang Li asked.","“Lord Cang Li, it is because of how important this matter is that I wish to bring Yun Ao with me. His unwavering loyalty toward the sect will make him a credible witness. If Chu Feng truly is Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant, I’ll need someone trustworthy to corroborate my claim. He’ll be essential to convincing the other lords.","“I reckon that Baili Xukong will refute whatever evidence we have and fight us to the bitter end, so we’ll have to win over as many people as possible,” Dongfang Hansong said."]},{"number":6637,"title":"Chapter 6637: Chapter 6635: Trial Formation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6635: Trial Formation","“Yes, Yun Ao is the ideal person to bring along then.”","Cang Li heaved a sigh. “Haa~ I remember the days we conquered the Ancient Era’s races under Lord Netherworld Master’s leadership. We were united as one. It’s truly a pity that the Netherworld Sect is no longer the same as it was before. Too many people have changed. Only a handful of people like you and Yun Ao still preserve their spirit from back then.","“Baili Xukong revered Lord Netherworld Master so much back then, but now, all he wants is to claim the seat of the Netherworld Master. If he learns that Chu Feng is the Netherworld Master’s descendant, he might just assassinate Chu Feng.","“I should have discussed this matter with everyone, but I confided only in you because I’m worried that the others might harbor ulterior motives. They might get so ahead of themselves that they will stop me from even verifying this matter.”","“I think it is wise that you only confided in me, Lord Cang Li. Baili Xukong will surely do everything possible to stop you. Even if we verify that Chu Feng is Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant, there is no saying that he might do something disrespectful to Lord Netherworld Master,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“Forget it. Let’s not talk about this anymore. I do hope that Chu Feng is Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant so that our Netherworld Sect will finally have a leader,” Cang Li said.","“Rest assured, Lord Cang Li. This matter isn’t too hard. You can leave it to me.”","Dongfang Hansong took the jade bottle before bowing deeply to Cang Li. Then, he took his leave, found Yun Ao, and took him to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","In truth, he knew that not even Cang Li could cover for him if he left at this critical juncture, but he still did so without hesitation.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng was still confused as to what the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Saint-tier elders were up to, but he was more confident now that he had experts like Little Fishy and Fei on his side.","In fact, he was recruiting more members into the Chu Clan Alliance.","His true goal, however, was to lure the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion into attacking him; bringing in new members was just a plus.","But despite their brazen recruitment, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion didn’t respond at all.","...","Days later, Chu Feng was cultivating when Long Mucheng knocked on his door.","“Chu Feng, the Chu Clan Alliance has taken in some new members. These members have been put through a series of trials and should be reliable, but ultimately, the Chu Clan Alliance was founded for you. We’re hoping that you can decide whether those people are qualified to join us. Do you want to take a look?” Long Mucheng asked.","“I have no qualms about recruiting new members, but our current members are a tight-knit group who have braved death together. I don’t know much about the recruits, but I suspect most aren’t interested in fighting with us or bringing down the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Instead, they are hoping to profit from this situation. Those people can’t be relied on. We should filter them out,” Chu Feng said.","“I agree, but the most difficult thing to read in the world is a person’s heart. It’s only through tribulations that we know what they truly think,” Long Mucheng replied.","“A formation can do the job.”","“Ah! I nearly forgot you’re a master world spiritist. Most people can’t see through your formation, not to mention we don’t lack world spiritists now. We have plenty of recruits, so it might take some work to filter them. I’ll tell them to wait until the formation is ready before holding the final trial,” Long Mucheng said.","“I have told Ling Xiao and the others to prepare the formation. It is ready,” Chu Feng replied as he took out a formation.","This formation was constructed by Ling Xiao, his grandfather, and the other world spiritists. However, the formation blueprint was from Chu Feng, so he could activate it with ease.","“You’re meticulous!” Long Mucheng was delighted to see the delicate formation floating above Chu Feng’s palm.","“Elder, if you don’t mind, you can use this formation on the recruits. Those who clear the trial can become one of us,” Chu Feng said.","“Of course I don’t mind. Other than the recruits, all of us from the Chu Clan Alliance owe our lives to you. We’ll heed your command. We won’t hesitate even if you ask us to march to our deaths,” Long Mucheng said with a grin.","Even though she was now a rank five Heavenly God, she didn’t put on airs in front of Chu Feng.","“All right. Let’s see how many are qualified to join us,” Chu Feng said.","...","Long Mucheng had gathered all potential recruits for the Chu Clan Alliance into a single realm. All in all, there were more than three billion people.","That was not many people compared to the vastness of the world of cultivation. Even a smaller Lower Realm would have more people than that.","However, this was still an impressive number considering the strict recruitment conditions.","One, the recruits must have the guts to stand against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Netherworld Sect.","Two, they must have the ability to travel to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy.","Three, they must clear the prior trials.","Three billion people had cleared these requirements to join the Chu Clan Alliance. This showed the impressive rallying power of the Chu Clan Alliance.","These people were going to face their final trial now. If they cleared it, they would be accepted as members of the Chu Clan Alliance.","Long Mucheng appeared in the sky together with the Dragon Breath Clansmen. She grandly announced the content of the final trial—the recruits would be accompanying them to ambush a Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s secret base.","This secret base was located in the very realm where they were standing, which was why they were gathered here. The secret base was guarded by not just the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s experts but several Saint-tier elders as well.","It was going to be a tough battle.","The recruits wouldn’t have to fight on the frontline, but they shouldered the important responsibility of channeling a formation. If the ambush failed, they would lose their lives as well.","Those who were afraid could still back off, since they weren’t official members of the Chu Clan Alliance yet.","Half of the people immediately left after hearing Long Mucheng’s words and more left after thinking it over. Within moments, the initial three billion people fell to two hundred million.","“Looks like recruitment isn’t that easy, either.” Long Mucheng sighed helplessly.","She had thought that at least half of the people here would be reliable, since they had already cleared the previous trials. However, she had gravely underestimated how fickle-minded people could be in the face of danger.","She turned her eyes to those remaining.","“Let’s see how many of those remaining are sincere about fighting alongside us.”"]},{"number":6638,"title":"Chapter 6638: Chapter 6636: The Fearless Ones","paragraphs":["Chapter 6636: The Fearless Ones","The so-called secret base was just an illusory formation, but it was constructed so exquisitely that there was no chance of anyone beneath Heavenly God or Heaven Dragon seeing through it.","The illusory formation had two exits.","One led into a square sealed off by a barrier, and the other was outside the barrier. Where the recruits exited the illusory formation from would determine whether they were worthy of joining the Chu Clan Alliance or not.","Those who entered the square were excited, whereas those who ended up outside the square had regretful looks.","By now, they had realized that the life-and-death trial was just an illusory formation, though those who had failed harbored not much feeling for the Chu Clan Alliance in the first place.","Very few people cleared the trial; it was not even one in ten thousand. As such, there were countless people outside the barrier but only a small handful inside the square.","A woman emerged from a spirit formation gate and stepped into the square. It was Wang Yuxian. She had just learned that everything she had gone through was an illusory formation. Before she could process what was going on, an elder from the Dragon Breath Clan walked up to her with a smile.","“Congratulations, young friend. You have cleared our final trial and are now a member of the Chu Clan Alliance.” The elder handed a Chu Clan Alliance token and a Cosmos Sack to her.","The resources in the Cosmos Sack were extremely generous by Wang Yuxian’s standards.","“Thank you.” Wang Yuxian bowed politely.","She looked around and noticed a huge disparity between the number of people in the square and the number of people outside. There were only ten thousand people inside the square.","Based on the massive crowd outside, she deduced that the trial was nearing its end.","“Hm?”","Just then, she noticed a familiar face. It was the woman with pink pupils, Mo Yuhan.","Like before, Mo Yuhan immediately noticed Wang Yuxian’s gaze and looked over. She might have felt a sense of camaraderie with Wang Yuxian after clearing the same trial, so she nodded and smiled at the latter.","Wang Yuxian appeared cold due to her air of impeccability, but she had a bubbly personality, especially when talking to other women. She had a good impression of Mo Yuhan from before, so she walked up to the latter and engaged her in a conversation.","They quickly learned each other’s names, though they didn’t probe into each other’s backgrounds. They didn’t think their past was important, since they were all now members of the Chu Clan Alliance.","“There are quite a few people who want to die,” a voice suddenly boomed thunderously.","The crowd looked over and saw a middle-aged man walking out of the spirit formation gate into the square. His voice sounded ancient. As he walked, his appearance transformed into that of a white-haired old man. With a wave of his sleeves, a world spiritist cloak layered over his robe.","It was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s cloak!","The hidden figures in the sky immediately noticed the anomaly. Other than Long Mucheng and the Dragon Breath Clansmen, there were also Little Fishy and Fei.","“Someone has snuck into our bunch of recruits. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion sure is headstrong,” Fei remarked.","“There is no lack of fools in this world,” Long Mucheng added.","But neither of them made a move. They knew that this situation didn’t require their intervention.","Even though the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s old man had seen through the illusory formation, which allowed him to sneak into the square, he failed to spot the Chu Clan Alliance’s experts hiding in the realm.","That was why he dared to act so arrogantly. He thought that no one here could stop him.","He unleashed his oppressive might, which sealed off the surroundings and distorted the space in the square. The recruits suddenly noticed that they could no longer see, hear, or smell. Even the Dragon Breath Clan’s elders were forced to their knees.","He was a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","But not everyone could sense his spirit power, such as Wang Yuxian, Mo Yuhan, and the weaker recruits.","“This aura...”","The two ladies felt the threat of death looming close. They had never felt so helpless before. This was not their first time seeing an expert of this caliber, but they had never been subjected to such powerful oppressive might before.","It was only now that they understood the huge gap between them and a Heavenly Dragon.","Those inside the square thought that they were doomed, but those who had been eliminated by the trial gloated as they were not subjected to the oppressive might.","“Well done! The Chu Clan Alliance was just mocking us with their illusory formation. Karma immediately struck them afterward. An expert from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion swoops in right away to teach them a lesson.”","“Hahaha! There’s no better way to prove your loyalty to the Chu Clan Alliance than to die for them right now!”","“Those fools. It’s not as if the Chu Clan Alliance has given you anything. Is it worth giving up your lives just like that?”","Whether to distance themselves from the Chu Clan Alliance or because they truly thought so, these people began insulting the Chu Clan Alliance.","“Kill those arrogant fools! Let them know the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is the strongest power in the world of cultivation!”","“I only came here to get some freebies from the Chu Clan Alliance. Only a fool would stand against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and die in vain.”","“Chu Feng is just a junior. Do you think that he can lead you to greater heights? Dream on!”","“Milord, teach those idiots a lesson!”","An increasing number of people insulted the Chu Clan Alliance, especially when they realized that none of the Chu Clan Alliance’s members present had the means to deal with the old man. Even Chu Feng was not spared from insults.","There were smart ones who fled right away to avoid being implicated, but there was no lack of people who gloated at the misfortune of others.","In the sky, Little Fishy’s eyes turned cold. Her eyes sifted through the flood of people below as she quietly remembered everyone who insulted Chu Feng and the Chu Clan Alliance."]},{"number":6639,"title":"Chapter 6639: Chapter 6637: The Same Plight","paragraphs":["Chapter 6637: The Same Plight","“Quiet!”","Much to everyone’s surprise, the one who shouted was not a member of the Chu Clan Alliance but the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elder. He cast a sweeping glance of reprehension and disdain at the crowd.","“Do I need you to teach me how to do things? Who do you think you are? Do you think I don’t know why you lesser beings are here? Your sins won’t be absolved just because you switched sides at the last moment. I spared you because I am kind; it doesn’t mean you don’t deserve to die. Stop being an eyesore and get out right now!” the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elder said.","The faces of those who insulted the Chu Clan Alliance turned awry as if someone had stuffed feces down their throats. Not only had they failed to fawn on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but they had also offended the Chu Clan Alliance on top of that.","Fearing that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elder would kill them if they continued lingering, they quickly fled the scene.","“Stop right there,” a voice echoed.","A piercing sound shook the air as a sword pierced through the barrier, shattering the oppressive might of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elders.","Next, fresh blood splattered everywhere as if a resplendent firework.","Countless people were decapitated within moments. It happened so fast that most people didn't see what happened, but they immediately understood that a massacre was happening right before their eyes.","That prompted the crowd to flee even more frantically, fearing that they would be the next victim.","Fresh blood splattered like blossoming flowers.","But the smarter ones noticed something amiss. They realized that the ones who were being killed were the ones who switched sides at the last moment and insulted the Chu Clan Alliance. This must be the Chu Clan Alliance’s doing.","Soon, the imposing sword returned to the square, into the hands of a certain man.","“Chu Feng!”","The culprit behind the massacre was Chu Feng. He had raised his cultivation to rank one Heavenly God level through the Monster Slayer Sword, but despite being able to deal with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elder, he turned a blind eye to the latter.","“Our Chu Clan Alliance welcomes others to join us. Even if you fail our trial, we will not make things difficult for you. However, I want you to get it into your heads that the Chu Clan Alliance is not an entity that you can insult.”","Those words explained the earlier massacre.","Most people didn’t sympathize with the deceased; they should have watched their mouths, especially since they were in the Chu Clan Alliance’s base. Even if they wanted to switch sides, they could have just done so quietly.","“Chu Feng!!!” the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elder roared.","A formation whirred amid the clouds and swiftly enveloped the skyline. Even those who had escaped earlier were caught inside the formation.","This was the power of a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","Clang!","There was a flash of cold light, and the formation began to dissipate. It took a while before the crowd realized that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elder had been killed.","“This...”","Wang Yuxian and Mo Yuhan widened their eyes in disbelief. Despite knowing that Chu Feng had become very strong, it still shook them up to see the unimaginably powerful Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elder being decapitated.","They did consider the possibility of Chu Feng defeating the other party, but they couldn’t imagine that the battle would end in a single slash. That was a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist!","Just then, golden lights appeared out of thin air and flowed to everyone in the square. These were the treasures from the deceased elder’s Cosmos Sack. Chu Feng had taken them out to share them with those who had cleared the trial.","“Everyone gets a share,” Chu Feng said.","Those inside the square were delighted. They accepted the treasures and thanked Chu Feng.","Boom!","A blinding golden light suddenly appeared on the horizon. It was a formation constructed by many Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists! From the moment the formation appeared, the crowd felt as if a guillotine were hanging above their heads.","“Yes, everyone gets a share. None of you will be getting out of here alive today!”","Fifteen Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elders descended from the sky. They were all Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, and two of them had reached rank two. Their eyes blazed with anger and excitement.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had issued an order that forbade members from attacking the Chu Clan Alliance without permission, but there was no lack of proud people in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Some of them secretly liaised to form this team.","They had come here to restore the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s honor, and they were prepared to die for that. When they saw Chu Feng standing alone without any helpers, they thought that they might just succeed.","They were defying the Mansion Master and the Saint-tier elders’ orders right now, but if they could apprehend or kill Chu Feng, they would immediately become heroes of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Boom!","Just then, several terrifying black auras suddenly descended from the sky like ferocious dragons, crushing everything in their path. Not only did they shatter the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists’ formation, but they even rushed at them as well.","There was no time for the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists to dodge. By the time they registered what was going on, they were already caught by the black aura.","“Who is this bunch of nobodies trying to kill?”","Two figures descended from the sky—Bai Yunqing and Li Wu.","“They are...?”","The situation was changing with every passing moment, but the crowd was still able to make sense of it.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had laid an ambush in this realm, but as soon as their people appeared, they were subdued. The ones who subdued them were the man and woman descending from the sky.","The man and the woman descended to Chu Feng’s side.","“Big brother, did I arrive on time?” Bai Yunqing said.","Big brother?","This confirmed the crowd’s suspicion that they were from the Chu Clan Alliance.","“The Chu Clan Alliance is truly unfathomable.”","Those qualified to join the Chu Clan Alliance were overjoyed, whereas those who failed looked regretful. It was hard to tell what would happen in the future, but the Chu Clan Alliance looked to be in a good position right now.","At the very least, they seemed to stand a chance against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“You came just in time,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“Chu Feng, how should I deal with them?” Li Wu dragged the captured Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elders before Chu Feng.","Chu Feng raised his blade...","Shing shing shing—","Blood splattered. Heads rolled.","Like the one before, these Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were all decapitated by the Monster Slayer Sword.","This was Chu Feng’s answer. No matter their spirit power or background, as long as a Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s member dared stand before him, the only outcome awaiting them was death."]},{"number":6640,"title":"Chapter 6640: Chapter 6638: It’s Been a Long Time","paragraphs":["Chapter 6638: It’s Been a Long Time","The crowd gathered in the square buzzed with excitement.","In truth, they had only been able to clear the Chu Clan Alliance’s final trial because of their histories.","Most had their loved ones murdered by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but there was no way for them to redress their grievances until the Chu Clan Alliance appeared. Some had been oppressed by other powers and looked up to Chu Feng after hearing about his story.","However, two people felt delighted on top of excitement—Wang Yuxian and Mo Yuhan. They had witnessed the lower periods of Chu Feng's life and how difficult his journey had been.","In particular, Wang Yuxian had known Chu Feng for longer and knew more about his history. Even though he was now known throughout the world of cultivation, she remembered how many people had looked down on him back when he was weaker in the Nine Souls Galaxy, and that included her fellow seniors.","Chu Feng was talented, but he had to advance a step at a time.","Far weaker cultivators had towered in his path like mountains in the past, and some had even almost claimed his life.","What Wang Yuxian saw was not just the glory Chu Feng enjoyed. She also saw someone who had slaughtered his way to the top and yet still remembered his roots.","“Right. Let me introduce two friends to you,” Chu Feng told Bai Yunqing.","No one thought much about those words initially as Chu Feng knew far too many people. It was only when Chu Feng turned around and looked at Wang Yuxian that she realized that Chu Feng had noticed her.","And indeed, Chu Feng began making his way to Wang Yuxian, and the crowd opened a path for him.","“It has been a while,” Chu Feng smiled.","His eyes reflected the earnest joy of reuniting with an old friend. He didn’t mind the disparity in their strength and standing at all. With that, Wang Yuxian was certain that Chu Feng was still the same person as before.","“It has been a while,” Wang Yuxian replied with a smile, only to freeze up right after.","It turned out that Mo Yuhan had blurted out the same words at the same time.","The two ladies exchanged surprised looks, only to laugh right after. It was evident that the two of them were friends with Chu Feng.","“How did the two of you end up together?” Chu Feng asked.","That confirmed their guess.","“It might be fate,” Wang Yuxian replied with a smile.","Mo Yuhan smiled as well. It could have been because she had traveled alone for far too long, but reuniting with an old friend brought her some warmth.","After trading some pleasantries, Chu Feng brought the two of them to a more private location and called Little Fishy, Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, and the others over. He wanted to introduce Wang Yuxian and Mo Yuhan to them.","Fei insisted on tagging along, saying that they were around the same age even though he was much, much older. Chu Feng wasn’t bothered with such trivialities, so he brought Fei along.","Long Chengyu and the others treated Wang Yuxian and Mo Yuhan warmly upon learning that they were Chu Feng’s friends; they didn’t look down on the two ladies at all.","But Mo Yuhan couldn’t help but feel awkward when interacting with famed prodigies like Little Fishy and Long Chengyu. The difference in their standing was deep-rooted in their minds, making it difficult for them to break free right away.","In contrast, it was Wang Yuxian, despite her humbler birth, who adapted faster and befriended these formidable individuals.","This gathering among juniors only lasted four hours, but it was a joyous conversation.","Through their conversation, Chu Feng learned how Wang Yuxian and Mo Yuhan became acquainted and why they joined the Chu Clan Alliance. He also learned that Feng Ling was in closed-door training, and she should make a huge breakthrough afterward.","Li Wu and Bai Yunqing came to reinforce Chu Feng upon learning about his war against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They left a letter for Feng Ling to inform her to head over after emerging from her closed-door training.","But some things were inappropriate to mention in this kind of setting.","After the impromptu gathering ended, Li Wu and Bai Yunqing approached Chu Feng and told him that Wen Xue had tried to make a move on Li Wu.","The news made Chu Feng’s heart squeeze, but again, knowing Wen Xue, he was not that surprised.","“I should have been more mindful. I’m glad that you’re fine,” Chu Feng told Li Wu and Bai Yunqing in self-reproach.","“Don’t say that, big brother. If not for you, Miss Li Wu and I would have died in the Undying Starfield. Besides, Miss Wen Xue might not have harbored any bad intentions. She might have earnestly wanted to test my feelings for Miss Li Wu,” Bai Yunqing said.","That remark invited a glare from Li Wu.","Chu Feng knew that Bai Yunqing was only saying that to console him, as he was on good terms with Wen Xue.","“Based on my understanding of Wen Xue, she probably intended to make a move. I’m not sure what held her back, but when I see her again, I’ll make her apologize to you,” Chu Feng said.","“There’s no need for an apology. All is good as long as she doesn’t do that again. That scared the hell out of me,” Bai Yunqing said.","“All right, may I trouble you for something, Miss Li Wu? Can you hand this over to Mo Yuhan and make sure that she accepts it?” Chu Feng said as he passed a Cosmos Sack to Li Wu.","It was filled with resources and treasures.","“Sure.” Li Wu took the Cosmos Sack.","“Take this as well. It is God’s Era’s power. It will help with your cultivation.”","Chu Feng took out two portions of God’s Era’s power and handed them to Bai Yunqing and Li Wu. The latter two knew Chu Feng’s temperament; he wouldn’t take no for an answer, so they graciously accepted the gift.","After parting ways, Chu Feng didn’t return to the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect right away. Instead, he made his way to Wang Yuxian’s residence. They might all be friends, but that didn’t mean that they were all equal.","Wang Yuxian had braved death with him many times. They might have chatted a lot earlier, but some things had to be said in private.","For instance, Chu Feng didn’t hand the resources to them earlier in front of the others because he didn’t want them to feel burdened.","“What is a busy man like you doing here instead of resting?”","Wang Yuxian was surprised and delighted to see Chu Feng. He had to be extremely busy, but he still spent so much time to accompany them. She thought that it wouldn’t be as easy to meet him again in the future, but who could have thought that they would meet once more so soon?","Not to mention, Chu Feng was the one taking the initiative here."]},{"number":6641,"title":"Chapter 6641: Chapter 6639: Helping a Friend","paragraphs":["Chapter 6639: Helping a Friend","“I’m resting by spending time with you. Lele, won’t you accompany me for a walk?” Chu Feng asked.","Lele was Wang Yuxian’s nickname, used only by those closest to her.","“The famed Chu Feng is inviting me for a walk? I can’t turn down such an honor,” Wang Yuxian smiled as she rubbed her hands together, as if a pervert.","Chu Feng knew that Wang Yuxian was not a lustful person; she was just joking around.","“You look licentious. It doesn’t suit that face of yours.”","Chu Feng lightly poked Wang Yuxian’s forehead before walking out. Wang Yuxian followed him with a grin.","The two slipped away from the Chu Clan Alliance’s temporary palace cluster toward a quieter part of the night sky.","A full moon hung in the sky; the atmosphere felt tranquil.","Wang Yuxian was still fooling around earlier, but she fell silent as if infected by the atmosphere. She enjoyed spending time alone with Chu Feng, even in silence.","Before meeting him, she had wondered if it was possible for their relationship and feelings to remain the same, considering how his social circle was now dominated by galaxy overlords like the Totem Dragon Clan.","It was at this moment that her heart was finally at ease. Chu Feng was still the same Chu Feng. Other than being stronger than before, he was the same as before.","“Here.” Chu Feng tossed a Cosmos Sack over. “Don’t turn it down if you consider yourself a friend.”","“I was intending to make full use of our friendship. There’s no way I’d turn down your gift.”","Despite her words, her mouth still fell agape when she saw the contents of the Cosmos Sack.","Humans were inevitably biased, and Chu Feng was no different. There was a difference in the Cosmos Sacks he gave Wang Yuxian and Mo Yuhan.","Wang Yuxian’s Cosmos Sack not only contained a huge amount of resources but three God Armaments as well.","“What are these?”","Wang Yuxian took out the three God Armaments and looked at them with expectant eyes, but she dared not to touch them. She could sense that these weapons were incredibly valuable and domineering, far beyond what the current her could use.","This was only normal. Even galaxy overlords like the Totem Dragon Clan cherished every God Armament they had, let alone a cultivator who resided in the Eastern Region like Wang Yuxian.","Most people in the Eastern Region hadn’t even heard of God Armaments, let alone see one.","“This is a God Armament,” Chu Feng said.","“God Armament?” Wang Yuxian’s eyes gleamed. However, she soon shook her head and said, “This won’t do. This is too valuable.”","“What did you just say? Do you not consider me a friend?” Chu Feng asked.","“We are, of course, friends, but this... is too valuable! There is more than enough good stuff in the Cosmos Sack. These are things I’d only see in my dreams. I-I...” Wang Yuxian stuttered.","“What are you saying? God Armaments are indeed valuable, but I have plenty of them.”","Chu Feng grandly waved his hand, and many God Armaments appeared around him.","Wang Yuxian was shocked speechless.","A single God Armament could stir endless bloodshed if it fell into the Nine Souls Galaxy, but Chu Feng had so many of them.","“You might not be able to use a God Armament now, but it is only a matter of time, given your talent. Keep them well,” Chu Feng said.","“This... One is enough,” Wang Yuxian said.","“Didn’t I already show you that I have more than enough God Armaments? Stop dawdling around and take them.” Chu Feng stuffed the three God Armaments back into Wang Yuxian’s Cosmos Sack.","“You sure are generous. I didn’t think you’d give out such treasures just like that.” Wang Yuxian finally accepted the gift, but she couldn’t stop grinning.","“I wouldn’t give it out to just anyone, but you are Lele. We have been through a lot together,” Chu Feng replied with a smile. He was glad that she liked his gifts.","The reason he cultivated was to protect the people around him, and that included helping them rise through the ranks as well. He was still lacking compared to the top-tier experts, but at least he could help Wang Yuxian now.","“Hm?”","The duo looked toward the Chu Clan Alliance’s temporary palace cluster. A pink light suffused the world, casting a dreamlike glow over the night sky.","“What a beautiful phenomenon. I can smell a faint fragrance, too. Did someone make a breakthrough?” Wang Yuxian asked.","“It’s Mo Yuhan,” Chu Feng replied.","He had given the God’s Era’s power to Mo Yuhan as well. While the power had not been very useful to Chu Feng, it was tremendously helpful to weaker cultivators like Mo Yuhan. She must have realized that as well and immediately assimilated it.","Other resources wouldn’t have such immediate effectiveness.","“What’s your current cultivation?” Chu Feng asked.","“You tell me what your current cultivation rank is first,” Wang Yuxian replied with a pair of curious eyes.","“Rank nine True God level.”","“Rank nine... True God?!”","Wang Yuxian was so shocked that her mouth fell agape.","She had no idea how strong Chu Feng was despite seeing him in action earlier. Even a rank one True God was already a powerhouse to her, let alone a rank nine True God, a being on the verge of reaching Heavenly God.","“What’s going on? Most cultivators struggle to make a breakthrough the further they advance, but why are you going faster and faster like a snowball? I knew you’d leave me in the dust, but I didn’t expect the gap to be so big!” Wang Yuxian exclaimed as she revealed her aura.","She was at rank two Half-God level.","“I only reached this level because of the resources Princess Miaomiao gave me. Otherwise, I wouldn’t even have been able to reach Half-God level. To be honest, I didn’t join the Chu Clan Alliance just because of you. I also thought that it was an opportunity for me to venture out into the world and challenge myself. I don’t want to stay in the Nine Souls Galaxy my entire life,” Wang Yuxian said.","Being a rank two Half-God level cultivator easily placed her among the ranks of experts in the Nine Souls Galaxy, though it was lacking in the scope of the vast world of cultivation. That was also why other galaxies looked down on the Ancestral Martial Galaxy and Nine Souls Galaxy.","Soon, the phenomenon Mo Yuhan triggered appeared once more, and this time, it was more intense than ever.","“Another breakthrough?” Wang Yuxian’s eyes widened in shock and envy.","She knew that Mo Yuhan’s cultivation was around the same level as hers, so it shouldn’t have been so easy for her to make a breakthrough.","“Are you envious?” Chu Feng asked.","“Why can I not be?” Wang Yuxian replied.","Chu Feng couldn’t help but sigh a bit on the inside. He knew that Wang Yuxian was actually very talented, perhaps even surpassing renowned prodigies like Long Chengyu. Her cultivation was lacking compared to theirs because she didn’t have an entire galaxy overlord backing her.","Her master might have been able to aid her growth when she was younger, but now, she only had herself to count on.","“Why don’t you guess why Mo Yuhan was able to make consecutive breakthroughs?” Chu Feng asked.","“Why?” Wang Yuxian’s eyes glowed with curiosity.","“It’s because of this.” Chu Feng took out God’s Era’s power with a wave of his hand. “With your talent, you might be able to reach True God level right away.”"]},{"number":6642,"title":"Chapter 6642: Chapter 6640: It Has Finally Begun","paragraphs":["Chapter 6640: It Has Finally Begun","“True God level?”","Wang Yuxian’s expression became incredibly exaggerated. She was feeling not just astonishment but also horror. Such shortcuts were tempting—this was a once-in-a-lifetime chance for her to reach a level where she might never reach right away.","However, she knew that hastiness in cultivation was a cardinal sin. It would hinder her future breakthroughs.","“You should feel it for yourself,” Chu Feng said as he pushed the God’s Era’s power toward Wang Yuxian.","Wang Yuxian grabbed a small bit of it and absorbed it into her body. Moments later, her lower jaw slackened, and her eyes lit up in delight.","Every breakthrough was a process of remolding one’s body and soul, granting them greater strength and abilities.","A certain kind of energy was required to remold one’s body. Natural energies were the foundation of cultivation, but unfortunately, they were limited. To cultivate faster, cultivators sought resources that harnessed natural energies.","But it would be premature to assume that two cultivation resources were the same just because they harnessed the same natural energies.","A good cultivation resource provided energy that was easy to assimilate.","An excellent cultivation resource harnessed martial enlightenment as well, allowing the cultivator to overcome their bottlenecks.","Not all martial enlightenment was equal.","Martial enlightenment had to be personally deciphered and understood by the cultivators, so ease of deciphering was critical.","The power Chu Feng had just given to Wang Yuxian contained the highest level of martial enlightenment, and there were no side effects whatsoever.","“This is God’s Era’s power, but each individual can only assimilate a limited amount. With your talent, there is a good chance you can reach True God level right away,” Chu Feng said.","“You’re giving away God’s Era’s power just like that?!”","Wang Yuxian thought that the gift was too much for her to accept.","“As I have told you, each individual can only assimilate a limited amount of it. I have already given it out to many people, but I still have a lot of it left. You are my friend. There’s no way I wouldn’t reserve a portion for you. You should assimilate it now, so that I can help you if you encounter any problem,” Chu Feng replied.","“All right.” Wang Yuxian finally nodded.","Thus, a series of consecutive phenomena appeared in the sky.","Wang Yuxian underwent consecutive breakthroughs, but she stopped at rank nine Half-God level in the end, just a step away from True God level.","“You don’t want to make a breakthrough anymore?” Chu Feng asked.","“You can tell?” Wang Yuxian was surprised.","“I can sense it. You could have reached True God level in a single breath if you wished to,” Chu Feng replied.","“It looks like I can’t hide anything from you. Chu Feng, I do think that it is a miracle for a cultivation resource without any side effects to exist, but I think that I should pave my path one step at a time to ensure a solid foundation. I want to acclimatize myself to the power of rank nine Half-God level before continuing my breakthrough. I believe that will be helpful to me,” Wang Yuxian replied.","“That works as well.” Chu Feng nodded.","If there were a way for him to make a breakthrough without shaking his foundation, he would have gone for it right away. Wang Yuxian’s worry was unfounded. However, everyone had their personal beliefs about cultivation. If this put Wang Yuxian’s heart at ease, it would be better for her to do so.","Otherwise, this matter might nurture an inner demon and hinder her future cultivation.","Next, Chu Feng made his way to the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. He needed to settle the matter concerning Wen Xue.","Soon, he learned that Wen Xue had already left, and the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster was currently in closed-door training. No one told him about Yaoyao, as they didn’t know that Wen Xue had taken her away.","There were many people whom Chu Feng cared about in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. Some were friends whom he had made inside the sect, but he had kin and friends residing here as well.","Back when the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion first stationed people in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy under the pretext of protecting it, the sectmaster was worried that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion might go after Chu Feng’s loved ones, so she brought them all into the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect to protect them.","She prepared independent realms for them to reside in, and she even granted a chance for juniors with whom Chu Feng was on close terms to join the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect.","This was a fortuitous encounter for some of them. They wouldn’t miss such an opportunity.","As a result, Chu Lingxi, Xia Yun’er, Li Yue’er, Wuma Shengjie, Kong Tianhui, Kong Ci, Long Ning, Xian Yun, and many others were now members of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect.","These people had been cultivating or doing missions at different places of the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, but upon learning that Chu Feng had returned, the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect made an exception and called all of them over.","They had already heard about the situation outside.","Kong Longxi and the others wanted to join the Chu Clan Alliance and fight the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion alongside Chu Feng.","However, Chu Feng told them to stay in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect. His mind would be more at ease this way.","A long-awaited reunion among good friends was a prime time to catch up, but Chu Feng was worried that a mishap would happen while he was away. So, he left right after handing them the resources he had prepared for them.","Chu Lingxi, Xia Yun’er, and a few others looked wistfully in the direction where Chu Feng had left. Kong Tianhui, on the other hand, didn’t hesitate to open the Cosmos Sack to see what Chu Feng had given him.","“Let me see what my Brother Chu Feng has brought. H-h-h-h-holy shit!”","Kong Tianhui fell on his bottom in shock.","His reaction invited confused gazes from the others.","“L-little sis, take a look for me. Am I seeing things? Did my monthly period go haywire, causing me to hallucinate? The items inside the Cosmos Sack can’t be real, right?” Kong Tianhui asked as he passed his Cosmos Sack to his little sister, Kong Ci.","“What do you mean by your monthly period going haywire? You don’t even have periods!” Kong Ci rolled her eyes at her big brother, though she did reach out and take his Cosmos Sack.","Everyone initially thought that Kong Tianhui was causing a big fuss out of nothing. Some even secretly laughed. They didn’t think that such a reaction was warranted just because Chu Feng gave them something.","Even Kong Ci thought the same.","But when she took the Cosmos Sack and inspected its contents, she, too, became stupefied. She quickly checked the Cosmos Sack that she had received from Chu Feng herself, and all of a sudden, she couldn’t pick up her slackened jaw anymore.","“My gosh, my gosh, my gosh! Isn’t C-C-Chu Feng being t-t-too generous? E-e-everyone, look at your own Cosmos Sacks!”","Upon seeing Kong Ci’s reaction, the others quickly inspected their Cosmos Sacks. What they saw completely shocked them. No matter how beautiful or dashing they were, their expressions were all more exaggerated than the other.","Compared to them, Kong Ci’s response could be considered dignified.","The treasures inside the Cosmos Sack were like a dream to them.","“Uwaaaaa!” Kong Tianhui suddenly burst into tears.","“My brother didn’t lie to me. He said that he’d bring me better resources the next time he returns. He has held to his promise. Can he be more amazing than this?” Kong Tianhui cried despite having a wide grin on his face.","The previously dazed crowd burst into laughter upon seeing his exaggerated expressions. At the same time, it confirmed that this was all real. Chu Feng had given them things surpassing their wildest imagination.","Once again, their cultivation was going to grow by leaps and bounds.","And thinking about it, the last time their cultivation surged forward was also thanks to Chu Feng.","While the others didn’t express themselves as intensely as Kong Tianhui, they shared the same emotions as him. They felt warmth from the bottom of their hearts.","They knew people who forgot their old friends and distanced themselves from their kin after making it big, so they could better integrate themselves into a higher social class. But Chu Feng remembered them no matter how high he climbed.","It felt good to have a friend like that.","...","Chu Feng was on the way to meet Little Fishy and the others when he sensed something amiss. He quickly stopped, activated his observation means, and examined God’s Era. His face quickly turned grim.","“It has finally begun.”"]},{"number":6643,"title":"Chapter 6643: Chapter 6641: Claiming the Upper Hand","paragraphs":["Chapter 6641: Claiming the Upper Hand","The remaining two powers of God’s Era had been revolving around its humongous silhouette for some time now. Many believed that it contained some clue, so they devoted their time to deciphering it.","But Chu Feng determined on the spot that the transformation was merely a decoy to exhaust one’s energy.","However, the transformation happening right now was the real deal.","Two bundles of power surged forth from God’s Era’s humongous silhouette.","Boom!","A loud buzz rippled through the world of cultivation, reaching every ear no matter where they were. It was not a piercing sound, but one could feel the weight and power behind it.","The sound was caused by the two powers exploding at the same time, and that caused them to scatter as two surges of meteor showers. Even as meteor showers, the sound of them whizzing through space could still be clearly heard.","“Chu Feng, how can we hear so clearly when we’re so far away? It’s almost as if we’re right beside the meteor showers. Is God’s Era taking special care of you, or does everyone hear it as well?” Eggy asked out of curiosity.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng activated his observation means to better examine the ongoing transformations. His gaze easily peered into other realms, where he noticed that most people were staring at the sky with flabbergasted looks. That gave him the answer to that question.","“Everyone heard it. God’s Era is doing it intentionally,” Chu Feng replied.","“Forget it. Chu Feng, you focus on observing the transformations first. We need to know where those powers are going to land,” Eggy said.","“All right.”","By this point, Chu Feng had already switched from Heaven’s Eyes to the Three Realms Divine Eyes. Soon, he noticed some peculiar details about those two surges of meteor showers.","They looked identical, but there were key differences between them. Discerning these key differences was vital to obtaining the energy.","“Look! There’s a change in the copper mirror!”","The Chu Clan Alliance was also observing the transformations in God’s Era.","Previously, Chu Feng and Jie Tianran’s silhouettes were stationary in the copper mirror, but now, both of their eyes were emitting extraordinary lights that moved alongside the two meteor showers.","“What does this phenomenon mean? Are Chu Feng and Jie Tianran observing the meteor showers right now?”","“It should be.”","Most people arrived at that deduction.","Indeed, Chu Feng was not the only one observing God’s Era. Jie Tianran was also using the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s observation formation to observe God’s Era transformations.","Most Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists were also doing the same.","“Something is off, Eggy,” Chu Feng suddenly said.","“What’s wrong?” Eggy asked in confusion.","“The difficulty seems lower than the previous time. I don’t think it’s likely that God’s Era will make the trial easier after throwing us so many decoys. Furthermore, God’s Era is so far away that we can’t see its transformations without using our observation means, but why are those sounds being projected all the way here?” Chu Feng asked.","“Didn’t you just say that God’s Era was doing it intentionally?” Eggy replied.","“But why is it doing this?”","“Are you thinking that something is hidden in the sounds?”","“Yes, that’s right. There has to be something hidden in the sounds. Perhaps the crux here is not what can be seen but what can be heard.”","Chu Feng was excited.","“Chu Feng, I was just blurting things out. Don’t listen to me too much. You should trust your judgment more.”","Eggy panicked. Her words had been thought through, but there was so much at stake here that she would rather Chu Feng rely on his instincts.","“It’s fine, Eggy. I have already memorized all visual clues, but I don’t think it should be this simple. I think that the sounds must be the crux. I’ll focus a bit,” Chu Feng said before closing his eyes.","As he closed his eyes, his silhouette in the copper mirror did the same, too.","“What’s going on? Why did Chu Feng suddenly close his eyes? Did something happen?”","The Chu Clan Alliance was horrified to see Chu Feng closing his eyes. They thought that something had happened to him, and their hearts began beating anxiously.","“Calm down, everyone. This could be a special observation means. It doesn’t mean that something has happened to Chu Feng,” Long Mucheng tried to calm the crowd down.","But the crowd remained nervous.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng was making progress.","Despite having closed his eyes, he could still track the movements of the two meteor showers through the sounds, especially since he had already studied them previously. He mapped their movements out in his mind, but for some reason, the trajectories were different.","“Eggy, you’re right. The crux lies in the sounds. No, to be exact, it lies in the heart. It can’t be seen with the eyes; it has to be felt through the heart! Eggy, it’s all thanks to you for imparting to me Heaven’s Eyes!”","Chu Feng was in a good mood after verifying his conjecture. He had found the right way to observe the phenomenon, but it only went smoothly because of Heaven’s Eyes.","Heaven’s Eyes trained not just his eyes but his heart, too. When he closed his eyes and tried to feel with his heart instead, he was actually tapping into Heaven’s Eyes observation prowess. He wouldn’t have perceived the clue so clearly if not for that.","“It’s good that it worked. Stop talking and focus.” Eggy was happy for Chu Feng as well.","“All right.” Chu Feng nodded.","Under the watchful eyes of countless, the two meteor showers parted ways. One fell into the Immortal Sea Galaxy, and the other fell into the Totem Galaxy.","The two powers were scattered into many fragments across many realms. Unlike before, these fragments emitted radiant light, making their locations obvious.","Chu Feng opened his eyes and looked toward the Immortal Sea Galaxy and Totem Galaxy.","He was not surprised by these changes. He turned his gaze toward God’s Era’s silhouette. When he saw that Jie Tianran’s silhouette was still emanating a brilliant light, he became certain that he had claimed the upper hand here."]},{"number":6644,"title":"Chapter 6644: Chapter 6642: An Imminent Battle","paragraphs":["Chapter 6642: An Imminent Battle","In the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, Jie Tianran mapped out the locations of the power fragments in the Totem Galaxy and the Immortal Sea Galaxy. Then, he began deploying personnel to extract the power fragments.","In particular, six Saint-tier elders and many elite elders were dispatched to an Upper Realm in the Totem Galaxy.","“Lord Mansion Master, is there something special about the power fragment there? Is there anything we should look out for?” a Saint-tier elder asked.","He had closely observed the earlier phenomenon, so he could tell that the Upper Realm contained one of the strongest power fragments, but he didn’t notice anything else aside from that. It seemed unnecessary to dispatch six Saint-tier elders if it was just that.","There must be something more to it.","“I can’t see through what’s in that Upper Realm as well, but the power fragments scattered across the Totem Galaxy seem to form a formation. Those two realms are where the formation cores are located,” Jie Tianran said.","“Formation?”","The elders scrutinized the layout of the power fragments, but their frowns only deepened. They couldn’t see the formation Jie Tianran mentioned, so they were unable to tell whether those two realms were truly the formation cores or not.","“Lord Mansion Master, do the power fragments in the Immortal Sea Galaxy form a formation as well, or is that only the case for the Totem Galaxy? What is the formation for?” a Saint-tier elder asked.","“I can’t discern what the formation is for or even confirm whether it is a formation or not. However, it does have the outline of a formation. That’s the case for the Immortal Sea Galaxy as well, but the Totem Galaxy’s formation is more unfathomable. While both galaxies are in the Northern Region, the Immortal Sea Galaxy has always been stronger than the Totem Galaxy.","“There must be a reason the God’s Era chose the Northern Region. I suspect it is related to the powers harnessed by the two galaxies. While the Totem Galaxy’s formation is more enigmatic, I believe that the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s power is more important. So, I’ll personally check out the Immortal Sea Galaxy. You just have to follow my deployment,” Jie Tianran said.","...","While Jie Tianran was issuing orders, Chu Feng returned to the Chu Clan Alliance and led everyone back into the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, where the bulk of their forces were stationed.","On the way back, Chu Feng drafted plans, but his plans were different from Jie Tianran’s.","“Chu Feng, are you avoiding the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, or is there another reason behind your decision?”","The crowd was baffled.","Unlike before, the current wave of power fragments constantly emitted light, making their locations known. The power fragments could be broadly classified into three tiers, from weak to strong.","For some reason, Chu Feng had ordered them to compete for the weakest power fragments.","“Yes, I am trying to avoid the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s main force, but I have my considerations as well. Please trust me, elders.” Chu Feng had intentionally left his words ambiguous lest the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion have a spy here.","“I trust you, Chu Feng. I’m just asking out of curiosity. We’ll go wherever you order us to go,” the crowd proclaimed.","Some even apologized to Chu Feng via voice transmission, fearing that he would be angry at them for questioning his judgment. Of course, Chu Feng was not a narrow-minded person, and he understood their curiosity.","“Chu Feng, what do you plan to do? Surely you aren’t going to keep me in suspense as well, are you?” Eggy’s euphonious voice was dripping with curiosity.","“The energies pulsating from the power fragments are a decoy. The seemingly ‘weaker’ power fragments are actually the ones that contain the most energy, but they have to be refined via a formation first.","“God’s Era has already constructed the refinement formation. There is a formation core in each galaxy.","“In contrast, the seemingly ‘stronger’ power fragments are much harder to extract, and they serve as fuel for the refinement formation. That’s why I told the others to collect the ‘weaker’ power fragments. Once we gather all the ‘weaker’ power fragments, I’ll activate the refinement formation, and the ‘stronger’ power fragments will be expended,” Chu Feng explained.","In other words, there was no point in collecting the ‘stronger’ formation cores.","“Where are the formation cores?” Eggy asked.","“They are in these two realms.” Chu Feng conjured a map of the two galaxies in his World Spirit Space to indicate the locations of the two formation cores.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has limited manpower, so they will prioritize the extraction of the ‘stronger’ power fragments. It shouldn’t be too hard for our people to gather the ‘weaker’ power fragments. However, those two realms contain the ‘strongest’ power fragments. It’ll be a bitter fight in those places. Do you intend to conquer them separately or together?” Eggy asked.","“The Nine Heavens Secret Domain doesn’t have teleportation formations near those two realms, so it’ll be difficult to conquer them one by one. We have to quickly conquer those two formation cores to claim the upper hand, or else the tables might be turned on us. We’ll have to split ways and conquer them simultaneously,” Chu Feng said.","“That shouldn’t be too hard. You have Yu’er and Fei,” Eggy remarked.","“It’s a good thing that Fei is strong, or else we would have been in trouble. I don’t think Jie Tianran has deciphered the deeper layer of the phenomenon, but he might notice that the layout of the power fragments forms a formation. If so, he could deduce where the formation cores are located.","“Even if he doesn’t have the full picture, his instincts as a world spiritist would be to guard the formation core until he deciphers the truth.","“The Immortal Sea Galaxy’s formation is considerably easier to decipher than the Totem Galaxy’s formation, so it is less likely for Jie Tianran to have deciphered the latter. I’ll send Fei, Elder Long Mucheng, and the Dragon Breath Clan to the Totem Galaxy’s formation core, while Yu’er and I head to the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s formation core.","“It’ll be safer this way, since even if we bump into Jie Tianran in the Immortal Sea Galaxy, we can still escape with Elder Divine Deer’s help,” Chu Feng said."]},{"number":6645,"title":"Chapter 6645: Chapter 6643: The Strongest Weapon, the Celestial Master Sacred Sword","paragraphs":["Chapter 6643: The Strongest Weapon, the Celestial Master Sacred Sword","“Not bad. You planned everything out quickly. You’re starting to act like the leader of the Chu Clan Alliance,” Eggy remarked with a smile.","“Stop teasing me, Eggy. The elders may trust me, but I’m still a junior,” Chu Feng replied.","“What junior? The Chu Clan Alliance was founded for you. Whether you like it or not, it has already been established. To hell with age! Everyone views you, Chu Feng, as their leader,” Eggy said.","“Haa~” Chu Feng sighed. Then, he remarked with a smile, “That’s why I’m feeling a lot of stress.”","He didn’t mind leaping right into danger alone, but he was shouldering the fate of countless people right now. His decisions could easily spell the difference between life and death for them. How could he not feel any stress?","“You don’t need to be stressed. They chose this path of their own volition. Putting aside the fact that they do owe you a favor, I’m sure they are also interested in God’s Era’s power. Cultivators seek fortune amid risk. If they die, they only have their own misfortune to blame. Countless cultivators die while pursuing treasures each day,” Eggy replied.","“I didn’t expect my Eggy to be so good at consoling people. I feel much less stressed after hearing your words,” Chu Feng smiled.","“Of course. There is nothing I am not good at,” Eggy replied gleefully.","It didn’t take long before Chu Feng and the others arrived at the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city.","He was planning to immediately rally the people together and head to the Northern Region, but just then, Sikong Changsheng stepped forward.","“Chu Feng, someone named Fu Xing is here for you. She seems to be in a rush to talk to you. Do you want to meet her first?”","“Fu Xing?” Chu Feng’s face lit up in delight.","The Chu Clan Alliance had been observing major events that happened in the world of cultivation, so he already knew about Jie Tianran wiping out the Celestial Master Sacred Sect.","Not long ago, Fu Xing had invited Chu Feng to cooperate with the Celestial Master Sacred Sect. He didn’t expect the Celestial Master Sacred Sect to be destroyed before they could even join forces.","While lamenting the destruction of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect, he was also worried about Fu Xing. He was glad to hear that she was safe and had made her way here.","Naturally, he made his way over to meet her.","“Elder, I’ll be counting on you to update the others about the situation,” Chu Feng said.","Long Mucheng nodded.","Then, Chu Feng followed Sikong Changsheng to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. He eventually met Fu Xing in a bamboo garden.","“Chu Feng, please help me exact vengeance!” Fu Xing kneeled on the ground.","She had traveled to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, but she didn’t know how to enter it, so she could only shout Chu Feng’s name outside. Sikong Changsheng already knew about her relationship with Chu Feng, so he brought her in.","Fu Xing understood right away that Sikong Changsheng was Chu Feng’s greatest backer. Sikong Changsheng was a legendary figure; she had heard about him. That reignited her hope of exacting vengeance, which was why she dove straight to the topic upon seeing Chu Feng.","“Fu Xing, did the Celestial Master Sacred Sect really meet with a mishap?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s right.” Fu Xing nodded.","She shared everything she had gone through with Chu Feng.","Chu Feng first consoled Fu Xing before asking, “Does this mean that Jie Tianran had gained possession of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s treasures?”","“It’s possible, but the chances are slim. My masters sacrificed their lives to unleash a powerful attack to destroy our treasures, lest they fall into Jie Tianran’s hands. However... I can’t guarantee it. Jie Tianran emerged unscathed from the attack,” Fu Xing said.","“You know the Celestial Master Sacred Sect better than anyone else. How much stronger will the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion be after gaining possession of those treasures?”","It was only a matter of time before the Chu Clan Alliance had a frontal clash with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Chu Feng needed to get a good grasp of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion before then.","“It’ll depend on how well they can grasp our treasures. If they can’t control it well, it’ll be weaker than a cultivator’s God Armament. However, if they can properly control it, it can surpass God Armaments,” Fu Xing replied.","“That sounds troublesome.” Chu Feng frowned.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Saint-tier elders were already a hassle to deal with due to the enhancement of their Sacred Formation. It would be terrible news if they obtained the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s world spiritist treasures on top of that.","“Chu Feng, I’ll give this to you.”","Fu Xing presented an iron piece that was around 1.3 meters long.","Chu Feng’s eyes glowed despite the unassuming appearance of the item. He could tell that it was a mystical world spiritist treasure. It greatly enhanced its user’s spirit power and adjusted itself according to its user’s traits.","In Fu Xing’s grasp, the iron piece manifested as a rose-colored sword.","In Chu Feng’s hand, it transformed into a black greatsword.","Chu Feng had coveted this item for a long time now. Had it been in the past, he would have never turned down this gift from Fu Xing. However, he felt conscience-stricken to accept it, given the current situation.","“This won’t do. How can I take your possession? Don’t worry, Fu Xing. We share a common enemy. I won’t spare the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion or Jie Tianran even if you don’t give me anything,” Chu Feng said.","“Our Celestial Master Sacred Sect has ten guardian treasures, and this sword is one of them. As a world spiritist, you should have heard about it. This is our Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s strongest sword,” Fu Xing said.","“So it’s called the Strongest Sword,” Chu Feng murmured.","Fu Xing’s lower jaw dropped to the ground. “Hold on... Have you never heard about it before?”","“Um...” Chu Feng looked awkward.","“Its name is the Celestial Master Sacred Sword. It is known that our founder gathered mystical materials across the world of cultivation to forge our sect’s guardian treasures, but this sword is an exception. Outsiders think that it was forged by our founder as well.”","“Oh? Is that not the case?” Chu Feng asked.","“It was already a complete product when our founder chanced upon it in an ancient remnant. Despite not being forged by our founder, it is still recognized as the number one treasure of our Celestial Master Sacred Sect, the strongest world spiritist weapon in the world of cultivation.”"]},{"number":6646,"title":"Chapter 6646: Chapter 6644: Expedition","paragraphs":["Chapter 6644: Expedition","“Chu Feng, you are a world spiritist prodigy. I’m confident that you’ll be able to draw out its true prowess. I’m ashamed that our Celestial Master Sacred Sect has only further raised the difficulty in your battle against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Please accept this gift, or else I will not get up from my kneeling position,” Fu Xing said.","“Don’t do that. I’ll accept your gift. I have coveted your sword for a while now, but I didn’t expect it to be the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s strongest guardian treasure,” Chu Feng said as he took the Celestial Master Sacred Sword.","He channeled his spirit power in the Celestial Master Sacred Sword, and the iron piece transformed into a ten-meter-long black greatsword enveloped in a black aura. It looked imposing.","“The Celestial Master Sacred Sword is a wonderful sword indeed,” Chu Feng remarked in delight.","He couldn’t curb his excitement despite having once held this sword and experienced its power.","“Chu Feng, you mustn’t keep the Celestial Master Sacred Sword activated for too long, or else there’ll be a backlash. The longer you keep it activated, the greater the backlash. It’d be best for you to avoid activating it if possible,” Fu Xing reminded.","“There is a backlash?” Chu Feng was surprised, for he didn’t feel any backlash.","“Yes, there is. From the moment you grasp the sword, a black line will begin extending from your wrist. The moment it connects with your heart, the backlash will act up. The severity of the backlash depends on the speed at which the black line moves.”","Fu Xing stood up and rolled up Chu Feng’s sleeve. What she saw stunned her.","There was no black line on Chu Feng’s wrist.","Chu Feng asked out of curiosity, “Does this mean that I can last a long time before I am at risk of facing a backlash?”","Fu Xing couldn’t believe her eyes. She rubbed Chu Feng’s wrist and stared at it for a while longer before finally putting it down. “Forget it, use the sword however you want.”","“Why?”","“I don’t see the black line at all. I doubt you’ll be at risk of suffering a backlash.”","“Ah... That’s good news.” Chu Feng smiled.","Fu Xing, on the other hand, looked conflicted. This was their sect’s most important treasure, but it turned out to be more compatible with an outsider than any of their sectmembers.","“Chu Feng, I have some Ancient Era’s teleportation talisman papers as well. It harnesses immense power, such that normal Heavenly Gods won’t be able to stop it. However, these talisman papers need to be awakened first before they can be used, and it won’t be easy to awaken them. At least, we won’t be able to do it at our current level. However, Elder Sikong Changsheng might be able to do it. You can seek his help,” Fu Xing said as she took out several teleportation talisman papers.","Chu Feng’s eyebrows shot up when he saw the talisman papers. “Can I try awakening them?”","“Huh? Yes, feel free to give it a try.” Fu Xing harbored no expectations despite saying so.","Weng!","The next moment, the talisman papers lit up.","Fu Xing’s eyes widened in astonishment. She subconsciously snatched a talisman paper back from Chu Feng’s hands to inspect it. Then, she stared at Chu Feng with utmost shock. “How did you do it?”","Even her master would take more time than this to awaken these talisman papers. Didn’t this mean that Chu Feng was more capable than her master?","“I sensed that these talisman papers could be awakened using my bloodline power, so I gave it a try. I’m glad that my gut feeling was right,” Chu Feng replied.","“You...”","Fu Xing stared at Chu Feng incredulously, but she soon came to terms with the situation. The latter had already done plenty of things that were inconceivable to her over the years anyway.","In the end, she remarked with a sigh, “Forget it. It’s a good thing you can use them now. You should take this as well.”","She took out a box and opened it. In it were a pair of golden boots, two golden bracelets, a golden belt, a golden robe, and a golden hairpin. They emanated a brilliant gleam. This was a set of world spiritist treasures, and they could raise one’s fighting prowess.","But they were clearly tailored for Fu Xing.","“Fu Xing, the Celestial Master Sacred Sword is enough. Keep those for yourself. If you keep insisting on this matter, I’ll return even the Celestial Master Sacred Sword to you as well,” Chu Feng spoke insistently.","“Fine.” Fu Xing relented.","Her master had indeed crafted these world spiritist treasures specifically for her, so she was reluctant to give them away. However, she was counting on Chu Feng to exact vengeance for her sect, so she thought that she should give him everything she had to boost his odds.","“Chu Feng, can I join you and fight alongside you?” Fu Xing asked.","“Of course, but I have a condition,” Chu Feng replied.","“What’s the condition?”","She had a determined look on her face, as if she would accept any condition laid out by him.","“Take this.” Chu Feng handed a sliver of God’s Era’s power to Fu Xing.","Fu Xing had grown considerably since their last meeting; she was already at rank eight True Dragon World Spiritist. Clearly, the Celestial Master Sacred Sect had its own means as well. They were waiting for Fu Xing to return from her mission before helping her raise her spirit power.","“All right.” Fu Xing knew that this was a token of Chu Feng’s goodwill, so she graciously accepted the gift.","Following this, Chu Feng met up with the other members of the Chu Clan Alliance.","Long Mucheng had already informed the crowd about his plan.","Chu Feng divided the Chu Clan Alliance into many teams and sent them into different realms depending on his risk analysis.","Each member was given a teleportation talisman paper, which they could use to escape from danger. Of course, the strength of the teleportation talisman paper corresponded to the expected difficulty level they would face.","Those who were closer to Chu Feng, such as the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief and the Totem Nine Daoists, received the teleportation talisman papers that Chu Feng had just received from Fu Xing.","These talisman papers were so strong that not even rank six Heavenly Gods or rank six Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists could hinder them.","Last but not least, Chu Feng set a location in each of the two galaxies for the teams to gather at.","With that, all preparations were in place.","The massive army of the Chu Clan Alliance stood in an orderly formation above the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, emanating an imposing air.","Chu Feng stood before the army, with the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, Long Mucheng, the Totem Nine Daoists, Little Fishy, and the others behind him.","“This expedition will be fraught with danger. Don’t hesitate to flee if you encounter enemies beyond your means. However, if you manage to defeat your enemies, make sure to massacre every single one of them,” Chu Feng said.","“Understood!” the crowd replied thunderously.","They knew what Jie Tianran had done, and they understood why Chu Feng had waged war against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Their seething reply evoked a peculiar emotion in Chu Feng’s heart.","Chu Feng drew his Monster Slayer Sword and pointed it toward the Northern Region.","“Set out!”","Boom boom boom!","The surrounding space quaked as the Chu Clan Alliance made its way northward.","The members of the Chu Clan Alliance felt a tinge of unease, but more than that, they were excited. God’s Era’s powers were so important that there was no way the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion would pass on them.","Encounters with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were inevitable.","If the Chu Clan Alliance’s clashes with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to date were only minor skirmishes, this would be the first time that both armies were facing each other head-on. For this reason, they placed great importance on this expedition."]},{"number":6647,"title":"Chapter 6647: Chapter 6645: Ambushed","paragraphs":["Chapter 6645: Ambushed","As the Chu Clan Alliance made their way to their assigned locations, the only ones remaining on the spot were Chu Feng, Little Fishy, the Dragon Breath Clan’s experts, and Fei. They would be traveling together with Chu Feng.","Ling Xiao’s grandfather had informed them that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had even faster traveling means, but they were rarely used because they consumed too many resources. In view of the exceptional circumstances, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion would surely use them to get to the formation cores as quickly as possible.","While the Nine Heavens Secret Domain didn’t have teleportation formations near the two formation cores, it would still be faster if they traveled to the two galaxies via the Nine Heavens Secret Domain before using other means to rush to their destinations.","Chu Feng intended to first bring Fei and the Dragon Breath Clan to the Totem Galaxy before heading to the Immortal Sea Galaxy with Little Fishy.","Along the way, he took out a few blue stones and handed them to Long Mucheng and the others.","These were signaling stones. Chu Feng had crafted them based on life stones. To send a signal, one would crush one’s stone, and other stones of the same color would shatter as well.","“Chu Feng, what signal do you intend to relay using these stones?” Fei asked.","Chu Feng had already given the team leaders several stones earlier. The signal would differ depending on the color of the stones shattered. However, this was the first time Chu Feng had taken out a blue stone.","“There’s no need to send a signal to me if you successfully conquer the formation core. However, if you fail, send me a signal first before heading over to my side. If both sides fail, we’ll return straight to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city,” Chu Feng said.","“It’s unlikely we’ll use this stone unless we encounter Jie Tianran.” Fei took the stone even though he was brimming with confidence.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is not to be underestimated. They could have seen through the formation cores and dispatched many experts to conquer them. The most dangerous location will be the place you’re heading. Don’t force yourself if you aren’t able to conquer the formation core. Instead, retreat right away.","“The power fragments scattered across the two galaxies aren’t God’s Era’s true powers yet. They are just tools that give us an edge in the final race. There’s no need to risk our lives for them. As long as we remain alive, we’ll have a shot at God’s Era’s final power,” Chu Feng said.","So far, the revealed God’s Era’s powers were just appetizers.","Next, Chu Feng took out over a dozen teleportation talisman papers and handed them to Fei, Long Mucheng, and the Dragon Breath Clan’s experts. These were from Fu Xing.","In truth, there was no need for him to give them a teleportation talisman paper each. A single talisman paper could bring them all to safety, but he thought that it would be better to err on the side of caution.","“Don’t worry, Chu Feng. I’ll settle this matter for you. I might have let that Saint-tier elder slip away the last time, but I won’t allow that to happen a second time,” Fei crossed his arms as he spoke confidently.","“That’s good to hear,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“Chu Feng, we can use my boat if we’re in a rush. Mine’s very fast,” Fei said as he pulled out a copper boat.","“No need. Follow me. It’ll be faster,” Chu Feng replied.","“Oh?” Fei raised his eyebrows in skepticism.","Later, after they entered the Nine Heavens Secret Domain and emerged from its teleportation formation, Fei’s skepticism was replaced with astonishment. He stared at Chu Feng in disbelief as he asked, “We’re already at the Totem Galaxy?”","“Isn’t it fast?” Chu Feng asked.","“Fast. Too freaking fast! It only took us two hours to cross galaxies!” Fei exclaimed in shock.","“You can use your copper boat now,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","Chu Feng and Little Fishy parted ways with the others and headed to the Immortal Sea Galaxy. Some time later, they arrived at the realm where the formation core was located.","Chu Feng didn’t enter the realm right away. He first scanned it using his Heaven’s Eyes to confirm that everything was fine before finally entering the realm with Little Fishy.","As soon as they stepped into the realm, the space around them shook. A powerful surge of spirit power swiftly enveloped the realm and formed a sealing formation. Then, a spirit formation gate appeared, and several Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists stepped out.","Jie Tianran stood at the forefront of the group.","“Chu Feng, I knew you would come here, but I didn’t expect you to arrive so quickly. However, I am still one step ahead of you.”","Chu Feng was also surprised to see Jie Tianran. He might have taken a detour to the Totem Galaxy, but his traveling speed was still much faster than conventional means. He didn’t expect Jie Tianran to arrive ahead of him.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was still more powerful than Chu Feng had expected.","Little Fishy unleashed her bloodline power, raising her cultivation from rank one Heavenly God to rank five Heavenly God.","The world spiritists behind Jie Tianran looked at Little Fishy with conflicted faces. They had heard about her means, but it was a different story to witness it in person. They would have never imagined that a Heavenly God could raise their cultivation by four ranks.","Even Jie Tianran’s eyes flickered in unease. At this rate, it was only a matter of time before Little Fishy surpassed him.","“Xianhai Yu’er, you do possess exceptional talent. Your grandfather and father weren’t able to raise their heads in front of me. I wonder if you can restore some of their honor... though your cultivation is not enough to fight me. You’ll need more than that,” Jie Tianran sneered tauntingly.","His words hinted that he was stronger than Little Fishy.","Little Fishy was about to speak when Chu Feng stopped her.","“Yu’er, don’t bother arguing with that old bastard.”","Chu Feng activated the teleportation talisman he had received from Fu Xing. He planned to escape right away. Powerful teleportation energy enveloped both Chu Feng and Little Fishy.","But at the same time, clanging sounds echoed from the sealing formation.","Chu Feng realized right away that they were in trouble. There was something ominous about the sealing formation. The teleportation energy enveloping them was failing to work its wonder. He didn’t expect Jie Tianran to come prepared.","“Do you think I wouldn’t have anticipated this?” Jie Tianran sneered.","His oppressive might crushed down on Chu Feng and Little Fishy like a furious tsunami, moving at an exceedingly fast speed. His spirit power was at rank five Heavenly Dragon, but he wielded heaven-defying battle power capable of surmounting a cultivation rank.","There was no question that he was stronger than Little Fishy. Before Little Fishy could react, the oppressive might had already enveloped the two of them.","But Jie Tianran’s face stiffened up.","He sensed that his oppressive might had struck its targets, but for some reason, it had failed to inflict any harm on the two of them."]},{"number":6648,"title":"Chapter 6648: Chapter 6646: The Furious Divine Deer","paragraphs":["Chapter 6646: The Furious Divine Deer","Jie Tianran stared at Chu Feng.","Both Chu Feng and Little Fishy were cloaked in a layer of white light.","Little Fishy was not surprised by the situation, having known beforehand that Chu Feng had a secret hand if they encountered danger. Chu Feng also knew right away that it was the Divine Deer.","Soon, the white light expanded outward and manifested into a young lady. Her skin was as smooth as jade, and she wore a green dress. She commanded a domineering disposition that kept others at bay.","She was the Divine Deer.","Jie Tianran and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elders examined the Divine Deer. They, too, had realized that the Divine Deer was the reason behind Chu Feng’s fearlessness.","Chu Feng didn’t expect the Divine Deer to reveal herself. So far, she had only channeled her powers to bring him to safety.","The Divine Deer looked at Jie Tianran with a disdainful gaze. “I’ll be taking Chu Feng away with me now. Do you think you can stop me?”","“Are you taunting me right now?” Jie Tianran sneered.","“Taunt you? Would you taunt a mere ant?”","“What arrogance. Like master, like servant. Since you asked for it, I’ll let you have a taste of my means.”","Jie Tianran pulled out two talisman papers emanating ancient auras and formed a hand seal. The two talisman papers were set ablaze. They transformed into two giant aura dragons that surged into the sky. As they ascended, their bodies gradually became increasingly corporeal and larger.","In the blink of an eye, the two dragons had already surged out of the realm into space. Their massive bodies coiled around the realm, and the realm began to quake.","Towering waves gushed from one of the dragons’ bodies, forming a humongous barrier that sealed off the realm. These waves were so huge that some of them fell as torrential rain upon the realm.","Then, the other dragon unleashed waves of frigid air.","The frigid air also formed a barrier that enveloped the realm. Under its intense coldness, the torrential rain transformed into a furious snowstorm that dyed the entire realm white.","But the true threat lay in the barriers of surging frost and water above. These two barriers harnessed incomparable prowess. The frost barrier was impenetrable, and the water barrier was treacherous.","Sensing the danger they posed, Chu Feng was nervous. He sent a voice transmission to the Divine Deer, “Elder.”","The Divine Deer immediately replied, “You have nothing to worry about.”","She looked at Jie Tianran in contempt.","Jie Tianran’s face darkened. He didn’t like the Divine Deer’s attitude. She behaved as if everything was within her control, and everyone else was just playing second fiddle to her. Furthermore, he could sense that her attitude was not just superficial but that she earnestly looked down on him from the bottom of her heart.","“A mere ant you are indeed.”","Had these words been from anyone else, they would have come across as an insult. But from the Divine Deer, it felt like she was stating a fact. At least to her, Jie Tianran was truly no better than an ant.","The proof lay in how easily the Divine Deer flitted out of the realm with Chu Feng and Little Fishy. It was as if the impenetrable frost barrier and dangerous water barrier were nonexistent to her; she didn’t even have to destroy the barriers to traverse through them.","“Your grandson’s secret hand is quite something,” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body said.","Jie Tianran’s hands trembled under his sleeves. It was a rare show of emotions from him. His repeated failures against Chu Feng eroded his confidence, unraveling his composure. He let out a deafening roar of frustration.","“Run, Chu Feng! Run as far as you can. You declared war on the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion because you learned about your grandmother’s death. That foolish woman turned against me for you. She deserved to die for that, but all this wouldn’t have happened if not for you.","“You want to avenge Nianqing, don’t you? But you are weak and incompetent. All you have been able to do in my presence is run.”","Jie Tianran’s voice boomed across space, reaching Chu Feng’s ears.","“That shameless old thing!” Eggy sneered in anger. She wanted to step out from her World Spirit Space to cuss at Jie Tianran.","Even Little Fishy looked livid. Her little mouth puffed up in anger, and she was more than ready to defend Chu Feng’s honor.","But Chu Feng stopped them. “Ignore him.”","He didn’t look frustrated at all. As much as he hated Jie Tianran and wanted to avenge his grandmother, he wasn’t so weak-minded as to fall for such elementary taunts.","However, the Divine Deer stopped and turned around to look at Jie Tianran.","“Look at how old you are, and how old Chu Feng is,” the Divine Deer scoffed.","She placed a hand on her hip while pointing at Jie Tianran with her other hand. Her cold and lofty expression was now replaced with fury.","“Shameless old thing, look at your own face. Can you even call that wrinkled thing a face? You’re practically a bun now. Even calling you a bun is an insult to all buns. Buns have fewer wrinkles than you.","“How long have you been cultivating for now? How thick-skinned do you have to be to call yourself a prodigy when you have been stuck at Heavenly Dragon for many years now? Have you buried your shame in that thick pastry face of yours?","“Tell me, where do you find the confidence to bark so loudly when you can’t even stop a mere junior from escaping? It’s almost like you take pride in that. I don’t know much about the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but your predecessors must be blind to let trash like you inherit their mantle.”","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elders stiffened in shock.","No one could have expected such crude words from the lofty lady. Even Chu Feng and Little Fishy were stunned. This was Chu Feng’s first time seeing the Divine Deer cussing someone out like that.","After the Divine Deer spoke her piece, she regained her earlier composure as if nothing had happened. She looked at Jie Tianran and calmly continued, “Ant, cherish the times you get to see Chu Feng flee. Once he stops fleeing, you’ll be the one to flee.”","The Divine Deer disappeared together with Chu Feng and Little Fishy, but her words continued to echo in the surroundings.","These words cut deeper into Jie Tianran and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s elders than her earlier insult.","Indeed, Chu Feng was just a junior, and he was growing at a rapid pace. He had come a long way since the first time he wreaked havoc in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","If Little Fishy had grown so strong after reaching Heavenly God level, they shuddered to imagine how strong Chu Feng, the number one prodigy of the world of cultivation, would be once he overcame the hurdle and reached the Heavenly God and Heavenly Dragon levels.","None of them was confident of dealing with him."]},{"number":6649,"title":"Chapter 6649: Chapter 6647: Soloing Six Saint-tier Elders","paragraphs":["Chapter 6647: Soloing Six Saint-tier Elders","The Divine Deer transported Chu Feng and Little Fishy to safety.","“Elder, I didn’t expect you to have such a sharp mouth.”","Chu Feng grinned at the Divine Deer, feeling closer to her now. Her earlier action was reminiscent of an elder standing up for a junior bullied by outsiders.","“Who doesn’t know how to cuss? It was just beneath me to do so. But that trash of a grandfather you have was asking for it,” the Divine Deer replied as she returned into Chu Feng’s body.","Chu Feng wanted to chat more with the Divine Deer, but the latter had already reverted to her usual lofty attitude.","A moment later, Chu Feng’s face stiffened up. He noticed that Little Fishy had one hand crossing her chest and the other propping up her chin. She was staring at him with a bizarre, contemplative gaze.","“Yu’er... why are you looking at me like that?” Chu Feng asked.","“Big brother, it’s one thing for you to have that gorgeous big sister world spirit, but why is your secret hand a ravishing lady, too? I’m curious to know if it’s a coincidence or if you have chosen this,” Little Fishy said.","“It’s a coincidence,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“I see.” Little Fishy didn’t probe any further, but her gaze was one of skepticism.","Chu Feng felt wronged. He really was not a pervert. It was truly a coincidence... though he had to admit that he did enjoy this series of coincidences.","“Big brother, what should we do next? Should we head to the Totem Galaxy? Or do you have other plans in mind?” Little Fishy asked.","They still had more serious business to deal with.","“We have already bumped into Jie Tianran here. Considering his skeptical personality, the chances are that he’ll continue camping here and not reinforce the Totem Galaxy. Since that’s the case, we should just head to the Totem Galaxy.”","Chu Feng took out the signaling stone to inform Fei and Long Mucheng that they had failed.","As he crushed the signaling stone, Little Fishy leaned over to look at the other signaling stones. The other signaling stones were still intact, a sign that everything was still going well.","“Big brother, how do you think the other side is faring?” Little Fishy asked.","“I can’t say for sure. Since Jie Tianran was able to see through the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s formation core, he might be able to do the same for the Totem Galaxy’s formation core. The only question remaining is whether he has deciphered the use of the two formations. Let’s hope that he hasn’t figured that out yet,” Chu Feng replied.","The two of them began making their way to the Totem Galaxy.","Meanwhile, Fei, Long Mucheng, and the Dragon Breath Clansmen were near the realm where the Totem Galaxy’s formation core was located and were observing the situation.","They didn’t enter the realm right away because they had detected Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members.","“They got here a step faster than us.” Long Mucheng felt uneasy.","“Who cares? Let’s just beat them up.” Fei was unbothered by the situation. He was looking forward to a fight.","Just then, Long Mucheng and Fei widened their eyes. They reached into their respective Cosmos Sacks and took out a broken signaling stone. This was a sign that Chu Feng’s side had failed their mission.","“Chu Feng and Yu’er failed? Does that mean that Jie Tianran is on their side?” Fei remarked in surprise.","He had witnessed Little Fishy’s strength and knew what she was capable of.","“We have no choice but to make a move. Let’s go with what we discussed earlier,” Long Mucheng spoke with conviction.","She had made up her mind to do it with the Dragon Breath Clan.","Fei suddenly raised his hand to stop Long Mucheng. “Wait, I have another idea. You don’t go in first.”","“Didn’t we agree that our Dragon Breath Clan will support you through a formation?” Long Mucheng asked.","“We have different bloodlines. Even if your formation works on me, its effectiveness will be limited. Let me do it myself instead,” Fei said as he began flying into the realm.","The Dragon Breath Clansmen turned to Long Mucheng.","“Let him do whatever he wants,” Long Mucheng said with a sigh.","It didn’t take long for Fei to enter the realm.","Six surges of spirit power gushed out of the realm and scattered outward to form a barrier, trapping Fei within.","“Oh no!” Long Mucheng exclaimed.","The other party had laid an ambush for them.","Long Mucheng thought about charging through the barrier to reinforce Fei, but she quickly dropped that idea when she realized that she couldn’t even see through the barrier with her observation means.","That meant the other party was stronger than her, and that she would only be baggage if she joined the fray recklessly.","Meanwhile, Fei landed in the realm, and the powerful shockwave that rippled from his landing transformed the flat plain into a deep valley. He wasn’t planning on sneaking in; he had intended to cause this huge commotion from the very start.","But looking at the barrier in the sky, he realized that the enemy had already noticed him, so it didn’t matter whether he snuck in or not.","“Am I seeing things? There are six of you?” Fei remarked in surprise.","Six figures appeared in the sky. It was Fei’s first time seeing them, but he recognized the white aura shrouding their bodies. Those six people were Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Saint-tier elders.","“You must be the monstrous beast who attacked our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s territory,” one of the Saint-tier elders asked.","“That’s me. You aren’t going to run?” Fei asked.","“What arrogance.”","The six Saint-tier elders moved simultaneously to construct a massive golden formation resembling a mini realm that descended upon Fei.","In response, Fei’s martial power erupted like a volcano as he unleashed a punch. His fist penetrated the golden formation and shattered it into bits.","The six Saint-tier elders exchanged looks, then their bodies glowed brightly. To be exact, it was their world spiritist treasures that were glowing. They had been wearing these world spiritist treasures all along, just that they had concealed them earlier.","With the activation of these world spiritist treasures, the six Saint-tier elders’ strength further increased.","“Chu Feng is right. You have stolen the Celestial Master Sacred Sect’s treasures. Didn’t you declare that your philosophy diverges from that of the Celestial Master Sacred Sect? You look snug in their world spiritist treasures right now. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is truly shameless,” Fei scoffed.","Weng!","The clouds were suddenly ripped apart as a massive formation sword descended from the sky.","The six Saint-tier elders had no intention of debating with Fei and continued their assault.","Fei drew a golden God Armament spear with a flick of his wrist, and his aura surged. He took a step back before abruptly tossing his spear upward.","Boom!","The small God Armament spear clashed with the massive formation sword, causing the sword to crack before shattering into bits. Giant metal pieces rained from the sky like a meteor storm, as the spear flew back into Fei’s hand.","Despite having claimed the upper hand, Fei’s eyes flickered in unease.","It might look like he had thrown his spear casually, but in truth, he had infused a powerful bloodline martial skill into his God Armament. This was one of his strongest moves. He had expected the move to inflict significant damage on the six Saint-tier elders after shattering the formation sword, but the result was underwhelming.","Each of the six Saint-tier elders wielded strength comparable to his, but he was alone, whereas there were six enemies.","He was at a disadvantage here.","The six Saint-tier elders in the sky unleashed their spirit power alongside their bloodline power and converged them. A terrifying aura could be felt from their combined powers.","“Shit! Are those six old things really trying to kill me?”"]},{"number":6650,"title":"Chapter 6650: Chapter 6648: Fei’s Secret Hand","paragraphs":["Chapter 6648: Fei’s Secret Hand","That is...”","Long Mucheng and the Dragon Breath Clansmen watched the scene in unease. The transformations happening to the realm looked even more shocking from their perspectives.","Spirit power had already enveloped the realm, and it was transforming from a brilliant light into six devastating powers—lightning, ice, wind, fire, poison, and water.","“Could this be the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s legendary Calamitous Formation?” a Dragon Breath Clansman murmured.","Someone else immediately refuted, “But the Calamitous Formation requires six people to deploy. Could it be...”","The crowd turned to Long Mucheng.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion must have realized that this realm is important as well,” Long Mucheng said with a sigh.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion must have dispatched six Saint-tier elders here.","And that was indeed Jie Tianran’s intention. It took six people to deploy the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s strongest slaughter formation. He figured that should be enough to subdue the Chu Clan Alliance’s rank five Heavenly Gods.","Long Mucheng immediately ordered her clansmen to retreat. She didn’t think that Fei could overcome this formation to defeat the six Saint-tier elders, and that it was more likely that he would retreat.","Meanwhile, Fei reached into his Cosmos Sack, but he didn’t grab Chu Feng’s teleportation talisman paper. His eyes had been flickering in hesitation ever since he saw the six powers devastating the sky.","“But I have already given him my word. Isn’t it too embarrassing if I flee like that? Haa! It’s one thing for me to embarrass my master, but I can’t embarrass Junior Miaomiao as well.”","Fei pulled his hand out of the Cosmos Sack and looked at the sky.","“I’ll concede. That’s a formidable formation. But the six of you are unlucky to have bumped into me. Come at me. I’ll take you to the afterlife!” Fei looked at the six Saint-tier elders in the sky as he spoke tauntingly.","The expressions of the six Saint-tier elders hardened. They didn’t say a word, but they channeled even more of their spirit power into the Calamitous Formation.","Boom!","The six devastating powers descended simultaneously upon Fei.","“This feeling...”","The faces of the six Saint-tier elders warped in shock. To their astonishment, their formation had failed to kill Fei.","Fei’s body and soul were tattered, but the attack had failed to take him down. That was impossible! They could easily disintegrate even this realm with the power they currently wield, so how could they have failed to kill a mere Fei?","Soon, their expressions changed from confusion to horror.","Fei’s body was undergoing a metamorphosis.","“Suppress him with all our might!”","The six Saint-tier elders channeled all their energy into the Calamitous Formation, but their fear only deepened as if they were fighting against the inevitable.","Boom!","A green aura erupted from Fei and swiftly engulfed the realm, including the Calamitous Formation.","“What is that?”","Outside, the Dragon Breath Clansmen were astounded. A green aura had appeared out of nowhere and destroyed the powerful Calamitous Formation.","“That appears to be Fei’s means,” Long Mucheng blurted out.","“Fei? Is that fellow this powerful?”","The crowd felt delighted and mystified. They thought that Fei would have no choice but to retreat, but somehow, the latter managed to unravel the Calamitous Formation constructed by six Saint-tier elders.","Soon, the green aura receded. The barrier sealing the realm vanished along with it.","Long Mucheng and the Dragon Breath Clansmen could finally look into the realm.","They noticed that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists had vanished; there was only one person in the realm—Fei.","Long Mucheng quickly entered the realm and descended to Fei’s side.","“How are you, Fei?” Long Mucheng asked concernedly.","Fei’s body had turned dark red, and he was emitting searing heat. It was as if someone had lit a flame inside him.","“What can happen to me? I’m just annoyed that those six old things managed to force out my secret hand. How is it? Aren’t I incredible?” Fei asked gleefully.","“You’re practically invincible.”","Long Mucheng and the others lavished Fei with compliments.","Fei’s smile deepened.","“Here. Pass this to Chu Feng,” Fei said as he tossed a Cosmos Sack over to Long Mucheng.","Long Mucheng opened the Cosmos Sack. It was filled with world spiritist treasures and origin energies. Surprisingly, Fei meticulously preserved the treasures while devastating his enemies.","But Long Mucheng keenly sensed something amiss.","“Aren’t you going to wait for Chu Feng and the others to arrive?” Long Mucheng asked.","“My mission is to help Chu Feng once. I have already accomplished my mission, so the rest is up to him. Make sure to guard this place properly until he arrives. Don’t let my effort be in vain.”","A carefree smile appeared on Fei’s monstrous face. “Farewell.”","He rose into the sky and vanished.","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran was still in the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s formation core realm. His face looked awful, having yet to recover from the Divine Deer’s insult. Her words had struck a nerve.","Just then, his eyes widened.","He hurriedly took out a box and opened it. In it were a hundred life tokens placed neatly. They were tied to the strongest experts in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Six of the life tokens on the uppermost row had shattered.","“They managed to claim the formation core in the Totem Galaxy?” the old entity exclaimed in astonishment.","Chu Feng and Little Fishy had only just left, and there was no way they could reach the Totem Galaxy so quickly. This meant that the Chu Clan Alliance had other experts who were as strong as Little Fishy.","This didn’t bode well for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Focus on guarding this place, Jie Tianran. Don’t bother sending reinforcements over. Anyone else who goes will just face the same outcome. That grandson of yours is not that easy to deal with,” the old entity said.","Jie Tianran nodded. He had no qualms about sacrificing the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s members, but the Saint-tier elders were still valuable to him right now. It pained his heart to have lost six Saint-tier elders like that.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng and Little Fishy had reached the Totem Galaxy’s formation core realm.","Long Mucheng faced no trouble guarding the realm because the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had not sent any reinforcements over. She updated Chu Feng about the situation before handing him Fei’s Cosmos Sack.","“Where did Fei go?” Chu Feng asked.","“He said that he has accomplished his mission, and the rest is up to us,” Long Mucheng replied.","“I see.”","Chu Feng nodded. He didn’t probe deeper into the matter, but his face looked grim.","Next, he surveyed the realm.","He didn’t find anything at first, but when he closed his eyes and tried to perceive with his heart, he immediately found the formation core. While it was well-hidden, it wouldn’t be too difficult to activate it.","So, he activated the formation core. It turned out to be a strong protective formation.","“This realm actually has such a formidable protective formation? It’s a good thing those Saint-tier elders are nowhere near as sharp as you!” Long Mucheng and the others felt delighted and fearful at the same time.","On the one hand, they didn’t have to fear the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion invading this realm anymore. On the other hand, they couldn’t help but imagine how terribly things could have gone if those Saint-tier elders had actually found this protective formation.","“Yu’er, you stay here with Elder Long and the others. I need to do something,” Chu Feng said.","“Big brother, I’ll go with you,” Little Fishy said.","“I can handle this myself,” Chu Feng replied.","“That won’t do. I won’t let you go anywhere unless you take me along.” Little Fishy obstinately grabbed Chu Feng’s arm, displaying a rare forceful attitude.","“All right. Let’s go together,” Chu Feng acquiesced.","The two of them left the realm together and headed to the neighboring realm.","Little Fishy quietly followed Chu Feng without asking what he was looking for. It wasn't until she saw a figure in the distance that she finally understood why he had left so urgently.","It was Fei.","His body was crimson-red as if seared by lava. It wouldn’t have been surprising if his body exploded right there and then. His expression was warped in pain. Despite his attempts to stifle his voice, he still let out guttural moans.","Tears flowed from his feral eyes and evaporated right away.","It was clear that his days were numbered."]},{"number":6651,"title":"Chapter 6651: Chapter 6649: Cut the Nonsense","paragraphs":["Chapter 6649: Cut the Nonsense","Little Fishy was horrified by Fei’s severe injuries. He had incurred these injuries while helping Chu Feng. She was worried that Chu Feng would feel guilty for life if something were to happen to Fei.","In contrast, Chu Feng looked much calmer.","Before he reached Fei, he had already formed a hand seal and thrust his palm forth, delivering a surge of spirit power toward Fei. It was a recovery formation; he had constructed it on the way here.","“Chu...” Fei belatedly noticed Chu Feng and Little Fishy, but he was so feeble that he couldn’t even call out Chu Feng’s name.","“Stay still.”","Chu Feng grabbed Fei’s wrist to feel his pulse.","Moments later, he frowned. Fei’s injuries were worse than he had expected.","He took out three pills and placed them in Fei’s mouth.","One of the pills was not a recovery pill. Instead, it contained a formation Chu Feng had constructed on his way here. Shortly after Fei took in the formation pill, his body began to convulse intensely.","Chu Feng quickly constructed another formation.","“Big brother, do you need my help?” Little Fishy asked.","“Don’t worry, Yu’er. I can handle it,” Chu Feng replied.","Fei stared at Chu Feng in confusion.","Chu Feng explained, “The signalling stones are imbued with location formations. I can sense where you are as long as you’re within a certain radius. Elder Long Mucheng told me you have left, but I sensed you were in a neighboring realm. I knew right away that you must have sustained severe injuries but were too obstinate to weep in front of the others.”","“I-I di... didn't...” Fei’s face reddened in embarrassment. He tried his best to deny it, but he was so weak that he couldn’t even complete his sentence.","“Don’t be so obstinate. Your pride can’t be more important than staying alive,” Chu Feng said with a sigh. He turned to Little Fishy and said, “Yu’er, I’ll need you to step back. Don’t come in, no matter what happens, or else it’ll undermine the formation and endanger both Fei and me.”","“All right.” Little Fishy nodded as she backed off into the distance.","Chu Feng grandly flung his sleeves. An even larger formation enveloped him and Fei. He changed his hand seal.","“GAHHHH!!!”","Fei’s body levitated into the air, as his mouth, eyes, and ears began emitting a searing red aura. The red aura hissed aggressively like a feral beast, but it was currently being contained by Chu Feng’s spirit power.","There were only two targets that the red aura could attack now—Fei and Chu Feng.","So, the aura charged at Chu Feng, but the latter allowed it to enter his body without struggling. Soon, his body turned fiery red as if someone had set him ablaze. Even his skin began to crack.","“Big brother!”","Little Fishy panicked. She rushed forward to help Chu Feng, only to quickly halt her footsteps when she recalled his earlier words. He had asked her not to intervene, which meant that he had anticipated this situation and had a plan.","In truth, she wouldn’t know what to do even if she charged forward. Her inability to help him made her feel terribly helpless. She felt like someone was shredding her heart as she saw the excruciating pain he was put through.","Just then, Chu Feng turned around and looked at Little Fishy. He didn’t seem to be in pain. He even grinned, revealing his gleaming, white teeth.","“I’m fine, Yu’er. Such minor burns feel like nothing more than a cozy campfire to me.”","He turned around right after saying those words. Had he moved any slower, Little Fishy would have seen him gritting his teeth.","“Brother Fei, how are you able to tolerate this? This is unbearable,” Chu Feng asked Fei via voice transmission.","Fei looked at Chu Feng. He wanted to say something, but he couldn’t squeeze a word out.","“I hope you don’t mind me, Fei. I’ll assume that silence means consent,” Chu Feng said.","While Fei was making sense of those words, Chu Feng opened his mouth wide, and a concentrated surge of aura flowed out from his mouth. The aura was green, but it harnessed frost energy.","The frost energy was immediately devoured by the searing energy, but the green aura still flowed into Fei’s body intact.","Chu Feng changed his hand seal, and more red aura flowed into his body.","Fei finally understood what was going on.","Chu Feng had seen through his injuries.","Fei had used a forbidden skill to set his bloodline ablaze. It granted him a burst of strength, but the flames couldn’t be suppressed. The only thing he could do was to withstand the flame with his body, or else his bloodline would continue burning until it was vaporized.","Chu Feng understood that the only way to help Fei was to help him absorb the flame in his bloodline. It might look like his formation was intended to heal Fei, but in truth, it served as a barrier to stop Fei’s bloodline power from dissipating into the surroundings.","The formation pill he had fed Fei facilitated the extraction of Fei’s bloodline from his body, so that he could absorb the searing energy from Fei’s bloodline and channel the cleansed bloodline back into Fei’s body.","The method was effective. Despite having only cleansed a small portion of his bloodline power, Fei had regained his speech.","“You can’t, Chu Feng! You’ll die like that. You don’t know how fearsome the searing energy is. That isn’t something you can absorb with your body!” Fei exclaimed.","No one knew better than him how terrifying the searing energy was. Chu Feng would burn to death at this rate!","But Chu Feng ignored Fei’s persuasion and said, “Cut the crap.”","He changed his hand seal and opened his mouth again, releasing another surge of cleansed bloodline power back into Fei’s body.","Fei was surprised. Chu Feng was sturdier than he had expected. However, he still couldn’t accept Chu Feng saving him in such a manner.","“This won’t do. Your bloodline and soul will be impaired even if you survive this ordeal. It’ll affect your future cultivation!” Fei exclaimed.","“You’re still prattling?” Chu Feng snorted.","“Chu Feng...”","Chu Feng coldly interjected, “Cut the crap and focus.”","“You...”","Fei didn’t know what else to say. He looked at Chu Feng with a conflicted expression.","Xian Miaomiao had told him a lot about Chu Feng, including secrets no one else knew. In truth, he wasn’t interested in Chu Feng at all. He was only listening out of respect for Xian Miaomiao.","In fact, he had only come to help Chu Feng because he had been around Song Changsheng for too long and wanted to catch a breather.","Yet, Chu Feng was putting his life on the line to save him.","Despite his attempts to talk Chu Feng out of it, the latter ignored him and obstinately continued. He could feel Chu Feng’s sincerity.","Rumors were ultimately rumors. It was a different matter to experience it in person. Before this, he would have never thought that Chu Feng would put his life on the line for someone he barely knew.","What Chu Feng, Fei, and Little Fishy didn’t know was that someone else was hiding in the area, spying on them."]},{"number":6652,"title":"Chapter 6652: Chapter 6650: Song Changsheng Wants to Have a Son","paragraphs":["Chapter 6650: Song Changsheng Wants to Have a Son","As the treatment continued, Fei’s condition visibly improved, but Chu Feng’s condition visibly worsened. Chu Feng’s body turned searing red like a volcano on the verge of eruption, just like the earlier Fei.","Little Fishy was distressed. She couldn’t hold herself back despite having promised not to get involved.","“Big brother, I’m a world spiritist as well. Tell me the method. I can help you.”","“It’s fine, Yu’er. I can withstand this.” Chu Feng turned around and smiled at Little Fishy.","But his response only made Little Fishy feel worse. Anyone could tell that his smile was strained, let alone her. He was in such a terrible state that she considered forceful intervention. Either Chu Feng taught her the method to treat Fei, or she would stop him.","There was no way she could watch as Chu Feng died before her eyes.","“Don’t worry, miss. They won’t die,” a voice echoed from behind Little Fishy.","Chu Feng and Fei’s eyes lit up in delight. They recognized the voice.","All of them looked over and saw a middle-aged man carrying an axe standing behind Little Fishy. Even though he had revealed himself, he still exuded no aura whatsoever. Were it not for his speaking up, they wouldn’t have noticed him at all.","He was Fei’s master, Song Changsheng.","“MASTERRRRRRRRRR! SAVE MEEEEEEEEE!!!” Fei burst into tears.","Despite still being in the form of a monstrous beast, he cried like a child who had been bullied and was looking for his parents for support. He dropped his strong front to let his grievances all out.","Song Changsheng clutched his forehead helplessly.","Looking at the nonchalant Chu Feng, followed by his sobbing disciple, he felt awkward and embarrassed.","“Elder, are you able to save them?” Little Fishy asked with a hopeful gaze.","Song Changsheng nodded.","That eased Little Fishy’s mind. She had heard about Song Changsheng’s means and knew that he was unfathomably powerful.","However, Song Changsheng seemed to be in no rush to make a move. He walked up to Chu Feng and Fei, took out a scroll, and unfurled it. “You two, take a good look at this.”","The two looked over and saw the title of the scroll—Rank four God Taboo, Soul Flame Formula.","“Master, are you telling us to cultivate a martial skill right now? It’s too painful for me to focus!” Fei grumbled.","“Rank four God Taboo? Elder, I don’t think we can cultivate a rank four God Taboo at our current levels, right?” Chu Feng asked.","He had previously received a rank four God Taboo Martial Skill from the Great Monster Slayer Emperor’s legacy, but he didn’t cultivate it because his body couldn’t withstand its impact.","One's base cultivation had to reach at least rank five Heavenly God level to cultivate it.","“If Chu Feng can focus, why can’t you do the same? He can at least see that it is a rank four God Taboo.” Song Changsheng glared at Fei.","Then, he turned to Chu Feng and explained, “Yes, this would have been impossible under normal circumstances, but this Soul Flame Formula is a rather unusual martial skill. As long as you have a sufficiently potent and compatible medium, you can cultivate and channel it.","“It is nigh impossible to absorb the searing energy generated from Fei’s forbidden skill, but it happens to be compatible with the Soul Flame Formula. Even if you aren’t able to master the skill, you should at least be able to use it to store the searing energy and prevent it from causing further harm to you.”","“I understand. Elder, is there anything to take note of when cultivating the Soul Flame Formula?” Chu Feng asked.","“Not at all. You can begin cultivating now,” Song Changsheng replied.","“All right.”","So, Chu Feng sat on the ground and formed a hand seal.","“Hold on, Chu Feng,” Song Changsheng hurriedly interjected.","Chu Feng opened his eyes and asked, “Is there anything else, elder?”","“Have you grasped the cultivation method yet?” Song Changsheng asked.","“I have.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Ah... It’s nothing. You can carry on,” Song Changsheng replied.","Chu Feng closed his eyes and began cultivating.","Song Changsheng kept a close eye on Chu Feng, ready to intervene the moment the latter made a mistake. But watching Chu Feng’s impeccable movements, he was quickly forced to admit that Chu Feng had really fully grasped the cultivation method.","“Master,” Fei called out.","Song Changsheng looked over, only to see Fei’s confused eyes.","“Master, the scroll says that I have to first fuse my bloodline power with the medium before cultivating the God Taboo, but it doesn’t mention the fusion method. How am I supposed to do it?” Fei asked.","“The searing energy came from your bloodline! How can you not know how to fuse it? Even Chu Feng has figured it out!” Song Changsheng replied in irritation.","He used to think that Fei was a prodigy, just that some concepts were too complicated for him to grasp right away. So, he had always patiently taught Fei.","It was only now that he knew that it was not the concepts that were too complicated; Fei just wasn’t talented enough. A true prodigy could decipher convoluted concepts without them being explicitly explained.","And Chu Feng was such a prodigy.","Fei was surprised by Song Changsheng’s sudden outburst. He glanced at Chu Feng and saw that the latter had already begun recovering. He immediately understood the reason behind his master’s irate response.","“Master, stop looking at Chu Feng. At this rate, you won’t even want me anymore! You can’t compare me with the likes of him. He might look like a human, but between us, he is the real monster here!” Fei exclaimed indignantly as if Song Changsheng was abandoning him.","“Elder, it would be unfair to compare anyone else with my big brother. He is indeed a true cultivation monster,” Little Fishy remarked with a grin.","Her mood lifted when she saw Chu Feng controlling the searing energy within him using the Soul Flame Formula. Her earlier anxiety dissipated, and her smile widened.","“Haaa...” Song Changsheng sighed.","He also knew that it would be irrational to compare Fei and Chu Feng. When he thought about how Chu Feng was Chu Xuanyuan’s son, for the first time in his life, he felt tempted to have his own son as well. How great it would be if his son inherited his talent!","While Song Changsheng’s thoughts were wandering, Fei desperately pleaded, “Master, I’m going to be burned to death if you don’t offer me some pointers soon!”","“All right, all right,” Song Changsheng replied impatiently.","Using his martial power, he drew the human body along with all its meridians and began explaining the fusion method to Fei."]},{"number":6653,"title":"Chapter 6653: Chapter 6651: Pride","paragraphs":["Chapter 6651: Pride","Fei was a prodigy, after all. It didn’t take him long to grasp the cultivation method under Song Changsheng’s guidance. He clenched his jaws and began cultivating.","However, the searing energy was so excruciating that Fei struggled to concentrate.","In contrast, Chu Feng was so focused that it looked as if he was not in any pain.","Song Changsheng couldn’t help but feel conflicted. He flicked his wrist and took out two pills emanating frost auras. “Take this.”","He had prepared these pills, knowing it was only a matter of time before Fei resorted to his forbidden skill.","“Thank you, master.”","Knowing that his master had prepared these for him, Fei was so moved that he nearly teared up.","“Chu Feng, it won’t be easy to completely suppress the searing energy. You should take one.” Song Changsheng passed the other one to Chu Feng.","“Thank you, elder.”","Chu Feng took the pill and swallowed it, knowing that Song Changsheng was right. While he had managed to curb the searing energy for now, it was a huge hurdle to take complete control of it.","The pill lowered the effects of the searing energy, allowing him to heighten his concentration.","“Chu Feng, you can cultivate here at ease. I’ll inform you if the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion goes to that realm,” Song Changsheng said.","“I have troubled you, elder,” Chu Feng replied.","He wasn’t surprised that Song Changsheng knew about the formation core realm. It simply meant he had been observing the situation all this while.","Chu Feng and Fei might have grasped the cultivation method, but their cultivation was still too low to properly cultivate a rank four God Taboo. It also didn’t help that the searing energy was extremely violent, so it was not easy to fuse it with their bloodline and store it.","It would take a while for them to succeed.","It was a huge relief that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion obeyed Jie Tianran’s orders and steered clear of the Totem Galaxy’s formation core realm.","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran kept a close eye on the Chu Clan Alliance’s movements while guarding the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s formation core realm.","He had dispatched his stronger members to extract the stronger power fragments from God’s Era, but he was still reluctant to give up on the weaker power fragments. If possible, he wanted to monopolize everything.","So, he dispatched ordinary members to the realms with the weaker power fragments as well.","But how could those ordinary members be a match for the Chu Clan Alliance’s elites? It didn’t help that Chu Feng had ordered the Chu Clan Alliance to massacre everyone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","As a result, those ordinary members were massacred.","Neither Jie Tianran nor the Saint-tier elders were bothered by the deaths of those ordinary members, viewing casualties to be inevitable in war. However, there were bound to be people who paid attention to such details.","As deaths mounted, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion began to take this matter seriously and reported it up the command chain. Eventually, it reached Jie Tianran’s ear.","An elder explained the situation to Jie Tianran.","“Lord Mansion Master, our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion might have lost many people, but those are limited to our non-elite forces. Our main forces have yet to clash with the Chu Clan Alliance, and they have enjoyed great success in the extraction of God’s Era’s power fragments as well.","“I suspect that the Chu Clan Alliance is merely putting on a strong front and dares not confront us directly.”","The elder was gleeful despite having lost many of his brethren. His arrogance was bone-deep. This was a trait shared by many in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. It was why they looked down on the other powers.","“Are you telling me that those casualties are good news for us?” Jie Tianran eyed the elder.","The elder realized that he had misspoken and hurriedly dropped to his knees. “Lord Mansion Master, that’s not what I mean. It’s just that the Chu Clan Alliance was too arrogant. I only said those words out of frustration. Please punish me for misspeaking!”","Despite not being a Saint-tier elder, he was still a figure of considerable stature in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, evident from how he reported directly to Jie Tianran. He understood Jie Tianran’s personality, so he first explained himself before requesting to be punished.","And indeed, his response quelled Jie Tianran’s anger.","“What’s the use of punishing you? You aren’t the one killing our people. Get up and return to work.” Jie Tianran waved his hand.","The elder hurriedly left the room.","Jie Tianran looked troubled. He had noticed that the Chu Clan Alliance was targeting realms that contained weaker power fragments, but he didn’t expect them to limit themselves to just those realms.","Are they avoiding us out of fear? But that’s not how Chu Feng’s personality was.","“Elder, what do you think?” Jie Tianran asked the old entity inside him.","“If you’re posing that question to me, Jie Tianran, you must be wondering if your grandson has figured something out and is up to something,” the old entity replied.","“That little beast saw through the locations of the two formation core realms. I suspect he might have some kind of formidable treasure, or that a powerhouse is secretly helping him.”","“Aren’t I helping you as well? I might be greatly weakened, but I still retain my instincts as a world spiritist. Your grandson is not that capable, so put your mind at ease. You’re just being jumpy because of the setbacks you have suffered at his hands. This isn’t a good thing, Jie Tianran. Don’t let your grandson become your inner demon.”","“You’re right, elder.”","Despite his affirmative response, Jie Tianran still took out a talisman paper and wrote on it.","The old entity sighed.","The talisman paper allowed Jie Tianran to swiftly transmit messages to the elders carrying the corresponding message tokens. It was just that activating the talisman paper required a huge amount of energy, so Jie Tianran wouldn’t resort to it unless necessary.","Jie Tianran was ordering the elders to transport the extracted power fragments to the formation core realm right away.","This abrupt order was a sign that Jie Tianran was panicking. He was playing it safer than usual out of fear that things would go awry.","The old entity watched it unfold without saying a word.","The truth was that he had lied. He was also worried that Chu Feng had discerned something that they had missed, and that a mishap might occur due to that. He had wanted to warn Jie Tianran about this, but his pride got in the way, and the words came out differently."]},{"number":6654,"title":"Chapter 6654: Chapter 6652: Your Son Resembles His Mother","paragraphs":["Chapter 6652: Your Son Resembles His Mother","Some time passed.","All the power fragments extracted by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to date had been delivered into Jie Tianran’s hands.","Despite having received a massive bundle of God’s Era’s power, Jie Tianran remained in a brooding mood. While he could sense the potent energy within, he was still unable to determine its use.","Until he could figure out how to put it to use, it was nothing more than an artwork.","On top of that, the power fragments were scattered like a formation, and there was even a formation core. There had to be something here that he hadn’t deciphered yet, and that further stoked his unease.","“What do you think, elder? Do we need to refine the power before it reveals its true properties?” Jie Tianran asked.","“It’s possible, but I can’t tell what kind of formation is required for the refinement,” the old entity replied.","“Could it be this formation?” Jie Tianran gestured at the formation core.","“Are you suggesting that the two formations can be activated?” the old entity asked.","“I’m not sure, which is why I wanted to seek your opinion, elder. What are your thoughts on this matter?” Jie Tianran asked.","“You’re overthinking it. The formation is likely a feint. You shouldn’t be thinking that this formation core is important just because Chu Feng has been here. Have you forgotten what I told you earlier about not letting your grandson lead you by the nose?” the old entity said.","“You’re right, elder,” Jie Tianran replied, but that didn’t lessen his unease.","His instincts as a world spiritist told him that this matter was not as simple as it looked.","In truth, the old entity was also unsure. He had refuted the formation because he didn’t know how to take control of it. If he admitted that it was a formation, he would also be admitting that his eyes were not sharp enough to see through it.","So, he could only gamble that the formation was useless, but the fact was that he was less confident than Jie Tianran. He could only pray in his heart.","Don’t let it be a formation. Even if it’s a formation, don’t let that brat, Chu Feng, decipher the method to channel it. Otherwise, my reputation will be sullied.","...","On the other hand, while the Chu Clan Alliance had incurred some casualties in their clashes against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, most of them successfully extracted God’s Era’s power fragments and gathered them in the Totem Galaxy’s formation core.","The preparations were in place. They were only waiting for Chu Feng to return.","In the meantime, Chu Feng’s complexion finally returned to normal. By the time he got up, he had already fully grasped the rank four God Taboo, Soul Flame Formula.","“Have you succeeded?” Song Changsheng asked.","He could already tell that Chu Feng had succeeded despite his question. Glancing at his disciple, whose body was still reddened from the searing energy, his admiration for Chu Feng deepened.","Chu Feng’s talent far surpassed not just Fei's but Xian Miaomiao's as well.","“Yes, but there’s too little searing energy. Even if I use it sparingly, I can only activate the Soul Flame Formula thrice,” Chu Feng replied.","He finally understood why even a True God like him could use this rank four God Taboo.","Due to the limitations of his body, he couldn’t activate the Soul Flame Formula using normal methods. Instead, he had to rely on the searing energy that had tortured him earlier. He had only stored a limited amount of searing energy, so he could only use the god taboo thrice.","Once he depleted the searing energy, he wouldn’t be able to use this god taboo anymore until his base cultivation rose to rank five Heavenly God level.","“Three times is already good enough. I suspect that my disciple will only be able to use it once, given the imperfections in his execution of the God Taboo, as well as the loss of searing energy while fusing it into his bloodline and storing it.","“But that’s of secondary importance. I prepared this martial skill to save him when he resorts to his forbidden skill. Being able to use the Soul Flame Formula is just an additional benefit,” Song Changsheng said.","Chu Feng could sense how much Song Changsheng cared about Fei.","“Thank you for your help, elder. If not for you, I would still be debilitated right now,” Chu Feng replied.","“Out of curiosity, Chu Feng, did you really intend to withstand the searing energy through sheer willpower?” Song Changsheng asked.","“That’s the only solution I could think of due to the limitations of my capabilities,” Chu Feng replied.","“Miaomiao was right. You are a loyal friend,” Song Changsheng said in admiration.","“Brother Fei put his life on the line to help me. I can’t turn a blind eye to his plight. I’m only doing what is right,” Chu Feng replied honestly.","“Pardon my frankness, but my disciple likely had other intentions in mind when he helped you. He might have lived for a long time, but he is nowhere near as mature as you. If anything, he feels more like the junior here.","“I bet he made a promise and didn’t want to embarrass himself, so he was determined to accomplish it even if it meant putting his life on the line. So...”","Before Song Changsheng could finish his piece, Fei suddenly interjected, “Please stop talking, master. Miss Yu’er is still here. Please spare my pride.”","Feu had opened his eyes and was grumbling indignantly. There was a tinge of redness on his ferocious, thick-skinned face.","“All right, I’ll stop talking. Focus on cultivating. It’s almost like you value your pride higher than your life,” Song Changsheng said with a sigh.","He knew that Fei’s control was not as strong as Chu Feng's. It was extremely dangerous for him to halt his cultivation halfway through.","“Regardless, Brother Fei has done me a huge favor this time. I’ll remember this debt,” Chu Feng said.","Song Changsheng nodded. “Fei needs more time cultivating. I’ll stay here to protect him, so go ahead and do what you must.”","“I’ll be taking my leave then.” Chu Feng bowed to Song Changsheng.","Little Fishy walked over to Chu Feng’s side and bowed deeply to Song Changsheng. Then, she said with a grin, “Elder, you are the most unfathomable expert I know in the world of cultivation. I hope to see you again the next time big brother is in trouble, too.”","Song Changsheng responded with a faint smile, neither agreeing to nor rejecting her remark.","With that, Chu Feng and Little Fishy quickly made their way over to the formation core realm.","Song Changsheng watched the two departing juniors with a smile. “Chu Xuanyuan, how did a scoundrel like you have such an outstanding son? He probably resembles his mother more.”","In the distant Ninth Galaxy, a middle-aged man dressed in straw garments sneezed."]},{"number":6655,"title":"Chapter 6655: Chapter 6653: Do You Dare Marry Both?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6653: Do You Dare Marry Both?","Chu Feng and Little Fishy rode Qin Jiu’s bamboo boat back to the formation core realm.","Both their eyes gleamed expectantly. On the one hand, Fei’s mishap turned out to be a blessing in disguise. On the other hand, there was finally going to be a conclusion to the fight for the two galaxies’ power fragments.","“Big brother, how does the rank four God Taboo feel like? Is it exceptionally strong?” Little Fishy asked out of curiosity.","Even she had yet to grasp a rank four God Taboo Martial Skill.","“It is extremely strong. A rank four God Taboo paired with a God Armament should be more than enough to crush all enemies in the same cultivation rank,” Chu Feng replied.","“That sounds amazing! Big brother, why don’t you show me its prowess?” Little Fishy replied with a mischievous grin.","Chu Feng knew that she was joking. She had heard him say that the rank four God Taboo could only be used three times.","“Sure.” But Chu Feng accepted her request and summoned a flame.","“Big brother!”","Little Fishy was horrified. She anxiously grabbed Chu Feng’s arm and infused martial power into it to stop him.","Chu Feng revealed a playful grin.","Only then did Little Fishy realize that the flame was made out of spirit power and not martial power. In other words, he had only pretended to use the Soul Flame Formula.","“Big brother, you tricked me!” Little Fishy’s cheeks puffed up.","“Oh? Does that mean our Yu’er really wants to see it? All right, I’ll use it then.”","Little Fishy anxiously interjected, “Don’t! I’m joking with you.”","Even though Chu Feng had already tricked her earlier, she knew that Chu Feng would really use the Soul Flame Formula if she didn’t stop him. He was very much capable of it.","Chu Feng chuckled, amused by her response.","Just then, a fist suddenly appeared out of nowhere and smacked Chu Feng’s head. He turned around and saw a beautiful woman standing behind him—Eggy.","“Bad Chu Feng. Don’t you bully Milady Queen’s Yu’er!” Eggy glared at Chu Feng.","“I didn’t bully her.” Chu Feng rubbed his head with an aggrieved expression.","Little Fishy revealed a triumphant grin. She was delighted that Eggy was standing up for her... but her smile soon became strained.","Eggy’s killing intent flared as she pulled out a two-meter-long black axe and swung it down on Chu Feng. “How dare you bully my Yu’er? I’ll kill you!”","“No, beautiful big sister!”","Horrified, Little Fishy instinctively released her Heavenly God martial power to stop Eggy.","The moment her martial power touched the black axe, it dissipated into thin air. Eggy’s attack turned out to be a feint.","Confused, she turned to Eggy and saw the latter’s mischievous grin. It was the same expression as Chu Feng’s. It finally dawned upon her that Eggy was teasing her.","“Beautiful big sister, you’re as bad as big brother!” Little Fishy protested.","The earlier situation had given her a huge scare.","Chu Feng chuckled by the side. He had known from the moment Eggy whipped out the axe that she was teasing Little Fishy. If he could only choose one person in the world to entrust his life to, that person would surely be Eggy.","There was no way she would kill him.","“What are you saying, Yu’er? I’m teaching Chu Feng a lesson on your behalf, so why are you siding with him now?” Eggy said.","Chu Feng continued to laugh, but Eggy’s subsequent words wiped the smile off her face.","“Yu’er, you’re prioritizing your husband over me.”","Little Fishy’s face turned as red as an apple.","“ Cough cough... ” Chu Feng coughed nonstop as if having choked on his saliva.","But Eggy didn’t intend to let Little Fishy go just like that. She danced around Little Fishy with bare feet while teasing, “Look at how red your face is. I must have hit the nail on the head.”","Little Fishy’s face remained red, but she didn’t let herself succumb to embarrassment. Instead, she grinned at Eggy and said, “It will be even better if our beautiful big sister is willing to marry big brother Chu Feng together with me!”","Those words choked Eggy. She stiffened up in place while blushing furiously. Then, she glared at Chu Feng and protested, “Look at what you’ve done! You have corrupted even a lady as pure as our Yu’er! You really are a bad influence!”","Eggy smacked Chu Feng’s head one more time before returning to the World Spirit Space.","“You two are the ones bickering. What did I do?” Chu Feng grumbled indignantly while grabbing his throbbing head. “But Eggy, I think Yu’er’s words make sense. Why don’t you consider it?”","Eggy spat angrily, “Stinky Chu Feng! You want to marry us both? Dream on!”","Chu Feng smirked in glee. This was the effect he wanted.","But Eggy continued, “Do you dare to marry the two of us?”","Somehow, it didn’t sound like Eggy was playing around anymore.","“Only a fool wouldn’t marry you two,” Chu Feng replied right away.","“You greedy scoundrel! I’ll beat you to death!” Eggy swung her little fists inside the World Spirit Space, though the corners of her lips were slowly curling up.","Chu Feng instinctively glanced at Little Fishy, who was still blushing furiously. He had always viewed her as a little sister because she was only a child when they first met. He couldn’t shake off that impression he had of her.","But after everything they had been through, he realized that his heart had begun wavering.","“What’s wrong, big brother? I was... just joking earlier. You don’t have to take my words seriously. I just wanted to tease that beautiful big sister back,” Little Fishy hurriedly explained.","“Yes, I know.” Chu Feng nodded as he replied with a smile.","But he wasn’t looking at her to seek an explanation. He just wanted to see her."]},{"number":6656,"title":"Chapter 6656: Chapter 6654: Activating the Galaxy Formation; the Mansion Master’s Dao Heart Shatters","paragraphs":["Chapter 6654: Activating the Galaxy Formation; the Mansion Master’s Dao Heart Shatters","It didn’t take long for Chu Feng and Little Fishy to return to the formation core realm.","Chu Feng first examined the power fragments extracted by the Chu Clan Alliance, but he couldn’t figure out what use they served. He would have to refine it with the formation to learn its true purpose.","The members of the Chu Clan Alliance stood neatly on the ground, forming a sea of people. They looked in the same direction, where Chu Feng floated alone in the sky.","The entire realm was the formation core. It would be much easier for Chu Feng to channel the formation from the sky. He had already figured out how to activate the formation.","“Let the show begin!” Chu Feng declared.","Spirit power flowed from his body and fused into the surrounding space.","Soon, the crowd’s eyes widened in excitement.","By now, they had already learned about Chu Feng’s plan. There was a humongous formation concealed in the Totem Galaxy, and this realm was the formation core to channel it. Needless to say, such a hulking formation couldn’t have been easy to activate.","But the crowd was weirdly confident since the one who was going to activate it was Chu Feng. They stared at Chu Feng while waiting with bated breath, not daring to make any noise.","Their excitement overflowed. They believed they were witnessing history in the making. What an honor it was to be present at a time like this!","Boom!","A resonant buzz echoed from the sky, sounding not just in the formation core realm but the entire Totem Galaxy. It was just a noise at first, but soon, spirit power began emerging from the stars in the sky.","The spirit power swiftly traversed across from realm to realm, forming a formation that resembled a painting. It didn’t take long for a complete formation to manifest in the Totem Galaxy.","Even God’s Era dimmed in the presence of this formation. At this moment, the formation was the brightest thing in the world of cultivation. There was not a single person who wasn’t shocked after witnessing this sight.","Jie Tianran was also observing the phenomenon via his observation means. His body was trembling, and his heart welled with conflicting feelings. The strongest emotion he felt was a crushing sense of defeat.","The weaker power fragments from both galaxies had been gathered in the formation core. Under the formation’s refining, these power fragments underwent a metamorphosis as their lights glowed brighter than ever.","Jie Tianran discerned more from the situation than the others.","He finally understood why Chu Feng had risked his life to conquer a formation core, as well as why the Chu Clan Alliance had only targeted the realms with weaker power fragments. Clearly, the weaker power fragments were more important here.","The two galaxy-scale formations were designed specifically to refine the weaker power fragments.","If his deduction was right, it would mean that he had wasted his effort gathering the stronger power fragments. This intensified Jie Tianran’s sense of defeat, so much so that anger began blazing in his heart.","“Elder, didn’t you say that the formation is likely to be a feint?” Jie Tianran questioned the old entity. He was so angry that he even dropped his respectful tone.","“I didn’t expect this to be true. Not only did Chu Feng see through the formation, but he also knew how to activate it. Chu Feng must be carrying many formidable treasures,” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body said.","“Why don’t you have such treasures then, elder?” Jie Tianran questioned.","“What are you getting at, Jie Tianran? Are you insinuating that I’m withholding my treasures from you? My treasures require a minimum level of spirit power to wield. You aren’t able to use them with your current spirit power.","“I have told you before that I’m in a severely weakened state. I barely have a fraction of my previous strength. If not for that, I wouldn’t have to seek refuge in your body,” the old entity roared in response.","He knew that he was at fault for claiming that the formation was fake to preserve his pride, but someone of his stature couldn’t possibly apologize to Jie Tianran. He could only put on a tough front.","And his words worked.","Jie Tianran regained some of his rationality. He knew that he couldn’t have reached his current level of accomplishment and obtained so many treasures without the old entity’s help. No matter how displeased he was, he couldn’t afford to offend the old entity yet.","“Elder, I am not blaming you, but God’s Era is of utmost importance. The power fragments scattered across the Immortal Sea Galaxy and the Totem Galaxy will likely be vital later on. I won’t be able to live with it if Chu Feng obtains God’s Era’s final power,” Jie Tianran explained.","“Calm down, Jie Tianran. The fight is not over yet. Even if Chu Feng somehow claims God’s Era’s final power, I’ll definitely wrestle it over for you,” the old entity said.","“Elder, does that mean that you’re almost done with your cultivation?” Jie Tianran’s complexion finally improved a little.","“I need a while more, but I should be able to make it in time,” the old entity replied.","“That’s wonderful.”","Jie Tianran still felt defeated, but he finally calmed down, knowing that he had a powerhouse to fall back on.","“Hm?”","Just then, Jie Tianran noticed a treasure from the Totem Galaxy heading toward the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. He hurriedly turned to God’s Era, specifically the figure reflected in the copper mirror.","“What’s wrong?” the old entity asked.","“I feel an inexplicable link between my body and the copper mirror,” Jie Tianran replied.","...","The formation caused a huge stir, but it didn’t take long for it to refine all the power fragments. As soon as the formation stopped whirring, the quiet formation core realm suddenly erupted into thunderous cheers and applause.","Some lavished Chu Feng with compliments, while others were just happy about their success. The atmosphere was celebratory.","The crowd could already sense what the powers were for.","This time, the powers enhanced not one’s cultivation but one’s bloodline and soul. On top of that, they wielded potent recovery energy.","Chu Feng thought that it might aid in the recovery of his aunt, Jie Tiannian."]},{"number":6657,"title":"Chapter 6657: Chapter 6655: Connection with the Copper Mirror","paragraphs":["Chapter 6655: Connection with the Copper Mirror","This power could save not just Jie Tiannian but possibly Jie Baobao as well. If the two of them were here, Chu Feng would have immediately used the power to heal them.","“Chu Feng, hurry up and use the power on your bloodline!” Eggy urged.","While Chu Feng was thinking about how the power could be used for those around him, Eggy thought about how Chu Feng could benefit from the power.","“Let me try sensing it,” Chu Feng said.","He drew a wisp of power from the humongous lake of energy that had manifested after refining God’s Era’s powers. The energy didn’t appear to have any negative side effects, but Chu Feng remained vigilant out of habit.","No one complained about Chu Feng getting first access to the power. In their view, it was only normal that he had the first claim to it.","Chu Feng was the leader of the Chu Clan Alliance, after all.","The wisp of power seeped into Chu Feng’s palm and flowed into his soul. His fatigue swiftly dissipated, and he felt energized.","However, his heart clenched up.","Half of the energy collected was focused on recovery, whereas the other half was focused on enhancing one’s bloodline. He was counting on the latter half to raise his cultivation and fighting prowess.","But his Heavenly Lightning Bloodline and Ruler’s Bloodline rejected the energy, not allowing a single drop of it in. Chu Feng felt regretful, but he wasn’t surprised by the outcome.","There were two ways to enhance one’s bloodline power.","One was gathering resources to enhance one’s bloodline. The other was to alter the very nature of one’s bloodline to strengthen it.","God’s Era’s power was likely in the latter category, or else it wouldn’t have been rejected by his two bloodlines. His bloodlines wouldn’t accept being altered to a weaker state of themselves.","Chu Feng told Eggy about it.","“That’s a good thing. It means that your bloodline is indeed the best!” Eggy consoled Chu Feng. Despite her hearty appearance, she was rather sensitive to Chu Feng’s feelings.","“Milady Queen is right,” Chu Feng replied with a grin.","While it was regrettable that this energy was useless to him, he didn’t plan to let this matter affect his mood. Besides, the three powers released from God’s Era thus far were only the appetizers. The main dish was still lying in the three gates inside the humongous silhouette.","No one knew what the final power was, but Chu Feng’s gut feeling told him that it would be extremely useful to him.","“Yu’er, can you use it?”","Chu Feng grabbed a sliver of the power and passed it to Little Fishy. Her bloodline was only second to his among those present. If she could benefit from the power, the others should be able to do so as well.","Little Fishy grabbed the power and absorbed it. Soon, her face lit up.","“It works, big brother! This energy stabilizes my bloodline and enhances my fighting prowess,” Little Fishy said excitedly.","That was good news.","Little Fishy’s talent was already top-notch. The fact that she could benefit from the power showed just how formidable God’s Era was.","Long Chengyu and the other juniors trembled in excitement.","Seeing that, Chu Feng told them to give it a try as well.","Indeed, the energy worked on all of them, though it was particularly potent for the Totem Dragon Clansmen. This sparked a thought in Chu Feng.","Maybe it’s not a coincidence that these two powers landed in the Totem Galaxy and the Immortal Sea Galaxy. The Totem Dragon Clan and the Immortal Sea Clan might be the greatest beneficiaries of this power... though I can’t confirm it since the rest of the Immortal Sea Clan is still in hibernation, and Little Fishy is an exceptional case.","Upon confirming that there was nothing wrong with the energy, Chu Feng first extracted a portion of it and stowed it away before using the remaining energy to construct a massive cultivation ground.","Next, he invited all members of the Chu Clan Alliance to train in the cultivation ground, regardless of their identities, backgrounds, or cultivation levels. They were free to take however much they were capable of taking.","His decision surprised the crowd. Most powers observed a hierarchy when it came to the allocation of resources. How could a normal cultivator enjoy the same cultivation resources as the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief?","It was an unconventional approach, but most people welcomed it.","As a result, almost every member of the Chu Clan Alliance stepped into the cultivation ground and began cultivating. Some made huge progress in their cultivation due to the enhancements to their bloodlines.","The weaker the cultivator, the more they benefited from God’s Era’s powers. It greatly boosted their talent.","This thrilled the crowd, particularly the weaker members. They were so overjoyed that the smiles didn’t disappear from their faces even as they cultivated. This was far more valuable than any cultivation resources they had previously used.","How often could one find a treasure that raised the upper ceiling of one’s cultivation?","The amount of energy one could absorb was limited based on how potent one’s bloodline was. Those with weaker talent might have undergone the greatest growth, but they were also the first ones to reach their limits and had to stop cultivating.","They only spent a while in the cultivation ground before they had to leave. In moments, the crowded cultivation ground became empty once more.","The only ones who remained were the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, Long Mucheng, the Totem Nine Daoists, and the older experts, as well as prodigious juniors like Little Fishy, Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, and Bai Yunqing.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng used his observation means to examine God’s Era.","Even when he was still channeling the formation to refine God’s Era’s power fragments, he could already sense a connection being established with God’s Era. However, the connection was faint, so he chose to ignore it for now.","The connection got stronger as time passed, which made him realize that there might be a change in God’s Era soon.","However, he didn’t notice any changes in God’s Era. Rather, it was his connection with the copper mirror that continued to deepen."]},{"number":6658,"title":"Chapter 6658: Chapter 6656: The Despicable Jie Tianran","paragraphs":["Chapter 6656: The Despicable Jie Tianran","“Chu Feng, why do you keep looking at the copper mirror? Did you notice something?” Eggy asked out of curiosity.","Chu Feng told Eggy the reason.","“Does it mean that God’s Era is opening? You have earned its qualification, after all,” Eggy asked in excitement.","While it would appear from the copper mirror’s reflection that Jie Tianran had obtained the qualification as well, Eggy had confidence in Chu Feng.","“I don’t know, but I think my consciousness might flow into the copper mirror soon,” Chu Feng replied.","It was like a self-fulfilling prophecy. As soon as he uttered those words, his consciousness slipped away from his body and whizzed through space at a speed even faster than the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s teleportation formations.","Despite his rapid speed, he could still clearly see everything in the world of cultivation.","“Waa! Chu Feng, how can you see so clearly despite moving so quickly? It feels almost like you’re seeing the world from the perspective of a true god,” Eggy said.","“Eggy? You can see what I’m seeing?” Chu Feng was surprised.","More often than not, Eggy couldn’t follow his consciousness when it slipped away from his body. This was a peculiar exception.","“Ah, you’re right. How is it that I’m still sharing your sight and hearing even though your consciousness is not in your main body? God’s Era sure is interesting compared to the other remnants out there,” Eggy remarked.","It didn’t take long for Chu Feng’s consciousness to arrive in the copper mirror, where he possessed his own reflection. He noticed that nine-colored lightning was still crackling around him.","“Hm?”","Chu Feng noticed that Jie Tianran, who was beneath him, had begun moving and was examining the surroundings with excited eyes. From that, he figured that Jie Tianran’s consciousness had been transported into the copper mirror as well.","“Old thing, what are you looking for?” Chu Feng asked.","Jie Tianran raised his eyes and saw Chu Feng’s taunting gaze. He realized that Chu Feng’s consciousness had been transported into the copper mirror as well.","“Little beast!”","Jie Tianran was still infuriated at having been outdone by Chu Feng. He immediately raised his hand to attack Chu Feng, only to realize that he was unable to channel his powers. His current body wielded no cultivation or spirit power at all.","“You want to kill me? Give it a try then.”","Chu Feng raised his hand, and the nine-colored lightning in the sky grew even fiercer. It was as if he were in control of the nine-colored lightning.","Boom boom boom!","Jie Tianran’s face turned livid. He wielded no powers here, whereas Chu Feng seemed to be able to channel the nine-colored lightning. This put him at a huge disadvantage.","“Damn it!” he cursed at the unfairness.","Chu Feng pointed his finger at Jie Tianran, but the nine-colored lightning didn’t descend. Instead, it receded and reverted to its former state.","“Are you afraid? I guess that’s all you amount to,” Chu Feng said with a smirk.","Jie Tianran realized that Chu Feng was just putting on a brave front. The latter might be standing in the sky, but his body harnessed no power as well.","All was fair in here.","“Little beast, you only dare to provoke me in here. Have you forgotten how you always end up fleeing frantically from me out there?” Jie Tianran sneered.","“You seem to take pride in the fact that you were taking advantage of a junior. I should have known better than to expect a scum who stoops so low as to harm his wife and daughters to have a sense of shame,” Chu Feng scoffed.","Jie Tianran figured that since they had been transported into the copper mirror, the rest of the world should be able to see what was happening here. So, he had no intention of admitting to those deeds. Instead, he criticized Chu Feng.","“Those things would have never happened if not for you. You are the one who deserves to die the most!” Jie Tianran roared.","Indeed, the world of cultivation could see and hear what was happening inside the copper mirror. Most people activated their means right away to observe the situation in the copper mirror.","And that included the Chu Clan Alliance.","They had noticed that the real Chu Feng was standing perfectly still, not responding to any questions. That confirmed the fact that Chu Feng’s consciousness had been transported into the copper mirror.","Just then, a sliver of energy from the cultivation ground Chu Feng had just constructed using God’s Era’s power fragments flowed toward Chu Feng’s forehead. At the same time, an aura appeared around Chu Feng’s silhouette in the copper mirror.","There was a striking resemblance between the energy and the aura. This further confirmed that Chu Feng’s consciousness was in the copper mirror.","Similarly, Jie Tianran’s body was being imbued with God’s Era’s energy as well, though his aura was different from Chu Feng’s.","“Elder, God’s Era’s energy has flowed into my body through my consciousness. It doesn’t grant me any offensive prowess, but I’m sure it is important,” Jie Tianran told the old entity inside him.","He was hoping for the old entity to help him.","“Jie Tianran, distract Chu Feng by talking to him. Don’t let him turn around. There is a formation blueprint hidden in the clouds behind him. You focus on him. I’ll decipher the formation blueprint on your behalf,” the old entity said.","Jie Tianran realized that God’s Era had summoned them here because they needed to forge something using the formation blueprint. He knew that this was an opportunity to get an upper hand against Chu Feng, so he continued to insult Chu Feng.","He did hold back in view of his reputation, but it was still beneath someone of his lofty stature to engage in a verbal bicker with a junior.","The crowd initially didn’t think much about it, but they didn’t expect their verbal exchange to continue for four whole hours. It wasn’t even an exchange of insults anymore.","At the start, Jie Tianran was still able to stand his ground by the sheer thickness of his skin, but he soon ran out of insults, whereas Chu Feng continued to gain steam. It reached a point where Jie Tianran was just getting completely thrashed.","“You... You...” Jie Tianran trembled in anger.","Even though his main goal was to distract Chu Feng, he still lost his cool at Chu Feng’s awful insults. He had been born into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion as a top prodigy, and he rose to the top of the world of cultivation after he became the Mansion Master.","No one had ever dared to insult him like that.","And Chu Feng’s mouth was truly foul.","“I what I? I am your father! You keep stuttering nonstop like a senile old fart. Heaven took pity on you and bestowed you with two outstanding daughters, but you murdered them in cold blood. Perhaps that’s the reason heaven refused to bestow you with a son. Heaven must have realized its mistake after seeing you, so it was determined not to allow another one of you to exist.”","Chu Feng’s curses were so vile that Jie Tianran trembled nonstop. He was so angry that his blood nearly shot out from the top of his head.","He had always wanted to capture Chu Feng to plunder his Ruler’s Bloodline, but right now, he was willing to give up on the Ruler’s Bloodline to rip Chu Feng into pieces."]},{"number":6659,"title":"Chapter 6659: Chapter 6657: Humiliated Across the World of Cultivation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6657: Humiliated Across the World of Cultivation","Jie Tianran suddenly frowned. He sensed his connection with the copper mirror weakening.","This signaled that his consciousness was reaching its limit here, and he would soon be ejected back to his body.","“Jie Tianran, I have grasped the formation blueprint. I’ll send it to you right now,” the old entity said as he sent a formation blueprint to Jie Tianran’s head.","“Make haste, Jie Tianran. You need to construct the formation inside this copper mirror as it requires you to refine God’s Era’s energy through your consciousness. The formation blueprint will be useless once you leave this place,” Jie Tianran said.","Jie Tianran could tell as well.","While the old entity was advising him, Jie Tianran had already formed a hand seal and began channeling energy to construct the formation. The process went smoothly; it only took a moment for the aura surrounding him to gather in his palm and manifest into a glowing sword.","Unlike normal swords, this sword resembled a key.","“What is that?”","Those outside noticed the sword in Jie Tianran’s grasp. This made them realize that he hadn’t been blindly receiving insults from Chu Feng; he was secretly doing something in the meantime.","With the sword in hand, Jie Tianran looked at Chu Feng smugly, his humiliation from earlier vanishing without a trace. Their consciousnesses were already on the verge of returning to their bodies, so there was no chance for Chu Feng to grasp the formation anymore.","He had won this showdown.","Chu Feng might have won the verbal fight, but he had foolishly lost the war.","“Did you have fun insulting me, Chu Feng? You’ll have to pay a price for it. Why do you think I lowered my stature to waste time on a beast like you? “ Jie Tianran sneered.","“What are you saying?” Chu Feng replied with a confused expression.","Jie Tianran was stumped. He thought that his words were plenty clear. Did Chu Feng go deaf from the foulness of his words?","“Ah. You’re saying that I have to pay the price for my insults. Are you talking about the thing in your hand?” Chu Feng asked.","He clenched his fist, and the surrounding aura flowed toward his palm and manifested into another key-shaped sword. However, his sword was longer and more elegant than the one in Jie Tianran’s hand.","Clearly, Chu Feng had the superior sword here.","“How did you...” Jie Tianran’s smugness vanished. He anxiously turned around to take a look, but there was nothing behind him that resembled a formation blueprint. He couldn’t understand how Chu Feng had grasped the formation blueprint.","Did Chu Feng grasp an entirely different formation blueprint? Otherwise, it doesn’t make sense for there to be a disparity in our formation swords.","“I know you didn’t want to argue with me. You were distracting me from looking at the formation blueprint hidden in the clouds behind me. You thought that you were smart, but little did you know that I was also distracting you,” Chu Feng said as he inspected his sword.","“What do you mean by that?” Jie Tianran’s cheeks twitched.","“Your eyes don’t just reflect what you see. In fact, the formation blueprint I see through your eyes is the more complete version. You thought that you were claiming the upper hand by taking my insults for four hours, but little did you know that you were helping me by standing still there,” Chu Feng sneered.","“Elder? What’s going on?” Jie Tianran asked the old entity.","“He’s lying. How can the formation blueprint become perfected just because it was reflected in your eyes? I have never heard of anything like that. There must have been a formation blueprint behind you as well, just that it dissipated after he grasped it. Your grandson is too cunning. He said those words to shake your mind. Don’t fall for such cheap trickery,” the old entity said.","There was no way to verify the matter anymore, but there was no denying that Chu Feng had claimed the upper hand in this clash. Jie Tianran had received four hours of insults for nothing.","To make things worse, this had happened in public.","While it was not his first time suffering a setback because of Chu Feng, the previous times had happened in private. He could at least console himself that outsiders didn’t know about it. But he couldn’t say the same this time around.","He was completely humiliated in front of the whole world of cultivation.","Chu Feng could tell what Jie Tianran was thinking, and he wasn’t planning on letting the latter off the hook easily.","“Jie Tianran, I thought that you would have everything under control after spending so much time in God’s Era. You couldn’t even decipher the power fragments that fell into the Immortal Sea Galaxy and Totem Galaxy. You occupied a formation core realm, but you don’t know how to activate it.","“Is this all the Mansion Master of the number one world spiritist power is capable of? Tsk tsk. Your reputation precedes you,” Chu Feng sneered.","Both Jie Tianran and Chu Feng’s consciousnesses were ejected from the copper mirror and returned to their bodies.","There was a new soul imprint on Chu Feng’s palm. When he channeled the soul imprint, it transformed into the sword he had forged in the copper mirror.","“Chu Feng, you’re back?”","The crowd, who were staring at the copper mirror, immediately surrounded Chu Feng.","“Yes, I just returned.” Chu Feng nodded.","“You’re spectacular, Chu Feng. You have dragged Jie Tianran’s reputation through the mud. Did you know that we can hear everything you said in the copper mirror?”","“Hahaha! You insulted Jie Tianran for four whole hours! Did you see how pale his face was? That was my first time seeing him with such an awful expression. It looked as if he was going to spit blood!”","Even the usually composed Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief was gloating at Jie Tianran’s plight. He smiled so widely that his teeth were showing.","Jie Tianran was not just the overlord of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion but the entire world of cultivation. Whenever the galaxy overlords joined forces, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion always received the lion’s share.","But no one had ever dared to speak up against Jie Tianran, let alone insult him.","It was indeed his first time seeing Jie Tianran being put down like that. He felt more exhilarated than anyone else."]},{"number":6660,"title":"Chapter 6660: Chapter 6658: Jie Tianran’s Wrath","paragraphs":["Chapter 6658: Jie Tianran’s Wrath","“What’s even funnier is how he thought he was distracting you, only to be made use of by you. Chu Feng, were you telling the truth earlier, or were you just trying to make him angry?” Long Mucheng asked with a gloating smile.","“It’s true. I deciphered the formation through his eyes. I nearly burst into laughter a few times when I thought about how he was taking my insults just to stop me from seeing the formation blueprint behind me,” Chu Feng said with a smile.","“Jie Tianran has really embarrassed himself this time,” Little Fishy said with an exhilarated grin.","“Indeed. This is much better than us stealing God’s Era’s powers under his nose.” Even Long Muxi piled in on Jie Tianran.","Chu Feng understood why the crowd was so excited.","Jie Tianran had dominated the world of cultivation for many years now, getting his way in everything. No one had been able to curb him. But beneath his domineering attitude was a heart more fragile than the rest.","All his life, he had been fawned over by those around him. No one had been able to utter a word of insult in his presence. A single line of insult could easily echo in his head for ten days, let alone all the nasty words Chu Feng had uttered earlier before the entire world of cultivation.","Jie Tianran must be feeling extremely stifled right now.","“All right, let’s continue cultivating,” Chu Feng urged.","He noticed that there was no one left in the cultivation ground.","“Big brother, we’re done cultivating,” Little Fishy said.","“That’s right. Both my and my big sister’s cultivation have made significant advancements,” Long Chengyu said as he released his martial power.","He had reached rank seven True God level. It was a huge jump.","Long Muxi also revealed her martial power—she was also at rank seven True God level.","Long Chengyu was right. The Totem Dragon Clansmen benefited more from the powers than anyone else. This lent credence to Chu Feng’s conjecture that the powers were more beneficial to the Totem Dragon Clan and the Immortal Sea Clan.","“What about you, Yu’er? Were you able to make advancements in your cultivation?” Chu Feng asked.","Since the powers had been so effective on the Totem Dragon Clan, it should have been the same for Little Fishy as well. Even at rank one Heavenly God, she could stand against rank five Heavenly Gods. If she could make a breakthrough here, they wouldn’t have to fear the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Netherworld Sect anymore.","“Big brother, I also benefited greatly from the powers. My bloodline has been reinforced, and my fighting prowess has risen. However, I wasn’t able to make a breakthrough,” Little Fishy replied with a radiant smile.","“Shall we distribute the remaining energy? Even though you can’t use it for your cultivation anymore, you still can use it for your recovery. Keep some with you, in case of emergencies,” Chu Feng said despite knowing that they wouldn’t bear to use such invaluable energy to heal their injuries.","While the people here had already absorbed all the energy they could, they were bound to have friends or family they could share it with.","Otherwise, they could sell it for money as well.","Chu Feng wasn’t averse to that. Since he had given it to them, they were free to do whatever they wanted with it.","It was just that he couldn’t support that course of action, since some of it would surely fall into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Netherworld Sect’s laps if too many people chose to do that. That would be harmful to the Chu Clan Alliance.","Chu Feng had opened the cultivation ground to everyone in the Chu Clan Alliance because he knew that each person could only absorb a limited amount of energy. The remaining energy, however, had to be distributed based on merit. It was only fair for those who contributed more to receive more.","He had wanted to give more to the crowd, but they refused and insisted that he keep more for himself. In the end, they came to a compromise.","Chu Feng would give out two-thirds of the energy, with people like Little Fishy and the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief receiving more. The weaker cultivators received less, but they still got a portion of the loot.","Everyone was satisfied with this outcome. In other organizations, the weaker cultivators wouldn’t even get a chance to access such an invaluable resource. The upper echelons would rather reserve it to nurture young prodigies.","Chu Feng took the remaining one-third. It was still a massive amount. He didn’t need that much, but Long Mucheng and the others declared that they would back out of the Chu Clan Alliance if he gave away his portion. It didn’t seem like they were joking, judging from their agitated looks.","He conceded, knowing that they were good-intentioned. Besides, he had contributed the most, so he was qualified to lay claim to the power.","After distributing the energy, Chu Feng quickly led the Chu Clan Alliance back to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. He wanted to see if the energy could heal Jie Tiannian and Jie Baobao or not.","Meanwhile, in the Immortal Sea Galaxy’s formation core realm, Jie Tianran stared at the imprint on his palm for a long time without saying a word. He had been like that since returning from the copper mirror.","“Lord Mansion Master, a-are you all right?” an elder asked out of concern.","Jie Tianran shot a frigid glare over. “Do I not seem all right?”","His tone was sharp and fierce.","The elder immediately realized that he was in trouble and dropped to his knees. However, a powerful suction force pulled him before Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran grabbed the elder by his neck and asked, “I’m asking you. Do I not seem all right?”","The elder dared not utter a word.","“You must think that I am an embarrassment for letting Chu Feng play me like a fool in the copper mirror, don’t you? You think that I am incapable of taking such insults, and that my dao heart will collapse, don’t you?” Jie Tianran questioned.","But the elder couldn’t speak a word. Jie Tianran had sealed off his voice with his spirit power.","A murderous gleam gleamed in Jie Tianran’s eyes. However, he sensed other elders from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion approaching the place, so he flung that elder out with a wave of his sleeves.","“Lord Mansion Master, I was wrong! I shouldn’t have misspoken!” The elder dropped to his knees and kowtowed profusely.","But Jie Tianran was in no mood to listen to his apology. He roared, “Scram!”","The elder ran off, knowing that he was lucky to escape with his life.","The other elders had come because they were worried about Jie Tianran, but upon seeing the rage he was in, they turned tail and left."]},{"number":6661,"title":"Chapter 6661: Chapter 6659: The Identity of the Netherworld Master","paragraphs":["Chapter 6659: The Identity of the Netherworld Master","Jie Tianran was finally the last one left in the area.","“Jie Tianran, you lost yourself for a moment there. No matter how angry you are, you shouldn’t take it out on your underling,” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body said.","“Elder, you underestimate me. I’m not mad at being laughed at by the world. It’s just that I’m slowly losing control over God’s Era. I fear that it’ll fall into Chu Feng’s hands at this rate,” Jie Tianran said.","“It’s fine. Haven’t I said that I’ll snatch it over if someone else claims it?” the old entity said.","Big words! You were present earlier, but you didn’t change a thing at all. I might have embarrassed myself earlier, but it’s the same for you as well. It’s just that the world doesn’t know about it because I’m shouldering the consequences for you.","Jie Tianran was tempted to say those words aloud, but he held himself back at the last moment. “I’m glad to have your backing, elder, but I also can’t sit still and do nothing. I believe it’s time to make some sacrifices to secure God’s Era.”","He ordered all members to return to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. He was worried that the Chu Clan Alliance would lay an ambush on their teleportation formations, so he instructed his members to use their treasures instead of their teleportation formations.","After issuing the order, he also got moving, but he made his way toward the Totem Galaxy instead of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","...","Soon, the rest of the world also realized that both Chu Feng’s and Jie Tianran’s consciousness had left the copper mirror to return to their bodies.","In the Ancestral Martial Starfield’s Great Chiliocosm Upper Realm, the environment was so barren that there should have been no one capable of observing God’s Era. Yet, there were two people using their means to observe it.","They were the Netherworld Sect’s Dongfang Hansong and Yun Ao.","They had traveled to the Great Chiliocosm Upper Realm under Cang Li’s order to search for the possessions of Chu Feng’s grandfather, Chu Hanxian, to verify if the latter was the Netherworld Master.","Standing on a mountain peak, shrouded in a treasure’s concealment energy, they continued observing the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s God’s Era despite knowing that Chu Feng and Jie Tianran had already returned to their bodies. They didn’t want to miss anything.","Behind the two of them was a special formation, where two energies were undergoing fusion.","One was the Netherworld Master’s aura. The other was the aura they had extracted from Chu Hanxian’s possession.","“Jie Tianran is an embarrassment. He wanted to take advantage of Chu Feng, only to end up being deceived,” Yun Ao remarked.","He was gloating despite being a Netherworld Sectmember. He had a high opinion of Chu Feng, especially after learning that Chu Feng’s grandfather could be the Netherworld Master. If Chu Feng were the Netherworld Master’s descendant, the Netherworld Sect could easily conquer the entire world of cultivation.","Weng!","The formation suddenly glowed.","Dongfang Hansong and Yun Ao immediately looked over, and the latter's eyes widened. The Netherworld Master’s aura had impeccably fused with that of Chu Hanxian’s. Clearly, the two of them were the same person!","“It fused! Chu Feng’s grandfather is our Netherworld Master, which makes Chu Feng the Netherworld Master’s grandson! It’s not a coincidence! Chu Feng must have activated the Netherworld Embryo Spirituality Summoning Altar. That caused the sacred item to react. That’s how he was able to control the sacred item without any backlash. It all makes sense now!”","Yun Ao was so excited that he prattled on and on. He initially laughed frenziedly, but soon, he fell to his knees and began weeping.","“Hansong, there’s no need for the new faction and conservative faction to fight anymore. We have found our true master. To think that the Netherworld Master’s descendant was so close to us, not to mention so outstanding. There is hope for our Netherworld Sect. With Chu Feng’s help, we’ll surely be able to awaken the sacred item. Our Netherworld Sect can finally achieve what we have set out to do!”","The old Yun Ao cried so hard that his body trembled, and his tears fell nonstop to the ground.","“Lord Yun Ao.”","Dongfang Hansong walked up to Yun Ao and gently tapped his shoulder.","Yun Ao’s face warped in horror as he felt Dongfang Hansong violently grab his shoulder and channel his martial power into his body. His organs shattered right away, and the martial power gushed toward his soul.","Yun Ao quickly turned around and saw Dongfang Hansong staring calmly at him, but lurking beneath his composed gaze was murderous intent.","“Lord Yun Ao, Chu Feng cannot join the Netherworld Sect. No one can know that he’s the descendant of the Netherworld Master,” Dongfang Hansong said. “Only Chen Hui can become the Netherworld Master. He... should have been known as Dongfang Hui. He is my son.","“Please don’t blame me, Lord Yun Ao. I only want the best for my son. You have been looking after Chen Hui since he was still a child and are fond of him, so I’m sure you understand how I feel, right?”","He continued channeling his martial power into Yun Ao’s body even as he spoke.","Yun Ao’s body crumbled until his soul disintegrated.","Dongfang Hansong dropped to the ground with a darkened face. He was crying as well. Perhaps he was conscience-stricken for killing Yun Ao, or maybe it was just crocodile tears.","He murmured under his breath, “It’s all for the children. How can a parent not plan for their child’s future? I’m sure Lord Netherworld Master agrees as well...”","He looked at the impeccably fused bloodline powers. He stood up, walked over, kneeled before the fused bloodline powers, and kowtowed. “Lord Netherworld Master, I have let you down, but I have no choice. Please don’t blame me. Please don’t blame me...”"]},{"number":6662,"title":"Chapter 6662: Chapter 6660: Jie Tianran’s Motive","paragraphs":["Chapter 6660: Jie Tianran’s Motive","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Ling Clan’s Clan Chief had also been extracting God’s Era’s power fragments scattered across the Totem Galaxy. He believed the power fragments would be of the essence until Chu Feng activated the Totem Galaxy’s formation.","When he saw the power fragment bursting into flame, he suddenly realized that all the power fragments he had extracted thus far were nothing but fuel for the galaxy formation. Yet, despite being the head of the Ling Clan, he had been completely oblivious to it.","Jie Tianran was far from the only one who felt defeated. The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief received a massive shock as well.","When he received Jie Tianran’s order, he ordered all his clansmen to return to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. However, he didn’t personally lead them. Instead, he entrusted the job to his subordinate, while he took a warship toward where two of the Saint-tier elders were.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was accompanied by his two granddaughters, Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er, as well as a loyal subordinate of Chu Feng’s grandmother, Shuang Yu.","The three of them had made up their minds to support Chu Feng, but they didn’t want to become enemies with the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief, so they visited him in hopes of persuading him.","Shuang Yu thought that since the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was indebted to Chu Feng’s grandmother, there was a chance he might support Chu Feng in view of that.","“Grandfather, you saw what happened in the copper mirror. Jie Tianran isn’t a match for Chu Feng. He only retains the upper hand due to his age and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s strong foundation, but that is transient. God’s Era is already beginning to side toward Chu Feng. It is only a matter of time before Chu Feng obtains God’s Era’s final power.","“Xianhai Yu’er can already rival rank five Heavenly Gods despite having only just reached Heavenly God, and Chu Feng’s talent surpasses hers. Is there anyone in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion who can stop Chu Feng once he reaches Heavenly God?","“Chu Feng won’t spare anyone from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. If we wait till then, it will be too late for our Ling Clan to switch sides. Grandfather, you mustn’t continue to blindly follow Jie Tianran, even for the sake of our Ling Clan,” Ling Sheng’er said.","This was not her first time saying these words, but she thought that her grandfather might change his mind after witnessing Chu Feng’s recent accomplishments. Even she was shocked to see what Chu Feng had done, so surely her grandfather would feel the same.","“Grandfather...”","Noticing a lack of response from her grandfather, Ling Sheng’er stepped forward.","Pah!","A slap sent Ling Sheng’er flying into a wall. Her cheek stung so much that it went numb.","Ling Sheng’er was stunned. So was Ling Mo’er. This was the first time the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief had struck Ling Sheng’er.","“Grandfather, you know that Sheng’er is right. Why did you strike her for speaking the truth?” Ling Mo’er asked.","“I have gone easy on her. Have you forgotten your places? You two are now the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s traitors! I am the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Ling Clan’s Clan Chief. It’s out of mercy that I didn’t take your lives. You three get lost right now. Otherwise, I’ll apprehend you and let the Mansion Master deal with you. Scram!!!” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief roared as he tossed two Cosmos Sacks toward Ling Mo’er.","“Do you really think that your granddaughters would harm you? Have you forgotten the grace Lord Nianqing has shown you? How can you remain unmoved after witnessing Lord Nianqing’s tragic death? Jie Tianran is out of his mind! He is capable of anything! If you continue being so stubborn, the next one will be you!” Shuang Yu bellowed.","She had begun losing her patience after many attempts to persuade the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief had ended in futility.","Boom!","“Why do you think you are still breathing right now? If not for Lord Nianqing, you would have been dead by now. If you’re really tired of living, I can grant you your wish right now!” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief said with a murderous glint in his eyes.","“We’ll leave right now, grandfather. Please spare Lord Shuang Yu.” Ling Sheng’er hurriedly kneeled before the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief, grabbed his thighs, and pleaded.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief looked at his most doted granddaughter and her swollen cheek with conflicted eyes. He turned around and waved his sleeve.","“Get lost.”","Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er swiftly grabbed Shuang Yu and dragged her away.","With that, the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was the only one left on the warship.","“Sheng’er, Mo’er, I also know deep down that I’m walking down the path of doom. But the one I’m loyal to isn’t Jie Tianran but the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. The Ling Clan rose to prominence through the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I cannot shoulder the burden of being labeled a traitor, and so can’t the Ling Clan,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief murmured with a sigh.","All of a sudden, his eyes narrowed.","He formed a hand seal and conjured a spirit formation gate on his palm. A compass flew from the gate. A figure was moving on the compass. The figure was coming from another direction, but it appeared to be heading toward the same destination as him.","“Where is Jie Tianran heading?” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was confused.","He had received this compass from the previous Ling Clan’s Clan Chief. The latter had left an imprint on Jie Tianran to track his whereabouts. This matter was a secret. In the Ling Clan, he was the only one who knew about this compass.","Not even his two granddaughters knew about this.","“Does he have other arrangements?”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was not certain at first, but upon confirming that Jie Tianran was heading toward the two Saint-tier elders, he slowed his footsteps. He knew that Jie Tianran was in a bad mood, and it wouldn’t be wise to appear before him right now, lest he be implicated.","The two Saint-tier elders whom the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was looking for were Jie Qingsu and Jie Zhenfu. They hosted the entrance examination that inducted Chu Feng and Fu Xing into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","The two Saint-tier elders were returning to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion with eighty million elite world spiritists. Space was boundless, but eight thousand warships traveling in a tight formation were still a sight to behold.","All of them looked crestfallen due to their failure to secure God’s Era’s powers.","And when Jie Tianran appeared in front of them, they began trembling in unease and nervousness."]},{"number":6663,"title":"Chapter 6663: Chapter 6661: The Crux","paragraphs":["Chapter 6661: The Crux","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief quickly stopped his warship and concealed it. He stood at the front of the warship, holding onto an exquisite white jade box. In the box was a leaf manifested from compressed spirit power.","He stared at the leaf with a conflicted expression.","Out of curiosity, he had used his observation means to spy on Jie Tianran, only to see that the latter had constructed a huge concealment formation that obscured the entire area.","This leaf was a treasure passed down through the Ling Clan. It could greatly enhance his observation prowess, allowing him to see through Jie Tianran’s concealment formation.","He sensed that something was amiss and wanted to know why Jie Tianran was looking for the two Saint-tier elders, but the very fact that Jie Tianran had constructed an observation formation meant that he didn’t want anyone to pry into his business.","It was one thing if it were anyone else, but Jie Tianran was the Mansion Master. It would be inappropriate for the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief to probe here.","At this moment, he remembered what Ling Sheng’er, Ling Mo’er, and Shuang Yu had told him. Jie Tianran’s actions thus far had indeed piqued his vigilance.","“Why am I hesitating here? My loyalty lies with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, not Jie Tianran.” With this realization, the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief lifted the leaf and gently dabbed it on his eyes.","The leaf’s spirit power thinned.","When the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief opened his eyes once more, his vision became so sharp that he could easily peer through the concealment formation and lock onto Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran stood before the two Saint-tier elders and the army they led.","The army halted the moment they noticed Jie Tianran, and they bowed deeply to the latter. “Paying respect to Lord Mansion Master.”","Even the two Saint-tier elders rushed out from their respective palaces to greet Jie Tianran.","“If you had extracted the power fragments faster, Chu Feng wouldn’t have been able to activate the galaxy formation so smoothly. Do you plead guilty?” Jie Tianran coldly asked.","“Lord Mansion Master, we were useless. We extracted the power fragment too slowly!” Jie Qinghe and Jie Zhenfu knelt in front of Jie Tianran and conceded their mistake.","It was clear to them now that Jie Tianran had come to pin the blame on them.","Formations were powered by energy, and the galaxy formation was powered by God’s Era’s power fragments. If the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had been any faster at extracting the ‘stronger’ power fragments, Chu Feng couldn’t have tapped into those power fragments to activate the galaxy formation.","“Jie Qinghe and Jie Zhenfu, I have expended a huge amount of Immemorial Divine Water and the power I have obtained from God’s Era to raise your spirit power. If not for that, I could have claimed the upper hand in the competition for God’s Era and triumphed over Chu Feng. Yet, you two are of no use to me at all. I am very disappointed,” Jie Tianran said with a sigh.","All the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists present lowered their heads in shame. They had made breakthroughs in their spirit power thanks to Jie Tianran, but they were of little help to him.","In contrast, Jie Qinghe and Jie Zhenfu felt like cussing Jie Tianran out.","Yes, the Immemorial Divine Water allowed them to reach unthinkable heights within a short time, but they paid a hefty price for it. Their lifespans were less than ten years. If they could choose again, they would rather live longer than to advance their spirit power.","Jie Tianran only revealed the immense shortening of their lifespans after the deed was done, not giving them a chance to back out at all.","However, they dared not voice their complaints aloud. They subserviently replied, “We were incompetent and have let down Lord Mansion Master’s expectations in us.”","“Forget it. I don’t want to pursue this matter. However, you should have realized by now that Chu Feng is not an easy opponent. At this rate, he’ll lay claim to God’s Era’s final power. He could very well make a breakthrough to Heavenly God and Heavenly Dragon at the same time.","“None of you can match Xianhai Yu’er after her breakthrough; I doubt that I’d be a match for Chu Feng after he makes a breakthrough as well. By then, our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion wouldn’t be able to curb him anymore. Even our protective formations won’t be able to stop him.","“That little beast, Chu Feng, is a vicious one. There’s no doubt that he’ll proceed to massacre our people. Our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion will be destroyed within less than a year,” Jie Tianran said.","The crowd was taken aback. This was the first time Jie Tianran acknowledged the threat posed by Chu Feng. This didn’t bode well for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Were they doomed to be massacred at this rate?","“Lord Mansion Master, what should we do?” Jie Zhenfu asked in a panic.","“I do have a solution, and you are the crux of it,” Jie Tianran replied.","The crowd was stunned. We are the crux of the solution? That would be a huge honor! Lord Mansion Master isn’t here to hold us responsible but to give us a chance to bring honor to our ancestors!","“But you’ll have to make some sacrifices,” Jie Tianran added.","“Lord Mansion Master, we will scale a mountain of knives or venture into a sea of flames if we can defeat Chu Feng,” Jie Zhenfu and Jie Qinghe said.","“Our strength and lives belong to Lord Mansion Master. Please command us, Lord Mansion Master. We’re willing to brave death for you!” the army roared.","Jie Tianran nodded in satisfaction.","“I knew that there were no cowards in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I’m heartened that all of you are willing to lay down your lives for the Sacred Mansion,” Jie Tianran said.","No one noticed the cruel gleam in his eyes."]},{"number":6664,"title":"Chapter 6664: Chapter 6662: Tribute","paragraphs":["Chapter 6662: Tribute","“We’ll fight for the Sacred Mansion! We’ll fight for Lord Mansion Master!”","Jie Qinghe and Jie Zhenfu expressed their stances once more. Even the army behind them was enthused at being able to contribute to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Weng!","Jie Tianran suddenly retreated into the far distance. A brilliant red light shone from where he previously stood. The red light swiftly spread outward, instantly engulfing the army. Everyone’s body glowed with a sinister, fiery-red light.","The faces of the crowd paled. As world spiritists, they immediately realized that they were caught in a refinement formation.","“Lord Mansion Master, why?!” Jie Zhenfu and Jie Qinghe looked at Jie Tianran.","“None of you have any value. The only thing that holds value is your lives,” Jie Tianran said.","The two Saint-tier elders and the others stiffened in place. They were still trying to convince themselves that the refinement formation was merely Jie Tianran’s way to test their loyalty, but the latter’s words caused their hearts to turn cold.","Jie Tianran was really planning to refine them into energy.","“Lord Mansion Master, I’d rather die in battle for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion than to be killed by you like that. Even if we have wronged you, please send us to the battlefield to atone for our sins. We aren’t afraid of death, but we don’t want to die like that!”","Many voices echoed in the air.","Many of them were afraid of death, but some earnestly felt that way. They would rather die on the battlefield than be refined like that.","But Jie Tianran ignored their pleas. He took out a scroll labeled Immemorial Divination Art.","Shoosh!","Jie Tianran formed a hand seal with his left hand while flinging his right. Both the formation and the scroll transformed.","GAHHH!","Tragic cries echoed. Sharp blades manifested in the formation and penetrated the crowd’s bodies, severing their arteries. Fresh blood rained torrentially.","At the same time, the scroll emanated an eerie glow. It swiftly expanded while flying beneath the refinement formation. The torrential blood rain fell on the scroll.","“Lord Mansion Master...”","The crowd was in so much pain that they desperately begged Jie Tianran for mercy.","But Jie Zhenfu roared with a darkened face, “Shut up! Do you still not get it? That is a forbidden skill from the Immemorial Divination Art. Jie Tianran isn’t punishing us. He is using us as tribute to channel the Immemorial Divination Art!”","The crowd fell deathly silent. They couldn’t believe what they were hearing. Did Jie Tianran really intend to use them as tribute?","“Looks like there’s someone who understands.” Jie Tianran smiled.","“Why, Lord Mansion Master? Why?”","Many people felt indignant.","“Rest assured. I’ll tell others that you died from the Chu Clan Alliance’s ambush. Your family members will be handsomely compensated, and you’ll become martyrs of our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Your souls will be placed in our Hero Hall,” Jie Tianran declared.","Realizing that they were all going to die here, the crowd began to curse Jie Tianran.","However, Jie Tianran was unfazed. “Tolerate it. It’s all for the Sacred Mansion.”","He changed his hand seal. The crowd’s bodies and souls began to be refined into special energy that flowed into the scroll labeled Immemorial Divination Art.","Soon, the space fell silent. The only survivor remaining was Jie Tianran.","He conjured countless blades with a wave of his sleeve and devastated the warships. Then, he turned around and left the area.","Shortly after he left, the concealment energy obscuring the area vanished.","Little did Jie Tianran know that a pair of eyes had witnessed everything that had just happened.","“Jie Tianran...”","Unease and horror were inscribed into the face of the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief. He had heard about Jie Tianran’s deeds, but he didn’t expect the latter to make a move on their brethren like that.","“It’s the long-lost Immemorial Divination Art. He was the one who stole it. Was he the one behind the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s massacre back then?”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief suddenly remembered the tragic incident where over ten million families lost their lives. There was a commonality linking all of them—they had a child who was less than a year old.","Many conspiracies surfaced regarding that. Some deduced that it was a sacrificial ritual. Some suspected the Immemorial Divination Art’s forbidden skill. But those conjectures were overthrown as they didn’t think that someone could do something like this to their fellow brethren.","Only the most respected elders of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were qualified to learn the Immemorial Divination Art, after all.","“It’s him. He must be the one who did it. You monster, Jie Tianran!” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief’s eyes blazed with fury.","He realized that the Ling Clan could also be reduced to Jie Tianran’s sacrifices if they continued remaining inside the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“I cannot continue my folly anymore. Otherwise, I’m just bringing harm to my clansmen.” Determination gleamed in the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief’s eyes.","...","Ling Sheng’er, Ling Mo’er, and Shuang Yu were cruising through space on a boat.","Since they had failed to persuade the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief, they decided to head to a nearby realm and use an ancient teleportation formation to travel to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy. From there, they would travel to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city and join Chu Feng.","“Sheng’er, you might not fear pain, but your face is completely swollen,” Ling Mo’er said.","She wanted to treat Ling Sheng’er, but the latter refused to let her do so.","“No.” Ling Sheng’er puffed up her cheeks like an unyielding child.","“Sheng’er, grandfather still cares about us. He wouldn’t have given us cultivation resources and protective treasures otherwise. However, he has his considerations as well. He has been in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion his entire life. We need to understand where he’s coming from,” Ling Mo’er said.","The two of them were holding onto the Cosmos Sacks that the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief had given them before chasing them away."]},{"number":6665,"title":"Chapter 6665: Chapter 6663: Forbidden Skill","paragraphs":["Chapter 6663: Forbidden Skill","“I understand that grandfather has his difficulties, but we’re doing this for his and the Ling Clan’s sake. I don’t want to see grandfather or our clansmen dying in Chu Feng’s hands. It might seem like Chu Feng is being extreme here, but he’s not at fault. None of us can find any reason to tell him to stop. Grandfather... is just too stubborn. His old age must be hindering his judgment. Not only does he refuse to listen to me, but he even struck me!”","Ling Sheng’er slowly grew more agitated as she spoke, to the point where she began roaring.","“He’s becoming an old fool,” Ling Mo’er agreed.","“Who’s an old fool?” a voice suddenly echoed from behind.","The trio tensed up. They quickly turned around. Unbeknownst to them, the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was standing on their boat.","“Grandfather, h-how...”","Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er were nervous. Shuang Yu put up her guard. It wouldn’t be surprising for the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief to make a move on them, considering where his allegiance lay.","“Old fool? Is that how you talk about me in private?” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief stared at Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er.","“Of course not. We were just grumbling in a fit of anger,” the two sisters tried to explain.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief didn’t believe them. He rolled his eyes before asking, “Are you certain that Chu Feng will take you in?”","“He will,” the two sisters replied in unison.","But Shuang Yu didn’t speak a word. She remembered what she had done to Chu Feng back then, so she wasn’t sure if he would be willing to take her in.","Shoosh!","An ancient communication talisman paper fell into Ling Sheng’er’s hand.","“If Chu Feng takes you in, tell him that our Ling Clan is willing to help him. As a show of sincerity, we will do any one thing he asks of us, as long as it doesn’t involve killing members or destroying the property of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Use this communication talisman paper to relay the message to me,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief said.","Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er were overjoyed to hear that. “Grandfather... do you mean it? You have thought things through?”","“Of course. Or would you only believe me if I announce to the entire world that our Ling Clan is going to betray Jie Tianran to side with Chu Feng?” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“Of course not. I’m just curious to know what made you change your mind, grandfather,” Ling Sheng’er asked with a grin.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief considered telling them what he had just seen, but he decided against it. The nature of this matter would change if he spoke the truth. It would seem like the Ling Clan was seeking refuge out of fear of Jie Tianran, rather than them believing that what Chu Feng had done was right.","So, he said, “I have thought things through. Your words make sense. However, I should clarify that I’m only turning my back on Jie Tianran; I am still a member of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Tell Chu Feng that I’ll help him, but I hope that he won’t go after other members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. He should go after the true culprit, Jie Tianran.”","“Jie Tianran isn’t the only one involved in Lord Nianqing’s death. There’s nothing wrong with what young master Chu Feng is doing. Far too many people in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion deserve death. Can you say that you won’t do the same if you were in his position?” Shuang Yu asked.","“At least ask him to spare the members of our Ling Clan,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“Grandfather, I’ll relay your words to Chu Feng. I think he’ll compromise if you’re earnest about wanting to help him. I’ll inform you if he agrees,” Ling Sheng’er was so happy that she did a little joyful dance.","“This communication talisman paper can only be used once. We can’t use it on something so trivial.” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief hesitated briefly before proposing, “Why don’t I follow you? You try inviting him out for a face-to-face talk with me.”","“Won’t that be too dangerous?” Ling Mo’er was worried about her grandfather’s safety.","The Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect was the Chu Clan Alliance’s turf. So far, the Chu Clan Alliance had already slain six members of the Saint-tier elders. While her grandfather was ranked higher than the Saint-tier elders, he wasn’t stronger than them.","Her grandfather wouldn’t be able to escape if Chu Feng decided to take his life.","“It’s fine. I know Chu Feng. He’ll accept grandfather if grandfather is sincere about wanting to join him,” Ling Sheng’er said.","She had a deeper understanding of Chu Feng compared to Ling Mo’er and Shuang Yu.","“I’m not looking to join Chu Feng. I want to join forces with him to deal with Jie Tianran,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief emphasized.","“I understand, grandfather.” Ling Sheng’er stepped forward, grabbed her grandfather’s arm, and sat him down. “Let’s look for Chu Feng together.”","“All right.”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief nodded. He took out a talisman paper and fused it into the boat, greatly increasing its speed. He noticed that his palm print was still on Ling Sheng’er’s happy face, and his heart suddenly felt heavy.","His obstinacy had nearly brought harm upon the entire Ling Clan. Ling Sheng’er was not wrong when she said that he was an old fool.","Weng!","Ling Sheng’er suddenly felt the pain on her cheek vanish. Her grandfather had constructed a recovery formation on his palm and was treating her.","“Does it still hurt?” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“It hurts, but it’s nothing. I’m delighted to see that you have come around,” Ling Sheng’er said with a grin.","“You lass.”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief smiled at his adorable granddaughter. His heart, which had felt nervous for the longest time, suddenly felt at ease. Perhaps, from the very start, he had already known that siding with Chu Feng was the right option here.","...","Jie Tianran didn’t return to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Instead, he made his way to an Upper Realm in the Totem Galaxy.","This Upper Realm had no potent resources, so there were no formidable powers stationed here. However, it boasted a huge land mass and population.","A massive formation quietly enveloped the entire realm. Jie Tianran stood at the center of the formation with his scroll, which had shrunk to its original size. The scroll was unfurled, and one could see the wailing souls in it.","These were the eighty million elite world spiritists from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They were still alive despite having undergone refinement, writhing inside the scroll from sheer pain, despite having lost their consciousness.","Jie Tianran took out a sixty-centimeter-tall straw doll. It was plastered with many talisman papers, but the talisman papers on its back were blank.","He took out a special brush and wrote five words on the talisman paper—’Chu Heavenly Clan’s Chu Feng’.","Next, he took out a jade bottle containing Chu Feng’s aura. He formed a hand seal and infused the aura into the straw man. The straw man began moving as if coming to life.","Its facial features were crude, but if one took a closer look, it bore some resemblance to Chu Feng."]},{"number":6666,"title":"Chapter 6666: Chapter 6664: Chu Feng’s Weakness","paragraphs":["Chapter 6664: Chu Feng’s Weakness","“Jie Tianran, are you sure this will work?” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body asked.","“Elder, aren’t you the one who told me about how ingenious the Immemorial Divination Art is?” Jie Tianran replied.","“The other aspects of the Immemorial Divination Art are dog shit, but its forbidden art is ingenious. As long as you offer sufficient tribute, the forbidden skill will not just prophesy but offer you tangible help regarding what you’re asking about. But I don’t think the tens of millions of world spiritists you have are enough,” the old entity replied.","“It’s not just tens of millions of world spiritists. There are a hundred Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists as well, with two of them being at rank five,” Jie Tianran replied.","“That barely hits the mark in terms of spirit power, but a forbidden skill requires acts of taboo. Gathering eighty million infants would have worked far better than that,” the old entity said.","“Elder, it might not have hit the mark if they were outsiders, but the people I’m using as tribute are the pillars supporting our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They are essential to us. It tears my heart to use them as tribute as well. I’m sure the forbidden skill can sense our relationship and understand my pain.","“I’m already in a tough spot. I can’t let the situation continue as it is. I have to do something, even if the chances of success are bleak. That said, I think that there is a good chance of this working out,” Jie Tianran said.","“I’m not telling you to stop; I’m telling you to add to the tribute. But again, it might not make a difference. Forget it, let’s go with this,” the old entity said.","Jie Tianran placed the straw man inscribed with Chu Feng’s name into the Immemorial Divination Art’s scroll. He formed a hand seal, and the realm inside the scroll instantly unfurled and dyed the world red. The souls screaming in agony inside made it seem like a hellscape.","Something even more eerie happened. An ancient and bizarre voice echoed from the scroll, “What do you want?”","The voice was unnerving, as if it didn’t belong in this world. Even Jie Tianran tensed up.","Jie Tianran nervously replied, “Milord, this child is Chu Feng. He is competing with me over God’s Era. How can I defeat him? Where does his weakness lie?”","“Your tribute is inferior. There is a low chance of a successful prophecy. Do you want to proceed?” the terrifying voice echoed from the scroll.","“Milord, these are the fellow brethren from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They are my beloved friends and brothers. There is no better tribute I can offer. I am counting on you, milord.”","It was rare for Jie Tianran to behave so respectfully. He wasn’t this polite even toward the old entity inside him.","“Mm,” the voice in the scroll replied.","The tens of millions of souls inside the scroll suddenly writhed with greater fervor while screaming in incomparable agony. A massive mouth that was big enough to devour a starfield had appeared within the scroll, and it was devouring everything within it.","Including the straw man inscribed with Chu Feng’s name.","Soon, the realm closed and reverted into a scroll. Countless runes flowed on the surface of the scroll like schools of fish.","Jie Tianran was nervous. The longer the prophecy took, the less effective it was. He hoped that the prophecy would appear as soon as possible. But looking at how faint the runes on the scroll were, he doubted that was likely.","“I remember how, when you prophesied Jie Ranqing’s future, everything went smoothly. The prophecy was out in the blink of an eye. That was the most perfect and accurate prophecy. But things are different this time around. The longer it takes, the less accurate the prophecy is. Jie Tianran, you shouldn’t harbor high hopes about this,” the old entity said.","“I was just giving it a try. I wasn’t expecting much from it. Ultimately, we still have to count on ourselves,” Jie Tianran replied as he looked toward God’s Era.","His instincts told him that God’s Era could change his fate. It could become the key to whether he could establish himself in the Ninth Galaxy. He couldn’t let that power fall into anyone else’s hand.","“Elder, I’ll be counting on you if Chu Feng defeats me in the fight for God’s Era. Please snatch that power over for me no matter the price. Otherwise, our journey in the Ninth Galaxy won’t be smooth sailing,” Jie Tianran said.","“You need not emphasize that, Jie Tianran. I know that we are in the same boat. I still have to rely on you. God’s Era’s power will be yours,” the old entity replied.","...","Chu Feng and the others returned to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city.","The first thing Chu Feng did upon returning was to find Sikong Changsheng to give him a portion of God’s Era’s powers, but he was unable to find the latter.","So, he looked for his aunt, Jie Baobao, Jie Shanxian, and Daoist Starseizer instead to treat them.","The results were satisfactory.","The energy further stabilized Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer’s conditions. They were still unable to cultivate, but they could now live a healthy life, and their lifespans had been extended.","As for his aunt and Jie Baobao, the energy further healed their bodies, reconstructed their bloodlines, and repaired their dantian. Their lost spirit power wouldn’t return, but they could at least cultivate once more.","On the bright side, the energy had metamorphosed their bloodlines. With their current talent, they should be able to reach and surpass their previous levels easily. It could be considered a blessing in disguise.","Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief.","However, he couldn’t help but lower his head in shame when he looked at Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer.","“Chu Feng, this is a good thing. Why do you look so gloomy?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“Elder, I’ll restore your spirit power one day,” Chu Feng declared.","Chu Feng felt ashamed because he couldn’t help Jie Shanxian and Daoist Starseizer reclaim their spirit power."]},{"number":6667,"title":"Chapter 6667: Chapter 6665: Seeking Refuge","paragraphs":["Chapter 6665: Seeking Refuge","“Chu Feng, don’t heap so much stress on yourself. Lord Jie Shanxian and my injuries have nothing to do with you. It’s all Jie Tianran’s doing. Cultivators are bound to encounter crises along the way. It’s already a miracle in itself that we are still alive now, and that is all thanks to you,” Daoist Starseizer said.","Jie Shanxian added with a confident smile, “Chu Feng, I have faith that you can restore our spirit power one day, but there is no need to rush it. Make sure to remain safe. We are counting on you.”","“Mm.” Chu Feng nodded.","He looked at his aunt and Jie Baobao, who were still sleeping. As much as he trusted his judgment, he couldn’t help but harbor a seed of doubt until they woke up.","Fortunately, his aunt woke up not long later.","“Tiannian, Chu Feng has reconstructed your bloodline using God’s Era’s powers. You should be able to cultivate now. Quick, give it a try,” Jie Shanxian said.","Jie Tiannian was taken aback, but she quickly inspected her own body and attempted to cultivate. She realized that there was a brand-new bloodline within her. Not only was it stronger than before, but it was also perfectly compatible with her.","With the deep insights she had accumulated over many years, she would surely be able to cultivate many times faster than before. This good news thrilled her so much that she even wept tears of joy.","She was ultimately a world spiritist prodigy. How could she not care about her spirit power? She felt like she had just been given a new lease on life.","“Chu Feng, how can I ever thank you?” Jie Tiannian looked at Chu Feng with teary eyes.","“You’re my aunt. I’m just doing what I should. Since you’re able to cultivate now, these should be useful to you.” Chu Feng took out a Cosmos Sack and handed it to his aunt.","It contained many cultivation resources, as well as the God’s Era’s powers for cultivation and recovery.","Jie Tiannian was taken aback. Her tears had barely stopped when they began flowing once more as if someone had opened their flood gates. She sensed Chu Feng’s concern for her in the Cosmos Sack. These were invaluable treasures.","Even Jie Tianran hadn’t been so generous to her back when he was nurturing her.","She felt a surge of familial warmth from Chu Feng, especially since she hadn’t been particularly close to Chu Feng before.","“Don’t cry, aunt.” Chu Feng felt his heart clench up.","Others might think Jie Tiannian had lived a privileged life, being born into a powerful clan and possessing exceptional talent, but in truth, she had lived like a puppet. Jie Tianran treated her like a pawn, controlling everything about her life, including her marriage. He even crippled her spirit power and attempted to kill her.","Her life hadn’t been easy at all.","Despite being respected by others, she didn’t have many friends. More often than not, others approached her with ulterior motives. It was rare for anyone to treat her with earnest sincerity. That was why she cried when she felt Chu Feng’s genuine concern for her.","And that was also why Chu Feng felt bad for her.","“I’m fine, Chu Feng. I’m just happy. I’m glad that Ranqing had a good son like you. I’m glad to have a nephew like you. People often say that we should have sons care for us when we’re old. My son was unreliable, but I was able to bask in Ranqing’s halo,” Jie Tiannian said.","“Don’t say that, aunt. Jie Tian has merely been misled by Jie Tianran. He isn’t a bad person at heart. At the very least, he cares about you. If not for him, I wouldn’t have been able to save you back then,” Chu Feng replied.","He used to look down on Jie Tian, but his impression of Jie Tian changed when the latter activated a forbidden skill to stall Jie Tianran to buy time for Chu Feng to rescue Jie Tiannian.","His words brought Jie Tiannian back to that day. Using that forbidden skill had caused Jie Tian’s soul to crack.","“Chu Feng, is Tian’er still alive?” Jie Tiannian anxiously asked.","Such severe injuries should have resulted in Jie Tian’s death, but Chu Feng learned that Jie Tian was still alive and had gone into closed-door training. At the very least, there was no news about Jie Tian’s death from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Jie Tianran is a beast, but he wields exceptional means. I’m inclined to think that Jie Tian is alive,” Chu Feng replied.","Jie Tiannian’s face brightened up. No matter what, Jie Tian was still her son. There was no way she wouldn’t care about him.","Besides, Jie Tian was not irredeemable. His willingness to sacrifice himself to save her had touched her heart. She hoped that he was well and that someday they would be able to reunite.","“Wuuu~” another voice echoed.","Jie Baobao had awoken.","Chu Feng rushed over. Jie Tiannian, Jie Shanxian, and Daoist Starseizer followed suit.","“Chu Feng?”","Jie Baobao was surprised to see Chu Feng, as she had thought that she was dead.","“How are you feeling?” Chu Feng asked gently.","“A-am I still alive?” Jie Baobao asked in uncertainty, not daring to believe that she was still alive.","“Silly lass. You’re definitely alive, but you might have to cultivate again from the start. However, you don’t have to worry too much. Chu Feng has reconstructed your bloodline. It’ll take time for you to reach your previous level, but you’ll surely surpass your past self,” Jie Shanxian said.","Jie Baobao belatedly noticed the three people standing beside her.","“Lord Jie Shanxian? Lord Jie Tiannian? Lord Starseizer?”","Jie Baobao hurriedly got up and bowed to the trio.","“There’s no need for formalities. Get up. You don’t know how worried Chu Feng was while you were unconscious,” Jie Tiannian said as she pulled Jie Baobao back to her feet.","“Am I really still alive?” Jie Baobao asked.","“If you’re dead, doesn’t that mean that we’re dead as well?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“That’s not what I mean. I-I...” Jie Baobao hurriedly replied.","The realization that she was alive only heaped greater stress on her. These three people were legends to her, particularly Jie Shanxian, who was an old ancestor of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“You don’t need to be so nervous. We aren’t in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. From this day on, you’re just our junior,” Jie Shanxian said.","It took Jie Baobao a while to come to terms with the fact that she was still alive. However, this news didn’t console her. Instead, she felt embarrassed.","“Chu Feng, about what I said that day...” Jie Baobao stuttered, not daring to look at Chu Feng.","“It’s not important. All that matters is that you’re safe and sound.” Chu Feng patted Jie Baobao’s shoulder.","His tender gesture calmed down the tense Jie Baobao. She nodded obediently.","Chu Feng quickly shared the news with Ling Xiao and the others and urged them to head over to accompany her.","Moments later, he received a report. Ling Sheng’er had come to join him."]},{"number":6668,"title":"Chapter 6668: Chapter 6666: Little Ling","paragraphs":["Chapter 6666: Little Ling","Upon hearing the report, Chu Feng rushed out to welcome Ling Sheng’er.","She was the first friend he had befriended in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. He was still small fry then, but Ling Sheng’er, despite being the lofty daughter of the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief, didn’t put on airs in front of him and treated him like a friend.","Due to that, Chu Feng had a really good impression of her.","Ling Sheng’er and the others were brought into a hall, where most of the Chu Clan Alliance’s upper echelon was gathered.","Ling Mo’er and Shuang Yu looked nervous as they weren’t sure how Chu Feng would react to their arrival. In contrast, Ling Sheng’er sat calmly, eating and drinking whatever that was offered to her. Despite being surrounded by foreign faces, she behaved as if she was at home.","“Has someone been starving you?” a familiar voice echoed.","“Chu Feng!!!” Ling Sheng’er hopped up to Chu Feng like a little rabbit. “I miss you so much!”","She lightly punched Chu Feng’s shoulder. Her gesture was brotherly despite looking like an adorable princess.","“You have grown prettier over the years.” Chu Feng pinched Ling Sheng’er’s little face, but not even the distortion of her face could conceal her beauty. If anything, it made her more adorable.","“You have also grown more handsome,” Ling Sheng’er replied as she pushed Chu Feng’s nose until it was compressed like a pig’s snout. She laughed. “Yes, you look much better like that.”","Anyone could tell that they were extremely close.","In contrast, Ling Mo’er and Shuang Yu were extremely reserved. They had become acquainted with Chu Feng at the same time as Ling Sheng’er, but they had chosen to take a different route from Ling Sheng’er. That resulted in their current awkward position.","“Chu Feng, we’re looking to join you. Do you welcome us?” Ling Sheng’er asked while gesturing to the duo behind her.","“Of course,” Chu Feng replied.","Shuang Yu couldn’t hold herself back anymore. She wanted to kneel before Chu Feng and apologize for what she had done back then. “Young master Chu Feng, I...”","Before her knees could hit the ground, Chu Feng grabbed her arm and supported her. “Elder Shuang Yu, I’ve heard about it. You didn’t know who I was back then, and you were helping my grandmother. I won’t blame you for that. The Chu Clan Alliance welcomes you.”","His smile showed that he truly intended to accept Shuang Yu.","Shuang Yu’s body trembled as she wept. In the end, she murmured a reply, “Young master, my life is yours from now on.”","...","“Chu Feng, there’s someone else who wishes to work with you. It’s my grandfather,” Ling Sheng’er told Chu Feng via voice transmission.","She told him about the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief’s intention, and that the latter was waiting for him outside the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city.","Chu Feng trusted Ling Sheng’er, but that didn’t mean that he trusted the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief. So, he brought Little Fishy, Jie Tiannian, Jie Shanxian, and Daoist Starseizer out with him.","Meanwhile, the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was standing some distance away from the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city. He had pulled out his extravagant warship and was standing on its deck with an air of loftiness.","He was not here to seek refuge but to negotiate a partnership with Chu Feng. Since it was a partnership, he planned to negotiate terms beneficial to the Ling Clan. Thus, he couldn’t lower his posture.","When he sensed a warship approaching, he put on even more airs. He placed his hands behind his back and turned away, as if Chu Feng was the one begging him for a partnership.","“Little Ling, you have finally thought things through.”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was startled. He quickly turned around, only to see Jie Shanxian emerging from Chu Feng’s warship and stepping onto his deck.","Behind Jie Shanxian were Jie Tiannian, Daoist Starseizer, Chu Feng, Little Fishy, Ling Sheng’er, and the others.","“Paying respect to Lord Shanxian!”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief fell to his knees and kowtowed to Jie Shanxian. He still harbored deep respect for Jie Shanxian despite knowing that she had lost her cultivation. In fact, he felt another wave of resentment toward Jie Tianran when he saw her once more.","Jie Shanxian had devoted her entire life to protecting the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, saving it from several major crises, but Jie Tianran plotted against her and caused her to lose her cultivation. She might have even died if not for Chu Feng.","Bitter regret washed over him. He suddenly wondered why he had been so obstinate about standing with Jie Tianran.","“Little Ling, don’t pull this with me. I’ll only ask you one time. Do you intend to join Chu Feng, or do you have an ulterior motive?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“Milord, I came here to pledge loyalty to Chu Feng on behalf of the Ling Clan, so that we can destroy Jie Tianran and avenge you,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief said.","Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er were taken aback. That was not what their grandfather had said.","Little did they know that their grandfather didn’t intend this, either. Sometimes, it only took an instant for a person to change their mind. Due to his change of mind, the negotiation between him and Chu Feng went smoothly.","In truth, Chu Feng did not harbor high expectations of the Ling Clan.","They were Jie Tianran’s pawns; their switching sides would not be a turning point for this war. They didn’t even know about the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body; it was unlikely that they could divulge any essential information that would help him deal with Jie Tianran.","Soon, both sides came to an agreement.","Rather than bringing the Ling Clan into the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect’s main city, it was better for them to stay put in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They might be able to better contribute from there.","Chu Feng promised not to kill any Ling Clansmen, though the caveat was that the Ling Clansmen mustn’t kill anyone from the Chu Clan Alliance.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief agreed. Even he couldn’t guarantee that everyone from the Ling Clan would be willing to join Chu Feng’s side.","He knew that Jie Tianran had been spreading his influence within the Ling Clan, such that many Ling Clansmen were very loyal to Jie Tianran. Some of them were even serving as Jie Tianran’s spies, providing him with updates about the Ling Clan’s movements.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief knew that there was no saving those people.","Ling Sheng’er passed the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief’s communication talisman paper to Chu Feng.","If Chu Feng ever needed the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief’s help, he could relay his instructions over via the talisman paper.","After hashing out the details, the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief began making his way back to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. There were many things he needed to do now. First of all, he had to sift out the trustworthy Ling Clansmen and bring them together.","“Lord Jie Shanxian, I’ll be taking my leave.” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief kowtowed once more.","“You’re leaving already? Even though Chu Feng was magnanimous to let go of the past and take you in, you can’t be so shameless as to accept his goodwill without showing some sincerity, right?” Jie Shanxian said."]},{"number":6669,"title":"Chapter 6669: Chapter 6667: Heaven Protection Shield Spirit","paragraphs":["Chapter 6667: Heaven Protection Shield Spirit","“Milord, Chu Feng has many treasures. I don’t have anything worth offering. Actually, I did prepare something, but I was worried that Chu Feng might not want it,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief said with an awkward smile as he handed a Cosmos Sack over.","“Take a look,” Jie Shanxian said.","Chu Feng poured out the treasures inside the Cosmos Sack. It was filled with valuable treasures, ranging from world spiritist materials to natural oddities. There were even materials that were not available on the market.","Ling Sheng’er was amazed. She didn’t expect her miserly grandfather to be so sincere.","But Jie Shanxian scoffed, “It really isn’t much. No wonder you’re worried that Chu Feng won’t want it.”","Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er were stunned. This isn’t much?","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief smiled awkwardly. The truth was that he didn’t prepare anything. It was out of respect for Jie Shanxian that he gathered some items together on the spot, and even so, he was already feeling the pinch.","This was already the greatest extent of his sincerity.","“Little Ling, I remember that your Ling Clan has a hereditary treasure bestowed from the first Mansion Master known as the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit, but no one has been able to awaken it to date. Since you aren’t able to put it to good use anyway, why don’t you let Chu Feng give it a try? He might be able to awaken it,” Jie Shanxian said.","“Ah...” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief looked troubled.","He was about to say something when Jie Shanxian added, “Don’t say that you didn’t bring it with you. I’ll search your body if you dare say that.”","“I brought it, I brought it. I was thinking of giving it to Chu Feng as well, but it seems insincere to give a treasure that can’t be awakened,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief replied.","“Not at all. I think it is the perfect gift. What do you say, Chu Feng?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“I think you are right, elder. There is no greater sincerity than this if the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief is willing to give the treasure to me. No matter what, I’ll cherish it. Besides, the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit sounds like a formidable treasure. I’d like to see what it is.”","Chu Feng’s eyes were practically glowing.","Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er were dumbstruck. It was true that no one had been able to awaken the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit, but that was still one of the Ling Clan’s greatest treasures.","Ling Sheng’er had previously asked her grandfather to give her the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit, but the latter only allowed her to try awakening it. After she failed, he refused to let her touch it anymore.","She didn’t think that her miserly grandfather would be willing to give it to Chu Feng.","But the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief took out a palm-sized copper treasure and handed it to Chu Feng. “Why don’t you give it a try first, Chu Feng?”","The copper treasure resembled a mirror, but there was no reflective surface. A hideous beast was sculpted on one side. As Chu Feng took the copper treasure, he noticed the beast’s gaze falling upon him.","“It’s alive?” Chu Feng asked.","“Alive?” Ling Sheng’er and the others were taken aback.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief replied firmly, “It’s not a living being. It is a treasure that manifests a powerful protective formation when activated.”","“Chu Feng, did you notice something?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“I sensed an assessing gaze from the treasure,” Chu Feng replied.","“Do you mean it? Does this mean that you’re able to awaken the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit?” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was astounded, particularly because it was his first time hearing about this.","It was the same for Jie Shanxian, Jie Tiannian, and Daoist Starseizer as well.","Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er stared at Chu Feng with agape mouths. They had previously attempted to awaken the treasure, but they didn’t sense any gaze.","“I’ll give it a try.”","Chu Feng grabbed the treasure and attempted to fuse his spirit power into it. The Heaven Protection Shield Spirit began to emanate a faint glow.","“Oh my...” Ling Sheng’er and Ling Mo’er widened their eyes in shock.","Back when their grandfather told them to try awakening the treasure, he said that as long as they could make the treasure glow, they stood a chance of awakening it. A Ling Clan’s ancestor once succeeded in doing so, but he died in a battle against the Celestial Master Sacred Sect.","Since then, no one has succeeded in that feat.","The light became brighter as Chu Feng channeled his bloodline power into the treasure.","Shoosh!","Martial power enveloped the surroundings. It was Little Fishy’s doing.","The light was getting too bright, and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was bound to be surveilling the area. It would be safer to isolate the area to avoid catching their attention.","Actually, the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief should have been the one to do that, but he was so focused on the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit that he wasn’t paying attention to anything else. This was his first time seeing such a reaction from it.","Soon, the beast sculpted on the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit began to move.","“Grandfather, is it really alive?” Ling Sheng’er exclaimed.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief stared at the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit with unblinking eyes.","The beast changed its position and curled into a ball. The brilliant light faded, and the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit reverted to its original form. However, the crowd continued staring at the treasure.","“It really is alive! No wonder it’s called the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit! I thought the beast was just a decoration, but to think that it’s alive! Chu Feng, have you awakened the treasure?” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“I’m afraid I failed.” Chu Feng shook his head.","“You failed?”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was initially conflicted, but then his mood lifted.","Many people had questioned if the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit was just a gimmick, since no one had been able to activate it. But Chu Feng’s feat proved its value. And since Chu Feng had failed to awaken it, there was no need for him to gift the treasure to him.","Right as the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was about to take the treasure back, Jie Shanxian interjected, “Chu Feng, since you almost succeeded in awakening the treasure, you should keep it and give it a few more tries. I’m sure you’ll succeed in due time. If you aren’t able to do it, I doubt that anyone else can.”","Jie Shanxian turned to the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and asked, “Don’t you agree, Little Ling?”","“Um... About this...”","While the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was racking his brain for a way to retrieve the treasure, Chu Feng bowed to the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief with a wide smile and said, “Thank you, elder!”","Before the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief could say a word, he stuffed the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit into his Cosmos Sack.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was dumbfounded.","“What’s wrong, elder? Why does your complexion look so awful?” Chu Feng asked.","“I-it’s nothing.” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief sighed. Even his voice sounded subdued.","Ling Sheng’er and Jie Shanxian giggled. Both of them knew how miserly the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief was, and they could imagine the pinch he was feeling right now.","“Hm?” Chu Feng suddenly sensed something and narrowed his eyes. He quickly turned to the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief."]},{"number":6670,"title":"Chapter 6670: Chapter 6668: Bad Chu Feng!","paragraphs":["Chapter 6668: Bad Chu Feng!","“Elder, do you have treasures to observe God’s Era?” Chu Feng asked the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief.","“I do.”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief took out an old mirror from his Cosmos Sack. It contained a tiny observation formation, but it could only be activated for a limited number of times.","Chu Feng took the old mirror, pointed it at God’s Era, and activated it. The mirror flew out of his hand and transformed into a hundred-meter-tall giant screen reflecting God’s Era. Only then did the crowd realize that something was happening to God’s Era’s massive silhouette.","The silhouette had lifted the three doors with both hands toward its chest. Three different patterns had appeared on the doors. They weren’t there before.","“Is God’s Era about to open? How did you know, Chu Feng?”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief looked at Chu Feng in astonishment. They were all chatting a moment ago, but of them, only Chu Feng noticed the changes in God’s Era.","“I have forged a connection with God’s Era. I can sense its movements,” Chu Feng replied.","“Connection? Ah...”","Chu Feng’s accomplishments were so frequently discussed in the world of cultivation that one’s ears could grow calluses from hearing about them. No one in the world of cultivation would deny that Chu Feng was a monstrous prodigy.","But it was a different matter to witness it in person.","Seeing Chu Feng’s feats close up, the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief affirmed that he had been too foolish to insist on protecting the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. He should have switched over to Chu Feng’s side a long time ago.","He grumbled, “Damn it. I used to think that the Totem Dragon Clan was dumb to have thrown their lot with a junior like Chu Feng, but in hindsight, I was the dumb one. The Totem Dragon Clan is the wise one to have the foresight to move pre-emptively.”","The more he thought about it, the more regretful he felt.","The patterns vanished shortly after. The three doors emanated a brilliant light, signaling that they were now open.","“It seems like we can go in now,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief said. He looked at Chu Feng for confirmation as he trusted the latter’s judgment more.","“Yes. God’s Era is really open this time,” Chu Feng replied.","“There seems to be a difference among the three doors,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief added","“Yes, but I can’t tell for sure what the differences are,” Chu Feng replied.","“You can’t tell, either? Do you think we can obtain God’s Era’s final power this time?” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“I think so,” Chu Feng replied.","In the meantime, the mirror reverted to its original size and returned to Chu Feng’s hand.","“Milord, I’ll have to head back now. Now that God’s Era has opened, Jie Tianran will surely make a move,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief reported to Jie Shanxian.","“All right.” Jie Shanxian nodded.","“Take care, grandfather.” Ling Sheng’er was worried about her grandfather.","“Don’t worry, I’ll be fine,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief replied.","“Stay safe, elder.” Chu Feng bowed to the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief.","“Chu Feng, about that...”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief hesitantly looked at the mirror in Chu Feng’s hand. He could already tell that Chu Feng wasn’t planning to return the mirror to him, but he had to give it a try anyway. The mirror was an invaluable treasure!","“Little Ling, stop being so miserly. It’s just a mirror!” Jie Shanxian berated.","“Ah, I was thinking of giving this mirror to Chu Feng straight,” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief quickly replied, though his heart was bleeding as he said those words.","He bade the others farewell and returned to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Big brother, don’t you have observation treasures as well? Have you used up all of them? Why don’t I give you some?” Little Fishy said as she reached into her Cosmos Sack.","“Don’t worry, I still have plenty of observation treasures,” Chu Feng replied with a mischievous smile.","The crowd chuckled. They knew that Chu Feng was just teasing the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief.","Ling Sheng’er lightly punched Chu Feng’s shoulder and complained, “Bad Chu Feng. You’re bullying my grandfather.”","The group then returned to the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect. They needed to make arrangements now that God’s Era had opened.","“Chu Feng, what did you decipher from those patterns?” Eggy asked.","“How do you know I have deciphered something?” Chu Feng asked with a grin.","“Did you think you could fool me? You trust Ling Sheng’er and the others, but that doesn’t extend to the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief. That’s why you didn’t want to share your findings with him.”","“My Eggy knows me the best.”","“So, what did you discover?”","“The three doors converge to the same destination, but each path has a different danger level. The first door poses the greatest risk, and it requires an activation item. However, I still haven’t figured out what the activation item is. Without the activation item, entering the first door results in certain death.","“The second door leads to a relatively dangerous trial, but failure to clear it doesn’t result in certain death. The third door is relatively safer.","“While the three doors lead to the same destination, the chances of reaching the destination differ from door to door. Clearing the first door guarantees access to the destination, but for the second door and the third door, the probabilities are 70% and 50% respectively,” Chu Feng said.","“What about the key sword you constructed, Chu Feng? Isn’t that the activation item?” Eggy asked.","“While the three doors appear to be open, they can’t be accessed without the key sword. The key sword only grants me the right to challenge the three doors; it isn’t the activation item,” Chu Feng replied.","“What could the activation item be?” Eggy murmured in the World Spirit Space. As much as possible, she wanted Chu Feng to have the upper hand in God’s Era.","“I don’t know. Even from the first time I entered God’s Era, I have already sensed that an activation power is required to obtain the final power. However, I still haven’t found any signs of the activation item yet. I guess that the activation item lies in one of the doors.”","Chu Feng was in a good mood.","God’s Era was developing in the direction he anticipated. He couldn’t wait to find out what God’s Era’s final power was."]},{"number":6671,"title":"Chapter 6671: Chapter 6669: Chu Feng’s Weakness","paragraphs":["Chapter 6669: Chu Feng’s Weakness","Jie Tianran had also just finished observing God’s Era.","“What did you get, Jie Tianran?” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body asked.","“The first door grants the highest chance of obtaining God’s Era’s final power, but it is a death trap. Those who enter it are bound to die.","“The second door has a slightly lower chance of obtaining God’s Era’s final power, but it is still extremely risky. Those who enter it are unlikely to survive.","“The third door still poses some danger, but there is a higher chance of survival. At the same time, one still has a chance of obtaining God’s Era’s final power,” Jie Tianran said.","“That is what I got as well. Do you intend to head to the second door or the third door?” the old entity asked.","“My sword key is pointing me toward the third door,” Jie Tianran replied.","“What about your own thoughts?”","“I want to follow the guidance.”","Right after saying those words, Jie Tianran turned around as he sensed a change in the Immemorial Divination Art’s scroll. However, what he saw made him sigh in disappointment.","The runes had dissipated, signaling the failure of the prophecy.","“I told you that the tribute isn’t enough. Forget it. Don’t bother with this since God’s Era has already opened. As long as you obtain God’s Era’s final power, that grandson of yours won’t pose a threat at all,” the old entity replied.","Jie Tianran had anticipated this outcome, but he was still disappointed by it. He stowed away the Immemorial Divination Art’s scroll.","“Hold on,” the old entity suddenly said.","Jie Tianran hurriedly turned at the scroll and noticed a line of words. It only remained there for a brief moment, but he saw it clearly.","Chu Feng’s weakness is now at the Bloodline Galaxy.","“The prophecy succeeded?” the old entity remarked in delight.","Jie Tianran quickly used his observation means to examine the Bloodline Galaxy. He was initially worried that he wouldn’t be able to find the weakness, considering how big the Bloodline Galaxy was.","His worry was unfounded, for what the prophecy was pointing toward was conspicuous. However, he frowned in worry.","“What... is that?”","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng had gathered the higher-ups in the Chu Clan Alliance to discuss their plan for God’s Era.","Just then, someone rushed over to report a phenomenon in the Bloodline Galaxy.","Chu Feng and the others quickly employed their observation means, and what they saw made their hearts clench.","A phenomenon had appeared in the Bloodline Galaxy. It was not as big and spectacular as God’s Era, but it spanned the size of a starfield. The phenomenon projected a beautiful scenery that felt like a mirage in the middle of space.","It was the crater of a volcano that towered in the middle of a mountain range. The crater was so high that it was above the clouds. The surrounding mountains were covered in greenery, but the crater was shrouded in snow.","“What a peculiar phenomenon. Why does it look so much like a scenery?”","Chu Feng and Ling Sheng’er weren’t the only ones observing the phenomenon. A large group of people stood behind Chu Feng, and all of them harbored the same doubt.","Chu Feng took out a scroll and unfurled it. It depicted the scenery as well.","“Chu Feng... why is your painting identical to this phenomenon?” Ling Sheng’er asked in astonishment.","“Chu Feng, what is that place?” Long Mucheng and the others anxiously asked.","They figured that Chu Feng knew what that place was since he had that painting.","“My friends and clansmen in the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm suddenly went missing some time ago, and the incident is related to a mysterious person. That person left me this painting as a clue. For many years, I have been searching for this place but to no avail.”","Chu Feng trusted those who were currently with him, so he told them the truth.","“Does that mean that your friends and clansmen are trapped in that phenomenon?” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“I’m not sure, but I’ll have to make a trip there,” Chu Feng said.","“Are you heading there after God’s Era?” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief asked.","“No, I’ll head to the Bloodline Galaxy first,” Chu Feng replied.","The crowd looked conflicted as they understood the importance of God’s Era.","“Chu Feng, why don’t we split ways? I’ll investigate the Bloodline Galaxy on your behalf, so you can head to God’s Era with ease of mind. If we find your friends and clansmen, you can be sure that we’ll rescue them,” Long Mucheng said.","“Elder, I have to head there in person,” Chu Feng replied.","“I’ll follow you,” Little Fishy said.","Long Mucheng, the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, and the others would have preferred Chu Feng to venture into God’s Era first. They knew that Jie Tianran would enter God’s Era, and that Chu Feng might lose his upper hand if he was late.","They had already experienced God’s Era’s powers in person, and they could hardly imagine how potent its final power would be. It would be disastrous for them if Jie Tianran were to obtain God’s Era’s final power.","But when Chu Feng insisted on heading to the Bloodline Galaxy first, none of them tried to dissuade him. They knew that Chu Feng prioritized the safety of his friends and family over his pursuit of power.","They had all experienced that in person.","“I’ll go alone. You don’t have to worry about me. I can protect myself. Yu’er, you should have seen it for yourself,” Chu Feng replied.","He was referring to the Divine Deer’s power, but in truth, the Divine Deer’s power hadn’t recovered yet. He didn’t have any secret hand right now. The only hand he had was the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit, but he hadn’t fully awakened it yet.","However, the Bloodline Galaxy was the Netherworld Sect’s turf. He knew it would be dangerous, so he didn’t want Little Fishy and the others to tag along.","“Big brother, I know that you possess powerful means, so it would be safer for me to stick with you, no?” Little Fishy replied."]},{"number":6672,"title":"Chapter 6672: Chapter 6670: Let’s Enjoy the Scenery","paragraphs":["Chapter 6670: Let’s Enjoy the Scenery","“Yu’er is right. Since you have defensive measures, we should be safe with you. Didn’t the Netherworld Sect bully you not too long ago? We’ll get back at them for you if we can defeat them. Otherwise, we can just fall back on your escape means,” Long Mucheng said.","This put Chu Feng in a spot.","“Chu Feng, take them with you. Shouldn’t friends brave danger together? You shouldn’t be sharing the benefits but shouldering the risks alone. What is the point of the Chu Clan Alliance if so? Besides, they are doing this of their own volition. You might think you’re protecting them, but you’re undermining them by turning down their earnest desire to help,” Eggy said.","Those words moved Chu Feng, especially when he saw the determined faces around him. These people earnestly wanted to fight alongside him. They were willing to brave death just so that they could be of any help to him.","He didn’t think there was anything more valuable than this in life.","“You’re right, Eggy,” Chu Feng replied. He turned to the crowd and said, “All right.”","“I’ll be going as well, Chu Feng.”","“Me too!”","Long Chengyu and Long Muxi volunteered themselves.","“Chu Feng, bring us along as well.” The Totem Nine Daoists also spoke up.","More and more people expressed their desire to follow Chu Feng to the Bloodline Galaxy.","“We’ll all go together,” Chu Feng said.","Those words brought smiles to the faces around. It was as if they were going on a fun adventure instead of marching into the heart of danger.","But what Chu Feng said next surprised the crowd.","“I don’t just mean the ones present here. I’m talking about everyone in the Chu Clan Alliance. Everyone will go to the Bloodline Galaxy together,” Chu Feng said.","“Everyone?” The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief was taken aback.","The top experts of the Chu Clan Alliance were already gathered here. The others would only be baggage if they tagged along.","“That’s right. Tell the others that this journey will be fraught with danger, and they can sit out of this one if they want to,” Chu Feng said.","“All right, I’ll get that done right away,” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief replied. He didn’t question Chu Feng’s judgment after seeing the serious look on the latter’s face.","Chu Feng had a reason for that.","The outcome of a fight between two powers was determined by their most powerful expert. Quality mattered more than quantity. But that didn’t mean that weaker cultivators were useless. There was a way they could contribute—through formations.","Similar to how the Dragon Breath Clan could maximize their fighting prowess by channeling a formation in unison, Chu Feng could also construct a formation that could be channeled solely via martial power to raise their fighting prowess.","Such formations relied heavily on numbers.","The Chu Clan Alliance was small compared to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but the Totem Dragon Clan was a behemoth in itself, and there had been many recruits recently. If all of them were to channel Chu Feng’s formation, they could provide significant aid to Little Fishy and the others.","Chu Feng told the others about his intention before proceeding to construct a formation.","The formation was complex, but with the aid of the Chu Clan Alliance’s world spiritists, they should be able to quickly finish the foundation. The foundation was a formation realm, which could be used to house members of the Chu Clan Alliance.","After the Chu Clan Alliance’s members entered the formation realm, Chu Feng would make further refinements to ensure that the crowd could efficiently channel the formation. This was a crucial step to optimize the formation.","More importantly, once everyone was inside the formation realm, Chu Feng would be able to travel via the Nine Heavens Secret Domain and swiftly reach the Bloodline Galaxy.","...","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran was gathering the members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had the advantage in accessing God’s Era due to its proximity to it.","But neither Jie Tianran nor the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s main force was at the Seven Realms Galaxy. They were still returning from the Totem Galaxy and the Immortal Sea Galaxy. So, Jie Tianran issued an order to his members to gather somewhere and await his orders.","He also sent a message to the Netherworld Sect, requesting them to lay an ambush in the area around the phenomenon, no matter the cost.","Jie Tianran prioritized God’s Era over everything else, so there was no way he would miss it. However, while he didn’t understand the phenomenon, the prophecy stated that it was related to Chu Feng’s weakness, so he couldn’t turn a blind eye to that.","This was the perfect moment to mobilize the Netherworld Sect.","...","Soon, Chu Feng was done constructing the formation’s foundation. The Chu Clan Alliance entered the formation.","Only trusted world spiritists and important figures like Long Mucheng and the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief traveled with him outside the formation.","With the preparations in place, Chu Feng was about to make a move when a figure suddenly entered the Ancestral Martial Spiritist Sect.","“Aren’t you too much, Chu Feng? You dumped me at the Totem Galaxy and didn’t call me along,” the person spoke grudgingly.","It was Fei.","“Brother Fei, what brings you here?” Chu Feng asked with a smile.","“Why can’t I be here?” Fei grumbled.","“I thought you’d return with Elder Song Changsheng after recovering. You have already helped me once, after all,” Chu Feng replied.","“I helped you once, but you saved my life. We’re equal now, so I can help you once more,” Fei replied.","“That’s perfect. We’re about to do something huge.”","“Is it God’s Era? God’s Era has just opened, right?”","Fei had also noticed the changes in God’s Era.","However, Chu Feng shook his head and replied, “I’ll take you out to see good scenery.”","So, the group set forth together with Fei.","Along the way, Chu Feng issued instructions to the world spiritists to perfect the formation. The formation got increasingly harder as they made progress, to the point where world spiritists like the Totem Nine Daoists and Ling Xiao’s grandfather could no longer grasp the big picture. They could only obediently follow Chu Feng’s instructions.","To more easily construct the formation, the group traveled in a massive warship.","The warship’s deck was jam-packed with world spiritists. Countless surges of spirit power flowed from specific points toward a spherical formation in an orderly fashion.","It was a majestic sight.","Even Long Mucheng and the others, despite not being world spiritists, were mesmerized.","“Chu Feng is a monstrous prodigy,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather suddenly remarked.","Ling Xiao, who was seated next to his grandfather, asked out of curiosity, “Grandfather, have you managed to grasp Chu Feng’s formation?”","“Not at all.” Ling Xiao’s grandfather shook his head.","“Then why are you suddenly praising Chu Feng?”","Ling Xiao knew that his grandfather didn’t like others ordering him around, even when constructing a formation. He had been worried that his grandfather would throw a tantrum, but unexpectedly, his grandfather was excited about the work.","“Because this formation feels good to construct,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather replied.","“Elder, I thought you didn't like to follow instructions? How does this feel good?” Ling Sheng’er asked from afar.","She was looking at the duo from a distance away.","“I don’t like to follow instructions because most people are incompetent. They issue wrong instructions, then pin their failure on me. However, young master Chu Feng’s instructions are clear and concise. I can just follow them without second thoughts. On top of that, I can sense the formation perfecting under his orders. I have never felt so relaxed constructing a formation before,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather replied.","“Agreed.”","The surrounding world spiritists voiced their agreement.","It was no easy feat to coordinate world spiritists for a formation this complicated. Mistakes were commonplace, and time would inevitably have to be squandered on fixing the errors.","However, Chu Feng was somehow able to ensure perfection in every step. His leadership, multitasking capability, and grasp of the formation were at an unprecedented level. At the very least, those present had never seen anything like this.","Not even Jie Tianran could match this.","To the world spiritists present, they weren’t just witnessing the birth of a powerful formation. They were also witnessing the rise of a great world spiritist."]},{"number":6673,"title":"Chapter 6673: Chapter 6671: Netherworld God Bestowment","paragraphs":["Chapter 6671: Netherworld God Bestowment","Before Chu Feng and the others could enter the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s entrance, the Netherworld Sect had already received Jie Tianran’s notice.","Six elders were seated side by side in the innermost depths of the Netherworld Sect’s hall.","One was the 1.5-meter-tall, hunched old man, Cang Li.","One was the 10-meter-tall, brawny old man, Lie Shan.","The remaining four had similar physiques. Their hair had all turned white, and all of them kept long beards. They were Ting Yun, Lang Kun, Qiu Feng, and Hao Lei.","They were the six elders of the Netherworld Sect’s neutral faction.","The other five elders were all indebted to Ting Yun, so he commanded the greatest say in the group.","“Jie Tianran has sent a message saying that the phenomenon is related to Chu Feng. He’s telling us to seal off the phenomenon and ambush Chu Feng no matter the cost. What are your thoughts about this?” Ting Yun asked.","Gathered beneath the six neutral elders were the Netherworld Marshals. Due to Dongfang Hansong’s absence, the only one in the group who commanded the same influence as the six neutral elders was Baili Xukong.","That said, Baili Xukong and Dongfang Hansong still addressed the six neutral elders with utmost respect.","“Milord, Chu Feng is our mortal enemy, and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is our ally. Jie Tianran has no reason to deceive us. There is no need for consideration. We should devote our full force to taking down Chu Feng,” Baili Xukong said.","“I heard you have already dispatched personnel to construct a formation?” Cang Li asked. His face was still pale as he hadn’t fully recovered.","“Lord Cang Li, I don’t know where Jie Tianran got the news from, but I don’t think he would carelessly disseminate such important information without verifying it. Considering Chu Feng’s means, I believe that we should make preparations as soon as possible, lest he slip into the phenomenon before we can even react. I’m doing this out of consideration for the Netherworld Sect. Is there any problem with that?” Baili Xukong asked.","His opinion of Cang Li had dropped after the latter opposed him every step of the way, resulting in his attitude being less respectful than before.","“That might be true under normal circumstances, but surely you aren’t so dense as to be ignorant about the current situation, right?” Ting Yun asked. He raised his hand to reveal the black bracelet on his wrist.","A vine had extended from the black bracelet and embedded itself in Ting Yun’s flesh.","Everyone in the hall who had used the black bracelet to awaken the sacred item revealed conflicted looks, except for Baili Xukong. They knew that the bracelet had not just encroached on their flesh but their souls as well.","“Milord, didn’t we know from the start that there’s a backlash from using the bracelets?” Baili Xukong asked.","“The backlash is more severe than we expected. This thing has encroached on not just our bodies but our souls as well. This is not just a backlash; something else is at play. Or are you telling me that you don’t see anything odd about this situation?” Ting Yun asked.","They had been using the black bracelets to awaken the sacred item. They did make progress, but the changes in the bracelets worried them.","On top of that, Cang Li had been reiterating that Jie Tianran was not trustworthy. This sowed doubts in their minds.","“Milord, the bracelets’ energy might have seeped into our bodies, but we can sever it. We have only refrained from doing so because the bracelets will lose their effectiveness afterward,” Baili Xukong replied.","His words were also true. Those present felt that they could sever their connection with the bracelets right away if they wanted to. In fact, some had tried it, but the black bracelets would crumble right after.","On top of that, the backlash immediately struck at the moment of its shattering.","It wasn’t severe enough to cause death, but it was still not to be underestimated.","“Elders, as the saying goes, ‘Don’t use those whom you doubt, and don’t doubt those whom you use.’ If you believe that Jie Tianran is untrustworthy, we can terminate our partnership with him right now. However, I won’t participate in the awakening of the sacred item anymore. You’ll have to figure out a way to awaken the sacred item on your own,” Baili Xukong said.","“Baili Xukong, are you threatening us now?”","A furious roar reminiscent of that from a ferocious beast shook the hall. It was from another neutral elder, Lie Shan. He was a man of few words, but he had an explosive temper.","“Lord Lie Shan, I am not threatening you but making my stance known. Why do you think I ventured into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion alone to strike a deal with Jie Tianran? I don’t get anything out of this. I am merely driven by my loyalty to the Netherworld Sect.","“You can see for yourself whether Jie Tianran has contributed to the awakening of our sacred item. If not for him, we would have been powerless when Chu Feng tried to take control of our sacred item. The sacred item is now on the verge of awakening, but you still harbor doubt at this critical moment. You aren’t just doubting Jie Tianran but me as well,” Baili Xukong said.","“Milords, I have been wanting to say this for a while now. If you don’t trust Lord Baili Xukong, you should figure out a solution yourself!” Xiahou Jue slammed the table and stood up.","“Sit down! You have no place to speak here!” Baili Xukong unleashed his oppressive might, forcing Xiahou Jue back into his seat.","Xiahou Jue and the other members of the new faction remained displeased despite Baili Xukong’s order for them to step down. They were only loyal to Baili Xukong.","“Baili Xukong, we don’t trust Jie Tianran, but we trust you. I ask you not to overthink our concerns. It’s just that you want us to channel the Netherworld God Bestowment to ambush Chu Feng.","“The Netherworld God Bestowment is a powerful illusory formation that can be used to curb traitors, but its true purpose is to strengthen the Netherworld Embryo. It’s simply that very few people have been able to withstand its prowess. We can only channel it three more times now. It’s one thing if Chu Feng comes, but if he doesn’t, we would be squandering a chance,” Ting Yun revealed the true reason behind his hesitation.","If they truly doubted Jie Tianran, they would have already taken off the black bracelets. What they were really concerned about was the Netherworld God Bestowment.","The Netherworld God Bestowment used the Netherworld Embryo as a medium to drag an individual into an illusory formation. It was a powerful formation that practically curbed anyone who possessed a Netherworld Embryo. Furthermore, it spanned a huge area, so it was the perfect weapon to use against Chu Feng.","However, it was extremely difficult to channel. Failure could result in not just severe injuries, but loss of cultivation and even death.","The six neutral elders had once channeled it under the Netherworld Master’s guidance, but the process had been so fraught with danger that they dared not do it a second time despite having succeeded then.","It was too risky."]},{"number":6674,"title":"Chapter 6674: Chapter 6672: Ambush","paragraphs":["Chapter 6672: Ambush","“Elders, I’ll take responsibility if we fail to capture Chu Feng after channeling the Netherworld God Bestowment,” Baili Xukong said.","“Take responsibility? How do you intend to do so?” Cang Li sneered.","“You can decide how you wish to deal with me. I’ll have no complaints even if you choose to take my life,” Baili Xukong said.","Those words shocked all six neutral elders, including Cang Li, as well as the members of the conservative faction. Did Baili Xukong really trust Jie Tianran so much as to stake his life on this matter?","“Baili Xukong, you have to keep your word,” Cang Li said.","“I, Baili Xukong, am a man of my word,” Baili Xukong replied adamantly.","“Xukong, there’s no reason for us to take your life even if Chu Feng doesn’t come, but this matter concerns the Netherworld God Bestowment. Squandering it is equivalent to squandering our Netherworld Sect’s future and our Netherworld Master’s efforts. If Chu Feng doesn’t come, you’ll have to listen to us from now on,” Ting Yun said.","“I, Baili Xukong, swear to obey the six lords unconditionally if Chu Feng doesn’t come. I won’t hesitate even if you ask me to kill Jie Tianran right away then.” Baili Xukong raised his palm and made a vow.","His words cornered the six neutral elders, though they had only steered the conversation in this direction because they were already inclined to activate the Netherworld God Bestowment.","“Let’s go with this, then. We shall activate the Netherworld God Bestowment to ambush Chu Feng,”","Ting Yun looked at the other five, who nodded in agreement. The six neutral elders were aligned on this matter.","“Elders, I understand that channeling Netherworld God Bestowment is extremely dangerous, which is why I have requested Jie Tianran to craft talisman papers based on the Netherworld God Bestowment’s stringent requirements to aid you. I have inspected the talisman papers and confirmed that they are safe, so you can use them with ease of mind,” Baili Xukong said.","He took out a box and opened it. In it were eighteen talisman papers.","“Baili Xukong, you were already planning for us to activate the Netherworld God Bestowment to capture Chu Feng right from the start, weren't you?” Cang Li looked at Baili Xukong in contempt.","“Milord, I’m doing this all for the Netherworld Sect,” Baili Xukong replied.","Back when Chu Feng barged into the Undying Starfield, Baili Xukong had subtly suggested that the six neutral elders channel the Netherworld God Bestowment to capture Chu Feng. However, the six neutral elders turned down the suggestion under the pretext of it not being with them.","But how could they not bring something as valuable as the Netherworld God Bestowment with them?","Baili Xukong knew that the six neutral elders were merely afraid that failure would cost them their lives, though he didn’t point that out. In truth, the six neutral elders were indispensable to the current Netherworld Sect. Losing them would be a huge blow to the Netherworld Sect.","That was why Baili Xukong didn’t insist on the matter, instead requesting Jie Tianran to forge these talisman papers.","The six neutral elders took the talisman papers and inspected them. Upon confirming that they were effective, they breathed a sigh of relief.","“You have done well, Xukong,” Ting Yun said.","“Milord, this is all for the Netherworld Sect,” Baili Xukong replied. He was repeating his previous words, but those present could tell that he was getting at something.","With that, the meeting was dismissed.","Even though Dongfang Hansong was absent from the meeting, the members of the conservative faction dared not disobey the seven other elders. So, they followed the orders and formed a defense line around the phenomenon.","As other Netherworld Sectmembers scattered, the six neutral elders remained in the hall.","Ting Yun took out a sculpture that emanated a red aura. It resembled a humanoid monster, and it felt terrifying and imposing. It was the Netherworld God Bestowment.","Weng!","One of the talisman papers suddenly turned into energy that enveloped Lie Shan’s body.","“Why are you using it so quickly?” Ting Yun asked.","“We’re risking our lives to channel the Netherworld God Bestowment. Each of us has three talisman papers anyway; there’s no need for us to scrimp and save. We can just ask Jie Tianran for more if we finish them. You should try it as well. It feels good,” Lie Shan replied.","His words made sense, so the other five also activated a talisman paper each. Soon, a satisfied smile appeared on their faces.","Even Cang Li couldn’t help but drop a compliment, “Jie Tianran is indeed a formidable world spiritist.”","This talisman paper greatly increased their chances of successfully channeling the Netherworld God Bestowment.","Just then, Cang Li narrowed his eyes and said, “You all set off first. I’ll arrive a bit later.”","“Is Hansong back?” Ting Yun asked.","“That’s right.”","“What did you tell Hansong to do?”","“Just some private matters. Can I not reveal it first?”","“Of course. We might be close brothers, but we should still respect each other’s privacy. Tell Hansong to focus on ambushing Chu Feng and steer clear of the black bracelet. It’d be ideal if it’s just a backlash, but if Jie Tianran really tampered with the bracelets, we might end up as his puppets. One of us should at least remain to pass down the Netherworld Sect’s legacy.","“I don’t doubt Baili Xukong’s loyalty, but if I have to entrust the Netherworld Sect to someone, Hansong is a more trustworthy candidate,” Ting Yun replied.","“All right.” Cang Li nodded.","He made his way to the location he had agreed upon with Dongfang Hansong.","...","“He isn’t Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant?” Cang Li was disappointed when he heard the result from Dongfang Hansong.","“Lord Cang Li, I also wish that Chu Feng were Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant, but the result speaks for itself.”","Dongfang Hansong took out the two fused bloodline auras; they were rejecting each other, a sign that they weren’t from the same person. He had tampered with the bloodline auras, but he was so skilled that not even Cang Li could see through his deception.","“I must have been thinking too much.” Cang Li lowered his head in disappointment. He suddenly recalled something and asked, “Yun Ao’s life token has shattered. Is that true?”","“I split ways with Lord Yun Ao to search for Chu Hanxian’s possessions, but the Great Chiliocosm Upper Realm is where Chu Feng’s clan resides. The Chu Clan Alliance has stationed many experts there. Lord Yun Ao stumbled upon them and was killed,” Dongfang Hansong replied.","“How dare the Chu Clan Alliance murder a cherished elder of our Netherworld Sect?” Cang Li was infuriated. He trusted Dongfang Hansong and didn’t doubt the latter’s words. “The Chu Clan Alliance was built for Chu Feng, so he is still the culprit of it all.”"]},{"number":6675,"title":"Chapter 6675: Chapter 6673: Ancient Era’s Stele","paragraphs":["Chapter 6673: Ancient Era’s Stele","“Of course. He might be talented, but anyone who opposes the Netherworld Sect deserves death. We have just received a message from Jie Tianran that the phenomenon in the Bloodline Galaxy is related to Chu Feng. He says that Chu Feng will definitely be there, and he told us to prepare an ambush for him, no matter the cost.","“I was hoping for Chu Feng not to be there, but now, I wish he would come instead, so that I can personally avenge Yun Ao.”","Cang Li gritted his teeth in anger. He told Dongfang Hansong about the Netherworld Sect’s plan to channel the Netherworld God Bestowment.","“If Jie Tianran’s news is reliable, this would be a good opportunity to kill Chu Feng. How is the sacred item’s awakening going? How did the other lords react to my refusal to participate in the awakening of the sacred item?” Dongfang Hansong asked worriedly.","“Don’t worry. They know that you’re doing something for me, and they don’t blame you for that. Also, it’s a blessing in disguise that you didn’t participate in the awakening.”","Cang Li shared with Dongfang Hansong the concerns they had regarding the awakening of the sacred item, as well as the neutral faction’s high expectations of him.","Dongfang Hansong was delighted. “I’ll not let you down!”","...","Despite the intricate formation blueprint, Chu Feng was able to complete the formation within two hours with other world spiritists, right before entering the Nine Heavens Secret Domain.","The world spiritists present could sense how powerful the formation was, and they felt a rush of pride.","“Are we already reaching the destination?”","The world spiritists were confused.","Even though they had been focused on constructing the formation, they were aware that it hadn’t been long since they entered the teleportation formation. It was bizarre how quickly they exited the teleportation passageway.","“I’m going to show you the true form of the Nine Heavens Secret Domain,” Chu Feng said.","“The true form of the Nine Heavens Secret Domain?”","Ling Xiao’s grandfather and the others were both perplexed and excited at the same time.","Chu Feng had been reluctant to let more people know about the Nine Heavens Secret Domain, but with the opening of God’s Era and the revelation of where his clansmen and friends were, he had a feeling that he wouldn’t remain in the world of cultivation for long.","Since outsiders couldn’t enter the Nine Heavens Secret Domain anyway, he figured that there was no reason to keep it a secret. If anything, it could further reinforce the loyalty of Ling Xiao’s grandfather and the others.","As the giant warship flew into the Nine Heavens Secret Domain, the crowd saw the ancient steles and was awed. They were astounded by the Nine Heaven Secret Domain and the three steles.","The Immemorial Era’s stele was already cracked, whereas the present era’s stele only contained Chu Feng’s name. So, everyone’s gaze was fixed on the Ancient Era’s stele.","There were six names on the Ancient Era’s stele.","1: Qin Jiu","2: The name was blurred, as if the person was concealing their identity.","3: Song Shu’an","4: The name was also blurred","5: Ba Jiutian","7: Zhongli Bahuang","“Young master Chu Feng, do the names on the steles indicate the people who have grasped the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s power?” Ling Xiao’s grandfather asked.","“Yes, that should be the case.” Chu Feng nodded.","“My gosh. My gosh.” The eyes of Ling Xiao’s grandfather widened in shock.","“Elder, do you know the identities of the others on the Ancient Era’s stele?” Chu Feng asked.","“You should know Lord Qin Jiu, right?” Ling Xiao’s grandfather asked.","“I do. He is the World Spiritist Emperor, right? I have received some of his legacies,” Chu Feng replied.","“What about the Chaotic Era Scholar?”","“I know about him.”","“There are rumors that the Chaotic Era Scholar’s real name is Song Shu’an.”","“I see.”","Chu Feng was not surprised by the revelation. He had met the Chaotic Era Scholar and caught a glimpse of what the other party was capable of. The other party was truly an enigmatic expert.","“What about the others?” Chu Feng asked.","“I have never heard of the rest. I don’t think there have been any remnants or treasures regarding those people. But they must be formidable figures to have their names written on the same stele as the World Spiritist Emperor,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather replied.","“Elder, my big brother is the only one whose name is on the present era’s stele. What does that make him?” Little Fishy asked with a mischievous grin.","“Isn’t that obvious, Princess Yu’er? Young master Chu Feng is on par with those renowned figures from the Ancient Era. He is one-of-a-kind in the world!” Ling Xiao’s grandfather declared.","That prompted the others to look at Chu Feng in respect and admiration.","“Old man, how does my Brother Chu Feng compare with Jie Tianran?” Fei asked.","“Jie Tianran? He’s not worth a mention. That fellow’s head is crammed with shit,” Ling Xiao’s grandfather replied.","Everyone burst into laughter.","They were amused to see even the usually dignified Ling Xiao’s grandfather curse at Jie Tianran. This showed just how much people detested Jie Tianran.","After a brief stop, the group continued on its way. The Nine Heavens Secret Domain was a transit point to the Bloodline Galaxy. Upon entering the teleportation passageway, Chu Feng turned to the world spiritists.","“This formation serves as our final resort, but it might not be enough for us to defeat the Netherworld Sect’s rank five Heavenly Gods. So, I’ll need you to construct a concealment formation that can deceive even Heavenly Gods and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, as well as a teleportation formation if things go awry.”","Chu Feng began issuing orders to construct a concealment formation and a teleportation formation. The two formations were also intricate, but it was relatively simple for Chu Feng and the world spiritists present. They were able to complete it within two hours.","It didn’t take them long to arrive at the Bloodline Galaxy. They were still some distance away from the phenomenon, but it looked more majestic than ever now that they were in its vicinity.","“Chu Feng, the phenomenon seems to be shrinking. I don’t think it was this small before,” Long Mucheng said.","“Yes, it is shrinking,” Chu Feng replied.","The crowd exchanged uneasy looks. At this rate, the phenomenon might disappear for good. This wasn’t a good sign for them."]},{"number":6676,"title":"Chapter 6676: Chapter 6674: The Netherworld God Manifests","paragraphs":["Chapter 6674: The Netherworld God Manifests","“Is there an entrance into the phenomenon?” Long Mucheng asked.","“I don’t see one,” Chu Feng replied.","“Would it help if we went closer?” Long Mucheng asked.","“We can’t get any closer than this. I have spotted some Netherworld Sectmembers in the vicinity. They must have guessed that we would be here. They have prepared many measures to catch us. They haven’t noticed us yet due to our concealment formation, but we’ll be caught by their detection means if we get any closer,” Chu Feng replied.","“I also don’t see anything special about the phenomenon from here,” Long Mucheng said with a sigh.","“Eggy, don’t you think this phenomenon resembles an Immemorial Storage Realm?” Chu Feng asked Eggy.","Immemorial Storage Realms were spatial formations known for their security. It could only be accessed by those who knew the way to decipher it. Qing Xuantian had deposited the energy that would help the Dragon Breath Clan metamorphose inside the Immemorial Storage Realm back then.","“Shouldn’t Immemorial Storage Realms have a door? This phenomenon doesn’t have one,” Eggy replied.","She disagreed with Chu Feng’s judgment.","Chu Feng gave the matter some thought. It was just a gut feeling, and there was no way for him to verify the matter. Even if it was an Immemorial Storage Realm, he would have to find the way to decipher it before he could enter it.","Moments later, he made up his mind.","“I need to get closer to the phenomenon, but the Netherworld Sect has surrounded the area. Out of safety concerns, we can’t have too many people out here. Otherwise, the Netherworld Sect may notice us. So, I’ll need all of you to enter the formation,” Chu Feng said.","His words were the law in the Chu Clan Alliance. The crowd quickly entered the formation, including the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief and Long Mucheng.","Only two people remained by Chu Feng’s side—Little Fishy and Fei.","In the meantime, the Netherworld Sect had just completed their encirclement of the phenomenon and was beginning to reinforce their defense. The key component of their defense was the Netherworld God Bestowment, which was channeled by the six neutral elders.","The six neutral elders were gathered inside the phenomenon. A concealment formation had been constructed around them. They had channeled Jie Tianran’s talisman papers and were currently shrouded in runes.","Tapping into the talisman papers’ energy, the six neutral elders formed a series of hand seals. Soon, surges of peculiar energy flowed from their bodies and converged into the Netherworld God Bestowment at their center.","The six neutral elders suddenly jolted.","The Netherworld God Bestowment began emanating a dark red aura. It swiftly grew stronger until it enveloped all six of their bodies.","When the six neutral elders opened their eyes, their pupils had already turned dark red.","“It’s done!”","The six neutral elders breathed a sigh of relief. Channeling the Netherworld God Bestowment was highly risky, but the danger subsided once it was activated.","“These talisman papers are amazing. Jie Tianran is formidable. Let’s request him to prepare more of these talisman papers for us,” Lie Shan said.","“We can only channel the Netherworld God Bestowment two more times after this. We won’t need too many of these talisman papers,” Cang Li pointed out.","“Let’s not waste time since we have successfully activated the Netherworld God Bestowment. Activate the Netherworld God Detection,” Ting Yun ordered.","The six neutral elders change their hand seals.","Energy furiously gushed from the Netherworld God Bestowment into the surroundings. It took only an instant for it to envelop the phenomenon, but even so, it continued to expand outward.","The six neutral elders’ senses were linked to this energy through the Netherworld God Bestowment. They could keenly sense the areas where the energy enveloped, and it was a thousand times far sharper than their own senses.","It only further strengthened their faith in the Netherworld God’s indomitability and the Netherworld Sect’s future.","“Chu Feng?”","The six neutral elders’ expressions suddenly turned grim.","They had found Chu Feng—he was swiftly heading toward the phenomenon on Qin Jiu’s bamboo boat. However, he suddenly stopped the moment they sensed him.","“What’s wrong, big brother?” Little Fishy asked.","“I sensed something washing over us.”","Chu Feng immediately activated Heaven’s Eyes, but he couldn’t find anything at all. Nevertheless, he quickly made his decision. “We’ll retreat first.”","He was certain what he had just felt wasn’t just an illusion. The Netherworld Sect must have grasped a formidable power.","“Did Chu Feng sense us?” Cang Li was bewildered.","“That shouldn’t have been possible!” Lie Shan and the others were shocked.","The Netherworld God Bestowment’s energy was extremely discreet. It was unthinkable to them that anyone could even sense it.","“I don’t know how, but he has sensed us and is planning to retreat right now. We need to capture him right now and drag him into the illusory formation,” Ting Yun ordered.","The six neutral elders changed their hand seal, and a dark red light irradiated the world.","“What is that?”","Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Fei immediately noticed the dark red light.","The dark red light converged to form a terrifying silhouette that was almost as big as the phenomenon. It towered over the region like a demonic god, emanating such a powerful aura that it felt like it could obliterate everything.","“The Netherworld God has appeared. Chu Feng is here!” Baili Xukong’s face lit up in delight.","He quickly stopped what he was doing and took out an observation treasure.","“Is Chu Feng really here?”","Dongfang Hansong, who was somewhere else, also took out an observation treasure.","...","“Was that energy I felt from that silhouette?”","Chu Feng felt uneasy looking at the Netherworld God’s silhouette.","He had already channeled Qin Jiu’s bamboo boat to its maximum speed, but it was futile. It felt like the silhouette had locked onto him; there was no way he could escape.","“This feeling...”","Chu Feng’s face darkened. He sensed a stir in his Netherworld Embryo.","A dark red aura suddenly gushed from his body, but it was not his aura but the Netherworld God’s aura. It spread outward and enveloped the bamboo boat, forming a translucent dark red sphere.","The bamboo boat stopped moving altogether."]},{"number":6677,"title":"Chapter 6677: Chapter 6675: Netherworld Sect’s Sacred Realm","paragraphs":["Chapter 6675: Netherworld Sect’s Sacred Realm","Baili Xukong, Dongfang Hansong, and the others found Chu Feng via the observation treasure.","“It really is Chu Feng!”","Baili Xukong clenched his jaw, but his face was warped in joy and excitement. He was putting his future on the line when he requested the six neutral elders to channel the Netherworld God Bestowment.","What he didn’t know was that there was someone as excited as him—Dongfang Hansong.","No one desired Chu Feng’s death more than him.","Baili Xukong and Dongfang Hansong hurriedly gathered their people and rushed toward where Chu Feng was.","“It’s done.”","Lie Shan and the other neutral elders smiled.","The illusory formation had already locked onto Chu Feng and would soon drag him into its realm.","Baili Xukong and the others were already rushing over. Once they encircled Chu Feng, they would release the Netherworld God Bestowment, and they would be able to capture Chu Feng.","Only Cang Li looked conflicted. Despite having learned that Chu Feng wasn’t the Netherworld Master’s descendant, and that Dongfang Hansong had informed him that the Chu Clan Alliance had killed Yun Ao, he still felt regretful that a prodigy like Chu Feng was going to die here.","In the meantime, Chu Feng’s consciousness was dragged into the illusory formation.","“Don’t worry, Yu’er and Brother Fei. This seems to be targeted at people who possess the Netherworld Embryo, but there seems to be another use for this treasure. I might be able to overcome it,” Chu Feng said before he closed his eyes, allowing the energy to drag him into the illusory formation.","“Hold on. Something is weird. I feel like I’m being dragged into the illusory formation as well!” Lie Shan exclaimed in a panic.","“I feel the same as well.”","The other neutral elders were appalled as well.","They were the ones channeling the Netherworld God Bestowment; they shouldn’t have been dragged into it as well. But before they could figure out what was going on, their surroundings had begun to distort.","By the time they snapped out of it, they were already in the middle of a barren mountain range.","“Who are these brats?” Cang Li was taken aback.","Standing before him were no longer the five neutral elders but five children who looked to be around seven to eight years old.","“Aren’t you a child yourself?” one of the children asked.","“W-what the...”","Cang Li touched his face and was shocked by how smooth his complexion was. He was no longer an old man but a child.","Everyone was stunned. Despite their young appearances, they had mature expressions. Indeed, all of them had reverted to their younger selves.","“Something is amiss with Jie Tianran’s talisman papers. We didn’t just activate the illusory formation to take down Chu Feng. We fully activated the Netherworld God Bestowment, and that resulted in us being dragged into the sacred realm,” Ting Yun said.","“Aren’t we dead meat then?!” Lie Shan and the others were horrified.","“That doesn’t sound right. The sacred realm should be red, and the Netherworld God’s true form should be awaiting us there. This place is barren; there isn’t a single blade of grass to be seen. The sky is also blue with white clouds. This isn’t the sacred realm,” Cang Li replied.","“You’re right.” Ting Yun nodded in agreement.","But soon, the sky turned red, and the clouds took a darker shade of blood red. Even the barren mountain range looked blood red.","“We are... really in the sacred realm...”","The six neutral elders felt their hearts clenching up.","“Oh no. I feel my Netherworld Embryo stirring. It is the Netherworld God’s summon! We are really in the sacred realm! How did we get in here? We’re doomed! What should we do? Do we really have to challenge the Netherworld God?”","Lie Shan, despite being the largest child in the group, panicked. His face reflected his horror.","“We’ll die if we don’t challenge it,” Cang Li said, though his face was also marked with despair.","The Netherworld God Bestowment was rarely invoked because the chosen individual would be dragged into the sacred realm to challenge the Netherworld God. The challenge required one to withstand ten strikes from the Netherworld God, but thus far, no one had succeeded.","There had been many challengers in the Netherworld Sect’s history, and in the past, their sect used to have treasures that could be used alongside the Netherworld God Bestowment to see what was happening inside the sacred realm from the outside.","It was through these observation treasures that they knew how difficult it was to overcome the Netherworld God’s trial.","None of the challengers survived a single blow.","Barely after the Netherworld god raised his hand, the challengers were crushed by the sheer pressure of his falling strike.","“In the sacred realm, our ages are determined by the strength of our Netherworld Embryos. Despite our advanced ages, we still regressed into seven, eight-year-old children. This shows just how weak our Netherworld Embryos are. How can we challenge the Netherworld God in this condition? We’ll be obliterated by his fart!” Lie Shan exclaimed.","“Our talent and compatibility with the Netherworld Embryo have never been top-notch. We wouldn’t have attained our current level of strength if not for Lord Netherworld Master,” Cang Li remarked with a sigh.","Even the usually calm Ting Yun couldn’t help but grumble, “Baili Xukong has really put us in a spot this time.”","Boom!","Powerful oppressive might suddenly descended from the sky, causing the six neutral elders’ breathing to hasten. At the same time, the blood-red color in the sky deepened.","“Oh no. The sky is starting to change colors. The trial begins the moment the sky turns black. That’s the moment we are all going to die here!” Lie Shan cried.","“The darker the sky, the more intense the oppressive might. We don’t have our cultivation here; we’re only barely stronger than mortals due to our Netherworld Embryos. At this rate, we’ll be crushed by the oppressive might before the trial begins,” Cang Li said.","A cry of agony echoed.","Lie Shan kneeled on the ground, kowtowing and wailing, “Lord Netherworld Master, your unfilial subordinate will have to leave before meeting you!”","It was a ridiculous sight, but three other neutral elders followed suit and began kowtowing, too.","“Lord Netherworld Master, your servant misses you, but I was blind and allowed myself to be deceived by that dog thing, Baili Xukong!”","“Lord Netherworld Master, your servant is dying to witness your current grandeur in person, but I fear that I’ll never have a chance to do so!”","Their words and emotions were sincere.","“Enough.” Cang Li kicked Lie Shan and said, “It’s not over yet. There is a good chance that we can survive this ordeal.”","But the four kneeling elders didn’t believe him.","“You don’t need to deceive us. If even our elders can’t do it, how can we withstand Lord Netherworld God’s ten blows?” Lie Shan didn’t believe it.","“It is beyond us, but someone else might just pull it off,” Cang Li replied.","“Who?” Lie Shan asked.","Ting Yun exclaimed in astonishment,” Ah!”","The other three elders also thought of something and shot to their feet.","“Chu Feng!”"]},{"number":6678,"title":"Chapter 6678: Chapter 6676: The Elder’s Tear","paragraphs":["Chapter 6676: The Elder’s Tear","“Right! Chu Feng is here as well. We targeted him, so the Netherworld God Bestowment must have dragged him into the sacred realm as well. Our Netherworld Embryos are not be strong enough, but he might be able to pull it off!” Lie Shan shot to his feet in excitement.","“Who else can I possibly be talking about?” Cang Li rolled his eyes.","The neutral elders were already accustomed to Lie Shan’s slow-wittedness.","“We need to quickly find Chu Feng and inform him about the Netherworld God Bestowment so that he can challenge the Netherworld God!” Lie Shan said.","“How do you intend to find him? We don’t have our cultivation here. We can’t even sense him,” Cang Li scoffed.","“Ah? What can we do?” Lie Shan groaned.","“Chu Feng isn’t that dumb. I’m sure he can find the Netherworld God through the summoning,” Cang Lu replied.","“What should we do then?” Lie Shan asked.","“We’ll head there as well,” Ting Yun replied.","So, the six neutral elders followed their Netherworld Embryos’ guidance and began making their way toward the Netherworld God.","Their weak Netherworld Embryos had led to their weak bodies in the sacred realm, so their movement speeds were many times slower than usual. However, they had descended at a place that was already in proximity to the Netherworld God.","After trudging across several mountains, they arrived at an empty plain.","They had lost their cultivation, but their eyes remained sharp, and there were no obstacles hindering their vision. They were able to quickly lock onto the powerful entity standing in the middle of the plain.","It was the Netherworld God!","The Netherworld God was nowhere as towering as the humongous silhouette outside—he was only a hundred meters in height, and his body was made of an aura—but his might felt more tangible and fearsome.","He felt like the dominator of this world.","Thus, the six neutral elders fell to their knees and greeted the Netherworld God, “Paying respect to the Netherworld God.”","“Look, it’s Chu Feng!” Lie Shan pointed at another mountain.","A small figure was descending from another mountain. It was indeed Chu Feng.","“How weird. Why does Chu Feng look no different from usual?” Lie Shan exclaimed in surprise.","“That means that Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo is strong, or rather, he has almost perfect compatibility with it,” Ting Yun replied.","“Heavens! Doesn’t that make him the first person whose age didn’t regress after entering the sacred realm?” Lie Shan exclaimed.","“Indeed.” Cang Li nodded.","“Chu Feng is truly monstrously talented,” Ting Yun remarked.","“Hold on. Look at his hand. He’s holding a token,” Lie Shan shouted.","The other neutral elders took a closer look and saw a blood-red token in Chu Feng’s grasp, but they were too far away to decipher the words on it.","As Chu Feng stepped into the plain, the token began emanating a blood-red aura.","“Shit! I get it now!” Lie Shan spat.","“What did you get?” Cang Li asked.","“How is it that Chu Feng has that token when none of us do? That token obviously has something to do with the Netherworld God. I can only think of one explanation for this. The Netherworld Sect Bestowment was fully activated not because of Jie Tianran’s talisman papers or a mistake on our part.","“It is Chu Feng! He was the one who fully activated the Netherworld God Bestowment! That is why he received that token, whereas the rest of us didn’t!” Lie Shan exclaimed.","The other five neutral elders fell silent.","The Netherworld Sect had no records about that token, but Lie Shan’s explanation made sense.","“You’re being sharp-witted for once,” Cang Li remarked.","Lie Shan was on the mark about the token.","When the Netherworld God Bestowment locked onto Chu Feng and dragged him into the illusory formation, Chu Feng sensed grave danger, but at the same time, he also realized that there was a method to overcome the danger.","It only took him moments to figure out the method, and that was to completely activate the Netherworld God Bestowment.","He knew nothing about this place beforehand, but the token he received upon entering the illusory formation provided him with thorough knowledge about it.","He learned that the treasure that had locked onto him was the Netherworld God Bestowment, that he was currently in the Netherworld Sect’s sacred realm, and the method to overcome this trial.","Due to the sacred realm limiting his cultivation, Chu Feng didn’t sense the six neutral elders hiding on top of a mountain. He made his way straight toward the Netherworld God.","As he approached the Netherworld God, the latter noticed him as well.","The moment the Netherworld God turned to look at him, his token disintegrated into a wisp of aura. At the same time, a blood-red formation manifested from beneath the Netherworld God’s feet and swiftly expanded until Chu Feng was caught inside it as well.","Under the formation’s influence, Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo manifested as an aura entity that was over ten meters tall. Astonishingly, the Netherworld Embryo was identical to Chu Feng.","“His Netherworld Embryo looks exactly like him! It means he is perfectly compatible with it!” Lie Shan’s lower jaw fell agape.","The other neutral elders didn’t utter a word, but their hearts were shaken.","Just then, a huge amount of energy began converging before the Netherworld God to form a sphere of red aura. The Netherworld God was about to make a move.","At the same time, the oppressive might crushing the surroundings intensified.","If Chu Feng hadn’t been protected by his Netherworld Embryo, there was no way his current body could have withstood the oppressive might.","“This is the move that the previous challengers of our Netherworld Sect have all succumbed to,” Lie Shan murmured.","Boom!","Right after he said those words, the sphere of red aura gushed toward Chu Feng, enveloping the surroundings with red light.","The red light only lasted for an instant before receding. Everything reverted to its previous state.","The six neutral elders lost their composure.","Chu Feng remained unharmed despite the previous attack. On top of that, his Netherworld Embryo had grown even larger to twenty meters.","“This is ridiculous! Not only did he withstand the attack, but he’s unharmed?” Lie Shan exclaimed.","Meanwhile, the Netherworld God continued its attack. It didn’t take long for it to dish out nine attacks, and Chu Feng withstood all of them.","Chu Feng remained perfectly composed. He wasn’t worried about failing the trial at all.","However, the six neutral elders were completely astounded.","By the time Chu Feng withstood the ninth attack, his Netherworld Embryo had already expanded to over a hundred meters tall, making it as big as the Netherworld God. While there were still some discrepancies in terms of form and might, they were the same size now.","Each attack from the Netherworld God was stronger than the previous, but Chu Feng continued to emerge unscathed from each hit. This showed just how resilient he was.","“Lie Shan, why are you crying?” Cang Li suddenly asked.","Only then did the other neutral elders notice the tears and snot on Lie Shan’s face.","“I just feel regretful. Chu Feng is a gift from heaven to our Netherworld Sect, but why does his heart not lie with us? Why does he have to be our enemy?”","The other five neutral elders fell silent. They felt the same way."]},{"number":6679,"title":"Chapter 6679: Chapter 6677: He Drank the Strongest Move","paragraphs":["Chapter 6677: He Drank the Strongest Move","“Do you think Chu Feng will be willing to join our Netherworld Sect if we promise to help him deal with Jie Tianran?” Ting Yun suddenly asked.","You want to turn against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to recruit Chu Feng? Betraying our ally will sully our reputation, but again, what does the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion count as if it means having Chu Feng as an ally?","In the first place, reputation meant nothing to them. The Netherworld Sect had never enjoyed a good reputation.","“If Chu Feng joins us, I’ll make sure to destroy Jie Tianran. I have never seen such a dastardly grandfather. I have been wanting to pick a beef with him for a long time now.” Lie Shan rolled up his sleeves, indicating that he was ready to stand up for Chu Feng at any moment.","However, his gesture only looked amusing because of his childlike frame.","“It’ll be tough.” Cang Li shook his head. “There’s already a lot of bad blood between us. Given his personality, it won’t be easy to convince him.”","“We have to give it a try. When has the road ever been easy for our Netherworld Sect? We have faced hardships in strengthening the Netherworld Embryo. We have also faced hardships in awakening the sacred item. But we have never backed down in the face of adversity,” Lie Shan spoke excitedly, as if fearing that Cang Li would oppose his suggestion.","Cang Li glared at Lie Shan. “I’m more afraid of Chu Feng agreeing to join us.”","“Old Cang, isn’t that good news? What are you afraid of?” Lie Shan was confused.","“Can you guarantee that Chu Feng sincerely wants to join us, and that he’s not just using us to deal with Jie Tianran, just so that he can turn his back on us later on?” Cang Li asked.","The other neutral elders fell silent. None of them could guarantee that.","“We can’t forget that Baili Xukong has sided with Jie Tianran, and that there is a grudge between his son and Chu Feng. He won’t permit Chu Feng to join the Netherworld Sect. With Chu Feng’s caliber, it’s only a matter of time before we have to lower our heads to him. The six of us might be willing to do so, but what about Baili Xukong and his underlings?” Cang Li asked.","As much as he admired Chu Feng, he still had to consider how pragmatic the matter was and prioritize the Netherworld Sect’s interest.","“I’ll deal with Baili Xukong if he refuses to accept the matter. He says that he prioritizes the Netherworld Sect over all things; what could be more important than recruiting Chu Feng to the Netherworld Sect then? As for your concerns about Chu Feng’s trustworthiness, none of us can make any guarantees, but at the very least, Chu Feng has forged a good reputation for himself. He should at least be more reliable than Jie Tianran,” Lie Shan replied.","“Chu Feng cares deeply about his friends, but he is also known to be unscrupulous when dealing with his enemies. Do you think he sees us as a friend or an enemy now?” Cang Li asked.","“Isn’t it obvious that we’re enemies to him? We wouldn’t be worrying about this if he were an ally. This is a problem.” Lie Shan scratched his head in frustration. All of a sudden, he turned to the Netherworld God and exclaimed, “Eh? Why did Lord Netherworld God scatter?”","The other neutral elders had also noticed the same thing. The Netherworld God’s body had dissipated as a red aura.","“No, it’s not that Lord Netherworld God is scattering. His power is fusing into the sacred realm,” Ting Yun replied.","His judgment was right.","Huge swathes of blood-red clouds gathered in the sky, and a humongous silhouette could be vaguely seen reflected amid them. It was the Netherworld God, but he appeared far stronger than before.","This Netherworld God’s silhouette converged into a giant pillar of red light that descended from the sky toward Chu Feng’s body.","The six neutral elders clenched their fists out of nervousness. They could tell that this was a cataclysmic attack, but somehow, Chu Feng calmly raised his head and faced the pillar of red light without dodging.","Something even more shocking happened after.","Chu Feng opened his mouth, and so did his Netherworld Embryo.","The pillar of red light slammed into the plains, causing the ground to crack, but Chu Feng alone remained unharmed. Its energy flowed ceaselessly into his Netherworld Embryo’s mouth like an endless fountain of power.","“Heavens! He drank Lord Netherworld God’s strongest attack?”","Lie Shan was dumbfounded. The pillar of red light was still gushing, but he could already tell that it was only a matter of time before Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo took in all that energy, no matter how huge it was.","“That darned Baili Xukong. He turned a prodigy of this caliber into our enemy over that dimwit son of his,” Lie Shan cursed.","“Maybe it’s heaven’s will. The inheritor we have been searching for just had to be our biggest enemy,” Ting Yun lamented.","“Actually, there is one thing I have been withholding from you. I didn’t send Dongfang Hansong to deal with my private affairs. Rather, it concerns Lord Netherworld Master,” Cang Li said.","“Lord Netherworld Master? What is it?”","The other neutral elders immediately turned to look at Cang Li. They were the most loyal subordinates of the Netherworld Master. To them, there was no news more important than that concerning the Netherworld Master.","“After everything that has happened, I wondered if Chu Feng was Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant,” Cang Li said.","The other five neutral elders’ mouths fell agape.","Chu Feng was talented, but they had never associated him with the Netherworld Master.","Cang Li elaborated on the basis of his suspicion. The other five neutral elders narrowed their eyes in agitation. Their hands trembled nonstop, and cold sweat trickled down their backs.","“Y-y-you’re saying that Chu Feng...” Lie Shan was so agitated that he couldn’t even finish his sentence. He could only stare at Cang Li intently.","“Unfortunately, Chu Feng isn’t Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant,” Cang Li revealed.","“Shit!” Lie Shan smashed his fist into the ground.","The others also let out sighs like deflated balloons. They felt like their anticipation had culminated in disappointment.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo had taken in all the energy from the red light, causing it to grow into a behemoth of over ten thousand meters in height. The aura it emanated reached a terrifying level.","The Netherworld God had vanished. Chu Feng was now the ruler of the sacred realm.","“Amazing. He withstood Lord Netherworld God’s ten attacks,” Cang Li remarked.","“Above all, he overcame that insurmountable trial as easily as drinking water,” Lie Shan added.","Unease and despair seeped into their eyes.","Chu Feng was looking in their direction right now. It was obvious that his gaze was locked on them.","“You are the ones who dragged me into this realm, right?”"]},{"number":6680,"title":"Chapter 6680: Chapter 6678: The Rescuer","paragraphs":["Chapter 6678: The Rescuer","The six neutral elders turned pale from fright.","Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo had replaced the Netherworld God as the ruler of this realm. He might have noticed them because of how tall his Netherworld Embryo was, but it could also be that he had truly grasped full control over this realm.","If it were the latter, they were doomed.","Many thoughts flashed across the minds of the neutral elders, but none of them dared respond right away to Chu Feng’s question. There was a long pause before Cang Li finally replied, “Yes, it’s us.”","They could have chosen not to acknowledge it and hide their identities, but their pride wouldn’t allow them to do so. They thought that this would spell their deaths.","To their surprise, Chu Feng’s icy demeanor faded, and he said, “I didn’t have a grudge with the Netherworld Sect. It was Baili Xukong who kept pushing me. I heard that the Netherworld Sect’s neutral elders are rational people; I didn’t expect you to side with Baili Xukong against me. Even so, I’ll spare your life this once on the account that I have a good impression of Elder Cang Li.","“I hope that you can think it through who your true enemy is—me, Chu Feng, or Jie Tianran. However, you should know that this will be the last time I’ll show mercy. I am not in the habit of sparing those who are after my life.”","With that, the surroundings began to warp.","The six neutral elders were transported back to their bodies.","The trial had ended. They had survived.","However, they looked toward Chu Feng with turbulent feelings. The energy from the Netherworld God Bestowment had begun to fade, but his group was already surrounded by Netherworld Sectmembers.","Baili Xukong stood just a short distance away from Chu Feng, ready to make a move as soon as the Netherworld God Bestowment dissipated.","Things were going according to plan. The six neutral elders should have been celebrating their victory. However, their minds were a mess.","Chu Feng’s earlier attitude had shaken them. He could have killed them, but he spared them. This left them feeling conscience-stricken, and they felt like they were the worst scumbags in the world.","“I don’t know what the rest of you think, but I won’t let Chu Feng die. If your opinions differ from mine, I ask you to bind me right now. Otherwise, I’ll stop Baili Xukong if he lays his hands on Chu Feng,” Cang Li informed the other five neutral elders via voice transmission.","“I agree! Chu Feng cannot die. At most, we’ll capture him alive. He could have dealt with us there and then, but he spared our lives. I cannot turn a blind eye to that,” Lie Shan declared.","“Capture Chu Feng alive!” a voice echoed across space.","It was Ting Yun. He had relayed an order to the entire Netherworld Sect.","“Capture Chu Feng alive?” Baili Xukong was flabbergasted by the abrupt command.","“Milord.”","Baili Xukong’s underlings turned to him. They only obeyed Baili Xukong’s orders.","“I don’t know what those old things are planning, but Chu Feng carries many invaluable treasures, be it his Ruler’s Bloodline or the legendary Genesis Bloodline. His Netherworld Embryo is extraordinary as well. It might just be of great use to us. It’ll be best if we can capture him alive. Otherwise, kill him on the spot,” Baili Xukong ordered.","What Baili Xukong didn’t know was that the six neutral elders had come to a consensus regarding their stance toward Chu Feng. They had concealed their figures and had begun heading toward Chu Feng.","They wouldn’t stop Baili Xukong from dealing with Chu Feng, but they wouldn’t allow him to kill Chu Feng. If anyone attempted to take Chu Feng’s life, they would intervene right away.","Little did the six neutral elders know that Chu Feng was merely putting on a strong front earlier.","Chu Feng had only noticed them in the sacred realm because his Netherworld Embryo had grown so large that it towered above the mountains, granting him unblocked vision. It was also a guess on his part that those children were the Netherworld Sect’s neutral elders.","Similarly, he didn’t spare the neutral elders out of the kindness of his heart. In truth, he didn’t have the strength to kill them.","When he heard Ting Yun’s shout to capture him alive, he quickly surveyed the reactions of the Netherworld Sectmembers, and he immediately knew that his earlier deception had worked out. That order must have come from the neutral elders.","Even if he failed to escape today, he would at least be spared.","That said, Chu Feng wasn’t about to go down without a fight. He secretly took out the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit given to him by the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief. He secretly channeled it, but the treasure continued to resist him.","Seeing that the Netherworld God Bestowment’s energy was about to fully dissipate, he slowly lost his confidence.","A sealing formation had hindered the teleportation formation they had constructed, so they had no way to escape the encirclement. It would be tough for Little Fishy and Fei to fend against the Netherworld Sect’s experts by themselves.","Just then, Chu Feng noticed a tenacious glint in Little Fishy’s eyes, and his heart clenched up. He hurriedly said, “Yu’er, the Netherworld Sectmembers will obey the order from their neutral elder. They won’t go as far as to take our lives. I still have the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit in hand. I’m still trying to activate it right now, but it might work at any moment. So, you don’t need to put your life on the line.”","He knew that Little Fishy had tricks up her sleeves, and the chances were that not even Baili Xukong could stop her once she ran amok. However, employing such means would potentially cost her life.","Boom!","Deafening explosions suddenly echoed from afar.","Chu Feng looked over and saw blood-red sword rays wreaking havoc in the surroundings. Countless Netherworld Sectmembers died in a matter of moments.","Unlike the Netherworld Sect’s Netherworld Embryo, the blood-red sword rays didn’t feel malevolent. If anything, it felt righteous and even beautiful.","“That is...”","Chu Feng was immediately reminded of the phenomenon a while back that shook the entire world of cultivation—a blood lotus that enveloped an entire starfield.","“It’s Zi Ling!” Eggy exclaimed.","The surroundings were shrouded in a blood-red aura, but Chu Feng could still clearly see her. She was a gorgeous beauty, but her face was frigid, and her eyes flared with murderous intent.","She was Zi Ling."]},{"number":6681,"title":"Chapter 6681: Chapter 6679: Zi Ling’s Might","paragraphs":["Chapter 6679: Zi Ling’s Might","Brandishing her God Armament, Zi Ling sliced through the Netherworld Sectmembers with ease like an indomitable war goddess. No one could stop her.","Her cultivation had grown much stronger than before.","“It’s another rank five Heavenly God, and she’s gorgeous as well! Chu Feng, is she from your Chu Clan Alliance as well? Just how many experts do you have in your ranks?!” Fei exclaimed in astonishment.","Despite being a distance away, he could still feel Zi Ling’s incredible strength. Above all, he also saw Zi Ling’s beautiful face. He couldn’t help but gulp down his saliva.","“That’s my big brother’s lover, big sister Zi Ling,” Little Fishy hurriedly reminded, fearing that Fei would say something disrespectful out of ignorance.","“Zi Ling? I have heard about her. She’s a disciple from the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, right? Chu Feng met her in the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm. I didn’t know she’s this beautiful. Chu Feng, I must say that you have great luck with women!” Fei smacked Chu Feng’s shoulder.","“You know big sister Zi Ling?” Little Fishy was taken aback.","“Who doesn’t know about her? Practically everyone in the Ancestral Martial Galaxy knows about Chu Feng’s relationship with Zi Ling!” Fei replied.","“That’s true.” Little Fishy nodded in agreement.","Most of what she knew about Chu Feng and Zi Ling was from hearsay. Those things were not secrets; those who were curious about Chu Feng’s past could easily acquire this information just by asking around in the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm.","While Little Fishy and Fei were conversing, Chu Feng’s attention was focused on Zi Ling.","He could tell that Zi Ling’s base cultivation was not at rank five Heavenly God level; she should be at rank two Heavenly God level. She was enveloped in three layers of blood-red auras, with each layer presumably raising her cultivation by a rank.","“Yet another fearless one. Milord, I’ll deal with her,” Xiahou Jue said.","He raised his cultivation to rank five Heavenly God level before leading his troops to surround Zi Ling, attacking her from all directions.","Zi Ling appeared to have sensed their movements. Her body abruptly vanished, leaving just a lingering blood-red aura in her wake.","While the crowd was figuring out what was going on, a blood-red aura suddenly erupted from Chu Feng’s bamboo boat. The Netherworld God Bestowment’s energy had yet to fully dissipate, but the blood-red aura simply shrouded it as well.","Then, Zi Ling appeared on the bamboo boat. The blood-red aura surrounding her naturally manifested in the form of lotuses. There were also blood-red lotus imprints on her forehead and her eyes.","Her cultivation had further risen to rank six Heavenly God level.","“Big brother Chu Feng, did I arrive on time?” Zi Ling asked.","It was also then that the Netherworld God Bestowment’s energy finally fully dissipated. Had she been a second later, Chu Feng would have been in danger of being captured.","“How did you know I was here, Zi Ling?” Chu Feng asked.","“I saw this phenomenon shortly after I came out of closed-door training. I noticed that it was identical to the painting you once showed me. I thought that you would be here, so I came here to look for you,” Zi Ling replied via voice transmission.","She was being discreet because she knew what this phenomenon meant to Chu Feng, and that it would be unwise for others to know about it.","“Be careful, Zi Ling. It’ll be best if we can retreat from here. The Netherworld Sect has multiple people who can raise their cultivation to rank six Heavenly God level,” Chu Feng said.","“All right.” Zi Ling nodded.","Boom!","A powerful burst of martial power suddenly gushed toward Chu Feng. It was from Baili Xukong.","As Chu Feng had expected, Baili Xukong was able to raise his cultivation to rank six Heavenly God.","However, Zi Ling was prepared for this. She swung her sword and sliced Baili Xukong’s attack in half. “Big brother Chu Feng, I’ll bring you all to safety!”","She began charging out of the encirclement while pulling the bamboo boat with her using her blood-red aura.","“Activate the formation!” Baili Xukong shouted.","The Netherworld Sectmembers immediately formed hand seals.","The surrounding space began to warp, and the Netherworld Sectmembers seemed to vanish. The world turned reddish-purple, and miserable wails filled the air. It was as if they had been transported into hell.","Space suddenly shattered, and the earth collapsed. Several humongous mouths appeared out of nowhere. Dark-red auras gushed out from those mouths.","“Zi Ling, this must be a martial power illusion formation from the Netherworld Sect. Such formations typically don’t have formation cores, but they can absorb martial skills. You should be able to breach it by unleashing your most powerful strike without using any martial skills,” Chu Feng said.","Zi Ling did as she was told and swung her God Armament.","Clang!","The space reverberated.","A powerful sword aura gushed out, but it failed to pierce through the dark-red aura. It looked like the attack had been devoured by the world.","“What’s going on? I didn’t use any martial skill.” Zi Ling was confused.","The dark-red aura encroached on her, and her body began to rot. Bizarre wounds appeared on her body.","Zi Ling frowned.","“Chu Feng, let me out to help Zi Ling,” Eggy urged.","“There’s no need for that. She should be able to overcome it on her own,” Chu Feng replied, knowing that Eggy would have to sacrifice her life for that.","However, he meant his words. Zi Ling was likely able to deal with the current situation.","Chu Feng formed a hand seal. The formation constructed by the Chu Clan Alliance emanated a brilliant golden light as it poured a flood of martial power into Zi Ling’s body. “Zi Ling, accept the formation’s energy.”","He noticed that Zi Ling’s fighting prowess had gone down significantly when raising her cultivation from rank five to rank six Heavenly God, thus putting her at a huge disadvantage when dealing with the Netherworld Sect’s formation.","But as long as her fighting prowess was raised, she should be able to stand her ground.","Buffed by the Chu Clan Alliance’s formation, Zi Ling’s blood-red aura lotuses emanated a golden gleam, and her fighting prowess soared.","Seeing that the dark-red aura was encroaching on her once more, she swung her sword without any hesitation.","Her blade wielded unstoppable might, slicing through everything that stood in its path, be it the dark red aura and this bizarre realm. The bizarre realm dissipated, and the Netherworld Sect’s army reappeared before their lines of sight.","“She broke through our formation?” Baili Xukong’s expression turned grim as he pulled out his God Armament saber."]},{"number":6682,"title":"Chapter 6682: Chapter 6680: Another Ling","paragraphs":["Chapter 6680: Another Ling","Boom!","A blinding golden light erupted with a deafening explosion. Baili Xukong had unleashed a rank three God Taboo Martial Skill.","Zi Ling casually swung her sword.","Another loud explosion followed. Her red sword ray had sliced through the golden light, causing it to dissipate into the surroundings.","But that was not all to Baili Xukong’s attack. Tens of thousands of golden ferocious beasts roared from all around Zi Ling before attacking her at the same time.","In response, Zi Ling swung her sword once more, unleashing sword rays in all directions.","The golden ferocious beasts were instantly sliced apart.","Baili Xukong unleashed attack after attack, but Zi Ling neutralized all of them with ease.","Chu Feng noticed that the surrounding Netherworld Sectmembers had stopped their offense after Zi Ling revealed her prowess as a rank six Heavenly God. They retreated a distance away and channeled their Netherworld Embryos into a formation to strengthen Baili Xukong.","It was only thanks to the formation that Baili Xukong was able to keep up with Zi Ling.","“Chu Feng, your wife is incredible! There’s no need for me and Miss Yu’er to make a move at all!” Fei exclaimed. He was awed by Zi Ling’s formidable prowess.","“We won’t be of any help even if we make a move,” Little Fishy said. “Big brother, big sister Zi Ling is so strong.”","“Indeed.” Chu Feng nodded.","It should have been beyond him to discern the clashes between two rank six Heavenly Gods, but due to Zi Ling’s slower attacks and her powerful sword rays, he could still barely follow her movements.","Due to that, he could tell that she wasn’t just executing a simple martial skill but profound swordsmanship that was aligned with her current powers. There was no doubt that it was from the blood-red ancient tower.","“You are strong, but do you think I am the only expert in the Netherworld Sect?” Baili Xukong sneered.","The six neutral elders frowned. They could tell that Baili Xukong was urging them to make a move, albeit in a subtle manner. Zi Ling was strong, but not even five of her would be enough to deal with the six of them.","For that reason, they couldn’t make a move.","Cang Li and the other neutral elders turned to Ting Yun, their de facto leader.","Ting Yun informed them via voice transmission, “I just told Baili Xukong via voice transmission that a mishap happened while we were channeling the Netherworld God Bestowment. Chu Feng took control of the Netherworld God Bestowment and turned the treasure against us, so we aren’t in a good position to make a move right now. Make sure to align our words.”","Cang Li and the others were delighted to hear that. It was the perfect excuse, and it was not exactly a lie since Chu Feng did take control of the Netherworld God Bestowment and dragged them into the sacred realm.","They were merely distorting the truth a little.","“Baili Xukong doesn’t seem very happy about the situation,” Cang Li remarked.","Baili Xukong looked visibly frustrated due to the six neutral elders’ reluctance to join the battle.","“It can’t be helped since we’re injured. Let’s see if he dares say anything. I’ll wallop him!” Lie Shan scoffed indignantly as if he was really injured.","“Not even the lord of heaven can save Chu Feng today!”","Just then, a silver light surged over. Another expert had joined the battle.","It was Dongfang Hansong. He was wielding a God Armament and enveloped in his Netherworld Embryo’s aura. His cultivation had risen to rank six Heavenly God level.","“Dongfang Hansong? Why is he helping Baili Xukong?” Lie Shan and the others were confused.","Dongfang Hansong and Baili Xukong’s relationship had grown so cold that they wouldn’t join forces even when faced with a major enemy. Such a situation had happened before.","“This is bad. He must be seeking vengeance for Yun Ao!” Cang Li’s face darkened.","“Let’s just tell Dongfang Hansong what happened in the Netherworld God Bestowment, and that he should just let this matter go,” Lie Shan said.","This matter was of grave importance; Cang Li couldn’t make the call. Instead, he turned to Ting Yun.","“Go ahead, Cang Li,” Ting Yun said.","Cang Li quickly informed Dongfang Hansong about what happened in the Netherworld God Bestowment via voice transmission.","“Hurry up! That lass won’t last long at this rate,” Lie Shan exclaimed.","Zi Ling was slowly being pushed to a corner under the combined prowess of Baili Xukong and Dongfang Hansong.","“I have already told him, but Dongfang Hansong thinks that whether we’re bringing Chu Feng under our fold or executing him, we should first capture him. He insists on assisting Baili Xukong in capturing Chu Feng,” Cang Li replied.","“I guess there’s no other choice.”","The other neutral elders thought that Dongfang Hansong’s words made sense.","Little did they know that Dongfang Hansong had other intentions in mind.","The neutral elders had previously ordered for Chu Feng to be captured alive, and Dongfang Hansong had no intention to offend them. However, when he heard Cang Li’s words, he became convinced that he couldn’t let Chu Feng live.","Even if he were to be punished, he had to strike Chu Feng down.","Under the combined prowess of Dongfang Hansong and Baili Xukong, Zi Ling was cornered.","Chu Feng was worried.","Gah!","Just then, the Netherworld Sectmembers wailed in agony. Another person had arrived at the scene. It was yet another rank six Heavenly God.","Taking a closer look, it was also a familiar face—Feng Ling!","She wore a white cloak, and her body emanated a white light along with a faint grassy fragrance. Her demeanor, disposition, and halo made her seem like a fairy descending from heaven.","Even though she was brutally massacring the Netherworld Sectmembers, she remained pristine. But the moment she spoke, her disposition changed.","“Come at me, you shameless things!"]},{"number":6683,"title":"Chapter 6683: Chapter 6681: Being a Little Sister","paragraphs":["Chapter 6681: Being a Little Sister","Feng Ling was vicious. If left be, she might murder all of the Netherworld Generals and Netherworld Envoys present. This put the neutral elders in a spot. They didn’t wish such bloodshed to befall the Netherworld Sect.","But they had already claimed injury earlier. They would be putting themselves in a spot if they intervened now.","“You’re courting death!” Baili Xukong roared as he charged at Feng Ling.","“Hmph!” Feng Ling also charged at Baili Xukong with her God Armament in hand.","Feng Ling’s base cultivation was higher than Zi Ling’s—she was at rank three Heavenly God level. Her fighting prowess was formidable; she could stand her ground against Baili Xukong even though he had been buffed by the Netherworld Sect’s formation.","Her entrance lifted some pressure from Zi Ling’s shoulders, since she only had to deal with Dongfang Hansong now. While it was unlikely that she could defeat Dongfang Hansong, she had at least regained her footing for the time being.","“Zi Ling, you need to breach their sealing formation so that we can activate our teleportation formation to escape from here,” Chu Feng told her via voice transmission.","“Tell me what to do,” Zi Ling replied.","They quickly settled on a plan.","On the surface, it looked like Zi Ling struggled to stand her ground, and she had to flee all around to avoid Dongfang Hansong’s attacks. In truth, she was secretly releasing martial power shockwaves to damage the sealing formation.","To quicken the process, Chu Feng also sent a voice transmission to Feng Ling, and she aided in the process as well.","Once the sealing formation was almost destroyed, both Zi Ling and Feng Ling made their ways back to Chu Feng’s bamboo boat.","They had been so discreet in their destruction that both Baili Xukong and Dongfang Hansong didn’t notice what Zi Ling and Feng Ling had done. Instead, they thought that they were on the verge of defeating their respective opponents. They didn’t notice anything amiss at all.","It wasn't until a powerful surge of teleportation energy rushed out that Baili Xukong and Dongfang Hansong finally realized that things had gone awry.","“No! They are trying to escape via a teleportation formation!” Dongfang Hansong exclaimed.","He formed a hand seal with his left hand. His eyes turned glaringly blood red, and his fighting prowess surged. His spear became much more forceful and faster than before, tearing through not just the surrounding space but the teleportation energy as well.","“Hmph!”","Zi Ling, who had been retreating all this while, harrumphed.","With a simple swing of her sword, she unleashed a blood-red sword ray that neutralized Dongfang Hansong’s powerful attack.","Dongfang Hansong could only watch helplessly as Chu Feng and the others disappeared.","“Damn it!”","Baili Xukong was so angry that his face was completely distorted. It was only now that he realized that they had never claimed the upper hand. Instead, they were played as fools by Zi Ling and Feng Ling.","“It must be Chu Feng’s idea. He is too cunning!” Dongfang Hansong said.","Dongfang Hansong and Baili Xukong might not be world spiritists, but they were still powerful cultivators. Under normal circumstances, they would have noticed something amiss if someone were breaching their sealing formation.","Someone must have been giving Feng Ling and Zi Ling pointers regarding the destruction of the sealing formation, and the only one capable of that feat here was Chu Feng.","“How foolish must you be not to notice a thing when someone is breaching your formation?” Baili Xukong cursed.","Dongfang Hansong was dumbstruck. But you didn’t notice anything, either.","But on second thought, that was just the kind of person Baili Xukong was. The latter wouldn’t change his mind about Dongfang Hansong just because they had worked together to deal with Chu Feng once.","Had it been in the past, Dongfang Hansong might have retorted against Baili Xukong, but this time, he sent a telepathic message to the latter instead. “Baili Xukong, let’s have a talk later. I need to talk to you about the Netherworld Sect’s future.”","Baili Xukong was taken aback. He took a good look at Dongfang Hansong before leaving without saying a word.","Dongfang Hansong frowned. It would be tough for him to execute his plan without Baili Xukong’s help.","“Follow me,” Baili Xukong told him via voice transmission.","A smile emerged on Dongfang Hansong’s lips.","...","A far distance away, teleportation energy converged to form a spirit formation gate.","Qin Jiu’s bamboo boat flew out from the spirit formation gate. Riding on the bamboo boat were Chu Feng, Little Fishy, Fei, Zi Ling, and Feng Ling.","The group had briefly gotten to know one another while traveling through the teleportation passageway.","“Haha! What a coincidence. I came here to exact vengeance against the Netherworld Sect. I didn’t expect to bump into you here!” Feng Ling said with a hearty laugh.","She seemed to be in a good mood after having massacred some Netherworld Sectmembers.","“You sure are bold. The Netherworld Sect is nowhere as simple as it appears. You are brave to charge in there all alone,” Chu Feng said.","“What about it? They couldn’t stop us from leaving. Speaking of which, your wife is impressive. How is she able to raise her cultivation from rank two to rank six Heavenly God? Chu Feng, you are blessed with good romance luck,” Feng Ling complimented.","“That goes without saying,” Chu Feng replied gleefully.","“Little sister Zi Ling, you don’t mind me addressing you like that, right?” Despite Feng Ling’s sweet voice, her words were brash.","“Of course.” Zi Ling nodded.","“Oh my oh my! What a sweet lady you are. Can I call you big sister?” Feng Ling asked.","“Sure.” Zi Ling nodded once more.","“Are you sure?” Feng Ling asked with a mischievous grin.","“Yes, I am sure,” Zi Ling replied. She hadn’t figured out what Feng Ling was getting at yet.","“What I mean is that I’m going to marry Chu Feng as well, but since you got married to him earlier than I did, it’s only right for me to call you big sister.” Feng Ling looked at Zi Ling with a mischievous smile, as if waiting for the latter to be rendered speechless.","But Zi Ling simply smiled. She turned to Chu Feng and said, “You’ll have to ask my big brother Chu Feng first. I have no qualms if he agrees.”","Not only was Feng Ling rendered speechless, but the cheery Little Fishy lost her smile as well.","Feng Ling noticed Little Fishy’s reaction, and that sparked an idea. She ran up to Little Fishy and asked, “What’s wrong, little Yu’er. Why do you look like that? Do you want to be Zi Ling’s little sister as well?”","To her surprise, Little Fishy didn’t look embarrassed in the least. Instead, she replied with a brilliant smile, “You should direct that question to my big brother. If he’s willing, I have no qualms with it.”","“Very well. Chu Feng, pull Li Wu out from the formation realm right now. I’ll ask her if she’s willing to marry you as well, so that we, sisters, can stay together,” Feng Ling said.","“Hey! You’re getting overboard. Miss Li Wu belongs to my brother, Bai Yunqing,” Chu Feng hurriedly interjected. He was worried that Feng Ling would go on to involve Long Muxi and the others in this at this rate."]},{"number":6684,"title":"Chapter 6684: Chapter 6682: The Origin of the Brightmoon Spirit Tower","paragraphs":["Chapter 6682: The Origin of the Brightmoon Spirit Tower","“You are so excited about your breakthrough to Heavenly God level that you lost your restraint,” Chu Feng remarked.","“What do you mean by that? Can’t I use a joke to speak my mind? Little Yu’er, it looks like we aren’t worthy of your big brother’s notice.” Feng Ling put on an indignant face as she hugged Little Fishy.","Little Fishy simply smiled without responding. She unconditionally stood on Chu Feng’s side. There was no way she would speak up against Chu Feng, even as a joke.","Zi Ling also knew that Feng Ling was joking, so she wasn’t bothered by it.","Only Chu Feng felt his head hurt.","Just then, Fei said, “Miss Feng Ling, it might not be convenient for Brother Chu Feng, but I...”","“What about you?” Feng Ling asked.","“I’m single,” Fei replied.","“Yes, I can see that. What about it?”","“Well... what do you think about...”","“Ah, my head suddenly feels giddy. Let’s end this conversation here. I feel nauseated when I hear words that I don’t like.”","“Miss Feng Ling, you...” Fei was frustrated. He looked at Chu Feng with pitiful eyes and asked, “Brother Chu, can I take you as my master?”","“Huh?” Chu Feng was confused.","“I... want to get a partner as well,” Fei replied.","“I’m not good with such stuff.”","“You’re not good with such stuff?” Fei glanced at the three incredible beauties—Zi Ling, Feng Ling, and Little Fishy.","“Yes, I’m not good with such stuff, but I know a brother who might be able to help you. Why don’t I ask him to teach you when we meet?” Chu Feng whispered.","“Who is it?” Fei asked.","“His name is Wang Qiang.”","“It’s a deal then.”","“Yes, it’s a deal.”","The mood was much lighter now that they were out of danger. Even so, Chu Feng continued channeling the bamboo boat with his full strength.","He had confirmed that the Netherworld Sect couldn’t do anything about the phenomenon, though that was true for him as well. If he continued investigating the phenomenon, he would only be putting his allies in unnecessary danger.","So, he decided to first venture into God’s Era and acquire its final power.","Zi Ling lowered her guard toward Little Fishy and Feng Ling after learning that they were Chu Feng’s close friends, so she didn’t mind sharing confidential information like her cultivation with them.","Zi Ling’s swift growth was due to her obtaining the acknowledgment of the woman on the ancient tower’s first floor.","She had also established communication with the woman on the second floor, who was also a powerful expert. If she could obtain the latter’s acknowledgment, she would be able to maintain her fighting prowess even when raising her cultivation by four ranks.","On top of that, she had uncovered the true name of the ancient tower—the Brightmoon Spirit Tower.","“The Brightmoon Spirit Tower?” Feng Ling was so taken aback that she shot to her feet. She stared intently at Zi Ling with widened eyes.","“Little sister Zi Ling, are you sure the tower inside you is the Brightmoon Spirit Tower?” Feng Ling sought confirmation.","“Yes, it is.” Zi Ling nodded.","“Feng Ling, you know about the Brightmoon Spirit Tower?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course! That is the tower my master personally constructed for her little sister, Lord Mingyue!”","Feng Ling’s words piqued the curiosity of Chu Feng, Zi Ling, Little Fishy, and Fei.","“Who is your master?” Fei asked.","“Li Wu and I have existed since the Ancient Era, but our memories have been affected. We have forgotten many things, and we don’t know how true our remaining memories are. Li Wu has recovered better than I. Chu Feng, you should let her out and ask her,” Feng Ling said.","The bamboo boat was small, but it had no trouble housing a few more people. So, Chu Feng called Li Wu and Bai Yunqing out of the formation realm.","As the formation realm was isolated from the real world, Feng Ling told Li Wu that the Brightmoon Spirit Tower was currently inside Zi Ling’s body.","“You have the Brightmoon Spirit Tower? How did you get it? Who gave it to you?” Li Wu’s tone was harsh. She was practically interrogating Zi Ling. Unlike Feng Ling, she seemed displeased and even angry about the fact that Zi Ling had the Brightmoon Spirit Tower.","“Calm down, big sister. Little sister Zi Ling is Chu Feng’s wife. You shouldn’t talk to her like that,” Feng Ling advised.","“Our master constructed the Brightmoon Spirit Tower for Lord Mingyue. After Lord Mingyue passed away, our master sealed the tower away in her tomb. The reappearance of the Brightmoon Spirit Tower means that someone has dug Lord Mingyue’s tomb. How can I not be angry about that?” Li Wu spat.","Chu Feng’s heart clenched up.","Eggy sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng, “Oh no. Your father must have dug their Lord Mingyue’s tomb. No wonder she’s so angry. You’d be upset too if someone dug your family member’s tomb. Why don’t you consider severing your relationship with your father, lest they turn against you when they learn that your father is a tomb raider?”","She was gloating at Chu Feng’s dilemma.","Chu Feng had arrived at the same conclusion as well.","“Calm down, big sister. Have you forgotten that the Brightmoon Spirit Tower was not buried together with Lord Mingyue. To avoid disturbances to Lord Mingyue, her body was buried elsewhere. Besides, I remember our master mentioning that anyone who successfully breaches the seal is qualified to obtain the Brightmoon Spirit Tower,” Feng Ling reminded.","“You’re right. I got too agitated because it was something relating to our master and Lord Mingyue. My apologies, Miss Zi Ling.” Li Wu snapped out of her daze, bowed to Zi Ling, and apologized.","“It’s fine. I understand where you’re coming from. I received the Brightmoon Spirit Tower from my master—it isn’t my master in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect, but someone else. He prefers to maintain a low profile and doesn’t want anyone to know his whereabouts, so it’s inconvenient for me to divulge his name. I seek your pardon on that matter,” Zi Ling replied.","She wisely chose to conceal Chu Xuanyuan’s identity upon sensing that the Brightmoon Spirit Tower’s master was extremely important to Feng Ling and Li Wu.","“Miss Zi Ling, is your master very strong?” Li Wu asked.","“Yes, he is very strong.” Zi Ling nodded."]},{"number":6685,"title":"Chapter 6685: Chapter 6683: Bloodslaughter Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6683: Bloodslaughter Emperor","“Your master could have been the one who breached my master’s seal,” Li Wu said.","“Your master must be extremely powerful if that’s the case. You should have brought your master here, Zi Ling. With his help, we’ll be able to easily quash the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion like measly ants,” Feng Ling said.","“My master doesn’t involve himself with such matters,” Zi Ling replied.","“I see. He intends to leave you to your own devices. He must be very confident in you,” Feng Ling said.","Eggy chuckled from the World Spirit Space. “That guy is more than happy to leave his son in the lurch, let alone his daughter-in-law.”","“Feng Ling, is it convenient for you to reveal who your master is?” Chu Feng asked.","Li Wu revealed a troubled look.","“You don’t have to speak if it’s not convenient,” Chu Feng added.","“There’s nothing inconvenient about that. There are hardly any records about my master left anyway. My master is extremely powerful. My memories are incomplete, but I remember that even the Ancient Era’s powerhouses are afraid of her. Some call my master the Blood Emperor, whereas others call her the Bloodslaughter Emperor.","“You should be able to hear more about my master once you enter the Ninth Galaxy, but at present, I’m afraid I don’t remember too much about her. I only know that people feared her back in the Ancient Era,” Feng Ling said.","“My memories are about the same,” Li Wu replied.","“I heard that in the Ancient Era, the strongest humans were called ‘Emperors’, whereas the strongest monstrous beasts were called ‘Saints’. No wonder you two are so extraordinary. With such a master, there is no way you could have been normal,” Fei said.","“Not bad! You might be ugly, but you are quite knowledgeable,” Feng Ling complimented.","“Wow. Thanks a lot.” Fei rolled his eyes.","“I had guessed that Miss Li Wu was from a distinguished background, but I didn’t expect it to be at this level.” Bai Yunqing was awed. He was happy for her, but at the same time, it also eroded some of his self-confidence.","Chu Feng noticed that Bai Yunqing was feeling unconfident.","In truth, Bai Yunqing was also of considerable stature. He was already a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, but he was nowhere near his limit yet. He had inherited incredible legacies and harnessed the potential to become someone great in the future.","But that was how humans were. Love could make someone extremely small, though it could also make someone shine brighter than the sun. Those who failed to attain love tended to lack confidence.","Chu Feng wanted to say some words to console him, but Li Wu beat him to it.","“Those aren’t important. If anything, I’m happier to have met friends who share the same path, such as us,” Li Wu said with a smile.","“Miss Li Wu is right,” Chu Feng voiced his agreement.","“Indeed. Having a formidable background can inspire respect, but it doesn’t necessarily bring about sincerity. I’d rather have trustworthy friends than a formidable background,” Little Fishy said.","The crowd agreed with those words. Bai Yunqing’s smile didn’t look as strained anymore.","“Do you still remember anything about the Brightmoon Spirit Tower?” Chu Feng asked.","This concerned Zi Ling’s future, after all.","“I do. Three formidable natural oddities are sealed in the tower, and they have been further enhanced by my master. Little sister Zi Ling, you should know since you have attained some of their powers. They can easily crush the entire world of cultivation. They can obliterate the nonsense known as the Netherworld Sect and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion with just a snap of their fingers,” Feng Ling said.","“Yes, the two elders are unfathomably strong,” Zi Ling said.","“The Brightmoon Spirit Tower was meant to have five levels. Li Wu and I were meant to be sealed in it as well, but we take longer to reach maturity, and Lord Mingyue couldn’t wait any longer, so it was changed to three levels. However, we still failed to make it in time,” Feng Ling said.","“Have you met the three elders? Do you have any information about them?” Chu Feng asked.","“No, I have never met them, and I don’t have information about them. That’s all we know about the Brightmoon Spirit Tower. Chu Feng, I know you’re hoping to get more information from us to help little sister Zi Ling, but even Lord Mingyue had to conquer the tower by herself. Little sister Zi Ling has to earn their recognition to obtain their powers,” Feng Ling said.","“I see.” Chu Feng nodded.","In any case, the ancient tower inside Zi Ling’s tower was stronger than he had expected. This was a good thing.","While Chu Feng’s group was making its way toward God’s Era, the Netherworld Sect reinforced its encirclement of the phenomenon.","The six neutral elders and Dongfang Hansong were gathered in a palace to discuss how they could convince Chu Feng to join their Netherworld Sect. Cang Li and the others even proposed helping Chu Feng deal with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion if he joined them.","“Milords, these are the pills I have just concocted. Your Netherworld Embryos must be depleted after channeling the Netherworld God Bestowment. You should recuperate.”","Dongfang Hansong presented six pills to the neutral elders.","Cang Li and the others took the pill and swallowed it straight.","Channeling the Netherworld God Bestowment didn’t weaken them by much, but it did exhaust their Netherworld Embros. They had consumed Dongfang Hansong’s pills before—he had been occasionally giving them pills, and they were indeed rare tonics.","“Hansong, what are your thoughts?” Ting Yun asked.","“I agree with your view. Chu Feng is a rare talent. Losing him will be a huge loss to our Netherworld Sect. It’ll also be more reliable to have him awaken our sacred item—he has already proven his skills in dealing with the sacred item, and he has received the Netherworld God Bestowment on top of that.","“The only problem is that Chu Feng harbors animosity toward our Netherworld Sect. It’s a good thing that he values his ties, and our sect’s Chen Hui is on good terms with him. He kidnapped Chen Hui that day but returned him safely afterward. This shows that Chu Feng sees Chen Hui as a friend. There could be room for negotiation if we let Chen Hui talk to Chu Feng on our behalf,” Dongfang Hansong said.","The eyes of the six neutral elders lit up.","“That’s a good idea, Hansong. Chu Feng is a sentimental man. I doubt he’ll lie to Chen Hui if he thinks of the latter as a friend.” Lie Shan clapped in excitement,","“That’s right.” Cang Li and the others nodded with smiles.","They thought that it was a good idea to discuss this matter with Dongfang Hansong."]},{"number":6686,"title":"Chapter 6686: Chapter 6684: Traitors of the Sect","paragraphs":["Chapter 6684: Traitors of the Sect","“Six lords, Baili Xukong seeks an audience,” Baili Xukong’s voice suddenly echoed outside.","“Let him in,” Ting Yun said.","The six neutral elders slumped on their seats, feigning weakness.","The door opened, and Baili Xukong stepped in.","“Milords, my request for you to channel the Netherworld God Bestowment has resulted in your weakness. I’m apologetic for that. I have prepared some divine water for my breakthrough, but it should be useful for your injuries,” Baili Xukong said as he presented six exquisite jade bottles.","“At least you have a heart!” Lie Shan took the jade bottle and inspected its contents. Only after confirming that there was nothing amiss with it did he finally gulp it down.","The other five observed Lie Shan’s reaction before doing the same.","“Baili Xukong, you crossed blows with those two women. What is your evaluation of them?” Cang Li asked.","“They are very powerful, but they are only able to stand their ground because of your injuries. Otherwise, they wouldn’t stand a chance at all,” Baili Xukong said.","“Have you thought about how astonishingly fast they have grown, where they could only flee in our presence before, but now they can stand on equal footing with us? Are you confident that we can deal with them the next time we meet?” Cang Li asked.","“That’s why we have to awaken the sacred item as soon as possible. They won’t pose any threat to us once we acquire the sacred item’s power,” Baili Xukong replied.","“Are you that certain that the sacred item’s power will allow us to rival those juniors’ talents?” Cang Li asked.","“What do you mean by that, Lord Cang Li? Do you lack faith in our Netherworld Sect? Do you think that we can’t rival the so-called Chu Clan Alliance, even with the sacred item’s power?” Baili Xukong questioned.","“We don’t know how potent the sacred item’s power is, but we have witnessed what Chu Feng and his friends are capable of. We all know how difficult it is to raise our cultivation at Heavenly God level. If not for our Netherworld Embryos and Netherworld Master’s means, we wouldn’t even have been able to raise our cultivation.","“But look at those women. They easily raised their cultivation at Heavenly God level, and their talent is presumed to be inferior to Chu Feng’s. If Chu Feng were to reach Heavenly God level, I don’t know if our Netherworld Sect can stop him,” Ting Yun remarked.","Baili Xukong had been frustrated at Cang Li for a while now, but he still harbored respect for Ting Yun. He was surprised to hear such words coming from the latter. He realized that Ting Yun had begun siding with Cang Li now.","“Lord Ting Yun, do all of you mean to reconcile with Chu Feng?” Baili Xukong asked.","“What Chu Feng has done is understandable. For the Netherworld Sect’s future, it is more beneficial for us to befriend Chu Feng than to continue being enemies with him,” Ting Yun replied.","“I see.” Baili Xukong smiled bitterly.","Without any hesitation, he thrust his palm toward Ting Yun.","Ting Yun waved his sleeves and stopped the attack with ease.","Seeing that, Lie Shan, Cang Li, and the others stood up and exerted their oppressive might.","“Milords, you were really feigning injury? I see, I see.” Baili Xukong gritted his teeth in resentment.","The six neutral elders belatedly realized that they had given their act away in their fit of anger.","“Chu Feng is an outsider. Why do you insist on siding with him? Is it just because he is talented? He has crossed our Netherworld Sect and infringed on our bottom line on many occasions. Have you forgotten about that? Yet, you want to recruit him into our Netherworld Sect. Have your heads become rotten?!","“I have respected you all this while, but you completely ignored the Netherworld Sect’s safety and obstinately insisted on bringing our enemy in. How can you face Lord Netherworld Master?” Bailu Xukong grew more agitated as he spoke, eventually reaching a point where he shouted.","Cang Li and the others turned to Dongfang Hansong. There was no way Baili Xukong would know about their intention unless Dongfang Hansong told him.","“Milords, please don’t blame me. I have no choice but to take a stance for the Netherworld Sect. Chu Feng mustn’t be allowed to join the Netherworld Sect. He... has to die.”","Right after saying those words, Dongfang Hansong formed a hand seal. Baili Xukong formed the same hand seal as well.","Blood red aura seeped from the two of them and spread outward, swiftly forming a massive formation.","“The Netherworld Embryo Siphoning Formation?”","Cang Li and the others were infuriated. This formation sought to siphon their power away. Dongfang Hansong and Baili Xukong were looking to kill them!","Just as they were about to fight back, they felt their energies going into disarray, to the point where they thought their bodies might explode. They collapsed to the ground, unable to muster any strength.","“You... poisoned us?” Ting Yun pointed his finger at Dongfang Hansong.","They had inspected Baili Xukong’s divine water—there was no poison in it. This meant that the poison was in Dongfang Hansong’s pills.","“Milords, how can we be a match for you without pulling some tricks? I was reluctant to do this in view of our past ties, but I have to do it for the Netherworld Sect. Your decisions will lead our Netherworld Sect to its doom. You are the Netherworld Sect’s traitors! I can’t allow you to have your way. We shall inherit your strength and bring the Netherworld Sect to a greater height!”","Dongfang Hansong changed his hand seal. The six neutral elders’ faces distorted, and their bodies began to warp.","Martial power, along with their Netherworld Embryos’ auras, gushed from them and flowed into Baili Xukong and Dongfang Hansong’s bodies.","“Dongfang Hansong, we only wanted to discuss with you. Why...” Cang Li lay weakly on the ground, his eyes reflecting hatred and confusion.","Dongfang Hansong could have voiced his disagreement to their decision. They had never insisted on recruiting Chu Feng into their Netherworld Sect.","He didn’t expect Dongfang Hansong to be so vicious as to go after their lives, especially when they had been comrades for countless years now.","Under the formation, Cang Li and the others swiftly lost their cultivation and passed out.","“Traitors of the Netherworld Sect deserve to be executed.”","Baili Xukong drew his God Armament saber."]},{"number":6687,"title":"Chapter 6687: Chapter 6685: Rivalry in God’s Era","paragraphs":["Chapter 6685: Rivalry in God’s Era","“Forget it,” Dongfang Hansong intervened. “They are no longer able to resist. Let’s spare their lives. They don’t have long to live anyway.”","“What useless compassion,” Baili Xukong sneered as he retracted his saber.","He lifted his hand, and two black bracelets floated toward Dongfang Hansong. “Even though you saved the Netherworld Sect by tipping me off about their intention to work with Chu Feng, I still don’t trust you. I can only trust you if you work with me to awaken the sacred item.”","Dongfang Hansong smiled. He put the two black bracelets on his wrists and said, “Let’s go.”","He opened the door.","Those standing outside were all Baili Xukong’s and Dongfang Hansong’s aides. They could see the pitiful plights that had befallen the six neutral elders, but none of them were surprised.","After all, they had aided in the channeling of the Netherworld Embryo Siphoning Formation and even absorbed a small portion of the six neutral elders’ powers.","Dongfang Hansong made his way toward the sacred item, and Baili Xukong followed him.","When they reached their destination, Dongfang Hansong channeled the two black bracelets to aid in the awakening of the sacred item, resulting in him taking on a portion of the sacred item’s backlash power.","“Do you trust me now? My values might diverge from yours, but my heart is with the Netherworld Sect,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“How do you think Chu Feng should be dealt with?” Baili Xukong asked.","“Chu Feng has to die, but before that, we should exploit his full value,” Dongfang Hansong replied.","“How so?”","“Those six might be foolish, but we shouldn’t deceive ourselves. The fact that Chu Feng obtained the Netherworld God Bestowment’s acknowledgment proves that he has near-perfect compatibility with his Netherworld Embryo. He will be of great help in the awakening of the sacred item.","“We can inform Jie Tianran of this matter and have him construct a formation to make use of Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo in the awakening of our sacred item before killing him. If you think it’s feasible, I’ll leave it to you to communicate with Jie Tianran. You two should have a way to reach each other, right?” Dongfang Hansong asked.","Baili Xukong pondered for a moment before replying, “Leave it to me.”","...","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran, by using all his means without any regard for the cost, reached God’s Era first.","He had gathered all members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to construct a defensive encirclement around God’s Era to ambush Chu Feng, but he soon realized that it would be hard to do so.","Chu Feng’s sword key allowed him to enter any one of the God’s Era’s three gates as long as he was within a certain distance of it. The distance was so big that it was impractical to seal off the entire area.","The ambush might work if Chu Feng was simply teleported to an area near God’s Era when leaving it, but there was no guarantee about that.","“Aren’t you going to enter, Jie Tianran?” the old entity inside Jie Tianran’s body asked.","“Let me observe a while longer,” Jie Tianran said.","He was not observing the God’s Era’s three gates but the Bloodline Galaxy’s phenomenon.","His observation formation allowed him to see across galaxies, but he could only see brief outlines of what was going on. He saw the Netherworld God’s silhouette in the Netherworld God Bestowment, as well as ripples of martial power, but he couldn’t see Chu Feng at all.","From that, he deduced that Chu Feng had gone to the phenomenon. The phenomenon was indeed Chu Feng’s weakness, perhaps concealing a huge secret of his. However, he couldn’t tell if the Netherworld Sect had successfully taken Chu Feng down.","After all his failed attempts, he couldn’t help but worry.","He was no longer confident of defeating Chu Feng if the latter competed with him in God’s Era.","“Didn’t you give Baili Xukong a communication talisman paper? He knows that you are concerned about this matter, so he should update you on whether they were successful in catching Chu Feng or not. You don’t need to keep an eye there. You are too far away to do anything about it anyway,” the old entity said.","“But I might not be able to receive Baili Xukong’s message once I enter God’s Era,” Jie Tianran said.","All of a sudden, he reached into his robe and took out a talisman paper. Spirit power rippled on the surface of the talisman paper, and soon, words appeared on it. It was a message from Baili Xukong.","“That useless thing. How can they let Chu Feng escape from their clutches despite having the upper hand?” Jie Tianran was infuriated.","The message confirmed that Chu Feng was there but had gotten away.","But soon, his anger morphed into shock and unease. He learned that Chu Feng had gained two allies capable of raising their cultivation to rank six Heavenly God level.","On top of that, the Netherworld Sect’s six neutral elders had discovered Chu Feng’s potential and wanted to help him deal with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Fortunately, Baili Xukong had already crippled them and grew stronger as a result. He also proposed using Chu Feng to awaken the sacred item.","But overall, the message was still bad news for Jie Tianran.","“This isn’t good. It’s as if the Chu Clan Alliance has obtained God’s Era’s power. How are they growing so swiftly? This is ridiculous!","“It’s already ludicrous that Xianhai Yu’er is able to rival rank five Heavenly Gods as a rank one Heavenly God, but he now has rank six Heavenly Gods on his side as well. At this rate, it won’t be long before he has rank seven Heavenly Gods.","“I don’t think you’ll be able to deal with him if he has rank seven Heavenly Gods, right?” Jie Tianran asked the old entity.","The moment the Chu Clan Alliance had a rank seven Heavenly God, they would be as good as fish on the chopping board.","“Jie Tianran, if you lack confidence, you can give up on God’s Era’s power and go into hiding. Once I complete my formation, they won’t pose any threat to us even if one of them reaches rank seven Heavenly God,” the old entity said.","“Elder, how long will your formation take? Can you give me a timeline?” Jie Tianran asked.","“It should be soon, but I can’t give you an exact time,” the old entity replied.","“Elder, even though we have your formation as a backup plan, I can’t just let God’s Era’s final power fall into someone else’s hand. I have to go in there.”","Jie Tianran quickly made up his mind. He first issued some orders to his people before responding to Baili Xukong’s message. Then, he took out the sword key.","“Chu Feng, God’s Era’s final power is right before us. May the better one win.”","He activated the sword key.","Energy pulsated from the sword key and enveloped his body. He transformed into a surge of light that whizzed toward one of the God’s Era’s three gates."]},{"number":6688,"title":"Chapter 6688: Chapter 6686: Chu Feng Arrives on the Scene, Reactions From All Parties","paragraphs":["Chapter 6686: Chu Feng Arrives on the Scene, Reactions From All Parties","Chu Feng continued to observe two locations while rushing ahead—one was the Bloodline Galaxy’s phenomenon, whereas the other was God’s Era.","“What an extraordinary light,” Fei remarked as he looked at the comet.","Even though they were still a far distance away from God’s Era, the comet that Jie Tianran had morphed into was so brilliant that they could see it clearly through an observation formation.","“It’s related to God’s Era. That should be Jie Tianran,” Chu Feng replied.","“He chose the third gate. He’s quite conservative,” Little Fishy said.","Chu Feng took out his sword key and inspected it.","“What’s wrong, big brother Chu?” Zi Ling asked.","“I’m trying to see if I can enter God’s Era discreetly. If I morph into a brilliant comet like Jie Tianran did, they will be able to lock onto the location where I enter from even if I do it from somewhere further away,” Chu Feng said.","“What’s wrong with that?” Fei asked.","“I’m worried that I might be transported back to the same place when leaving God’s Era. If the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and the Netherworld Sect harbor the same suspicion, they will send their people to camp in the area where I set off from,” Chu Feng replied.","“I’ll beat them up if they dare come!” Feng Ling spat.","“It is one thing if it’s just the Netherworld Sect, but I’m worried that Jie Tianran might emerge from God’s Era ahead of me and ambush you. You shouldn’t come with me. Let’s set another location for us to meet up at. I’ll look for you after I come out,” Chu Feng said.","“That won’t do. It’s too dangerous,” Zi Ling and Little Fishy said in unison.","“It’s fine. Have you forgotten about this?” Chu Feng took out the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit.","“Big brother, I thought you weren't able to use that?” Little Fishy asked.","“I am able to use it now, just that I don’t want to use it unless necessary. The treasure is sentient, and its prowess weakens when more people are in its protection. It’ll be safer for me to go alone,” Chu Feng said.","“Are you certain, big brother?” Little Fishy narrowed her eyes in skepticism.","“Of course,” Chu Feng replied confidently.","“Whoever lies is a dog,” Zi Ling added.","“...” Chu Feng was rendered speechless. He was lying. He just didn’t want Zi Ling and Little Fishy to brave danger with him. Nevertheless, he still nodded, “Yes, whoever lies is a dog.”","“Fine, I’ll do as you say,” Zi Ling said.","Chu Feng passed to Zi Ling the formation where most members of the Chu Clan Alliance currently dwelled in, so that they could tap into the formation to protect themselves if they met with danger.","Then, Zi Ling and the others made their way to the location Chu Feng told them to wait at.","With that, Chu Feng was the only one left on the bamboo boat. His silhouette looked forlorn when contrasted against the vastness of space.","“You’re alone now, dog,” Eggy suddenly said.","“Why are you scolding me?” Chu Feng chuckled.","He might have felt lonely if he were truly alone, but with Eggy’s company, he didn’t feel lonely no matter where he went.","“You lied. You can’t channel the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit, can you?” Eggy asked.","“Nothing escapes Milady Queen’s notice.”","“Stop the bootlicking. The situation isn’t looking good. Your friends and clansmen have finally appeared. They might be safe in the phenomenon for the time being, but who knows when the phenomenon will open?","“Zi Ling and Feng Ling might have made huge advancements in their cultivation, but they are still no match for the Netherworld Sect. That bastard grandfather of yours also isn’t an easy foe to deal with.","“The Divine Deer hasn’t recovered its power yet, and you can’t channel the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit. That darned qilin pig has been deeply sleeping since forever. Haa, I doubt that it’ll be of any use even if it wakes up.","“There’s no other choice now. We have to obtain God’s Era’s final power to turn the tables around. Let’s set off now, Chu Feng, lest we miss the initiative. I’m also curious to know what lies inside that enigmatic God’s Era after all the commotion it has stirred,” Eggy said.","“Let’s go.”","Chu Feng steered the bamboo boat toward God’s Era.","When he reached a certain radius of God’s Era, his sword key began to react. It was much further than where Jie Tianran was before his sword key reacted.","So, Chu Feng stowed away the bamboo boat and channeled the sword key.","Energy enveloped Chu Feng. He morphed into a comet that whizzed toward God’s Era. The light he emanated was even brighter than that of Jie Tianran’s, and it immediately caught the attention of the crowd.","“Chu Feng is here. He actually chose the second gate. Is he that confident?”","Those from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were worried. From the brightness of their comets, it was evident that Chu Feng held the upper hand.","Little Fishy, Zi Ling, and the others continued to keep an eye on God’s Era even as they made their way toward the location marked by Chu Feng.","“Chu Feng...”","“Big brother...”","Zi Ling and Little Fishy were worried as well, though they were worried about Chu Feng’s safety.","...","In the Nine Souls Galaxy, a figure carrying an axe gazed at God’s Era. His usually casual gaze carried a hint of concern and anticipation today.","“This day has finally come. Chu Feng, no one in history has ever obtained God’s Era’s final power. I hope you achieve what no one before you has ever had.”","...","In the Bloodline Galaxy, Dongfang Hansong was observing God’s Era via an observation formation in his dark palace.","“Lord Netherworld Master’s descendant is truly impressive,” he remarked with a conflicted expression.","The door suddenly opened, and Chen Hui walked in.","“Paying respect to Lord Netherworld Marshal.” Chen Hui bowed respectfully.","“Enter the pool, Chen Hui,” Dongfang Hansong said as he glanced at the pool in the room.","The pool was filled with blood-red fluid that billowed furiously while emanating a strong but sinister aura.","“Yes, milord,” Chen Hui followed the order without questioning much.","He rarely met Dongfang Hansong, but the latter had been taking care of him. Whenever they met in private, Dongfang Hansong would always give him something good. This time wouldn’t be an exception, either."]},{"number":6689,"title":"Chapter 6689: Chapter 6687: The Throne at the Top","paragraphs":["Chapter 6687: The Throne at the Top","“The hell...”","The moment Chen Hui put a leg into the blood pool, his expression distorted, and he leaped out with a yelp. His leg was now covered in injuries, with fresh blood seeping from it.","Rather than a cultivation pool, it felt more like a man-eating monster!","“This pool will metamorphose your body. If you can’t even take this much, how can I entrust the conservative faction’s future to you?” Dongfang Hansong looked at Chen Hui in disappointment.","His words stabbed into Chen Hui’s heart like sharp daggers.","So, Chen Hui clenched his jaws and stepped into the blood pool once more. The moment he came into contact with it, his face distorted once more, and his complexion quickly turned pale.","It was so excruciating that he could die, but he stopped himself from letting out even a squeak as if to prove his masculinity.","While his mouth was stubborn, his body was more honest. Tears were already flowing from his eyes.","Soon, the pool began smelling like blood. Chen Hui’s flesh had melted into the pool.","“Try your best to relax and accept the energy. That will hasten the reforging of your body,” Dongfang Hansong said while averting his gaze. He couldn’t bear to see Chen Hui’s current state. “You can shout if you want to. It’s not embarrassing.”","“I-I can hold on,” Chen Hui said.","He regretted those words right away, for he was unable to hold on.","The more he relaxed, the more painful it became. Soon, a primal shout echoed endlessly in the hall. Those who didn’t know better would have thought that two apes were up to something.","Dongfang Hansong’s heart clenched, but he stopped himself from doing anything. He knew that this tempering would determine Chen Hui’s future, and that the latter had to succeed. To distract himself, he turned his attention to God’s Era’s formation.","“Hm?” Dongfang Hansong narrowed his eyes.","He saw Chu Feng approach God’s Era’s second gate and enter it.","...","Chu Feng was surprised by what he saw after entering the gate.","Instead of being transported into vast space, he found himself in a small room.","At the center of the room was a blank stone monument, and a brush was placed beside the monument. Other than these, there was nothing else in the room.","“Chu Feng, are we in the right place? This room is smaller than a pigsty.” Eggy frowned.","“This should be God’s Era, based on what I know,” Chu Feng replied.","“Are you sure? What’s the deal with the stone monument and the brush? Are you supposed to write your name on it to mark your arrival, or is there something more to it?”","“I think there is something more to it.”","Chu Feng observed the stone monument and the brush. Soon, his eyes lit up.","“I get it now, Eggy. There is something hidden in this room. We have to decipher it and write it on the stone monument,” Chu Feng said as he continued scanning the room.","But the surrounding walls were completely bare. He couldn’t discern anything even through Heaven’s Eyes. So, he closed his eyes instead to perceive with his heart. Soon, he grasped something.","“Found it.”","“What is it?” Eggy asked anxiously.","Instead of answering her question, Chu Feng walked up to the stone monument, picked up the brush, and wrote down a word—’Bloodline’.","“Bloodline?” Eggy murmured as she watched with curious eyes.","Before she could ask anything, the ‘Bloodline’ word emanated a brilliant light that swiftly enveloped the room. It was so bright that Chu Feng struggled to see the word he had just written on the stone monument despite standing right in front of it.","Chu Feng suddenly felt a gust of cold wind tugging at his clothes. It would appear that he had been transported from the indoors to the outdoors.","Soon, the light receded.","Indeed, Chu Feng had been transported to a peculiar realm, where the ground was a humongous lump of flat metal. This realm was barren, resulting in the wind being exceptionally strong. It was also for the same reason that one could see to the horizons of the realm.","Beyond the horizons of the realm, God’s Era’s silhouette glowed with a sacred light.","Chu Feng seemed to be inside God’s Era, so he could see what was happening to it as well.","“You’re right, Chu Feng. I can see now that we are inside God’s Era.” Eggy exhaled in relief. She followed Chu Feng’s gaze and began observing the realm as well. “Chu Feng, the metal beneath your feet seems to be a metal for conducting electricity.”","“Yes, but that isn’t all. It seems to harness other powers.”","Chu Feng observed that the humongous metal ground had been inscribed with runes, just that the runes were so huge that they spanned tens of thousands of meters in length. Normal people would have thought that they were patterns instead of runes.","Just then, he looked toward space.","Something was happening to God’s Era.","A ray of light extended from the top of the second gate toward the head of God’s Era’s silhouette, forming a flight of stairs that connected the two. At the same time, the silhouette also began to transform.","The silhouette’s head accessory, which was previously incorporeal, slowly turned tangible, forming a three-sided golden altar. The altar was simple in design, but it looked domineering.","An item was placed on the altar—a golden throne.","The golden throne felt like the most important aspect of God’s Era. It drew in anyone who laid their eyes on it. The crowd instinctively understood that the person who sat on the throne would receive God’s Era’s final power.","And the throne was connected to the second gate by a ray of light. Chu Feng must have something to do with it."]},{"number":6690,"title":"Chapter 6690: Chapter 6688: Lightning Baptism","paragraphs":["Chapter 6688: Lightning Baptism","While Chu Feng was deciphering the situation, a deep, resonant voice suddenly boomed.","“Congratulations on clearing the first trial. In the next trial, your body will be tempered by lightning. Each time you succeed, a step will be created in the passageway. The sturdiness of the step will be determined by the intensity of the tempering.","“You’ll have to complete all the steps to enter the passageway. If you reach the top and sit on the throne, you’ll obtain God’s Era’s power. If your tempering is imperfect, the steps may break and fail to reach the top, resulting in your failure.","“Even if you fail the trial, you still have to undergo all the tempering before you’re allowed to leave. There is a possibility you may die. You have a choice now. If you give up now, you’ll be allowed to leave safely, but your sword key will be destroyed, and you won’t be able to enter God’s Era ever again.","“Choose wisely, junior.”","Those words had come from space, and they harnessed tremendous power that shook the realm. Perhaps, they might have been from God’s Era itself.","“Elder, may I know what is God’s Era’s final power? Will it advance my cultivation?” Chu Feng asked.","The previous trial suggested that God’s Era’s final power enhanced one’s bloodline, but Chu Feng’s bloodline was already strong enough. He doubted that there was a need to enhance it further.","Rather, he was more concerned about the progression of his cultivation.","He needed to enter Heavenly God as soon as possible, and it would be ideal if he could advance to rank two or rank three Heavenly God right away. That would allow him to defeat Jie Tianran and overcome his present quandary.","If God’s Era only enhanced his bloodline and not his cultivation, even if his fighting prowess rose, it would still be nowhere near enough for him to turn the tables around.","“What’s your decision? Will you challenge the trial or leave?” the voice asked impatiently.","Seeing that he wouldn’t get an answer, Chu Feng replied, “I’ll take the challenge.”","Boom!","Blue lightning crackled menacingly from space. There were only several bolts at first, but the frightening prowess they harnessed made Chu Feng shudder. Every bolt harnessed destructive might greater than the nine-colored lightning he faced whenever he made a breakthrough.","In the blink of an eye, the sky was already covered in thick, blue lightning bolts.","“Chu Feng, those lightning bolts aren’t as simple as they look. Are you sure you can handle them? Why don’t we just give up? There are other ways to deal with Jie Tianran. We don’t have to put our lives on the line here.”","Even Eggy panicked before this immense force.","“The shot has been fired. There’s no turning back. Besides, I think it’s a good thing that the tempering is potent. This fulfills my expectations of God’s Era,” Chu Feng replied confidently.","Boom!","As if provoked by Chu Feng’s confidence, a lightning bolt descended from the sky and struck Chu Feng’s body, vaporizing his clothes. Chu Feng collapsed to the ground, his skin torn open to reveal his flesh. His body stiffened, and he was in so much pain that he couldn’t even speak.","The blue lightning was indeed different from the nine-colored lightning.","The nine-colored lightning was more of a trial than an attack, which was partly why Chu Feng had always been able to withstand its prowess. In contrast, the blue lightning harnessed pure destructive might that threatened to claim his life if he lowered his guard in the slightest.","“Are you fine, Chu Feng? Can we still give up now? Let’s give up, all right?” Eggy exclaimed worriedly.","To her dismay, she couldn’t open the World Spirit Space’s gate. She could only watch helplessly as Chu Feng suffered.","Chu Feng was also dazed by the lightning strike. He wondered if he had overestimated himself. If this was only the first bolt, he couldn’t imagine surviving the trial.","But then, a blue aura appeared in his body. The lingering energy of the blue lightning bolt had seeped into his body, healing his wounds and removing the searing sensation engulfing him.","Chu Feng regained his mobility. Moreover, he noticed that his body and soul had gotten stronger than before.","Needless to say, he was thrilled. He leaped to his feet and shouted, “Exhilarating!”","Boom!","The blue lightning seemed to take his shout as a provocation, and it struck him with another lightning bolt.","Once again, Chu Feng collapsed to the ground. He didn’t fare any better than before.","“Hahaha! Interesting!”","Yet, he laughed manically.","He had always been able to accomplish feats that others struggled with due to his superior talent. Even when faced with the most terrifying nine-colored lightning tribulation in the world, he still slowly grew accustomed to it. It was still painful, but he had no doubt about his survival.","But it was different this time.","The blue lightning made him feel small and insignificant. He realized that, despite his outstanding talent, he was still nothing in the face of absolute power.","This realization didn’t drive Chu Feng into despair; instead, he welcomed and celebrated it. Challenges had always excited him.","Eggy also stopped trying to dissuade Chu Feng. She could already tell from his voice that he would grit his teeth and get through this tempering no matter how difficult it was.","More blue lightning bolts descended.","Chu Feng realized that he was recovering at a faster speed. He still struggled to get to his feet, but he now had some spare time to look around before the next lightning bolt struck him.","He looked at the passageway linking his gate to the top of God’s Era’s silhouette. Steps that glowed with a nine-colored light had begun appearing at the bottom of the passageway. There were only several steps, but they looked sturdy.","“Why do the steps look so dim? Is it not perfect enough?” Eggy asked worriedly.","Chu Feng was not bothered about that. He looked at the sky and shouted, “Give me something stronger!”","Boom!","Another lightning bolt descended, slamming him back into the ground and ripping through his flesh.","...","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran was sitting in a room identical to the one Chu Feng had been in earlier. He finally opened his eyes, but his gaze reflected not just happiness but fatigue as well."]},{"number":6691,"title":"Chapter 6691: Chapter 6689: The Depressed Jie Tianran","paragraphs":["Chapter 6689: The Depressed Jie Tianran","“How is it? Did you manage to decipher the riddle?” the old entity in Jie Tianran’s body asked.","“The clues in this room point toward the word, ‘Bloodline’,” Jie Tianran said.","“Do you want to confirm it? You only have one try.”","“There’s no need for that. I trust my judgment.”","Jie Tianran picked up the brush and wrote the word ‘Bloodline’ on the stone monument.","The stone monument immediately reacted.","“The answer really is ‘Bloodline’. Does this mean that God’s Era’s final power enhances one’s bloodline? Or does it contain the strongest bloodline in the world, the God Bloodline?” the old entity murmured.","Jie Tianran picked up on his words and asked, “Elder, is the God Bloodline the strongest bloodline in the world?”","“No, that’s just my guess. This place is called God’s Era, after all. If the final power is really a bloodline, I reckon it would be the strongest one in the world. It wouldn’t be excessive to name it ‘God Bloodline’,” the old entity replied.","“Yes, that is possible.”","Jie Tianran thought that the deduction sounded plausible, and it raised his anticipation. His greatest bottleneck currently was his weak bloodline, which was why he had placed so much emphasis on Chu Feng’s Ruler’s Bloodline.","If God’s Era truly had the world’s strongest bloodline and he obtained it, his rise to greatness would be guaranteed. It would only be a matter of time before he rose to the top.","Weng!","The stone monument lit up. It was the same thing as what had happened to Chu Feng.","When the light receded, Jie Tianran found himself transported into a vast realm. He could see the horizons of this realm, as well as God’s Era’s silhouette, but unlike the realm that Chu Feng was on, this realm was shrouded in many layers of sealing formations.","And Jie Tianran was trapped inside the innermost sealing formation.","Jie Tianran’s trial was to breach the sealing formations.","But he didn’t get to action right away as he was distracted by the changes in God’s Era.","A ray of light gushed from the third gate toward the head of God’s Era’s silhouette. That naturally drew Jie Tianran’s attention toward the platform on top of the silhouette, as well as the golden throne.","However, he also noticed that there was already a link between the second gate and the golden throne, and that nine-colored steps had already begun appearing in that link.","“That darned Chu Feng!” Jie Tianran clenched his fists.","He had been the first one to enter God’s Era, but somehow, Chu Feng was still able to advance ahead of him.","The voice Chu Feng had heard earlier boomed in Jie Tianran’s realm. It told him that his realm was shrouded in many sealing formations, and that he had to breach the formations to forge the steps required to reach the golden throne. However, the sturdiness of the steps depended on how perfectly the formations were breached.","As soon as the voice faded, Jie Tianran began breaching the first sealing formation. He was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, after all. While the golden throne had caught his attention, it didn’t stop him from observing and figuring out the solution for the first formation.","It only took a moment for him to complete the deciphering formation.","As the two formations overlapped, the first sealing formation crumbled.","With that, Jie Tianran had deciphered the first formation.","However, the second sealing formation was only going to be tougher.","Jie Tianran turned to the link, curious to know what kind of step he had forged. Much to his dismay, the step appeared to be made from dirt, and it didn’t emanated the slightest glow.","He looked at Chu Feng’s step—it had nine colors and was glowing with a faint radiance.","There was a stark contrast between the two.","“Hahahaha!” Eggy laughed loudly when she saw the step forged by Jie Tianran.","“Chu Feng, your grandfather is making dirt bricks over there. Looks like my eyes have failed me. Your steps are already perfect as they are.” Eggy was laughing so hard that she was bent over.","Chu Feng crawled up from the ground. He, too, has noticed the dirt step, but he didn’t laugh. Instead, he said aloud, “Continue!”","Boom!","Another blue lightning bolt struck Chu Feng, causing him to collapse and his flesh to rip open once more. However, the blue aura appeared even faster than before, and his body recovered at a faster rate, too.","...","“How is this possible?”","Jie Tianran’s face turned livid. This matter was a huge blow to him.","“Don’t get distracted, Jie Tianran. Focus. Make sure your deciphering formation is impeccable,” the old entity said.","Jie Tianran pulled himself together and focused on the second formation.","He had already given his all for the first formation, doing everything he could to ensure that it was perfect. Since the result was not satisfactory, he began nitpicking the details more, resulting in the observation time and formation construction time to become much longer.","The eventual deciphering formation easily breached the second sealing formation.","However, the newly forged step remained a disappointment. It was still a dirt step.","“Why? Why is this happening?” Jie Tianran was frustrated.","He looked at Chu Feng’s step once more, and he dropped to his knee in frustration. He was already putting in his all, but it was to no avail. This was a massive blow to him. He was forced to wonder if the gap between him was Chu Feng was impossible to bridge.","“Am I destined to lose to that little bastard?” Jie Tianran had never felt so defeated before.","“Jie Tianran, are you planning to give up,” the old entity asked.","Jie Tianran didn’t answer. He was feeling confused.","“You should speak now if you intend to give up. We can leave now,” the old entity said.","Jie Tianran remained silent.","“If you don’t intend to give up, get up and continue. Stop kneeling uselessly here. I suspect that the steps you forged are inferior to Chu Feng’s due to the door you have chosen. Isn’t this door lower in terms of difficulty? Since there is a difference in difficulty level, the steps you forge are bound to be different,” the old entity said.","Those words brought a glimmer of light back to Jie Tianran’s eyes.","“If my guess is right, your standards for perfection would be different. Perhaps, you are already achieving the ceiling of what is possible for this gate. If so, what you have to do now is to speed up and catch up with Chu Feng. If you can ascend God’s Era faster than him, the flamboyant steps he forged will become a joke,” the old entity added.","Jie Tianran’s gloomy mood was cleared right away. He got back up to his feet. It didn’t make sense for him to give up now when he had worked so hard for this day.","“Elder, thank you for your reminder.”","Jie Tianran regained his fighting will."]},{"number":6692,"title":"Chapter 6692: Chapter 6690: Unexpected Outcome","paragraphs":["Chapter 6690: Unexpected Outcome","Jie Tianran completely immersed himself in the deciphering of the sealing formations.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng continued to be struck and tempered by the blue lightning. As the frequency of the lightning strikes increased, the amount of blue aura in his body, which aided his physical recovery, increased.","The blue aura was only a temporary buff—it was bound to disappear once the trial was over—but on top of raising his speed of recovery, he realized that he could wield it as his own cultivation as well.","It reached a point where the blue aura’s power surpassed his cultivation to reach Heavenly God level.","But Chu Feng had no interest in that. What was more important to him now was his speed of recovery. The faster he healed, the higher the intensity of blue lightning he could withstand, thus allowing him to build the steps faster.","...","Jie Tianran showcased the full extent of his talent, and the old entity within him was also offering him pointers. Despite the increasing difficulty, he was deciphering the sealing formations faster and faster.","The rest of the world was oblivious to the trials they were undertaking, but they could guess based on the steps that were being built from the gates to the golden throne. Everyone’s eyes were focused on the two stairs.","The stairs continued to rise, and in just a few short days, the trial concluded.","Zi Ling, Little Fishy, and the others had long arrived at the location they had agreed upon with Chu Feng. They had been keeping an eye on the changes in God’s Era. The atmosphere was tense.","Everyone was worried, be it Zi Ling, Little Fishy, the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, Long Mucheng, or even the older elders like Jie Shanxian.","Fei was the only one who was relaxed, sitting on a chair with crossed legs while munching on a roasted goose. It was as if everything that was happening right now had nothing to do with him.","“What’s there to worry about? This isn’t even a fight. Jie Tianran might be building fast, but their steps aren’t at the same quality. Brother Chu Feng’s steps are beautiful and glowing, whereas Jie Tianran’s steps are just mud bricks. Who knows? His steps might just shatter the moment he steps on top of them, causing that old thing to fall to his death,” Fei said while munching on his goose.","“That would be for the best,” Little Fishy replied.","The others couldn’t be bothered to answer.","Chu Feng’s stairs were very close to reaching the golden throne. He was only a few steps off. Victory was within sight.","But for some reason, his progress suddenly stopped when he was just short of the final step. The final step refused to appear. In contrast, Jie Tianran’s dirt steps were quickly catching up.","“What’s going on? Did a problem occur?”","Zi Ling and Little Fishy’s nervousness peaked. It was apparent to anyone that a problem had cropped up.","Meanwhile, in God’s Era, Chu Feng was enveloped in a thick blue aura that resembled armor. He looked awe-inspiring. By this point, the blue aura’s power was already comparable to rank eight Heavenly God level.","However, Chu Feng didn’t look happy in the least.","The blue lightning that had been crackling above him had scattered, suggesting that the tempering was over. Yet, he was still a single step away from reaching his destination. This missing step meant that he couldn’t enter the linkway and reach the top of God’s Era.","He... had failed.","“It’s fine, Chu Feng. We can do without God’s Era’s final power,” Eggy consoled.","“But how can I rival Jie Tianran if he obtains God’s Era’s final power?”","Chu Feng was not only disappointed at having failed to obtain God’s Era’s power. More than that, he was worried about the safety of his loved ones.","“Don’t worry. We’ll figure a way out when the time comes,” Eggy replied.","Those words only made Chu Feng feel worse. He knew that Eggy had means to drastically raise her cultivation, but the last thing he wanted was for her to lose her life helping him. He would rather be the one to put his life on the line, especially since he possessed similar means.","It was just that the price was too much for him to bear.","“Chu Feng, the spirit formation gate isn’t appearing. Does that mean your tempering isn’t over yet?” Eggy asked.","Chu Feng was still stuck in this realm even though the blue lightning had dissipated. The entity here hadn’t declared the result, either. Perhaps the trial was not over yet.","Those words sparked a sliver of hope in Chu Feng’s heart.","“You have failed,” a resonant voice echoed from space.","The result had been announced.","“Elder, is my tempering imperfect?” Chu Feng anxiously asked.","“It isn’t time yet,” the voice replied.","“Are there other ways?”","“That will depend on whether God’s Era’s power remains after this. The other person has cleared the preliminary trial.”","Chu Feng anxiously looked at Jie Tianran’s linkway.","Jie Tianran had successfully forged all of his steps and had been transported into the linkway. His body looked insignificant in contrast to the steps; every single step resembled a mountain before him. However, there was no need for him to climb at all, for a surge of energy was lifting him toward the peak.","Moreover, a massive silhouette had manifested around Jie Tianran. This silhouette was even larger than the steps, which made it seem like Jie Tianran was climbing his way to the top. Anyone observing God’s Era could tell that Jie Tianran had succeeded.","“Elder, are there more trials?” Chu Feng asked.","The voice had used the term ‘preliminary trial’, which suggested that there were more difficulties ahead.","In response, the voice simply chuckled.","A surge of teleportation energy enveloped Chu Feng and transported him back into space. He had returned to the location where he was standing before.","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion hadn’t laid an ambush for him, though he rather they had done so. His tempering might have failed, but the blue aura he had built up still lingered, though it was steadily dissipating into the surroundings.","If the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had laid an ambush for him, he could have easily massacred them. Even Jie Tianran wouldn’t have been a match for him in his current state.","It was a pity that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion wasn’t here, and Jie Tianran was still inside God’s Era.","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran kept glancing at Chu Feng’s linkway. Despite having claimed the upper hand, he looked extremely uneasy.","“What’s wrong? Are you still worried despite being ahead?” the old entity asked."]},{"number":6693,"title":"Chapter 6693: Chapter 6691: Kill Them All","paragraphs":["Chapter 6691: Kill Them All","“That little beast is full of tricks. He might not have completed his linkway, but its quality is above mine. I can’t help but feel that he’s up to something,” Jie Tianran voiced his worry.","“Yes, that grandson of yours is a sly one. We have to remain guarded against him. However, there’s no point worrying when you can’t even find anything amiss. You should focus on what’s at hand instead,” the old entity advised.","In truth, he was worried as well. Both of them had suffered setbacks in Chu Feng’s hands.","Boom!","A loud explosion suddenly rattled the world of cultivation.","It was particularly deafening to Jie Tianran, and it rattled even his linkway. He quickly looked over and saw Chu Feng’s steps and linkway collapsing. His face immediately lit up in glee.","“Big brother...”","Over in the Chu Clan Alliance, Zi Ling, Little Fishy, and the others couldn’t believe their eyes.","“Oh no...”","Even Fei was dumbstruck.","Even though they had been worried, none of them thought that Chu Feng would really fail. This outcome was beyond their expectations.","...","In the Nine Souls Galaxy, Song Changsheng revealed a rare hint of disbelief.","“What happened? Was young friend Chu Feng too anxious? But that shouldn’t be. That isn’t like him,” Song Changsheng murmured, but he was unable to make sense of the situation.","In the end, he sighed. “As expected of the legendary God’s Era. If even young friend Chu Feng has failed, I doubt that anyone can succeed in it.”","He doubted that Jie Tianran would succeed for a simple reason. Not even powerhouses in the Ancient Era had been able to claim that power. In his view, the only one who had a shot at success was Chu Feng.","If Chu Feng couldn’t do it, no one else could.","...","Over at the Bloodline Galaxy, Chen Hui was still bathing in a pool.","He had stopped howling, and his body had fully recovered, though his complexion remained pale. It wasn’t because he was injured or weakened; rather, it felt like something had changed inside him. His body felt empty, and something was required to fill it up.","Dongfang Hansong had been observing God’s Era. When he saw Chu Feng’s linkway collapse, he revealed a gloating smirk.","“That’s all you amount to, Chu Feng.”","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng was feeling conflicted.","He had rarely lost in any competitions. To think that he would fail at one as crucial at this.","“Did I choose wrongly?”","Chu Feng took out his sword key, thinking that he might be able to catch up with Jie Tianran if he entered the third gate now.","To his dismay, he couldn’t enter God’s Era from where he currently was. He needed to get closer to God’s Era first, perhaps even closer than where Jie Tianran had entered from.","Just then, the third gate channeled a surge of energy into Jie Tianran’s body, causing him to accelerate rapidly. The journey should have taken him much longer, but in the blink of an eye, he had already reached the top.","Jie Tianran was now standing on top of God’s Era’s humongous silhouette, below the platform where the golden throne was.","Just then, God’s Era’s silhouette moved.","The world of cultivation quaked.","The humongous silhouette formed a hand seal as if cultivating.","Incredible energy appeared within the silhouette and converged at the head, toward Jie Tianran. The light produced was so brilliant that it engulfed many realms; it was a sight more majestic than any phenomenon.","And Jie Tianran was the cause of it.","Light flowed around Jie Tianran like a sacred halo. At this moment, he seemed to have become a part of God’s Era.","This phenomenon didn’t last long.","Jie Tianran, still carrying a trace of lingering light, slowly raised his hand to feel the energy coursing through him. His wrinkled face no longer reflected unease but absolute confidence.","His bloodline had been strengthened.","He had obtained heaven-defying battle power capable of surmounting a cultivation rank. Despite still being at rank five Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, he could now stand his ground against rank seven Heavenly Gods.","On top of that, his spirit power was far more condensed than before. He was confident that he could fight off multiple rank seven Heavenly Gods in his current state.","More importantly, he was the only one who wielded such power in the present world of cultivation. He was unmatched now.","“I won, Chu Feng.” Jie Tianran regained his past confidence.","“You sound certain,” the old entity inside him remarked.","“My connection with God’s Era has deepened. I can sense a stronger power in that golden throne, and I can also sense the location of Chu Feng’s sword key. That little bastard is no longer in God’s Era,” Jie Tianran replied.","“Oh? It sounds like he has really failed.”","“Of course.” Jie Tianran smirked in glee.","He felt like the stress that had accumulated in him recently had all been released.","...","“Chu Feng, did your grandfather succeed?” Eggy asked.","“He hasn’t obtained God’s Era’s final power yet, but he received some benefits from it,” Chu Feng replied. “Hm?”","Just then, Chu Feng noticed a light gleaming in the distance. It was coming from the Bloodline Galaxy. He quickly used his observation means to take a closer look.","It was coming from the phenomenon.","The phenomenon had stopped contracting, but a gate had appeared in it. It seemed to be the entrance into the phenomenon, and it looked like it would open at any moment.","Chu Feng quickly stowed away the sword key.","Jie Tianran had already claimed the upper hand in God’s Era. Even if Chu Feng entered the third gate right now, it was unlikely that he would make it in time.","Furthermore, the land where his friends and kin were was on the verge of opening, and enemies were camping right outside. There was no way he could turn a blind eye to that.","Without any hesitation, he made his way toward the phenomenon.","Given the rate at which the blue aura was dissipating, his cultivation should recede to rank seven or rank six Heavenly God level by the time he reached the Bloodline Galaxy. That was more than enough to deal with the Netherworld Sect.","And he planned to slaughter them all."]},{"number":6694,"title":"Chapter 6694: Chapter 6692: Contempt","paragraphs":["Chapter 6692: Contempt","While Chu Feng was rushing over, Jie Tianran also sensed the changes happening in the Bloodline Galaxy. He quickly observed the Bloodline Galaxy.","“Something is amiss.” Jie Tianran’s glee faded.","“What do you mean?” the old entity asked.","“I can sense through Chu Feng’s sword key that he is heading toward the Bloodline Galaxy’s phenomenon. The prophecy states that it is Chu Feng’s weakness, but I don’t know what that means. I only know that Chu Feng cares a lot about that phenomenon. I’m worried that it might be a fortuitous encounter for him.”","“Fortuitous encounter? That phenomenon does look like a fortuitous encounter.”","“We can’t let him get his way.”","“Do you intend to give up on God’s Era to pursue your grandson? That’s not worth it. No matter how huge that fortuitous encounter is, it can’t be bigger than God’s Era.”","“There’s no way I would give up on God’s Era.” Jie Tianran shook his head.","“What do you plan to do then?” The old entity was confused.","“Elder, have you forgotten that I still have this?”","Jie Tianran pulled out an ancient talisman paper with the word ‘clone’ written on it.","“Your spirit power is still at rank five Heavenly Dragon, but you’re able to raise your spirit power by two ranks. That is enough to channel this talisman paper. But how do you intend to send the talisman paper out from here?”","“It might seem like we’re closer to God’s Era now, but we’re actually outside God’s Era at the moment. Furthermore, I don’t sense any energy impeding me. We’ll know whether it works or not once I give it a try.”","Jie Tianran channeled his spirit power into the talisman paper before plastering it on a Cosmos Sack. He pointed his finger outward, and the talisman paper and the Cosmos Sack flew out in a surge of light.","“It worked!” Jie Tianran smiled.","Now that he had sent the talisman paper out, he didn’t have to worry about the Bloodline Galaxy’s phenomenon anymore. He turned around and looked back at the platform.","“Now, let me see what power I can attain by conquering this platform and sitting on that golden throne!”","Jie Tianran closed his eyes. To reach the platform, he had to first grasp its energy. That was no easy feat; it was an even harder undertaking than the trial in the room. Still, he was hopeful.","...","Some time later, Chu Feng arrived at the Bloodline Galaxy.","Much of his blue aura had faded, resulting in his cultivation receding from rank eight to rank six Heavenly God level. Nevertheless, it was enough to deal with the Netherworld Sectmembers.","So, he didn’t bother to conceal himself. He whipped out his Lightning Flame Sword and went on a massacre.","...","Dongfang Hansong was still inside that dark palace, observing the changes in God’s Era. However, the glee he felt from Chu Feng’s failure had long given way to unease.","“Since the Ancient Era, no one has been able to attain God’s Era’s final power. If Jie Tianran obtains it, our Netherworld Sect will likely be beneath the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion even if we awaken our sacred item. Given Jie Tianran’s ambitions, I fear that our Netherworld Sect will be suppressed,” Dongfang Hansong said.","He looked at the black bracelet on his wrist. Its backlash energy had seeped into his soul.","“We can’t continue staying here. Regardless of whether we awaken the sacred item or not, we have to enter the Ninth Galaxy. The Netherworld Sect cannot be reduced into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s puppet,” Dongfang Hansong murmured.","Just then, he heard explosions in the distance, and his eyes narrowed.","He quickly checked out the situation using his observation formation. Countless sword rays were swiftly slicing through space, decapitating Netherworld Sectmembers.","When he finally found the culprit behind his massacre, his eyes widened in disbelief.","“Chu Feng? How did he get here so quickly? What’s going on with his cultivation? How did he reach rank six Heavenly God? Is it because of that blue aura shrouding him? Is that his secret hand?” Dongfang Hansong was perplexed.","But there was no time to ponder over these questions. Chu Feng was massacring his subordinates. Countless people had already died in just mere moments. There was even one rank four Heavenly God among the casualties.","That was one of Dongfang Hansong’s close aides!","At this rate, the conservative faction’s foundation would be unraveled, and Dongfang Hansong would no longer be able to compete with Baili Xukong","...","Chu Feng dashed through space with the Lightning Flame Sword in hand.","Wherever he passed, bodies were sliced apart, and blood splattered. Many Netherworld Sectmembers died before they could even react. All beings beneath rank six Heavenly God level were equal before Chu Feng’s blade.","For instance, the Netherworld Marshal whom Chu Feng had just killed was able to raise his cultivation to rank five Heavenly God level, but he was still killed in a single slash.","Chu Feng had no plan. His thought was to kill all Netherworld Sectmembers who appeared before him. The more he killed, the better it was. He was gathering origin energies for Eggy, after all.","“Chu Feng!!!” a roar echoed.","Dongfang Hansong charged at Chu Feng with his God Armament saber. He unleashed all his means, raising his cultivation to rank six Heavenly God level.","“Hmph.”","Chu Feng ignored Dongfang Hansong and swung his blade.","A golden sword ray gushed across space like a towering tsunami, piercing through a warship not too far away. There were at least hundreds of thousands of Netherworld Sectmembers in that warship, but they were killed before they could even scream.","They didn’t even leave origin energies behind; Chu Feng absorbed them into his body and transferred them into his World Spirit Space.","“I’ll rip you apart!”","Dongfang Hansong was furious as Chu Feng completely ignored him only to continue slaughtering the Netherworld Sectmembers. He was not just any Netherworld Marshal; he was the leader of the conservative faction! Even Baili Xukong dared not look down on him, so how dare a junior like Chu Feng do so?"]},{"number":6695,"title":"Chapter 6695: Chapter 6693: Gift","paragraphs":["Chapter 6693: Gift","Boom!","Dongfang Hansong whipped out his God Armament spear and charged forth. His spear tip trembled from the ridiculous amount of martial power channeled into it, and it unleashed a devastating beam that rushed at Chu Feng.","This strike could have easily destroyed any realm.","But Chu Feng merely shot it a look of contempt before dodging it with ease. Then, he counterattacked with a sword ray that was far faster and more powerful.","Dongfang Hansong, due to the momentum of his charge, could not dodge the sword ray, so he quickly unleashed a martial skill to counterattack.","Boom!","The two forces collided. Chu Feng’s sword ray easily sliced through Dongfang Hansong’s martial skill and advanced toward the latter.","Dongfang Hansong quickly conjured a barrier out of martial power. The sword ray struck the barrier and dissipated into ripples, but at the same time, Dongfang Hansong was sent flying into the distance.","He might have survived the attack, but it had left many holes in his barrier.","“Something is wrong. Chu Feng’s earlier sword ray is not a martial skill but a casual attack, so how can it wield so much power?” Dongfang Hansong’s heart skipped a beat.","His barrier had only managed to block Chu Feng’s sword ray because his martial skill had neutralized a portion of its prowess. Otherwise, the sword ray would have breached his barrier as well.","Meanwhile, Chu Feng flitted up to Dongfang Hansong and swung his Lightning Flame Sword down upon Dongfang Hansong.","Given their proximity, there was no time for Dongfang Hansong to unleash a martial skill at all. He could only raise his God Armament spear in a fluster while twisting his body to attempt an evasive maneuver.","But the moment their weapons clashed, Dongfang Hansong froze in place.","Chu Feng’s Lightning Flame Sword sliced through his supposedly nigh indestructible ‘True’ character God Armament as if it were tofu.","Psh!","Blood splattered. This miscalculation had cost Dongfang Hansong’s entire shoulder!","But that was not all. Chu Feng immediately redirected his Lightning Flame Sword to pierce Dongfang Hansong’s dantian.","This time, Dongfang Hansong didn’t even have time to dodge. He had no choice but to activate the life preservation treasure he had concealed inside his body.","The sword landed on target, but it had failed to pierce Dongfang Hansong’s body. Instead, Dongfang Hansong was sent flying from the sheer force of the attack.","A golden sphere covered in runes had enveloped Dongfang Hansong’s body, protecting him from Chu Feng’s earlier fatal attack. This was Dongfang Hansong’s strongest life preservation treasure, and it could only be used once. He wouldn’t invoke it unless cornered.","He had planned to use it against Baili Xukong, but little did he expect it to be squandered on Chu Feng.","The next moment, Dongfang Hansong’s face distorted.","Chu Feng had flitted up to him once more, but instead of swinging his Lightning Flame Sword, he raised his left hand and directed his palm toward him.","“Protection Bane!”","Bizarre energy surged out from Chu Feng’s left palm and enveloped Dongfang Hansong.","The golden sphere that had enveloped Dongfang Hansong’s body began to recede into the treasure that he had placed inside his soul. It felt like something mysterious force had unraveled his protection treasure.","But how could this be?","It had to be Chu Feng’s doing!","“What kind of monster are you?!” Dongfang Hansong stared at Chu Feng in fright.","This was his first time feeling so rattled while facing an enemy. He had never tasted such despair before. Despite his enemy being a mere junior, he saw no path to victory. He couldn’t even imagine surviving this ordeal.","All he could do was wait for his inevitable death.","Boom!","A saber suddenly descended from the sky to strike Chu Feng, but Chu Feng dodged it in advance.","“How useless can you be, Dongfang Hansong? You can’t even deal with a mere junior.”","Baili Xukong and his army had appeared. His army emanated blood-red auras that converged into Baili Xukong, making him look imposing. This was a formation from the Netherworld Sect that enhanced one’s fighting prowess, but it was stronger than the one he had used against Zi Ling and Feng Ling back then.","Baili Xukong was angry at having failed to defeat Zi Ling and Feng Ling, so he distributed his treasures to the Netherworld Sectmembers to further awaken their Netherworld Embryos, to further enhance the formation’s prowess.","He was far stronger than he was that day. In fact, he was confident he could single-handedly deal with both Feng Ling and Zi Ling.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","Blood-red auras flowed from the distance into Dongfang Hansong’s body. His subordinates had also arrived, and they were doing everything they could to strengthen Dongfang Hansong.","But Dongfang Hansong gritted his teeth in pain.","He was in a terrible state. Chu Feng’s attack had not only severely wounded his body but his soul as well. Even when he was augmented by a formation now, his fighting prowess was still far weaker than before.","“Chu Feng, I didn’t expect you to come knocking on your own accord,” Baili Xukong sneered.","Chu Feng glanced at the huge army behind Baili Xukong, and he quickly locked onto Baili Zilin.","“Did you only bring your son? You didn’t bring other family members along?” Chu Feng asked.","“What are you getting at?” Baili Xukong frowned.","“That would have been more convenient for me. I would have been able to purge you vermin from the face of the world in one shot,” Chu Feng replied.","He unleashed a powerful burst of martial power that induced a mini-phenomenon. The surrounding space turned blood red."]},{"number":6696,"title":"Chapter 6696: Chapter 6694: Heaven Protection Shield Spirit","paragraphs":["Chapter 6694: Heaven Protection Shield Spirit","“That is our Netherworld Sect’s rank three God Taboo, Demon Blood Inferno Slash. Does he know our Netherworld Sect’s sect-protection martial skill?” The Netherworld Sect members were not just shocked but enraged as well.","They felt like their treasure had been robbed.","“Could it have been... that time?”","Baili Zilin thought about the last time he crossed blows with Chu Feng. He had used Demon Blood Inferno Slash then, but Chu Feng easily overcame it with a simple clash.","After that, Chu Feng used a bizarre skill that siphoned something important away from him, but somehow, he didn’t feel like anything was off. He couldn’t understand what Chu Feng had done to him, and that left him uneasy.","It was only now, when Chu Feng employed Demon Blood Inferno Slash, that everything was clicking together.","“Baili Zilin, I shall use the same Demon Blood Inferno Slash that you have gifted me to vanquish your Netherworld Sect!” Chu Feng sneered.","That confirmed Baili Zilin’s suspicion.","“What? Baili Zilin gave Demon Blood Inferno Slash to Chu Feng?”","That caused a huge stir among the Netherworld Sectmembers. They wouldn’t have doubted it if Chen Hui was the one who did it, but Baili Zilin? How could that be?","All of them knew how much Baili Zilin hated Chu Feng!","“What nonsense. How can you possibly have learned our Netherworld Sect’s sect-protection martial skill? You’re merely trying to shake our morale!” Baili Xukong sneered as he directed his martial power at Chu Feng to grab him.","However, his martial power unraveled before it could reach Chu Feng.","Simultaneously, the blood cloud that was swiftly expanding from Chu Feng began to rain torrentially. The sight of rainfall in the middle of space was unnerving.","This was no normal rain. It harnessed oppressive might and blood.","The Netherworld Sectmembers immediately realized that they had underestimated Chu Feng’s means. All of them were bound in place. Even Baili Xukong and Dongfang Hansong found their movements and powers severely restrained.","The fallen blood rain didn’t descend any further; instead, they converged toward Chu Feng. These raindrops revolved around Chu Feng as if an army awaiting his orders. The blood-red light reflected off the raindrops on Chu Feng’s face made him look like a demon god.","“That is the highest level of Demon Blood Inferno Slash, Demon Blood Nine Heavens Suppression!” Xiahou Jue blurted out in fright.","Baili Xukong’s face paled. He had been unleashing attack after attack on Chu Feng all this time, but all his attacks were neutralized by the blood rain before they could reach Chu Feng.","He was quickly losing strength, and even escape was no longer possible.","He had no choice but to face reality. Chu Feng had not only grasped Demon Blood Inferno Slash, but he had even reached the highest level in it. To make things worse, Chu Feng’s fighting prowess far surpassed theirs.","This plunged them into despair.","There was no way for them to survive this.","Just then, Chu Feng cast his cold gaze at Baili Xukong and Baili Zilin and sneered, “Baili Zilin, Baili Xukong, you two are responsible for the Netherworld Sect’s current plight.”","Then, he swung his Lightning Flame Sword.","The Netherworld Sectmembers’ hearts jolted. They felt death encroaching on them. They could already imagine the demon blood morphing into sharp blades and slaughtering them all.","But that didn’t happen. The demon blood, as well as Chu Feng’s blade, froze midair.","Boom!","A blinding light shone from afar, unraveling the blood cloud and blood rain while also trapping Chu Feng and the Netherworld Sectmembers within it.","It was a sealing formation!","A glowing figure appeared in the formation. It was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Mansion Master, Jie Tianran! However, his body was translucent as it was completely made from spirit power.","Only the Cosmos Sack he carried was real; the other parts of him felt more like a soul entity.","Yet, he emanated an aura stronger than Chu Feng’s.","“This aura... Rank seven Heavenly Dragon level!” Baili Xukong blurted out.","The Netherworld Sectmembers saw a ray of hope. They knew that they had been saved. Jie Tianran was strong enough to save them from this desperate situation!","“How underhanded of you, Chu Feng. You tried to use God’s Era’s power to destroy the Netherworld Sect. However, the Netherworld Sect is the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s ally. I won’t let you get your way,” Jie Tianran spoke with the confidence and composure of a peerless expert.","He slowly descended from the sky, with each step of his causing space to quake. His aura as a rank seven Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist rippled outward, creating the illusion that a god had arrived.","“What’s in there, Chu Feng?” Jie Tianran glanced at the gate in the phenomenon as he asked.","Chu Feng didn’t answer. He secretly grabbed the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit.","He could tell that the person before him was not the real Jie Tianran but a clone, but even this clone wielded the power of rank seven Heavenly Dragon. There was no way he was a match for the other party.","On top of that, his blue aura was swiftly receding. It wouldn’t be long before his cultivation plummeted to rank five Heavenly God and beneath.","His only option other than putting his life on the line was to channel the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit.","“You refuse to speak? It’s fine. I have my ways,” Jie Tianran said.","He morphed his oppressive might into sharp blades to pierce Chu Feng’s body.","GRAR!","A pair of large eyes suddenly appeared in Chu Feng’s vicinity.","It emanated such an intimidating aura that it made everyone’s heart jolt. Then, it exerted a powerful force that jolted everyone back.","A massive, translucent light figure manifested around Chu Feng and revolved around him before eventually enveloping him, protecting him within it. It was the ferocious beast sculpted on the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit.","“At least you have a conscience.” Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief.","He had lied when he told Zi Ling and Little Fishy that the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit had the power to bring him to safety, but its defensive prowess was still formidable. At the very least, Jie Tianran’s clone was unable to breach it."]},{"number":6697,"title":"Chapter 6697: Chapter 6695: Awakening the Sacred Item","paragraphs":["Chapter 6695: Awakening the Sacred Item","“Why does that thing look familiar?”","Jie Tianran looked at the ferocious beast protecting Chu Feng with contemplative eyes, but he couldn’t figure out where he had seen it before.","“Chu Feng, you have many secret hands, but I reckon that treasure is time-limited. For how long can it protect you?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Jie Tianran, did God’s Era’s power only allow you to raise your cultivation by a rank?” Chu Feng replied with a question.","He had deduced that this was Jie Tianran’s clone, and that the clone was formed from a treasure. The treasure probably took on another form before this so that it could get to the Bloodline Galaxy quickly. However, the power wielded by the clone didn’t come from the treasure itself but from Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran’s base spirit power was at rank five Heavenly Dragon—that tallied with the information he had received from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion—but he wielded heaven-defying battle power capable of surmounting two cultivation ranks.","That was why he wielded power on par with rank seven Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists right now.","“Are you still thinking about God’s Era? Are you angry at your failure?” Jie Tianran sneered.","“You seem gleeful, but I don’t think you will be able to obtain God’s Era’s final power, either,” Chu Feng replied.","This was the deduction based on his observations.","“Hahahaha!” Jie Tianran raised his head and laughed loudly. Then, he looked at Chu Feng once more and said, “Since you are so curious, I’ll show you what I got.”","He reached into his Cosmos Sack and pulled out a talisman paper. The talisman paper flew from his hand, forming an observation formation that reflected the situation in God’s Era.","The crowd looked at the observation formation.","Jie Tianran’s main body was standing on top of the platform, just a step away from the golden throne. He was cloaked in a thick aura that resembled God’s Era’s humongous silhouette, both in terms of its airs and form.","And the silhouette was looking right in their direction.","Space quaked, and the tremors could be felt even from a far distance away. God’s Era’s silhouette seemed to come to life, and it took a step toward the Bloodline Galaxy. Its movements were slow, but it was so hulking that every step it took traversed countless realms.","Its speed was even faster than teleportation formations. At this rate, it wouldn’t be long before it reached the Bloodline Galaxy.","“Did your grandfather really obtain God’s Era’s final power?” Eggy panicked.","No one knew what God’s Era’s final power was, but it was clearly extremely powerful. If Jie Tianran really grasped it, it was unlikely that Eggy could defeat him even if she put her life on the line.","“Chu Feng, do you understand what I have obtained now? I have become one with God’s Era, making me the only god in this era. I don’t know what kind of fortuitous encounter or hidden hand awaits you inside that phenomenon, but there is no way you can defeat me,” Jie Tianran said gleefully.","“Fortuitous encounter? Hidden hand? Does your loser grandfather think that you have a hidden hand inside the phenomenon? No wonder he sent his clone after you despite being stuck inside God’s Era,” Eggy remarked with a sigh.","Jie Tianran waved his sleeves as if issuing an order.","Many humongous warships emerged from the cracks of space. Countless Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists stood on their decks.","“Activate the formation,” Jie Tianran ordered.","All the world spiritists sat down and formed hand seals, and formations began to surface from each of the warships. They interweaved to form a massive net that perfectly sealed off the area, trapping Chu Feng and his Heaven Protection Shield Spirit within.","This was the deployment Jie Tianran had made after receiving Baili Xukong’s message. He had dispatched 24 Saint-tier elders and the entire Sacred Mansion’s Shadow Corps for this ambush. The sealing formation was also a joint effort with Baili Xukong, designed specifically to curb Chu Feng.","A mysterious power pierced through the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit.","“Chu Feng, something is weird about that formation. Are you all right?” Eggy anxiously asked.","“I’m fine, Eggy. However, this formation utilizes the Netherworld Sect’s means to target my Netherworld Embryo. They are trying to extract the power of the Netherworld Embryo inside me. The power has locked onto me, but it is unable to inflict any damage upon me while the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit is still active,” Chu Feng told Eggy.","“Are they intending to use your Netherworld Embryo to awaken their sacred item?” Eggy asked.","“That’s likely the case.”","“Those despicable scums. They knew you’d return and laid this ambush!” Eggy was infuriated.","Somehow, Jie Tianran and the others seemed to know that the phenomenon was important to Chu Feng despite not knowing what it was about.","“Baili Xukong, are you fine?” Jie Tianran turned to Baili Xukong and asked.","“You arrived just in time, Mansion Master. Otherwise, our entire Netherworld Sect would have been in trouble,” Baili Xukong expressed his earnest gratitude to Jie Tianran.","“You have gotten stronger. It looks like you have dealt with those six old things from the neutral faction,” Jie Tianran said.","“They shouldn’t have betrayed the Netherworld Sect,” Baili Xukong replied.","“Mm.” Jie Tianran nodded with a satisfied smile.","He flicked his finger at Dongfang Hansong, releasing a surge of spirit power that transformed into a recovery formation. “We should help each other since we are allies. However, there is still one thing I should say. I know you are guarded against me, but you haven’t been channeling the black bracelets I have given you to the best of your ability, right?”","“Mansion Master, I guarantee that we have been following your instructions regarding the awakening of the sacred item, and we are making good progress. We are only a step away from success,” Baili Xukong replied.","“That is for the best. You have proposed using Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo to awaken the sacred item, but I have another idea. Your formation can indeed take the power of Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo, preventing him from dealing further damage to the sacred item, but you don’t need his power to awaken the sacred item.","“As I have previously told you, the black bracelets I have previously given you are incomplete. I have just finished crafting the final part of the black bracelets. With them, you can easily awaken the sacred item,” Jie Tianran said.","He opened his Cosmos Sack, and countless black objects flew forth. These were the missing portions of the black bracelets."]},{"number":6698,"title":"Chapter 6698: Chapter 6696: Middle-Aged Man","paragraphs":["Chapter 6696: Middle-Aged Man","Baili Xukong immediately grabbed one of the black objects and placed it into his black bracelet. The black bracelet’s aura immediately strengthened severalfold.","Baili Xukong and the other Netherworld Sectmembers were overjoyed. With such power, it should be a walk in the park for them to awaken the sacred item.","“Baili Xukong, if you trust me, you should awaken the sacred item right now. It’s fine if you still doubt me, but as allies, I’d like you to at least stay here and guard Chu Feng for now. Make sure he doesn’t escape until my main body arrives,” Jie Tianran said.","Baili Xukong looked at Chu Feng and saw that his cultivation had receded to rank five Heavenly God level. With that, there was no reason for him to fear Chu Feng anymore.","“Rest assured, Mansion Master. Since we are allies, I’ll make sure that Chu Feng doesn’t escape. We’ll also heed your advice and awaken our sacred item. Once our Netherworld Sect obtains the power of the sacred item and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion obtains the power of God’s Era, we’ll be unrivaled in the world of cultivation, Baili Xukong said.","Jie Tianran smiled. “We are already unrivaled in the world of cultivation. We should set our sights on conquering the Ninth Galaxy instead.”","Baili Xukong’s eyes lit up, and he nodded. “You’re right, Mansion Master.”","Jie Tianran walked up to Chu Feng and said, “Chu Feng, you are a lucky bastard. I have suffered several setbacks because of you, but ultimately, I am still the one who emerged victorious.”","There was a vile and provocative smile on his face as he said those words.","“Are you sure?” Chu Feng calmly asked.","“Hahaha!” Jie Tianran laughed in contempt.","“How stubborn. I’d like to see if you can still put on a strong front once I return with God’s Era’s final power.”","Jie Tianran formed a hand seal. His clone dissipated into a surge of spirit power, which then fused into the sealing formation trapping Chu Feng. Chu Feng immediately felt a spike in the rate at which his Netherworld Embryo’s energy was being siphoned.","Baili Xukong turned to the Saint-tier elders and bowed to them. “I’ll be counting on you, elders.”","He had never shown such respect to them before, but he understood that the power dynamics between the two powers had shifted after Jie Tianran obtained God’s Era’s power.","“You’re too courteous, Lord Baili. We are just following Lord Mansion Master’s orders. We will remain vigilant and give it our all,” one of the Saint-tier elders replied.","Baili Xukong then dispatched the black objects to his subordinates to complete their black bracelets, so that they could focus on awakening their sacred item.","“Baili Xukong, Chu Feng’s blue aura hasn’t fully receded yet. I fear that he might be feigning weakness. I’ll continue guarding this place until his blue aura recedes to a level where the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists can control him before heading over to aid you in the awakening of the sacred item,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“All right.” Baili Xukong nodded before leading his subordinates toward the sacred item.","His aides, such as Xiahou Jue and Wuma Hanshuang, followed him.","Once they were some distance away, Baili Xukong suddenly took out an exquisite wooden box and opened it. In it was a transparent pill that emanated the Ancient Era’s aura. He handed the pill to Xiahou Jue.","“Jie Tianran has obtained God’s Era’s power. We have to quickly awaken our sacred item, or else we risk being suppressed by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“The sealing formation trapping Chu Feng utilizes our sect’s secret skill and treasures, allowing it to siphon away the energy of Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo. I fear that Dongfang Hansong will covet that.","“This pill conceals you, but it’ll lose its effectiveness once you use a martial skill or wield your God Armament. I want you to take the pill and secretly follow Dongfang Hansong. Don’t stop him if he really covets Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo. Instead, I want you to report it to me right away,” Baili Xukong said.","“Yes, milord.”","Xiahou Jue consumed the pill and disappeared right away. Even his aura vanished. He turned around to follow Dongfang Hansong.","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran was still maneuvering God’s Era’s humongous silhouette toward the Bloodline Galaxy. The entire world of cultivation quaked with each step it took, though it didn’t cause any tangible damage.","Every single individual in the world of cultivation, no matter their galaxy, starfield, or realm, understood that something big was about to happen. The more timid ones broke down in tears, thinking that a catastrophe was about to befall them.","This huge commotion naturally caught the attention of all major powers, including Song Changsheng.","He knew that he couldn’t sit back anymore. He made his way to the Nine Souls Galaxy. His footsteps might seem slow, but realms flew past him with every step he took.","Just then, he noticed a comet whizzing across space, moving at an even faster speed than him. It was extremely discreet, though it was not enough to escape his notice. That person was using an invaluable, one-time-use world spiritist treasure.","The comet had come from the Ancestral Martial Galaxy and was headed for the Bloodline Galaxy.","“Elder, I guess you can’t sit still either,” Song Changsheng remarked with a smile.","...","Meanwhile, a powerful entity in the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect was observing the movements of God’s Era’s silhouette without using any observation formation.","“Lord Long Xie, did Jie Tianran really obtain God’s Era’s final power?” the monstrous old man asked.","“Have you gone senile? Even those lords back then have failed to obtain God’s Era’s final power. How can someone as insignificant as Jie Tianran possibly obtain it?” Long Xie scoffed.","He could tell that it was a one-time-use world spiritist treasure","“But isn’t Jie Tianran controlling God’s Era’s movements right now?”","“That’s hard to say. He could be the one controlling it, but God’s Era might also be moving on its own volition.”","“That is indeed possible. Milord, should we make a move if Chu Feng is in danger?”","“Don’t you think it’s beneath our stature to make a move against such a minor figure?”","Right after Long Xie said those words, all entities in the forbidden land turned to look in the same direction. In that direction stood a huge mountain that towered above the clouds, but if one were to take a closer look, one would realize that it wasn’t a mountain but a huge coffin.","That was where the Hidden Dragon Martial Sect’s sectmaster was in closed-door cultivation.","“It’s time for the lass to make a move,” Long Xie said.","The coffin shook.","Boom!","A gap appeared in the coffin, and a powerful aura gushed out.","“That lass has really undergone a metamorphosis. You’re right. She can definitely deal with Jie Tianran by herself,” the monstrous old man said excitedly.","Long Xie also smirked in glee. He was the one behind her metamorphosis, after all.","Shoosh!","All of a sudden, an object fell from the sky and landed on top of the coffin. It was a blank tombstone. It was small, standing at only a meter tall, but it emanated tremendous energy.","It closed the coffin shut once more and sealed it in place.","A middle-aged man’s voice echoed, “Let’s just watch the show. It wouldn’t be fun if you got involved in it.”","That voice echoed from all directions as if it were omnipresent."]},{"number":6699,"title":"Chapter 6699: Chapter 6697: Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6697: Emperor","“Who is it?” Long Xie was infuriated.","At the same time, countless devastating auras exploded from the forbidden land.","Some, like the monstrous old man, even drew their weapons. Their weapons were no ordinary God Armaments; just drawing them was enough to quake their surroundings. All of them raised their vigilance, knowing that someone had infiltrated their base.","“It has been many years, Long Xie, but you’re still as hot-tempered as ever,” the middle-aged man’s voice echoed once more, but this time, it came from the top of the coffin.","Long Xie looked over and saw a middle-aged man sitting on top of the sealed coffin.","“It’s you?”","Long Xie’s face warped as if he had encountered a dangerous enemy. He unleashed his oppressive might, causing cracks to appear in the surroundings—and that was an amazing feat considering the forbidden land’s incredible spatial resilience.","Any other realm would have been reduced to dust under his oppressive might.","All the experts in the forbidden land rose into the air and surrounded the coffin, but the middle-aged man seated on the coffin remained fearless.","“It’s one thing for your master to confront this emperor, but as you people... I suggest you think twice,” the middle-aged man said calmly.","Even Long Xie was sweating profusely, let alone the monstrous old man and the others. Eventually, Long Xie retracted his oppressive might, while the monstrous old man and the others sheathed their weapons. All of them lowered their heads in fear and indignation.","The atmosphere suddenly felt extremely repressed.","“That’s more like it. Let’s just watch the show, shall we?” the middle-aged man spoke calmly while looking at the Bloodline Galaxy’s phenomenon.","Even without an observation formation, he could clearly see not just the phenomenon but also Chu Feng and everyone else there.","...","Meanwhile, the Chu Clan Alliance had no idea that Chu Feng was already at the Bloodline Galaxy, but Zi Ling knew that his friends and family were confined in the phenomenon.","Even though Chu Feng had requested them not to make a reckless move and stay put here, she had a feeling that he had headed to the Bloodline Galaxy without them. That would explain Jie Tianran maneuvering God’s Era’s silhouette toward the Bloodline Galaxy.","“Little sister Yu’er, I need to leave for a while. You all wait here for Chu Feng,” Zi Ling said.","However, Little Fishy grabbed Zi Ling’s wrist and asked, “Big sister Zi Ling, do you have the same suspicion as me?”","“Ah?” Zi Ling was startled.","“Has big brother already left God’s Era for the Bloodline Galaxy, and Jie Tianran is heading there to look for him? You’re thinking of heading to the Bloodline Galaxy to look for big brother, right?” Little Fishy asked.","Long Mucheng, the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, and the others overheard those words and immediately surrounded Zi Ling.","“Is that the case, Miss Zi Ling?” Long Mucheng asked.","“Yes, that is my guess,” Zi Ling replied.","“We’ll go as well!” the crowd voiced out.","Zi Ling took another look at God’s Era via the observation formation. God’s Era’s silhouette was moving so quickly that even if they expended all their means, there was no way they could catch up.","Furthermore, she understood deep down that she didn’t have the strength to rescue Chu Feng. What she was doing right now was tantamount to suicide.","For that reason, she hoped that Chu Feng wasn’t in the Bloodline Galaxy.","“I’m sure you understand how dangerous this trip is, so I shan’t say too much. If you still want to come along, feel free to do so,” Zi Ling said.","The crowd nodded. No one here intended to back down.","So, the Chu Clan Alliance immediately used their most powerful means to rush toward the Bloodline Galaxy. However, they only got further and further away from God’s Era’s silhouette; there was no way for them to catch up with it.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng remained in the barrier of the Heaven Protection Shield Spirit.","There were hardly any Netherworld Sectmembers around him right now.","Instead, he was surrounded by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s world spiritists. They channeled the sealing formation to the fullest extent of their ability to siphon energy away from his Netherworld Embryo toward a space not too far away.","Chu Feng deduced that the space contained a treasure that served as a medium for the formation. Under normal circumstances, it should have been impossible to siphon his Netherworld Embryo’s energy through the barrier. It was due to the treasure and Jie Tianran’s formation that this was made possible.","In contrast, the world spiritists didn’t take a toll from channeling the formation.","Chu Feng could only watch helplessly as his Netherworld Embryo slowly lost energy.","“What are you thinking, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked.","“It’s nothing,” Chu Feng replied.","“Nothing? You’re even keeping things from me now?” Eggy snorted.","Chu Feng laughed. “Why aren’t you using the origin energies for your cultivation?”","He noticed that she didn’t touch the origin energies from Fei as well. Instead, she placed them around her and refined them with her energy.","“These origin energies are of inferior quality. It’ll shake my foundation if I absorb them straight. I’ll have to refine them first,” Eggy replied.","“Eggy, are these origin energies enough for you to reach Heavenly God level?” Chu Feng asked.","“I think so, but I won’t make it in time. Besides, I doubt that I can turn things around even if I reach Heavenly God level, especially with your grandfather wielding God’s Era’s power right now,” Eggy replied.","“He might not have reached the golden throne, but I can’t deny the fact that he has gained control over God’s Era,” Chu Feng said with a sigh.","He had to concede that they were in a terrible position. Eggy might be able to deal with Jie Tianran after reaching Heavenly God level, but would that be enough to deal with God’s Era?"]},{"number":6700,"title":"Chapter 6700: Chapter 6698: The Truth","paragraphs":["Chapter 6698: The Truth","“What are your current thoughts, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked. “I want to hear the truth.”","There was a brief pause before Chu Feng replied, “Eggy, it might be time for us to put our lives on the line.”","He had wanted to ask her if she blamed him for putting them in this plight, but Eggy interjected before he could pose that question, “Let’s do it then. We’ll teach your loser grandfather a lesson! You use your Bloodline Rampage, and I’ll use my means! We’ll let him know that he’s no match for us even if he obtains God’s Era’s power by some stroke of luck!”","She looked excited as if she had wanted to do this for a long time. She didn’t fear death.","Chu Feng felt heartened yet apologetic at the same time.","She had always supported him, even when she wasn’t fond of how he staked his life to protect his family and friends. She was willing to fight alongside him, even if it meant death.","“Hm?”","Chu Feng narrowed his eyes.","The siphoning of his Netherworld Embryo’s energy shouldn’t have had an effect on him, but all of a sudden, there was a change in the formation, and he felt a powerful force attempting to pull his consciousness from his body.","The force was coming from the space where his Netherworld Embryo’s energy was flowing toward, where the treasure medium was hidden.","Chu Feng tried to resist the force, but it was to no avail.","His consciousness was dragged into a dark palace. He noticed Chen Hui cultivating in a blood pool with closed eyes, as well as the severely injured Dongfang Hansong, whose face remained pale even though his body had recovered.","Dongfang Hansong had formed a peculiar hand seal and was channeling a formation. Many treasures were placed neatly around him, and they, together with the palace, made up a huge formation.","This formation was the culprit that dragged Chu Feng’s consciousness out of his body.","Concentrated surges of blood-red auras were continuously flowing into the palace. They were the energy siphoned away from Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo.","Sensing Chu Feng’s consciousness, Dongfang Hansong opened his eyes to look at Chu Feng. He spoke with a mocking voice, “Young master, you have worked hard.”","Chu Feng was confused. Young master? He thought that Dongfang Hansong had misrecognized him as someone else, but his consciousness looked identical to him. There was no room for a mistake.","“Young master?” Xiahou Jue murmured under his breath in confusion.","His presence was completely concealed after consuming Baili Xukong’s pill, allowing him to follow Dongfang Hansong all the way here without the latter noticing.","“Is Dongfang Hansong so grievously wounded that his eyes are failing him? That soul entity clearly belongs to Chu Feng, so why is he calling him ‘young master’? Who does ‘young master’ even refer to? Does the conservative faction have a young master?” Xiahou Jue mumbled.","Dongfang Hansong changed his hand seal, and the Netherworld Embryo’s energy in the palace surged toward Chu Feng’s consciousness.","“This is a forbidden method. He’s using this formation to gather the Netherworld Embryo’s energy inside Chu Feng’s soul entity before transferring it elsewhere. He plans to transfer all this energy into Chen Hui’s body! Dongfang Hansong does covet Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo!” Xiahou Jue exclaimed to himself.","Having seen through Dongfang Hansong’s ploy, Xiahou Jue was prepared to leave the palace and report this matter to Baili Xukong.","“What are you planning?” Chu Feng asked.","“You’re already a dead man, young master. Think of it as making one last contribution to the Netherworld Sect on behalf of Lord Netherworld Master,” Dongfang Hansong said.","Xiahou Jue froze in place.","“What are you saying?” Chu Feng asked.","“Heh...” Dongfang Hansong smiled.","He took out a pill and popped it into Chen Hui’s mouth. The latter immediately regained consciousness, but the first thing he did was to lurch in shock.","“Chu Feng?” Chen Hui stared at Chu Feng’s soul entity in disbelief.","“That’s right, Hui’er. That is Chu Feng’s consciousness. His body is not too far away, but that isn’t important now. If you want to become the Netherworld Sect’s future, you have to consume the energy of Chu Feng’s Netherworld Embryo. I designed this formation for the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to accomplish this task,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“Lord Netherworld Marshal, I...”","Chen Hui looked conflicted. Due to his ties with Song Yun, he couldn’t bring himself to hurt Chu Feng, even if it was Dongfang Hansong’s order.","“Hui’er, your unnecessary kindness resembles that of your mother,” Dongfang Hansong said.","“My mother? Lord Netherworld Marshal, do you know my mother?” Chen Hui anxiously asked.","He had grown up in the Netherworld Sect as an orphan, knowing nothing about his parents. The mention of his mother sparked his curiosity.","“Of course. I am your father,” Dongfang Hansong revealed.","Chu Feng narrowed his eyes. He understood what was going on now.","Xiahou Jue’s mouth fell agape.","However, the one who reacted the most intensely to the revelation was Chen Hui. His eyes widened in shock, and his mouth grew so big that one could stick a fist into it.","“Lord Netherworld Marshal, you mustn’t joke about such stuff,” Chen Hui said.","“I’m not joking, Hui’er. You are my son! Your name should have been Dongfang Hui, and I have been nurturing you as the Netherworld Sect’s future leader. I wanted to temper your character so that you don’t end up like Baili Zilin, which was why I hid your identity. You should understand where I am coming from, right?” Dongfang Hansong asked.","“This... I...”","Chen Hui felt like his head was about to explode. He would have never dared imagine something like that to be possible. In hindsight, Dongfang Hansong had taken great care of him in private without anyone questioning it.","This gave credence to Dongfang Hansong’s words."]}]);
